#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:238
msgid ""
"For large matrices, use the APDL Math operation :ref:`lsfactor` for "
"efficiency (see `APDL Math "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_apdl/apdlmathex.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:203
msgid "``MULT`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, MULT, ``Par2`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:32
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:205
msgid ""
"Matrix multiply: Multiplies ``Par1`` by ``Par2``. The number of rows of "
"``Par2`` must equal the number of columns of ``Par1`` for the operation. If "
"``Par2`` is input with a number of rows greater than the number of columns "
"of ``Par1``, matrices are still multiplied. However, the operation only uses"
" a number of rows of ``Par2`` equal to the number of columns of ``Par1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:37
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:210
msgid "``COVAR`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, COVAR, ``Par2`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:39
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:212
msgid ""
"Covariance: The measure of association between columns of the ``Par1`` input"
" matrix. ``Par1`` of size m runs (rows) by n data (columns) is first "
"processed to produce a row vector containing the mean of each column, which "
"is transposed to the output column vector ``Par2`` of n array elements. The "
"``Par1`` and ``Par2`` operation then produces ``ParR``, a resulting n x n "
"matrix of covariances (with the variances as the diagonal terms)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:45
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:218
msgid "``CORR`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, CORR, ``Par2`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:47
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:220
msgid ""
"Correlation: The correlation coefficient between columns of the ``Par1`` "
"input matrix. ``Par1`` of size m runs (rows) by n data (columns) is first "
"processed to produce a row vector containing the mean of each column, which "
"is then transposed to the output column vector ``Par2`` of n array elements."
" The ``Par1`` and ``Par2`` operation then produces ``ParR``, a resulting n x"
" n matrix of correlation coefficients (with a value of 1.0 for the diagonal "
"terms)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:53
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:226
msgid "``SOLV`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, SOLV, ``Par2`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:55
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:228
msgid ""
"Solution of simultaneous equations: Solves the set of ``n`` equations of "
"``n`` terms of the form a:sub:`n1` x:sub:`1` + a:sub:`n2` x:sub:`2` + "
":sup:`...` + a:sub:`nn` x:sub:`n` = b:sub:`n` where ``Par1`` contains the "
"matrix of a-coefficients, ``Par2`` contains the vector(s) of b-values, and "
"``ParR`` contains the vector(s) of x-results. ``Par1`` must be a square "
"matrix. The equations must be linear, independent, and well conditioned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:68
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:241
msgid ""
"``SORT`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, SORT, ``Par2``, ``n1``, "
"``n2``, ``n3`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:70
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:243
msgid ""
"Matrix sort: Sorts the columns of matrix ``Par1`` according to sort vector "
"``Par2`` and places the result back into ``Par1``. Rows of ``Par1`` are "
"moved to the corresponding positions indicated by the values of ``Par2``. "
"``Par2`` may be a column of ``Par1`` (in which case it will also be "
"reordered). Alternatively, you may specify the column of ``Par1`` to sort "
"using ``n1`` (leaving ``Par2`` blank). A secondary sort can be specified by "
"column ``n2``, and a third sort using column ``n3``. ``ParR`` is the vector "
"of initial row positions (the permutation vector). Sorting ``Par1`` "
"according to ``ParR`` should reproduce the initial ordering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:78
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:251
msgid "``NNEAR`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, NNEAR, ``Toler`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:80
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:253
msgid ""
"Nearest Node: Finds the nodes nearest to the given set of points in "
"``Par1``, where ``Par1`` is an n x 3 array of coordinate locations. ``ParR``"
" is a vector of the nearest selected nodes, or 0 if no nodes are nearer than"
" ``Toler``. ``Toler`` defaults to 1 and is limited to the maximum model "
"size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:84
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:257
msgid "``ENEAR`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, ENEAR, ``Toler`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:86
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:259
msgid ""
"Nearest Element: Finds the elements nearest to the given set of points in "
"``Par1``, where ``Par1`` is an n x 3 array of coordinate locations. ``ParR``"
" is a vector of the nearest selected elements, or 0 if no element centroids "
"are nearer than ``Toler``. ``Toler`` defaults to 1 and is limited to the "
"maximum model size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:91
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:264
msgid ""
"``MAP`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, MAP, ``Par2``, ``Par3``, "
"``kDim``, ``--``, ``kOut``, ``LIMIT`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:94
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:267
msgid ""
"Maps the results from one set of points to another. For example, you can map"
" pressures from a CFD analysis onto your model for a structural analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:97
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:270
msgid ""
"``Par1`` is the Nout x 3 array of points that will be mapped to. ``Par2`` is"
" the Nin x M array that contains M values of data to be interpolated at each"
" point and corresponds to the Nin x 3 points in ``Par3``. The resulting "
"``ParR`` is the Nout x M array of mapped data points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:101
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:274
msgid ""
"For each point in the destination mesh, all possible triangles in the source"
" mesh are searched to find the best triangle containing each point. It then "
"does a linear interpolation inside this triangle. You should carefully "
"specify your interpolation method and search criteria in order to provide "
"faster and more accurate results (see ``LIMIT``, below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:106
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:279
msgid ""
"``kDim`` is the interpolation criteria. If ``kDim`` = 2 or 0, two "
"dimensional interpolation is applied (interpolate on a surface). If ``kDim``"
" = 3, three dimensional interpolation is applied (interpolate on a volume)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:110
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:283
msgid ""
"``kOut`` specified how points outside of the domain are handled. If ``kOut``"
" = 0, use the value(s) of the nearest region point for points outside of the"
" region. If ``kOut`` = 1, set results outside of the region to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:114
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:287
msgid ""
"``LIMIT`` specifies the number of nearby points considered for "
"interpolation. The default is 20, and the minimum is 5. Lower values will "
"reduce processing time; however, some distorted or irregular sets of points "
"will require a higher ``LIMIT`` value to encounter three nodes for "
"triangulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:118
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:291
msgid ""
"Output points are incorrect if they are not within the domain (area or "
"volume) defined by the specified input points. Also, calculations for out-"
"of-bound points require much more processing time than do points that are "
"within bounds. Results mapping is available from the command line only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:122
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:295
msgid "``INTP`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, INTP, ``Par2`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:124
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:297
msgid ""
"Finds the elements that contain each point in the array of n x 3 points in "
"``Par1``. ``Par2`` will contain the set of element ID numbers and ``ParR`` "
"will contain their n x 3 set of natural element coordinates (values between "
"-1 and 1). ``Par1`` must be in global Cartesian coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:128
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:301
msgid ""
"``SGET`` - ( :ref:`moper`, ``ParR``, ``Par1``, SGET, ``Par2``, ``Label``, "
"``Comp`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:130
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.moper:303
msgid ""
"Gets the nodal solution item corresponding to ``Label`` and ``Comp`` (see "
"the :ref:`plnsol` command) and interpolates it to the given element "
"locations. ``Par1`` contains the n x 3 array of natural element coordinates "
"(values between -1 and 1) of the n element ID numbers in ``Par2``. ``Par1`` "
"and ``Par2`` are usually the output of the :ref:`moper`,,,INTP operation. "
"``ParR`` contains the n interpolated results."
msgstr ""

