#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:146
msgid ""
"``LT`` - Less than comparison: ``Par1`` < ``Par2`` gives 1.0 if true, 0.0 if"
" false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:32
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:148
msgid ""
"``LE`` - Less than or equal comparison: ``Par1``  :math:`equation not "
"available`  ``Par2`` gives 1.0 if true, 0.0 if false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:35
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:151
msgid ""
"``EQ`` - Equal comparison: ``Par1`` = ``Par2`` gives 1.0 if true, 0.0 if "
"false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:37
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:153
msgid ""
"``NE`` - Not equal comparison: ``Par1`` ≠ ``Par2`` gives 1.0 if true, 0.0 if"
" false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:39
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:155
msgid ""
"``GE`` - Greater than or equal comparison: ``Par1``  :math:`equation not "
"available` Par2 gives 1.0 if true, 0.0 if false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:42
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:158
msgid ""
"``GT`` - Greater than comparison: ``Par1`` > ``Par2`` gives 1.0 if true, 0.0"
" if false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:44
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:160
msgid ""
"``DER1`` - First derivative: d( ``Par1`` )/d( ``Par2`` ). The derivative at "
"a point is determined over points half way between the previous and next "
"points (by linear interpolation). ``Par1`` must be a function (a unique "
"``Par1`` value for each ``Par2`` value) and ``Par2`` must be in ascending "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:49
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:165
msgid ""
"``DER2`` - Second derivative: d :sup:`2` ( ``Par1`` )/d( ``Par2`` ) "
":sup:`2`. See also DER1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:51
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:167
msgid ""
"``INT1`` - Single integral:  ``Par1`` d( ``Par2`` ), where ``CON1`` is the "
"integration constant. The integral at a point is determined by using the "
"single integration procedure described in the `Mechanical APDL Theory "
"Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_biblio.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:55
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:171
msgid ""
"``INT2`` - Double integral:   ``Par1`` d( ``Par2`` ), where ``CON1`` is the "
"integration constant of the first integral and ``CON2`` is the integration "
"constant of the second integral. If ``Par1`` contains acceleration data, "
"``CON1`` is the initial velocity and ``CON2`` is the initial displacement. "
"See also INT1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:60
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:176
msgid ""
"``DOT`` - Dot product: ``Par1``. ``Par2``. ``Par1`` and ``Par2`` must each "
"have three consecutive columns of data, with the columns containing the i, "
"j, and k vector components, respectively. Only the starting row index and "
"the column index for the i components are specified for ``Par1`` and "
"``Par2``, such as A(1,1). The j and k components of the vector are assumed "
"to begin in the corresponding next columns, such as A(1,2) and A(1,3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:66
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:182
msgid ""
"``CROSS`` - Cross product: ``Par1`` x ``Par2``. ``Par1``, ``Par2``, and "
"``ParR`` must each have 3 components, respectively. Only the starting row "
"index and the column index for the i components are specified for ``Par1``, "
"``Par2``, and ``ParR``, such as A(1,1). The j and k components of the vector"
" are assumed to begin in the corresponding next columns, such as A(1,2) and "
"A(1,3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:71
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:187
msgid ""
"``GATH`` - Gather: For a vector of position numbers, ``Par2``, copy the "
"value of ``Par1`` at each position number to ``ParR``. Example: for ``Par1``"
" = 10,20,30,40 and ``Par2`` = 2,4,1; ``ParR`` = 20,40,10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:75
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:191
msgid ""
"``SCAT`` - Scatter: Opposite of GATH operation. For a vector of position "
"numbers, ``Par2``, copy the value of ``Par1`` to that position number in "
"``ParR``. Example: for ``Par1`` = 10,20,30,40,50 and ``Par2`` = 2,1,0,5,3; "
"``ParR`` = 20,10,50,0,40."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:79
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:195
msgid ""
"``ATN2`` - Arctangent: arctangent of ``Par1`` / ``Par2`` with the sign of "
"each component considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:82
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:198
msgid ""
"``LOCAL`` - Transform the data in ``Par1`` from the global Cartesian "
"coordinate system to the local coordinate system given in ``CON1``. ``Par1``"
" must be an N x 3 (that is, vector) or an N x 6 (that is, stress or strain "
"tensor) array. If the local coordinate system is a cylindrical, spherical, "
"or toroidal system, then you must provide the global Cartesian coordinates "
"in ``Par2`` as an N x 3 array. Set ``CON2`` = 1 if the data is strain data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:88
