#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:224
msgid ""
"Absolute values and scale factors can be applied to all parameters ( "
":ref:`vabs`, :ref:`vfact` ). Results can be cumulative ( :ref:`vcum` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:227
msgid ""
"Starting array element numbers must be defined for each array parameter "
"vector if it does not start at the first location, such as "
":ref:`voper`,A,B(5),ADD,C(3) which adds the third element of C to the fifth "
"element of B and stores the result in the first element of A."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:231
msgid ""
"Operations continue on successive array elements ( :ref:`vlen`, :ref:`vmask`"
" ) with the default being all successive elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:234
msgid ""
"Skipping array elements via :ref:`vmask` or :ref:`vlen` for the DER and INT "
"functions skips only the writing of the results (skipped array element data "
"are used in all calculations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:237
msgid ""
"Parameter functions and operations are available to operate on a scalar "
"parameter or a single element of an array parameter, such as SQRT(B) or "
"SQRT(A(4)). (See :ref:`starset` for more information.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:241
msgid ""
"Operations on a sequence of array elements can be performed by repeating the"
" desired function or operation in a do-loop ( ``*DO`` ). The vector "
"operations within Mechanical APDLm ( **\\*V** ``XX`` commands) are "
"internally programmed do-loops that conveniently perform the indicated "
"operation over a sequence of array elements. If the array is "
"multidimensional, only the first subscript is incremented in the do-loop; "
"that is, the operation repeats in column vector fashion down the array. For "
"example, for A(1,5), A(2,5), A(3,5), etc. The starting location of the row "
"index must be defined for each parameter read and for the result written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:249
msgid ""
"The default number of loops is from the starting result location to the last"
" result location and can be altered via :ref:`vlen`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:252
msgid ""
"A logical mask vector can be defined to control at which locations the "
"operations are to be skipped ( :ref:`vmask` ). The default is to skip no "
"locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:255
msgid ""
"Repeat operations automatically terminate at the last array element of the "
"result array column if the number of loops is undefined or if it exceeds the"
" last result array element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:258
msgid ""
"Zeroes are used in operations for values read beyond the last array element "
"of an input array column. Existing values in the rows and columns of the "
"results matrix remain unchanged where not changed by the requested operation"
" values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:262
msgid ""
"The result array column may be the same as the input array column, as "
"results in progress are stored in a temporary array until being moved to the"
" results array at the end of the operation. Results may be overwritten or "
"accumulated with the existing results ( :ref:`vcum` ). The default is to "
"overwrite results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/array_parameters.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.array_parameters.ArrayParameters.voper:267
msgid ""
"The absolute value can be used for each parameter read or written ( "
":ref:`vabs` ). A scale factor (defaulting to 1.0) is also applied to each "
"parameter read and written ( :ref:`vfact` )."
msgstr ""

