"following the :ref:`create` command, up to the :ref:`end` command, are "
"written to the specified file without being executed. An existing file of "
"the same name, if any, will be overwritten. Parameter values are not "
"substituted for parameter names in the commands when the commands are "
"written to the file. Use :ref:`cfwrite` to create a file if this is desired."
" The resulting macro may be executed with a :ref:`use` command (which also "
"allows parameters to be passed into the macro) or a :ref:`input` command "
"(which does not allow parameters to be passed in). Several macros may be "
"stacked into a library file ( :ref:`ulib` ). You cannot use :ref:`create` "
"within a DO loop."
