#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/macro_files.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.macro_files.MacroFiles.msg:114
msgid ""
"Allows writing an output message via the Mechanical APDL message subroutine."
" Also allows run termination control. This command is used only when "
"contained in a prepared file read into the Mechanical APDL program (that is,"
" :ref:`use`, :ref:`input`, etc.). A message format must immediately follow "
"the :ref:`msg` command (on a separate line, without parentheses, as "
"described below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/macro_files.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.macro_files.MacroFiles.msg:121
msgid ""
"The message format may be up to 80 characters long, consisting of text "
"strings and predefined \"data descriptors\" between the strings where "
"numeric or alphanumeric character data are to be inserted. The normal "
"descriptors are %I for integer data, %G for double precision data, %C for "
"alphanumeric character data, and %/ for a line break. The corresponding "
"FORTRAN data descriptors are I9, 1PG16.9 and A8, respectively. Each "
"descriptor must be preceded by a blank. There must be one data descriptor "
"for each specified value (8 maximum) in the order of the specified values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/macro_files.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.macro_files.MacroFiles.msg:128
msgid ""
"Enhanced descriptions may also be used:  This command contains some tables "
"and extra information which can be inspected in the original documentation "
"pointed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/apdl/macro_files.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.apdl.macro_files.MacroFiles.msg:131
msgid ""
"Do not begin :ref:`msg` format lines with ``*IF``, ``*ELSE``, ``*ELSEIF``, "
"or ``*ENDIF``. If the last nonblank character of the message format is an "
"ampersand (&), a second line will also be read as a continuation of the "
"format. Up to nine continuations (ten total lines) may be read. If normal "
"descriptions are used, then consecutive blanks are condensed into one blank "
"upon output, and a period is appended. Up to ten lines of output of 72 "
"characters each may be produced (using the %/ descriptor). Two examples "
"follow."
msgstr ""

