#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.esel:34
msgid ""
"Label identifying data, see :ref:`ESEL_tab_1`. Some items also require a "
"component label. If ``Item`` = PICK (or simply \"P\"), graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). Defaults to ELEM. If ``Item`` = STRA (straightened), elements are "
"selected whose midside nodes do not conform to the curved line or non-flat "
"area on which they should lie. (Such elements are sometimes formed during "
"volume meshing ( :ref:`vmesh` ) in an attempt to avoid excessive element "
"distortion.) You should graphically examine any such elements to evaluate "
"their possible effect on solution accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.esel:43
msgid ""
"Component of the item (if required). Valid component labels are shown in "
":ref:`ESEL_tab_1` below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.esel:47
msgid ""
"Minimum value of item range. Ranges are element numbers, attribute numbers, "
"load values, or result values as appropriate for the item. A component name "
"(as specified via the :ref:`cm` command) can also be substituted for "
"``VMIN`` (in which case ``VMAX`` and ``VINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.esel:52
msgid ""
"Maximum value of item range. ``VMAX`` defaults to ``VMIN`` for input values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.esel:54
msgid ""
"For result values, ``VMAX`` defaults to infinity if ``VMIN`` is positive, or"
" to zero if ``VMIN`` is negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.esel:58
msgid ""
"Value increment within range. Used only with integer ranges (such as for "
"element and attribute numbers). Defaults to 1. ``VINC`` cannot be negative."
msgstr ""

