"Minimum value of item range. Ranges are line numbers, coordinate values, "
"attribute numbers, etc., as appropriate for the item. If ``VMIN`` = 0.0, a "
"tolerance of ±1.0E-6 is used, or ±0.005 x ``VMIN`` if ``VMIN`` = ``VMAX``. A"
" component name (as specified on the :ref:`cm` command) may also be "
"substituted for ``VMIN`` ( ``VMAX`` and ``VINC`` are ignored). If ``Item`` ="
" MAT, TYPE, REAL, ESYS, or NDIV and if ``VMIN`` is positive, the absolute "
"value of ``Item`` is compared against the range for selection; if ``VMIN`` "
"is negative, the signed value of ``Item`` is compared. See the :ref:`llist` "
"command for a discussion of signed attributes."
