#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:28
msgid ""
"Label identifying data. Valid item labels are shown in the table below. Some"
" items also require a component label. If ``Item`` = PICK (or simply \"P\"),"
" graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI). Defaults to VOLU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:36
msgid ""
"Minimum value of item range. Ranges are volume numbers, coordinate values, "
"attribute numbers, etc., as appropriate for the item. A component name (as "
"specified on the :ref:`cm` command) may also be substituted for ``VMIN`` ( "
"``VMAX`` and ``VINC`` are ignored). If ``Item`` = MAT, TYPE, REAL, or ESYS "
"and if ``VMIN`` is positive, the absolute value of ``Item`` is compared "
"against the range for selection; if ``VMIN`` is negative, the signed value "
"of ``Item`` is compared. See the :ref:`vlist` command for a discussion of "
"signed attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:47
msgid ""
"Value increment within range. Used only with integer ranges (such as for "
"volume numbers). Defaults to 1. ``VINC`` cannot be negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:51
msgid "Specifies whether only volumes are to be selected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:53
msgid "``0`` - Select volumes only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:55
msgid ""
"``1`` - Select volumes, as well as keypoints, lines, areas, nodes, and "
"elements associated with selected volumes. Valid only with ``Type`` = S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:72
msgid ""
"This function contains specificities regarding the argument definitions. "
"Please refer to the `command documentation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VSEL.html>`_"
" for further explanations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.selecting.Selecting.vsel:78
msgid ""
"Selects volumes based on values of a labeled item and component. For "
"example, to select a new set of volumes based on volume numbers 1 through 7,"
" use :ref:`vsel`,S,VOLU,,1,7. The subset is used when the ALL label is "
"entered (or implied) on other commands, such as :ref:`vlist`,ALL. Only data "
"identified by volume number are selected. Data are flagged as selected and "
"unselected; no data are actually deleted from the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/selecting.pydocstring
