msgid "File read option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:11
msgid "``START`` - Reread :file:`start.ans` file (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:13
msgid "``NOSTART`` - Do not reread :file:`start.ans` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:29
msgid ""
"The :ref:`clear` command resets the database to the conditions present at "
"the beginning of the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:32
msgid ""
"The command is typically used between multiple analyses in the same run, or "
"between passes of a multipass analysis (such as between substructure "
"generation, use, and expansion passes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:35
msgid ""
"The command sets the import and Boolean options back to the default, deletes"
" all items from the database, and sets memory values to zero for items "
"derived from database information. (All files remain intact.) The command "
"also resets the jobname to match the currently open session :file:`.LOG` and"
" :file:`.ERR` files, returning the jobname to its original value or to the "
"most recent value specified via :ref:`filname` with ``KEY`` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:41
msgid ""
"After the database is cleared, the :file:`start.ans` file is reread (by "
"default) unless ``Read`` = NOSTART."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:44
msgid ""
"Additional commands cannot be stacked (via the $ separator) on the same line"
" as the :ref:`clear` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:47
msgid ""
"Use caution when placing the :ref:`clear` command within branching "
"constructs (for example, those using ``*DO`` or ``*IF`` commands), as the "
"command deletes all parameters including the looping parameter for do-loops."
" (To preserve your iteration parameter, issue a :ref:`parsav` command prior "
"to :ref:`clear`, then follow  :ref:`clear` with a :ref:`parres` command.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/database/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.clear:52
msgid ""
"This command is valid in any processor. Issuing this command at any point "
"clears the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/database/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.database.set_up.SetUp.resume.rst:2
