msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:34
msgid "Visibility key for shell elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:36
msgid ""
"``0`` - Off (default), surface load symbols are displayed only on visible "
"load faces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:38
msgid ""
"``1`` - On, surface load symbols are displayed even if load face is not "
"visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:41
msgid "Visibility key for contour legend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:43
msgid ""
"``ON`` - The symbols (arrows or face outlines) will show up in color with "
"the legend showing the corresponding color labels (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:46
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - The contour legend will not be displayed. The symbols (arrows or "
"face outlines) will show up in grey. The size of the arrows will be "
"proportional to the applied load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:63
msgid ""
":ref:`psf` determines whether and how to show surface loads on subsequent "
"model displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:65
msgid ""
"If surface loads are applied to solid model entities, only solid model plots"
" show the load symbols; node and element plots do not show them unless the "
"loads are transferred ( :ref:`sftran` or :ref:`sbctran` ). Similarly, solid "
"model plots do not show the load symbols if surface loads are applied to "
"nodes and elements. For node and element plots of shell element models, the "
"surface load symbols are shown only if the load face is visible from the "
"current viewing direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:71
msgid ""
"The effects of the **/PSF** command are not cumulative (that is, the command"
" does not modify an existing setting from a previously issued :ref:`psf` "
"command). Only the setting specified via the most recent :ref:`psf` command "
"applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:76
msgid ""
"If you issue a `postprocessing (POST1) "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CH2_7.html#cmdpost1failure>`_"
" plot command that produces result contours (such as :ref:`plnsol` ), "
":ref:`psf` has no effect. This behavior prevents conflicting contours in the"
" graphics window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:81
msgid ""
"When using the radiosity method ( ``Item`` = RDSF and ``Comp`` = ENCL) with "
"``Key`` = 2, the radiation arrows point outward from any element face."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:84
msgid ""
":ref:`psf`,STAT displays current :ref:`psf` settings, and :ref:`psf`,DEFA "
"resets them back to default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:87
msgid ""
"Other useful commands are :ref:`pnum`,SVAL,1 to show the values of the "
"surface loads, :ref:`vscale` to change arrow lengths, and :ref:`pbc` and "
":ref:`pbf` to activate other load symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:90
msgid ""
"For beam elements, only the colors representing shear (GREEN) and normal "
"(RED) pressures are displayed for the arrows. The color of these arrows does"
" not correspond to the magnitudes in the contour legend. The length of these"
" arrows does, however, correlate to the relative magnitude of the pressures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psf:95
msgid ""
"For elements ``SURF159``, ``SOLID272``, ``SOLID273``, ``PIPE288`` and "
"``PIPE289``, :ref:`psf` is not available when displaying elements with "
"shapes determined from the real constants or section definition ( "
":ref:`eshape` ). For ``PIPE288`` and ``PIPE289``, only external loads "
"applied via :ref:`sfbeam` are displayed."
msgstr ""

