msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `/PSYMB "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PSYMB.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:9
msgid "Show symbols as selected from the following labels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:11
msgid "``CS`` - Local coordinate systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:13
msgid "``NDIR`` - Nodal coordinate systems (on rotated nodes only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:15
msgid "``ESYS`` - Element coordinate systems (element displays only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:17
msgid "``LDIR`` - Line directions (line displays only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:19
msgid "``LDIV`` - Controls the display of element divisions on lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:21
msgid ""
"``ADIR`` - Area direction symbol (for keypoint, line, area and volume "
"plots)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:23
msgid ""
"``LAYR`` - Layer orientations (relative to the projected element x-axis) or "
"fiber orientations in smeared reinforcing elements. Used only within an "
"element display. Use ``KEY`` to specify the layer number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:27
msgid "``ECON`` - Element mesh symbols on keypoints and lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:29
msgid ""
"``DOT`` - Larger symbols displayed for node and keypoint locations. When "
"``Label`` = DOT, ``KEY`` = 1 by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:32
msgid "``XNOD`` - Extra node of surface or circuit elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:34
msgid ""
"``FBCS`` - Force boundary condition scaling. Subsequent ``KEY`` value "
"determines whether or not to scale the applied and derived forces/moments to"
" the same maximum value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:37
msgid ""
"``DEFA`` - Resets the symbol keys so that Mechanical APDL displays none of "
"the symbols controlled by the :ref:`psymb` command. The value of the ``KEY``"
" field is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:40
msgid ""
"``STAT`` - Prints the status of the settings of the symbol keys controlled "
"by the :ref:`psymb` command. The ``KEY`` field is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:43
msgid ""
"``MARK`` - Controls the marker size ( :ref:`gmarker` ). When ``Label`` = "
"MARK, ``KEY`` = 10 by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:49
msgid ""
"``-1`` - Effective only if ``Label`` = LAYR and solid shape element display "
"( :ref:`eshape` ) is active. Orientation of all layers appears with the "
"solid shape element display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:52
msgid ""
"``0`` - No symbol (default). If ``Label`` = LDIV, then ``KEY`` = 0 indicates"
" that the displayed element divisions will correspond to the existing mesh "
"(the word MESHED or EXISTING can also be substituted). Also, for ``Label`` ="
" LDIV, if you execute any meshing command (such as :ref:`amesh` or "
":ref:`vmesh` ), ``KEY`` is set to 0 (MESHED) automatically. If ``Label`` = "
"FBCS, then ``KEY`` = 0 indicates that boundary condition scaling will not be"
" common. The applied and derived forces/moments will be scaled to their "
"respective maximum values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:59
msgid ""
"``1`` - Include symbol. If ``Label`` = LDIV, then ``KEY`` = 1 indicates that"
" the displayed line divisions will correspond to the value assigned by "
":ref:`lesize` (the word LESIZE can also be substituted). Also, for ``Label``"
" = LDIV, if you execute the :ref:`lesize` command, ``KEY`` is set to 1 "
"(LESIZE) automatically. If ``Label`` = FBCS, then ``KEY`` = 1 indicates that"
" boundary condition scaling will be common. The applied and derived "
"forces/moments will be scaled to the same maximum value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:66
msgid ""
"``N`` - If ``Label`` = LAYR, then ``N`` is equal to the layer number. If "
"``Label`` = DOT, then ``N`` can be equal to 0,1,.....15, indicating the dot "
"size. If ``Label`` = MARK, then ``N`` can be equal to 1,.....10, indicating "
"the marker size. If ``Label`` = LDIV, then ``KEY`` = -1, indicates that no "
"element divisions will be displayed (the word OFF can also be substituted)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:85
msgid ""
"Includes various symbols on the display. Triads are right-handed with x "
"displayed as the longest leg. Where color is displayed, x is white, y is "
"green, and z is blue. For beams, x is always along the length of the "
"element. For lines, an arrow represents the direction of a line, from the "
"beginning keypoint to the end keypoint. See :ref:`plopts` command for "
"additional display options. Use :ref:`pstatus` or :ref:`psymb`,STAT to "
"display settings. Use :ref:`psymb`,DEFA to reset all specifications back to "
"their defaults. The command :ref:`psymb`,ECON,1 causes the symbol \"M\" to "
"be displayed on keypoints and lines associated with meshed entities. When "
"you issue the command :ref:`psymb`,DOT,1, a larger symbol is displayed for "
"each node and keypoint location. Using :ref:`psymb`,MARK,1, a smaller marker"
" size can be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:95
msgid ""
"PowerGraphics ( :ref:`graphics`,POWER) does not support :ref:`psymb`,ESYS "
"and :ref:`psymb`,LAYR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:97
msgid ""
"If ``KEY`` = ``N`` and PowerGraphics is off, the centroid of the surface "
"elements is connected to the extra node using a gray line. However, if "
"PowerGraphics is on, the color of the line connecting the centroid to the "
"extra node is the same as that for the elements themselves (as determined by"
" :ref:`pnum` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/labeling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.labeling.Labeling.psymb:102
msgid ""
"When ``Label`` = LAYR, the layer systems can be visualized with all current-"
"technology layered elements and the smeared reinforcing element "
"``REINF265``. To use :ref:`psymb`,LAYR with ``REINF265``, first set the "
"vector-mode graphics option ( :ref:`device`,VECTOR,1)."
msgstr ""

