"If only the common lines of non-coplanar faces are drawn (as per the "
":ref:`edge` command), then this command is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/scaling.rst:25:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:2
msgid "Sets the displacement multiplier for displacement displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `/DSCALE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_DSCALE_sl.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:10
msgid "The default value is AUTO or 0 except when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:12
msgid ""
"Large deflection effects are included ( :ref:`nlgeom`,ON) and it is not a "
"modal analysis; then the default is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:14
msgid ""
"It is a spectrum analysis ( :ref:`antype`,SPECTR); then the default is OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:15
msgid ""
"The amplitude of a time-harmonic solution is computed using the "
":ref:`hrcplx` command (OMEGAT _font FamName=\"Agency FB\"? ≥ /_font? 360 "
"_font FamName=\"Agency FB\"? ° /_font? ); then the default is OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:18
msgid ""
"The amplitude of a complex modal or harmonic solution is stored into the "
"database using the :ref:`set` command ( ``KIMG`` = AMPL); then the default "
"is OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:26
msgid "**dmult** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:27
msgid ""
"``AUTO or 0`` - Scale displacements automatically so that maximum "
"displacement (vector amplitude) displays as 5 percent of the maximum model "
"length, as measured in the global Cartesian X, Y, or Z directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:31
msgid ""
"``1`` - Do not scale displacements (that is, scale displacements by 1.0, "
"true to geometry). Often used with large deflection results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:34
msgid "``FACTOR`` - Scale displacements by numerical value input for FACTOR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:36
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - Remove displacement scaling (that is, scale displacements by 0.0, "
"no distortion)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:38
msgid ""
"``USER`` - Set ``DMULT`` to that used for last display (useful when last "
"``DMULT`` value was automatically calculated)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/scaling.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.slashdscale:55
msgid ""
"If Multi-Plots are not being displayed, and the current device is a 3D "
"device ( :ref:`show`,3D), then the displacement scale in all active windows "
"will be the same, even if separate :ref:`slashdscale` commands are issued "
"for each active window. For efficiency, the program maintains a single data "
"structure (segment) containing only one displacement scale. The program "
"displays the same segment (displacement scale) in all windows. Only the view"
" settings will be different in each of the active windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.scaling.Scaling.sscale.rst:2
