#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:17
msgid ""
"``AXES`` - Determines the color (specified in next argument, ``Clab`` ) that"
" the axes of a graph will be plotted in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:20
msgid ""
"``AXNUM`` - Determines the color (specified in next argument, ``Clab`` ) "
"that the numbering on the axes of a graph will be plotted in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:23
msgid ""
"``NUM`` - Discretely numbered items (such as element types, element "
"materials, etc., as shown on the :ref:`pnum` command). Also specify number "
"(1 to 11) in the ``N1`` field. For example, :ref:`color`,NUM,RED,3 will "
"assign the color red to all items having the discrete number 3 (material "
"displays would show elements having material 3 as red)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:28
msgid ""
"``OUTL`` - Outline of elements, areas, and volumes. Ex: "
":ref:`color`,OUTL,BLUE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:30
