"``AREA`` - Solid model areas. Use ``N1``, ``N2``, ``NINC`` fields for area "
"numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:36
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/style.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.style.Style.trlcy:15
msgid ""
"``VOLU`` - Solid model volumes. Use ``N1``, ``N2``, ``NINC`` fields for "
"volume numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:38
msgid ""
"``ISURF`` - Isosurfaces (surfaces of constant stress, etc.). This option is "
"particularly useful when capturing frames for animating a single isosurface "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:41
msgid ""
"``WBAK`` - Window background. Use ``N1``, ``N2``, ``NINC`` fields for window"
" numbers. The options that you select using ``Lab`` = PBAK will supersede "
"those applied using ``Lab`` = WBAK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:44
msgid ""
"``b.c.label`` - Boundary condition label. Enter U, ROT, TEMP, PRES, V, VOLT,"
" MAG, A, EMF, CURR, F, M, HEAT, FLOW, VF, AMPS, FLUX, CSG, CURT, MAST, CP, "
"CE, NFOR, NMOM, RFOR, RMOM, PATH. See the :ref:`pbc` command for boundary "
"condition label definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:48
msgid "``GRBAK`` - Graph background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:50
msgid "``GRID`` - Graph grid lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:52
msgid "``AXLAB`` - Graph X and Y axis labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:54
msgid ""
"``CURVE`` - Graph curves (identify curve numbers (1-10) in ``N1``, ``N2``, "
"``NINC`` fields)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:56
msgid ""
"``CM`` - Component group. Use ``N1`` field for component name, ignore ``N2``"
" and ``NINC``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:58
msgid ""
"``CNTR`` - Mechanical APDL contour stress colors. The maximum number of "
"contours available is 128. The number of colors that can be specified "
"interactively (GUI) is 9. ( :ref:`contour`, 9). Any other setting will yield"
" inconsistent results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:62
msgid ""
"``SMAX`` - Specifies that all stress values above the maximum value entered "
"in :ref:`contour` will be displayed in the color designated in the ``Clab`` "
"field. Defaults to dark grey."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:65
msgid ""
"``SMIN`` - Specifies that all stress values below the minimum value entered "
"in :ref:`contour` will be displayed in the color designated in the ``Clab`` "
"field. Defaults to dark grey."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.color:68
msgid ""
"``PBAK`` - Activates background shading options (see command syntax at end "
"of argument descriptions below). The options that you select using ``Lab`` ="
" PBAK will supersede those applied using ``Lab`` = WBAK."
msgstr ""

