msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:17
msgid ""
"``BBOX`` - Bounding box mode. For PowerGraphics plots involving elements "
"with :ref:`show`,x11 and :ref:`show`,win32, Mechanical APDL generally "
"displays dynamic rotations faster. If KEY = 1 (ON), then a bounding box (not"
" the elements) encompassing the model is displayed and rotated, rather than "
"the element outlines (ON is default in preprocessing). When KEY = 0 (OFF), "
"then dynamic rotations may be slower (Mechanical APDL redraws the element "
"outlines) for plots involving elements with :ref:`show`,x11 and "
":ref:`show`,win32. OFF is default in postprocessing. This command is ignored"
" if :ref:`edge`,WN,1 is set for any WN. This is ignored in POST1 and "
"SOLUTION plots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:25
msgid ""
"For any PowerGraphics plots involving elements, regardless of :ref:`show` "
"settings, plots will generally be displayed faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:28
msgid ""
"``VECTOR`` - Vector mode. In vector mode, areas, volumes, elements, and "
"postprocessing display geometries are shown as outlines (wireframes). When "
"vector mode is off (default), these entities are shown filled with color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:32
msgid ""
"``DITHER`` - When dithering is turned on (default), color intensity "
"transitions are smoothed. This selection a"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:35
msgid ""
"applies only to smooth-shaded images, that is, Z-buffered ( :ref:`slashtype`"
" ), or raster plots with Gouraud or Phong shading ( :ref:`shade` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:38
msgid ""
"``ANIM`` - Select the animation type used on 2D devices on the PC platform. "
"A ``KEY`` value of BMP (or 0) sets animation mode to the Mechanical APDL "
"animation controller (default). A ``KEY`` value of AVI (or 2) sets animation"
" mode to AVI movie player file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:42
msgid ""
"``FONT`` - Font selection for the Mechanical APDL graphics window. When "
"``Label`` = FONT, the command format is: :ref:`device`,FONT, ``KEY``, "
"``Val1``, ``Val2``, ``Val3``, ``Val4``, ``Val5``, ``Val6`` where ``KEY`` "
"determines the type of font being controlled, and values 1 through 6 control"
" various font parameters. These values are device specific; using the same "
"command input file ( :ref:`input` ) on different machines may yield "
"different results.. The following ``KEY`` values determine the font "
"information that will be supplied to the appropriate driver (for example, "
"Postscript, X11, Win32, JPEG,...):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:50
msgid ""
"``KEY = 1`` - The command controls the LEGEND (documentation column) font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:52
msgid ""
"``KEY = 2`` - The command controls the ENTITY (node and keypoint number) "
"font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:54
msgid "``KEY = 3`` - The command controls the ANNOTATION/GRAPH font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:56
msgid ""
"Linux: Values 1 through 4 are used to find a match in the X11 database of "
"font strings. Values 1, 2, and 3 are character strings; value 4 is a nonzero"
" integer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:59
msgid ""
"``Val1`` - Family name (for example, Courier). If ``Val1`` = MENU, all other"
" values are ignored and a font selection menu appears (GUI must be active)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:62
msgid "``Val2`` - Weight (for example, medium)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:64
msgid "``Val3`` - Slant (for example, r)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:66
msgid ""
"``Val4`` - Pixel size (for example, 14). Note that this value does no affect"
" the annotation fonts ( ``KEY`` = 3). Use the :ref:`tspec` command for "
"annotation font size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:69
msgid "``Val5`` - unused"
msgstr ""

