#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:106
msgid "``3`` - Designates the ANNOTATION/GRAPH font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.device:124
msgid ""
"The :ref:`device`,BBOX command is ignored in POST1 and SOLUTION plots. Also,"
" the elements are displayed and rotated if you use :ref:`device`,BBOX,ON and"
" :ref:`edge`,WN,1,ANGLE (effectively ignoring the BBOX option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.graphics.set\\_up.SetUp.dsys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/set_up.rst:44:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:2
msgid "Activates a display coordinate system for geometry listings and plots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `DSYS "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_DSYS.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:10
msgid "Global Cartesian ( ``KCN`` = 0) display coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:15
msgid ""
"Coordinate system reference number. ``KCN`` may be 0,1,2 or any previously "
"defined local coordinate system number. If a cylinder is displayed in its "
"cylindrical coordinate system (with a 1,0,0 view), it will be unrolled "
"(developed) into a flat plane (with theta along the Y direction)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:34
msgid ""
"Boundary condition symbols, vector arrows, and element coordinate system "
"triads are not transformed to the display coordinate system. The display "
"system orientation (for the default view) is X horizontal to the right, Y "
"vertical upward, and Z out of the screen (normal)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:38
msgid ""
"Line directions and area directions ( :ref:`psymb`,LDIR and "
":ref:`psymb`,ADIR) are not plotted for ``KCN`` >0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dsys:41
msgid ""
"When you create 3D annotation, the coordinates are stored to the database in"
" the display coordinate system that was active at the time of creation. "
"Changing the display coordinate system does not change the annotation "
"coordinate data in the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.graphics.set\\_up.SetUp.dv3d"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/set_up.rst:44:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:2
msgid "Sets 3D device option modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `/DV3D "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_DV3D.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:9
msgid "Mode label:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:11
msgid ""
"``ACCU`` - Activating the accumulation buffer for OpenGL graphics, providing"
" faster model rotation when shaded backgrounds are in use. This feature is "
"off by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:14
msgid ""
"``ACTR`` - Label term to designate the cursor position as the center for "
"automatic dynamic rotational center capability. The subsequent ``Key`` value"
" (see below) turns this capability on and off. This feature is on by "
"default. (Available for OpenGL displays only.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:18
msgid ""
"``ANIM`` - Animation mode. The ANIM option allows you to create animation "
"frames in pixmap mode instead of display list mode. This may improve large "
"model performance, but it eliminates local manipulation while animation is "
"in progress. This feature is on by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:22
msgid ""
"``ANTI`` - Label term to control Anti-aliasing, a smoothing technique for "
"your graph plots. (see below) The subsequent ``Key`` value turns this "
"capability on and off. The default for this feature is off. (Available for "
"OpenGL displays only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:26
msgid ""
"``CNTR`` - Switches banded contours on (1) or off (0) for your 3D contour "
"display. The default is 1 (ON). Other contour parameters such as number of "
"contours or the increment and range are defined using the :ref:`contour` "
"command. When either 9 or 128 contours are specified via :ref:`contour`, "
"this command is ignored and a smooth contour is always displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:31
msgid ""
"``DGEN`` - Local manipulation degenerate mode. You access the DGEN option to"
" set wire-frame local manipulation mode for 3D devices (device dependent). "
"This feature is off by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:34
msgid ""
"``DLIST`` - With DLIST, you can specify whether screen updates and redraws "
"will be performed using the Mechanical APDL display list (off), or the 3D "
"device's display list (on). DLIST is on by default for Windows systems, but "
"off for Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:38
msgid ""
"``DELS`` - You use DELS to suppress contour display screen overwrites when "
":ref:`noerase` is active. This prevents the bleed-through that occurs when "
"you overlay contour plots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:41
msgid ""
"``TRIS`` - Triangle strip mode. Tri-stripping provides faster 3D display "
"capabilities and is on by default. Some display enhancements, such as "
"texturing, are adversely affected by tri-stripping. You can turn off tri-"
"stripping in order to improve these display functions. Be sure to turn tri- "
"stripping on after the desired output is obtained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:47
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = ACCU:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:49
msgid "``0`` - (OFF) The accumulation buffer is not accessed. (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:51
msgid "``1`` - (ON) Access to the buffer is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:53
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = ACTR:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:55
msgid ""
"``0`` - (OFF) The cursor position has no effect on the existing rotational "
"center for dynamic operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:58
msgid ""
"``1`` - (ON) The rotational center for dynamic rotations in OpenGL is "
"determined by the position of the mouse cursor on (or within 15 pixels of) "
"the model. Any rotations that are initiated with the cursor more than 15 "
"pixels from the model will occur about the midpoint of the Z-axis at that "
"point in space. If the Z-buffer has not been refreshed the Z-axis will have "
"an infinite value, and rotations will appear to occur about an extremely "
"long Z-axis. This behavior stops when the graphics window is refreshed or "
"replotted. (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:65
msgid ""
"Note that when using the GUI in 3D mode, when ACTR = 1, the ``Rotational "
"Center`` option is grayed out under Utility Menu> PlotCtrls> View Setting "
"because the rotational center is determined strictly by the position of the "
"mouse cursor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:69
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = ANIM:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:71
msgid ""
"``0`` - Display list animation. The object can be dynamically manipulated "
"while animating. No legend, countour or annotation items are displayed. (see"
" Notes, below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:74
msgid ""
"``1`` - On Linux, device-dependent pixmap animation is used. On the PC, "
"bitmap animation is provided (default). When you animate in this mode, you "
"cannot dynamically manipulate your model (see Notes, below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:78
msgid ""
"``2`` - On the PC only, this option provides AVI animation which uses the "
"AVI movie player."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:80
msgid ""
"Although you can create animations of multiple Mechanical APDL window "
"schemes, animations created with OpenGL display lists ( :ref:`dv3d`, ANIM, "
"0) do not retain the windowing scheme information. You CAN save multiple "
"windows via the X11/WIN32 drivers, or via the OpenGL driver with "
":ref:`dv3d`, ANIM, KEY in effect (where KEY is not zero)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:85
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = ANTI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:87
msgid "``0`` - (OFF) Anti-aliasing is not active (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:89
msgid ""
"``1`` - (ON) The anti-aliasing technique will be applied to smooth the lines"
" in your displays (valid for OpenGL only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:92
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = DGEN:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:94
msgid "``0`` - Normal manipulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:96
msgid "``1`` - Wireframe Manipulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:98
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = DLIST:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:100
msgid ""
"``0`` - (OFF) The Mechanical APDL display list is used for plotting and "
"dynamic graphics manipulation (Linux default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:103
msgid ""
"``1`` - (ON) The local (3D device) display list is used for plotting and "
"dynamic rotation (Windows default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:106
msgid "The following key options apply to ``Lab`` = TRIS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:108
msgid "``0`` - (OFF) Tri-stripping is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:110
msgid "``1`` - (ON) Tri-stripping is on (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:126
msgid ""
"This function contains specificities regarding the argument definitions. "
"Please refer to the `command documentation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_DV3D.html>`_"
" for further explanations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.dv3d:130
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL uses display list animation for its 3D models. This memory "
"resident array method interfaces with the OpenGL model information to allow "
"the program to efficiently pan, zoom, rotate and dynamically manipulate your"
" model during animation. The logo, legend, contour and other annotation "
"items are produced in 2D and will not appear when :ref:`dv3d`, ANIM, 0 is in"
" effect. To display these items, use :ref:`dv3d`, ANIM, 1. All screen data "
"will be displayed, but manipulation of the model will not be possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/graphics/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.gcmd.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.graphics.set\\_up.SetUp.gcmd"
msgstr ""

