"displays. NODE, ELEM, KEYP, LINE, AREA, and VOLU are on by default. When "
"ELEM is activated, you can control the type of element displayed via the "
":ref:`gcmd` command (which also controls the type of graph display). When "
"the GRPH entity type is activated, all other entity types are deactivated. "
"Conversely, when any of the NODE, ELEM, KEYP, LINE, AREA, and VOLU entity "
"types are active, the GRPH entity type is deactivated."
