msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `PNGR "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PNGR.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:9
msgid "Specifies various PNG file export options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:11
msgid ""
"``COMP`` - If ``Kywrd`` = COMP, then ``OPT`` is either ON or OFF (blank is "
"interpreted as OFF). This option allows you to turn PNG file compression ON "
"or OFF. If OPT = ON, then The VAL field is read to determine the degree of "
"compression. See the VALUE argument for acceptable compression values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:29
msgid "``STAT`` - Shows the current status of PNG file export."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:34
msgid ""
"``ON, OFF`` - If ``Kywrd`` = COMP, the values On and Off control the use of "
"compression. The degree of compression is determined by VAL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:40
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.tiff:36
msgid ""
"``0, 1, 2`` - If ``Kywrd`` = COLOR, the numbers 0, 1, and 2 correspond to "
"Black and White, Grayscale and Color, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:43
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.tiff:39
msgid ""
"``1, 0`` - If ``Kywrd`` = TMOD, the values 1 and 0 determine whether bitmap "
"(1) or stroke text (0) fonts will be used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:46
msgid "**val** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:47
msgid ""
"``VAL`` is active only when ``Kywrd`` = COMP, and determines the degree of "
"compression applied to the exported file (see above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:50
msgid ""
"``-1`` - Apply the default, optimum value for compression. This value "
"represents the best combination of speed and compression. It varies "
"according to the release level of the ZLIB compression package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/graphics/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.graphics.set_up.SetUp.pngr:54
msgid ""
"``1-9`` - Use this value to specify a specific compression level. 1 is the "
"lowest compression level (fastest) and 9 is the highest compression level "
"(slowest)."
msgstr ""

