#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:2
msgid ""
"Applies a traveling wave animation to graphics data in a modal cyclic "
"symmetry analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ANCYC "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ANCYC.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:10
msgid ""
"The default :ref:`ancyc` command (issuing the command with no arguments) "
"specifies these implicit argument values: :ref:`ancyc`, 18, 0, 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:15
msgid "**numframes** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:16
msgid ""
"The number of plot frames for the animation. Valid values range from 5 "
"through 36. The default is 18. A low value (because it specifies fewer "
"graphical frames) produces a rougher animation but loads faster. A high "
"value produces a smoother animation but requires more time to load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:20
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.anim:11
msgid "**kcycl** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:21
msgid "The animation mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:23
msgid "``0`` - Continuous animation cycle (forward-reverse-forward)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:25
msgid ""
"``1`` - Discontinuous animation cycle (forward-reset-forward). This option "
"is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:28
msgid ""
"The time delay (in seconds) between animation frames. Valid values range "
"from 0.1 through 1.0. The default is 0.1 seconds, which produces a seemingly"
" real-time animation. A higher value produces a slower animation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:46
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ancyc` command is valid in a `modal cyclic symmetry analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#cycsym_postproc_modal>`_"
" only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:50
msgid ""
"The command animates the cyclic symmetry mode shape plot in the General Post"
" Processor ( :ref:`post1` ). When you issue a nodal- or element-results plot"
" command (for example, :ref:`plnsol`, :ref:`plesol`, or :ref:`pldisp` ) and "
"then issue the :ref:`ancyc` command, Mechanical APDL applies a traveling "
"wave animation to the mode shape plot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:55
msgid ""
"Each frame of the animation is created by expanding the cyclic symmetry mode"
" shape at increasing phase angles (via the :ref:`cycexpand` command) "
"starting at zero in equal increments over 360°. The phase-angle increment is"
" 360 / ``NUMFRAMES``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:59
msgid ""
"The animation display shows the traveling wave of the result quantity being "
"plotted. The traveling wave animation is applicable only to nodal diameters "
"(harmonic indices) greater than 0 and less than ``N`` / 2 (where ``N`` is "
"the number of cyclic sectors in the model)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/animation.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.animation.Animation.ancyc:63
msgid ""
"For more information, see `Applying a Traveling Wave Animation to the Cyclic"
" Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#gadvcyctwave>`_"
" in the `Cyclic Symmetry Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/cycsym_example.html>`_."
msgstr ""

