#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `/EFACET "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EFACET.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:10
msgid "As stated above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:15
msgid "Number of facets per element edge for element plots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:17
msgid "``1`` - Use 1 facet per edge (default for h-elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:19
msgid "``2`` - Use 2 facets per edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:21
msgid "``4`` - Use 4 facets per edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:37
msgid ""
":ref:`efacet` is valid only when PowerGraphics is enabled ( "
":ref:`graphics`,POWER), except that it can be used in FULL graphics mode for"
" element ``CONTA174``. (See the :ref:`graphics` command and element "
"``CONTA174`` in the `Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_"
" for more information.) The :ref:`efacet` command is only applicable to "
"element type displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:44
msgid ""
":ref:`efacet` controls the fineness of the subgrid that is used for element "
"plots. The element is subdivided into smaller portions called facets. Facets"
" are piecewise linear surface approximations of the actual element face. In "
"their most general form, facets are warped planes in 3D space. A greater "
"number of facets will result in a smoother representation of the element "
"surface for element plots. :ref:`efacet` may affect results averaging. See "
"`Contour Displays "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS5_3.html#>`_"
" in the `Basic Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS19.html>`_"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:54
msgid ""
"For midside node elements, use ``NUM`` = 2; if ``NUM`` = 1, no midside node "
"information is output. For non-midside node elements, ``NUM`` should be set "
"to 1. See the :ref:`plnsol` and :ref:`prnsol` commands for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:65
msgid ""
"For cyclic symmetry mode-superposition harmonic solutions, only ``NUM`` = 1 "
"is supported in postprocessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.efacet:70
msgid ""
"If you specify  :ref:`efacet`,1, PowerGraphics does not plot midside nodes. "
"You must use :ref:`efacet`,2 to make the nodes visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/controls.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm:2
msgid "Controls error estimation calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ERNORM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ERNORM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm:10
msgid ""
"Error estimation calculations are performed by default unless PowerGraphics "
"is enabled ( :ref:`graphics`,POWER)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm:18
msgid ""
"``ON`` - Perform error estimation (default). This option is not valid for "
"PowerGraphics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm:20
msgid "``OFF`` - Do not perform error estimation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.ernorm:36
msgid ""
"Especially for thermal analyses, program speed increases if error estimation"
" is suppressed. Therefore, it might be desirable to use error estimation "
"only when needed. The value of the :ref:`ernorm` key is not saved on "
":file:`file.db`. Consequently, you need to reissue the :ref:`ernorm` key "
"after a :ref:`resume` if you wish to deactivate error estimation again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.controls.Controls.force"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/controls.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:2
msgid "Selects the element nodal force type for output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `FORCE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_FORCE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:9
msgid "Type of force to be associated with the force items:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:11
msgid "``TOTAL`` - Total forces (static, damping, and inertia)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:13
msgid "``STATIC`` - Static forces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:15
msgid "``DAMP`` - Damping forces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:17
msgid "``INERT`` - Inertia forces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:33
msgid ""
":ref:`force` selects the element nodal force type for output with the POST1 "
":ref:`presol`, :ref:`plesol`, :ref:`prrfor`, :ref:`nforce`, :ref:`fsum`, "
"etc. commands, the POST26 :ref:`esol` command, and reaction force plotting ("
" :ref:`pbc` ). For example, :ref:`force`,STATIC causes item F of the "
":ref:`presol` command to be the static forces for the elements processed. "
"Element member forces (such as those available for beams and shells and "
"processed by Item and Sequence number) are not affected by this command. The"
" SMISC records extract the static force."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:40
msgid ""
"In a non-spectrum analysis that includes either contact or pretension "
"elements in the model, the :ref:`prrsol` command is valid with the "
":ref:`force` command. Otherwise, the :ref:`prrsol` command is not valid with"
" :ref:`force`. Use the :ref:`prrfor` command, which provides the same "
"functionality as :ref:`prrsol`, instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:45
msgid ""
"Use the :ref:`force` command prior to any load case operations ( "
":ref:`lcoper` ) to insure the correct element nodal force combinations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:48
msgid ""
"In POST26, the :ref:`esol` data stored is based on the active :ref:`force` "
"specification at the time the data is stored. To store data at various "
"specifications (for example, static and inertia forces), issue a "
":ref:`store` command before each new specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:52
msgid ""
"The :ref:`force` command cannot be used to extract static, damping, and "
"inertial forces for ``MPC184`` joint elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:55
msgid ""
"To retrieve the different force types, use the :ref:`get` command with "
"``Entity`` =ELEM and ``Item1`` =EFOR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:58
msgid ""
"The :ref:`force` command is not supported in a spectrum analysis. You can "
"specify the force type directly on the combination method commands ( "
"``ForceType`` on the :ref:`psdcom`, :ref:`srss`, :ref:`cqc`, etc. commands)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.force:62
msgid "The :ref:`force` command is not supported in a modal analysis."
msgstr ""

