msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:32
msgid ""
"Applies to stress and strain data for layered elements ``SHELL181``, "
"``SHELL281``, ``ELBOW290``, ``SOLID185``, ``SOLID186``, ``SOLSH190``, "
"``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, ``REINF264``, and ``REINF265`` ; heat flux and "
"heat gradient for ``SHELL131`` and ``SHELL132``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:36
msgid ""
"For `reinforcing "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/str_compreinfdirectemb.html>`_"
" elements, ``N`` is a given reinforcing member (individual reinforcing). "
"Specifying ``N`` = 0 (default) or ``N`` = 1 selects the first reinforcing "
"member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:41
msgid ""
"The :ref:`shell` command can then be used (with shell elements) to specify a"
" location (TOP, MID, BOT) within the layer for output. (The :ref:`shell` "
"command does not apply to thermal shell elements ``SHELL131`` and "
"``SHELL132``.) Transverse shear stresses for MID are linearly averaged from "
"TOP and BOT, and do not reflect a parabolic distribution. Setting KEYOPT(8) "
"= 2 for ``SHELL181``, ``SHELL281``, ``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, and "
"``ELBOW290`` writes the mid-surface values directly to the results file and "
"yields more accurate values than linear averaging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:48
msgid ""
"Because energy is a per-element quantity, you cannot use this command for "
"energy output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:50
msgid ""
"When using the :ref:`layer` command with ``SHELL181``, ``SOLID185``, "
"``SOLID186``, ``SOLSH190``, ``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, ``SHELL281``, and "
"``ELBOW290``, KEYOPT(8) must be set to 1 (or 2 for ``SHELL181``, "
"``SHELL281``, ``ELBOW290``, ``SHELL208``, and ``SHELL209`` ) in order to "
"store results for all layers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:55
msgid ""
"When ``NUM`` = FCMAX, you must provide the failure criterion input. If "
"specifying input via the :ref:`fc` command, all structural elements are "
"processed. For more information, see the documentation for the :ref:`fc` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.layer:59
msgid ""
"Use this command with :ref:`rsys`,LSYS to display results in the layer "
"coordinate system for a particular layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/controls.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:2
msgid ""
"Activates a coordinate system for printout or display of element and nodal "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RSYS "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RSYS.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:9
msgid "The coordinate system to use for results output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:11
msgid ""
"``0`` - Global Cartesian coordinate system (default, except for spectrum "
"analyses)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:13
msgid "``1`` - Global cylindrical coordinate system in Z."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:15
msgid "``2`` - Global spherical coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:17
msgid "``5`` - Global cylindrical coordinate system in Y."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:19
msgid "``6`` - Global cylindrical coordinate system in X."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:21
msgid "``> 10`` - Any existing local coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:23
msgid "``SOLU`` - Solution coordinate systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:25
msgid "``LSYS`` - Layer coordinate system (default for spectrum analysis)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:41
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rsys` command activates a coordinate system for printing or "
"displaying element results data such as stresses and heat fluxes, and nodal "
"results data such as degrees of freedom and reactions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:45
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL rotates the results data to the specified coordinate system "
"during printout, display, or element table operations (such as "
":ref:`prnsol`, :ref:`presol`, :ref:`plnsol`, and :ref:`etable` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:49
msgid ""
"You can define coordinate systems with various Mechanical APDL commands such"
" as :ref:`local`, :ref:`cs`, :ref:`clocal`, and :ref:`cskp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:53
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rsys` command has no effect on beam or pipe stresses, which "
"Mechanical APDL displays (via :ref:`eshape`,1 and PowerGraphics) in the "
"element coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:56
msgid ""
"Element results such as stresses and heat fluxes are in the element "
"coordinate systems when ``KCN`` = SOLU. Nodal requests for element results "
"(for example, :ref:`prnsol`,S,COMP) average the element values at the common"
" node; that is, the orientation of the node is not a factor in the output of"
" element quantities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:61
msgid ""
"For nearly all solid elements, the default element coordinate systems are "
"parallel to the global Cartesian coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:64
msgid ""
"For shell elements and the remaining solid elements, the default element "
"coordinate system can differ from element to element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:67
msgid ""
"For layered shell and layered solid elements, Mechanical APDL initially "
"selects the element coordinate system when ``KCN`` = SOLU. You can then "
"select the layer coordinate system via the :ref:`layer` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:72
msgid ""
"Nodal results such as degrees of freedom and reactions can be properly "
"rotated only if the resulting component set is consistent with the degree-"
"of-freedom set at the node. The degree-of-freedom set at a node is "
"determined by the elements attached to the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:76
msgid ""
"Example: If a node does not have a UZ degree of freedom during solution, any"
" Z component resulting from a rotation does not print or display in POST1. "
"Results at nodes with a single degree-of-freedom (UY only, for example) "
"should therefore not be rotated; that is, they should be viewed only in the "
"nodal coordinate system or a system parallel to the nodal system. (The "
"default global Cartesian system cannot be parallel to the nodal system.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:82
msgid ""
"Results at nodes with a 2D degree-of-freedom set (UX and UY, for example) "
"should not be rotated out of the 2D plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:85
msgid ""
"When ``KCN`` > 10, and the specified system is subsequently redefined, "
"reissue the :ref:`rsys` command for results to be rotated into the redefined"
" system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:88
msgid ""
"For element quantities, solution coordinate systems are the element "
"coordinate system for each element. For nodal quantities, they are the nodal"
" coordinate systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:91
msgid ""
"If an element or nodal coordinate system is not defined, Mechanical APDL "
"uses the global Cartesian coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:94
msgid ""
"If you issue a :ref:`layer`, ``N`` command (where ``N`` refers to a layer "
"number), the results appear in the layer coordinate system. (SOLU is the "
"default for spectrum analyses.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:97
msgid ""
"The default coordinate system for certain elements, notably shells, is not "
"global Cartesian and is frequently not aligned at adjacent elements. Avoid "
"setting ``KCN`` = SOLU with such elements, as it can make nodal averaging of"
" component element results (such as SX, SY, SZ, SXY, SYZ, and SXZ) invalid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:102
msgid ""
"When post-processing expanded nodal results in a cyclic symmetry analysis ( "
":ref:`cycexpand` ), use of :ref:`rsys`,SOLU is recommended so that the "
"appropriate cyclic nodal coordinate system is used (see :ref:`cyclic` "
"command). For any other coordinate system (for example, :ref:`rsys`,1), "
"cyclic rotation is not carried out, and nodal results at all sectors are "
"expressed in the specified coordinate system ( ``KCN`` ). See `Result "
"Coordinate System "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycpost.html#advcycrescosys>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:109
msgid ""
"For layered shell and solid elements, the results appear in their respective"
" layer coordinate systems. For a specific layer of interest, issue a "
":ref:`layer`, ``N`` command (where ``N`` refers to a layer number)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:113
msgid ""
"If a model has both nonlayered and layered elements, you can use "
":ref:`rsys`,SOLU and :ref:`rsys` ,LSYS simultaneously (with :ref:`rsys`,SOLU"
" applicable to nonlayered elements and :ref:`rsys`,LSYS applicable to "
"layered elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:117
msgid "To reverse effects of the LSYS option, issue an :ref:`rsys`,0 command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:119
msgid "LSYS is the default for spectrum analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:121
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL plots :ref:`plvect` vector arrow displays (such temperature,"
" velocity, and force) in the global Cartesian coordinate system ( "
":ref:`rsys` = 0). Subsequent operations revert to your original coordinate "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:126
msgid ""
"When using solution coordinate systems for results output ( "
":ref:`rsys`,SOLU), the deformed or displaced shape in a POST1 contour "
"display can be unexpected (although the contours are displayed in the "
"expected colors). The program does not rotate displacement values (Ux,Uy,Uz)"
" to global; instead, the displacements (stored locally) are added directly "
"to the global coordinates (X,Y,Z). For example, if in PREP7 the nodes are "
"rotated 90 degrees about the z axis and the global Uy displacements are "
"relatively large, the Ux values will be large, causing the model to display "
"a large deformation in the global X direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:134
msgid ""
"If large deflection is active ( :ref:`nlgeom`,ON), Mechanical APDL rotates "
"the element component result directions by the amount of rigid body "
"rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:138
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL displays the element component results in the initial global"
" coordinate system for the following elements: ``SHELL181``, ``SHELL281``, "
"``ELBOW290``, ``PLANE182``, ``PLANE183``, ``SOLID185``, ``SOLID186``, "
"``SOLID187``, ``SOLID272``, ``SOLID273``, ``SOLID285``, ``SOLSH190``, "
"``SHELL208``, and ``SHELL209``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:144
msgid ""
"All other element result transformations, therefore, are also relative to "
"the initial global system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:146
msgid "Nodal degree-of-freedom results are based on the initial geometry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.rsys:148
msgid ""
"For all other element types, component results displayed in the co-rotated "
"coordinate system include the element rigid body rotation from the initial "
"global coordinate system, and all other element result transformations are "
"relative to the rotated global system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/controls.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:2
msgid "Selects a shell element or shell layer location for results output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SHELL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SHELL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:9
msgid "Location within shell element (or layer) to obtain stress results:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:11
msgid "``TOP`` - Top of shell element (or layer) (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:13
msgid ""
"``MID`` - Middle of shell element (or layer). The default method averages "
"the TOP and BOT values to obtain a mid value. Setting KEYOPT(8) = 2 for "
"``SHELL181``, ``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, ``SHELL281``, and ``ELBOW290`` "
"uses MID results obtained directly from the results file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:17
msgid "``BOT`` - Bottom of shell element (or layer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:33
msgid ""
"Selects the location within a shell element (or a shell layer) for results "
"output (nodal stresses, strains, etc.). Applies to POST1 selects, sorts, and"
" output ( :ref:`nsel`, :ref:`nsort`, :ref:`prnsol`, :ref:`plnsol`, "
":ref:`prpath`, :ref:`plpath`, etc.), and is used for storage with the POST26"
" :ref:`esol` command. For example, :ref:`shell`,TOP causes item S of the "
"POST1 :ref:`prnsol` command or the POST26 :ref:`esol` command to be the "
"stresses at the top of the shell elements. For layered shell elements, use "
"the :ref:`layer` (POST1) or :ref:`layerp26` (POST26) command to select the "
"layer. The :ref:`shell` command does not apply to the layered thermal shell "
"elements, ``SHELL131`` and ``SHELL132``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:42
msgid ""
"For PowerGraphics ( :ref:`graphics`,POWER), the :ref:`shell`,MID command "
"affects both the printed output and the displayed results, while the "
":ref:`shell` (TOP or BOT) command prints and displays both the top and "
"bottom layers simultaneously. Note that :ref:`cycexpand`,ON automatically "
"turns on PowerGraphics; however, for cyclic mode-superposition harmonic "
"postprocessing ( :ref:`cycfiles` ), the :ref:`shell` command prints and "
"displays only the requested layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/controls.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.controls.Controls.shell:48
msgid ""
"In POST26, the :ref:`esol` data stored is based on the active :ref:`shell` "
"specification at the time the data is stored. To store data at various "
"specifications (for example, stresses at the top and bottom locations), "
"issue a :ref:`store` command before each new specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.element_table.ElementTable.esort.rst:2
