#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.load_case_calculations.LoadCaseCalculations.rappnd:2
msgid "Appends results data from the database to the results file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/load_case_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.load_case_calculations.LoadCaseCalculations.rappnd:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RAPPND "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RAPPND.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/load_case_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.load_case_calculations.LoadCaseCalculations.rappnd:9
msgid ""
"Load step number to be assigned to the results data set. If it is the same "
"as an existing load step number on the results file, the appended load step "
"will be inaccessible. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/load_case_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.load_case_calculations.LoadCaseCalculations.rappnd:13
msgid ""
"Time value to be assigned to the results data set. Defaults to 0.0. A time "
"value greater than the last load step should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/load_case_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.load_case_calculations.LoadCaseCalculations.rappnd:30
msgid ""
"This command is typically used to append the results from a load case "
"combination to the results file. See the :ref:`lcwrite` command to create a "
"separate load case file. Only summable and constant data are written to the "
"results file by default; non-summable data are not written unless requested "
"( :ref:`lcsum` command). ``RAPPND`` should not be used to append results "
"from a harmonic analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.curr2d.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.curr2d"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.curr2d:2
msgid "Calculates current flow in a 2D conductor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.curr2d:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `CURR2D "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CURR2D.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.curr2d:21
msgid ""
":ref:`curr2d` invokes a macro which calculates the total current flowing in "
"a conducting body for a 2D planar or axisymmetric magnetic field analysis. "
"The currents may be applied source currents or induced currents (eddy "
"currents). The elements of the conducting region must be selected before "
"this command is issued. The total current calculated by the macro is stored "
"in the parameter TCURR. Also, the total current and total current density "
"are stored on a per-element basis in the element table ( :ref:`etable` ) "
"with the labels TCURR and JT, respectively. Use the :ref:`pletab` and "
":ref:`pretab` commands to plot and list the element table items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr:2
msgid ""
"Calculates the relative error in an electrostatic or electromagnetic field "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EMAGERR "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EMAGERR.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr:21
msgid ""
"The relative error is an approximation of the mesh discretization error "
"associated with a solution. It is based on the discrepancy between the "
"unaveraged, element-nodal field values and the averaged, nodal field values."
" The calculation is valid within a material boundary and does not consider "
"the error in continuity of fields across dissimilar materials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr:26
msgid ""
"For electrostatics, the field values evaluated are the electric field "
"strength (EFSUM) and the electric flux density (DSUM). A relative error norm"
" of each is calculated on a per-element basis and stored in the element "
"table ( :ref:`etable` ) with the labels EF_ERR and D_ERR. Normalized error "
"values EFN_ERR and DN_ERR are also calculated and stored in the element "
"table. Corresponding quantities for electromagnetics are H_ERR, B_ERR, "
"HN_ERR, and BN_ERR, which are calculated from the magnetic field intensity "
"(HSUM) and the magnetic flux density (BSUM). The normalized error value is "
"the relative error norm value divided by the peak element-nodal field value "
"for the currently selected elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emagerr:35
msgid ""
"Use the :ref:`pletab` and :ref:`pretab` commands to plot and list the error "
"norms and normalized error values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf:2
msgid ""
"Calculates the electromotive force (emf), or voltage drop along a predefined"
" path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EMF "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EMF.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf:21
msgid ""
":ref:`emf` invokes a Mechanical APDL macro which calculates the "
"electromotive force (emf), or voltage drop along a predefined path "
"(specified with the :ref:`path` command). It is valid for both 2D and 3D "
"electric field analysis. The calculated emf value is stored in the parameter"
" EMF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf:26
msgid ""
"You must define a line path (via the :ref:`path` command) before issuing the"
" :ref:`emf` command macro. The macro uses calculated values of the electric "
"field (EF), and uses path operations for the calculations. All path items "
"are cleared when the macro finishes executing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emf:30
msgid ""
"The :ref:`emf` macro sets the \"ACCURATE\" mapping method and \"MAT\" "
"discontinuity option on the :ref:`pmap` command. The program retains these "
"settings after executing the macro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft:2
msgid "Summarizes electromagnetic forces and torques."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EMFT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EMFT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft:19
msgid ""
"Use this command to summarize electromagnetic force and torque in both "
"static electric and magnetic problems. To use this command, select the nodes"
" in the region of interest and make sure that all elements are selected. If "
":ref:`rsys` = 0, the force is reported in the global Cartesian coordinate "
"system. If :ref:`rsys` ≠ 0, force is reported in the specified coordinate "
"system. However, for torque, if :ref:`rsys` ≠ 0, this command will account "
"for the shift and rotation as specified by :ref:`rsys`, but will report only"
" the Cartesian components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft:26
msgid ""
"Forces are stored as items _FXSUM, _FYSUM, _FZSUM, and _FSSUM. Torque is "
"stored as items _TXSUM, _TYSUM, _TZSUM, and _TSSUM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.emft:29
msgid ""
"This command is valid only with ``PLANE121``, ``SOLID122``, ``SOLID123``, "
"``PLANE222``, ``PLANE223``, ``SOLID225``, ``SOLID226``, ``SOLID227``, "
"``PLANE233``, ``SOLID236`` and ``SOLID237`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:2
msgid "Calculates the flux passing through a closed contour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `FLUXV "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_FLUXV.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:21
msgid ""
":ref:`fluxv` invokes a Mechanical APDL macro which calculates the flux "
"passing through a closed contour (path) predefined by :ref:`path`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:25
msgid "The calculated flux is stored in the parameter FLUX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:27
msgid ""
"In a 2D analysis, at least two nodes must be defined on the path. In 3D, a "
"path of nodes describing a closed contour must be specified (that is, the "
"first and last node in the path specification must be the same)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:31
msgid ""
"A counterclockwise ordering of nodes on the :ref:`ppath` command gives the "
"correct sign on flux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:33
msgid ""
"Path operations are used for the calculations, and all path items are "
"cleared upon completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.fluxv:35
msgid "This macro is available for vector potential formulations only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.mmf.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.mmf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.mmf:2
msgid "Calculates the magnetomotive force along a path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.mmf:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MMF "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MMF.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.mmf:21
msgid ""
":ref:`mmf` invokes a Mechanical APDL macro which calculates the "
"magnetomotive force (mmf) along a predefined path ( :ref:`path` ). It is "
"valid for both 2D and 3D magnetic field analyses. The calculated mmf value "
"is stored in the parameter MMF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.mmf:25
msgid ""
"A closed path ( :ref:`path` ), passing through the magnetic circuit for "
"which mmf is to be calculated, must be defined before this command is "
"issued. A counterclockwise ordering of points on the :ref:`ppath` command "
"will yield the correct sign on the mmf. The mmf is based on Ampere's Law. "
"The macro makes use of calculated values of field intensity (H), and uses "
"path operations for the calculations. All path items are cleared upon "
"completion. The :ref:`mmf` macro sets the \"ACCURATE\" mapping method and "
"\"MAT\" discontinuity option of the :ref:`pmap` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.magnetics\\_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.rst:27:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:2
msgid "Generates a contour line plot of equipotentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `PLF2D "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PLF2D.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:9
msgid ""
"Number of contour lines to display. Issue in multiples of 9 (that is, 9, 18,"
" 27, etc.). Default is 27 contour lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:12
msgid "**olay** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:13
msgid "Overlay:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:15
msgid "``0`` - Overlay edge outlines by material number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:17
msgid "``1`` - Overlay edge outlines by real constant number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:19
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/areas.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.areas.Areas.anorm:8
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/areas.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.areas.Areas.areverse:8
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.aesize:8
msgid "**anum** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:20
msgid ""
"Highest material or real constant attribute number. Command will cycle "
"through ``ANUM`` element display overlays. Defaults to 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:23
msgid "**win** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:24
msgid "Window number to which command applies. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:40
msgid ""
":ref:`plf2d` invokes a Mechanical APDL macro which plots equipotentials of "
"the degree of freedom AZ. The equipotential lines are parallel to flux lines"
" and thus give a good representation of flux patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:44
msgid ""
"In the axisymmetric case, the display is actually r * AZ where r is the node"
" radius."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/magnetics_calculations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.magnetics_calculations.MagneticsCalculations.plf2d:46
