#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:27
msgid ""
"When a structure is rotating and the Coriolis or gyroscopic effect is taken "
"into account ( :ref:`coriolis` ), nodes lying on the rotation axis generally"
" exhibit an elliptical orbital motion. The :ref:`prorb` command prints out "
"the `orbit "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_rot/Hlp_G_ROTTERMINOLOGY.html#rotgloss1>`_"
" characteristics A, B, PSI, PHI, YMAX, ZMAX, and Whirl of each rotating "
"node, where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:33
msgid "A is the semi-major axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:34
msgid "B is the semi-minor axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:35
msgid "PSI is the angle between local y axis and major axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:36
msgid "PHI is the angle between initial position (t = 0) and major axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:37
msgid "YMAX is the maximum displacement along local y axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:38
msgid "ZMAX is the maximum displacement along local z axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:39
msgid ""
"Whirl is the direction of an orbital motion (BW for backward whirl and FW "
"for forward whirl)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:41
msgid ""
"Angles PSI and PHI are in degrees and within the range of -180 through +180."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:43
msgid ""
"To display the characteristics of the orbital path traversed by each node, "
"issue the :ref:`plorb` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:46
msgid ""
"The :ref:`prorb` command is valid for line elements (such as ``BEAM188``, "
"``BEAM189``, ``PIPE288``, and ``PIPE289`` ). :ref:`prorb` is not supported "
"for beam elements with the warping degree of freedom activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:53
msgid ""
"Because orbit data is written in the database, a :ref:`set` command must be "
"issued after the :ref:`prorb` command to ensure proper output for subsequent"
" postprocessing commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/results.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.results.Results.prorb:56
msgid ""
"The coordinate system for displaying nodal results must be global Cartesian "
"( :ref:`rsys`, ``KCN`` = 0). :ref:`prorb` is not supported if nodes are "
"rotated in a cylindrical coordinate system."
msgstr ""

