#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:119
msgid ""
"Key to sort the harmonic index results. This option applies to `cyclic "
"symmetry "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/cycsym_example.html>`_"
" buckling and modal analyses only, and is valid only when ``Lstep`` = FIRST,"
" LAST, NEXT, PREVIOUS, NEAR or LIST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:96
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:121
msgid ""
"``ORDER`` - Sort the harmonic index results in ascending order of "
"eigenfrequencies or buckling load multipliers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:99
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:124
msgid "``(blank)`` - No sorting takes place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:115
msgid ""
":ref:`rescombine` is a Mechanical APDL command macro enabling you to combine"
" results from a distributed- memory parallel ( DMP ) solution. A character "
"string input for any argument must be enclosed in single quotes (for "
"example, 'FIRST' input for ``Lstep`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:120
msgid ""
"In a distributed memory parallel solution, a global results file is saved by"
" default. However, if you issued :ref:`dmpoption`,RST,NO in the parallel "
"solution, no global results file is written and all local results files will"
" be kept. In this case, you can use :ref:`rescombine` in the general "
"postprocessor ( :ref:`post1` ) to read results into the database for "
"postprocessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:125
msgid ""
":ref:`rescombine` cannot be used to combine results from local files "
"generated during a distributed- memory parallel solution that used the "
"frequency or cyclic harmonic index domain decomposition method ( "
":ref:`ddoption`,FREQ or :ref:`ddoption`,CYCHI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:129
msgid ""
"To use :ref:`rescombine`, all local results files from the distributed-"
"memory parallel solution must be in the current working directory. If "
"running on a single machine, the local results files are saved in the "
"working directory by default. If running on a cluster, the local results "
"files are kept in the working directory on each compute node. For the latter"
" case, copy the local results files to the working directory on the primary "
"compute node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:135
msgid ""
"Similar to :ref:`set`, :ref:`rescombine` defines the data set to be read "
"from the results files into the database. Various operations can also be "
"performed during the read operation. (See :ref:`set` for more information.) "
"The database must have the model data available (or issue :ref:`resume` "
"before :ref:`rescombine` to restore the geometry from :file:`Jobname.DB` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:140
msgid ""
"After issuing :ref:`rescombine` to combine a set of data into the database, "
"you can issue :ref:`reswrite` to write the data set into a new results file."
" The new results file will essentially contain the current set of results "
"data for the entire (that is, global) model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:144
msgid ""
"Upon completion of a :ref:`rescombine` operation, the current file for "
"postprocessing ( :ref:`file` ) is set to the last local results file "
"specified via :ref:`rescombine`. For example, if reading in four local "
"results files, the results file for POST1 is specified as "
":file:`Jobname3.RST` when :ref:`rescombine` is complete. Therefore, be aware"
" that some downstream postprocessing actions (such as :ref:`set` ) may be "
"operating on only this one local results file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:150
msgid ""
":ref:`rescombine` is intended for use in POST1. If you want to postprocess "
"DMP solution results using the POST26 time-history postprocessor, combine "
"your local results files into one global results file ( "
":ref:`dmpoption`,RST,YES)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:154
msgid ""
"The load case commands in the general postprocessor (such as :ref:`lcdef`, "
":ref:`lcfile`, :ref:`lcoper`, etc.) are not supported when using "
":ref:`rescombine`. Those commands set up pointers in the results file used "
"for postprocessing; they cannot be used with the local results files used by"
" :ref:`rescombine`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.rescombine:159
msgid ""
":ref:`cycexpand`, which performs a cyclic expansion, cannot be used with "
":ref:`rescombine`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.reset.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.set\\_up.SetUp.reset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/set_up.rst:28:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.reset:2
msgid "Resets all POST1 or POST26 specifications to initial defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.reset:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RESET "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RESET.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.reset:21
msgid ""
"Has the same effect as entering the processor the first time within the run."
" In POST1, resets all specifications to initial defaults, erases all element"
" table items, path table data, and load case pointers. In POST26, resets all"
" specifications to initial defaults, erases all variables defined, and "
"zeroes the data storage space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.set\\_up.SetUp.set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/set_up.rst:28:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:2
msgid "Defines the data set to be read from the results file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SET "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SET.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:8
msgid ""
"From version 0.64 you can use the methods ``to_list`` and ``to_array`` on "
"the object returning from ``mapdl.set(\"list\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:31
msgid ""
"``LIST`` - Scan the results file and list a summary of each load step. ( "
"``KIMG``, ``TIME``, ``ANGLE``, and ``NSET`` are ignored.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:35
msgid ""
"Substep number (within ``Lstep`` ). Defaults to the last substep of the load"
" step (except in a buckling or modal analysis). For a buckling ( "
":ref:`antype`,BUCKLE) or modal ( :ref:`antype` ,MODAL) analysis, ``Sbstep`` "
"corresponds to the mode number. Specify ``Sbstep`` = LAST to store the last "
"substep for the specified load step (that is, issue a :ref:`set`, "
"``Lstep``,LAST command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:41
msgid ""
"If ``Lstep`` = LIST, ``Sbstep`` = 0 or 1 lists the basic step information. "
"``Sbstep`` = 2 also lists the basic step information, but includes the load "
"step title, and labels imaginary data sets if they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:46
msgid ""
"Scale factor applied to data read from the file. If zero (or blank), a value"
" of 1.0 is used. A nonzero factor excludes non-summable items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:49
msgid ""
"Harmonic velocities or accelerations can be calculated from the displacement"
" results from a modal ( :ref:`antype`,MODAL) or harmonic ( "
":ref:`antype`,HARMIC) analysis. If ``Fact`` = VELO, the harmonic velocities "
"(v) are calculated from the displacements (d) at a particular frequency (f) "
"according to the relationship v = 2 πfd. Similarly, if ``Fact`` = ACEL, the "
"harmonic accelerations (a) are calculated as a = (2 πf) :sup:`2` d."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:55
msgid ""
"If ``Lstep`` = LIST in an analysis using rezoning, ``Fact`` across all "
"rezoning data sets is listed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:61
msgid "``0 or REAL`` - Store the real part of complex solution (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:65
msgid "``3 or AMPL`` - Store the amplitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:67
msgid ""
"``4 or PHAS`` - Store the phase angle. The angle value, expressed in "
"degrees, will be between -180° and +180°."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:71
msgid ""
"Time-point identifying the data set to be read. For a harmonic analyses, "
"time corresponds to the frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:74
msgid "For a buckling analysis, time corresponds to the load factor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:76
msgid ""
"Used only in the following cases: If ``Lstep`` = NEAR, read the data set "
"nearest to ``TIME``. If both ``Lstep`` and ``Sbstep`` are zero (or blank), "
"read data set at time = ``TIME``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:79
msgid ""
"Do not use ``TIME`` to identify the data set to be read if you used the arc-"
"length method ( :ref:`arclen` ) in your solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:82
msgid ""
"If ``TIME`` is between two solution time points in the results file, a "
"linear interpolation occurs between the two data sets (except in cases where"
" `rezoning "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/Hlp_G_ADVRZSMP.html>`_"
" or selected results output ( :ref:`osresult` ) is used)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:87
msgid ""
"Solution items not written to the results file ( :ref:`outres` ) for either "
"data set will result in a null item after data set interpolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:90
msgid ""
"If ``TIME`` is beyond the last time point on the file, the last time point "
"will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:92
msgid ""
"If ``TIME`` is between two solution time points and both ``Lstep`` and "
"``Sbstep`` are zero (or blank), no interpolation is performed for the "
":ref:`prcint` / :ref:`plcint` commands. (That is, for results generated by "
"the :ref:`cint` command, only the data set associated with the lower of the "
"solution time points is used.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:98
msgid ""
"For harmonic elements ( ``PLANE25``, ``PLANE75``, ``PLANE78``, ``PLANE83``, "
"and ``SHELL61`` ), ``ANGLE`` specifies the circumferential location (0.0 to "
"360°) used when reading from the results file. The harmonic factor (based on"
" the circumferential angle) is applied to the displacements and element "
"results, and to the applied constraints and loads which overwrites any "
"values existing in the database. If ``ANGLE`` = NONE, all harmonic factors "
"are set to 1 and postprocessing yields the solution output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:105
msgid ""
"When using ``ANGLE`` = NONE with ``MODE`` > 0, the combined stresses and "
"strains are not valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:107
msgid ""
"The default value of ``ANGLE`` is 0.0; however if the :ref:`set` command is "
"not used, the effective default is NONE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:110
msgid ""
"For full harmonic analyses with the amplitude option ( ``KIMG`` = 3 or "
"AMPL), ``ANGLE`` is the prescribed phase angle at which the amplitude is "
"computed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:114
msgid ""
"Data set number of the data set to be read. If a positive value for ``NSET``"
" is entered, ``Lstep``, ``Sbstep``, ``KIMG``, and ``TIME`` are ignored. "
"Available set numbers can be determined by :ref:`set`,LIST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:140
msgid ""
"Defines the data set to be read from the results file into the database. "
"Various operations may also be performed during the read operation. The "
"database must have the model geometry available (or use the :ref:`resume` "
"command before the :ref:`set` command to restore the geometry from "
":file:`Jobname.DB` ). Values for applied constraints ( :ref:`d` ) and loads "
"( :ref:`f` ) in the database will be replaced by their corresponding values "
"on the results file, if available. (See the description of the :ref:`outres`"
" command.) In a single load step analysis, these values are usually the "
"same, except for results from harmonic elements. (See the description of the"
" ``ANGLE`` value above.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:149
msgid ""
"In an interactive run, the sorted list ( ``ORDER`` option) is also available"
" for results-set reading via a GUI pick option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:152
msgid ""
"You can postprocess results without issuing a :ref:`set` command if the "
"solution results were saved to the database file ( :file:`Jobname.db` ). A "
"distributed-memory parallel simulation, however, can only postprocess using "
"the results file (for example, :file:`Jobname.rst` ) and cannot use the "
":file:`Jobname.db` file since no solution results are written to the "
"database. Therefore, you must issue a :ref:`set` command or a "
":ref:`rescombine` command before postprocessing in a distributed- memory "
"parallel run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:159
msgid "When postprocessing amplitudes or phases ( ``KIMG`` = AMPL or PHAS):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:161
msgid ""
"The only appropriate coordinate system is the solution coordinate system ( "
":ref:`rsys`,SOLU). For layered elements, a layer ( :ref:`layer` ) must also "
"be specified. When displaying the displacement amplitudes, use a contour "
"display ( :ref:`plnsol` command). Because a deformed shape display ( "
":ref:`pldisp` command) could lead to a non-physical shape, the displacement "
"scaling is off by default ( :ref:`slashdscale`,,OFF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:167
msgid ""
"The conversion is not valid for averaged results, derived results (such as "
"principal stress/strain, equivalent stress/strain, and USUM), or summed "
"results obtained using :ref:`fsum`, :ref:`nforce`, :ref:`prnld`, and "
":ref:`prrfor`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:171
msgid ""
"Cyclic symmetry and multistage cyclic symmetry analysis results are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:173
msgid ""
"Coupled-field analysis results are supported when ``KIMG`` = AMPL, but they "
"are not supported when ``KIMG`` = PHAS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:177
msgid "Issuing :ref:`expand` in a Cyclic Symmetry Modal Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:179
msgid ""
"After issuing :ref:`expand`, ``Nrepeat`` in a cyclic symmetry modal "
"analysis, subsequent :ref:`set` commands read data from the results file and"
" expand them to ``Nrepeat`` sectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:183
msgid "Issuing :ref:`msopt`,EXPAND in a Multistage Cyclic Symmetry Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.set:185
msgid ""
"When issuing :ref:`msopt`,EXPAND in a multistage cyclic symmetry analysis, "
"subsequent :ref:`set` commands read the data set from the specified results "
"file and expand the nodes and elements to the stages and sectors specified "
"via :ref:`msopt`,EXPAND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.set\\_up.SetUp.subset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/set_up.rst:28:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:2
msgid "Reads results for the selected portions of the model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SUBSET "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SUBSET.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:13
msgid ""
"``FIRST`` - Read the first data set ( ``SBSTEP`` and ``TIME`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:15
msgid ""
"``LAST`` - Read the last data set ( ``SBSTEP`` and ``TIME`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:17
msgid ""
"``NEXT`` - Read the next data set ( ``SBSTEP`` and ``TIME`` are ignored). If"
" at the last data set, the first data set will be read as the next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:20
msgid ""
"``NEAR`` - Read the data set nearest to ``TIME`` ( ``SBSTEP`` is ignored). "
"If ``TIME`` is blank, read the first data set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:23
msgid ""
"``LIST`` - Scan the results file and list a summary of each load step. ( "
"``FACT``, ``KIMG``, ``TIME`` and ``ANGLE`` are ignored.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:27
msgid ""
"Substep number (within ``Lstep`` ). For the buckling ( :ref:`antype`,BUCKLE)"
" analysis or the modal ( :ref:`antype`,MODAL) analysis, the substep "
"corresponds to the mode number. Defaults to last substep of load step "
"(except for :ref:`antype`,BUCKLE or MODAL). If ``Lstep`` = LIST, ``SBSTEP`` "
"= 0 or 1 lists the basic step information, whereas ``SBSTEP`` = 2 also lists"
" the load step title, and labels imaginary data sets if they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:34
msgid ""
"Scale factor applied to data read from the file. If zero (or blank), a value"
" of 1.0 is used. Harmonic velocities or accelerations may be calculated from"
" the displacement results from a modal ( :ref:`antype`,MODAL) or harmonic ( "
":ref:`antype`,HARMIC) analyses. If ``FACT`` = VELO, the harmonic velocities "
"(v) are calculated from the displacements (d) at a particular frequency (f) "
"according to the relationship v = 2 πfd. Similarly, if ``FACT`` = ACEL, the "
"harmonic accelerations (a) are calculated as a = (2 πf) :sup:`2` d."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:44
msgid "``0`` - Store real part of complex solution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:49
msgid ""
"Time-point identifying the data set to be read. For harmonic analyses, time "
"corresponds to the frequency. For the buckling analysis, time corresponds to"
" the load factor. Used only in the following cases: If ``Lstep`` is NEAR, "
"read the data set nearest to ``TIME``. If both ``Lstep`` and ``SBSTEP`` are "
"zero (or blank), read data set at time = ``TIME``. If ``TIME`` is between "
"two solution time points on the results file, a linear interpolation is done"
" between the two data sets. Solution items not written to the results file ("
" :ref:`outres` ) for either data set will result in a null item after data "
"set interpolation. If ``TIME`` is beyond the last time point on the file, "
"use the last time point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:68
msgid ""
"Data set number of the data set to be read. If a positive value for ``NSET``"
" is entered, ``Lstep``, ``SBSTEP``, ``KIMG``, and ``TIME`` are ignored. "
"Available set numbers can be determined by :ref:`set`,LIST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/set_up.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.set_up.SetUp.subset:86
msgid ""
"Reads a data set from the results file into the database for the selected "
"portions of the model only. Data that has not been specified for retrieval "
"from the results file by the :ref:`inres` command will be listed as having a"
" zero value. Each time that the :ref:`subset` command is issued, the data "
"currently in the database will be overwritten with a new set of data. "
"Various operations may also be performed during the read operation. The "
"database must have the model geometry available (or used the :ref:`resume` "
"command before the :ref:`subset` command to restore the geometry from "
":file:`File.DB` )."
msgstr ""

