#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:89
msgid ""
"When you `expand the results of a modal cyclic symmetry analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycpost.html#ans_cycsym_res_coord_sys>`_"
" (via the :ref:`cycexpand` or :ref:`expand` command), the program combines "
"the real and imaginary results for a given nodal diameter, assuming no phase"
" shift between them; however, the modal response can occur at any phase "
"shift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:95
msgid ""
":ref:`cycphase` response results are valid only for the first cyclic sector."
" To obtain the response at any part of the expanded model, Ansys, Inc. "
"recommends using `cyclic symmetry results expansion "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycpost.html#ans_cycsym_res_coord_sys>`_"
" at the phase angle obtained via :ref:`cycphase`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:101
msgid ""
"The phase angles returned by :ref:`cycphase` contain the minimum and maximum"
" values for USUM, SEQV and other scalar principal stress and strain "
"quantities; however, they do not always return the true minimum and maximum "
"values for directional quantities like UX or SX unless the values fall in "
"the first sector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:106
msgid ""
":ref:`cycphase` does not consider midside node values when evaluating "
"maximum and minimum values, which may affect display quantities but no "
"others. (Typically, the program ignores midside node stresses and strains "
"during postprocessing.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:110
msgid ""
"Issuing :ref:`cycphase`,PUT clears the result values for midside nodes on "
"high order elements; therefore, this option sets element faceting ( "
":ref:`efacet` ) to 1. The command reports that midside nodal values are set "
"to zero and indicates that element faceting is set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:114
msgid ""
"If the sweep values are available after issuing a :ref:`cycphase`,PUT "
"command, the :ref:`prnsol` or :ref:`plnsol` command will print or plot "
"(respectively) the sweep values of structure displacement Ux, Uy, Uz, "
"component stress/strain X, Y, Z, XY, YZ, ZX, principal stress/strain 1, 2, 3"
" and equivalent stress/strain EQV. The vector sum of displacement (USUM) and"
" stress/strain intensity (SINT) are not valid phase-sweep results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:120
msgid ""
"You can specify any coordinate system via the :ref:`rsys` command for "
"displaying or printing :ref:`cycphase` results. However, after "
":ref:`cycphase` results have been extracted, you cannot then transform them "
"via the :ref:`rsys` command. If you try to do so, the program issues a "
"warning message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:125
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cycphase` command is valid in :ref:`post1` and for cyclically "
"symmetric models only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycphase:127
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycexpand:142
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycfreq:185
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:149
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:283
msgid ""
"To learn more about analyzing a cyclically symmetric structure, see the "
"`Cyclic Symmetry Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/cycsym_example.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/special_purpose.rst:57:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:2
msgid ""
"Defines the set of result items for a subsequent :ref:`cyccalc` command in "
"postprocessing a cyclic harmonic mode-superposition analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:5
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `CYCSPEC "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CYCSPEC.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:11
msgid ""
"No defaults are available for the :ref:`cycspec` command. You must issue "
"this command to define the set of result items for evaluation in a "
"subsequent :ref:`cyccalc` command used in computing results of a cyclic "
"harmonic mode-superposition analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:18
msgid "One of the following labels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:20
msgid ""
"``ADD`` - Adds a new specification to the set (default). The maximum number "
"of specifications that can be defined is 50."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:23
msgid ""
"``LIST`` - Lists the current set of specifications. ``Node``, ``Item``, "
"``Comp`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:25
msgid ""
"``ERASE`` - Erases the current set of specifications. ``Node``, ``Item``, "
"``Comp`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:27
msgid ""
"``DELETE`` - Deletes an existing specification. ``Item``, ``Comp`` are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:30
msgid ""
"The node at which to evaluate the results. If ``Node`` is a nodal component,"
" then all nodes in the component are included. All sectors containing this "
"node (or set of nodes) are evaluated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:33
msgid ""
"For ``LABEL`` = DELETE, use ``Node`` to indicate which specification in the "
"set to delete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:36
msgid "Specifies the type of values to evaluate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:38
msgid "``U`` - Displacement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:40
msgid "``S`` - Stress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:42
msgid "``EPEL`` - Elastic strain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:45
msgid ""
"Specifies the specific component of displacement, stress, or strain to "
"evaluate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:47
msgid "``X,Y,Z`` - Direct components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:49
msgid "``XY,YZ,XZ`` - Shear components (stress and strain only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:51
msgid "``1,2,3`` - Principal values (stress and strain only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:53
msgid "``EQV`` - Equivalent value (stress and strain only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:55
msgid "``SUM`` - Vector sum (displacement only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:57
msgid "``NORM`` - L2 norm for the set of nodes (displacement only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:73
msgid ""
"Up to 50 specifications can be defined for use in a subsequent "
":ref:`cyccalc` command. If more than 50 specifications are desired, erase "
"the table after the :ref:`cyccalc` operation and add new specifications and "
"repeat the :ref:`cyccalc` command. All the specified nodes, items, and "
"components are evaluated for all sectors and the maximum amplitude value "
"output. For combined stresses and strains ( ``Comp`` = 1,2,3 or EQV) or "
"displacement vector sum ( ``Comp`` = SUM), a 360 degree phase sweep is "
"performed at each location to determine the maximum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:80
msgid ""
"Additional POST1 controls are used to refine the specification. For "
"component values, components are in the :ref:`rsys` direction. For shell "
"elements, the results are at the :ref:`shell` location. For EPEL,EQV, the "
"results are based on the ``EFFNU`` value on the :ref:`avprin` command. The "
"controls active when the :ref:`cyccalc` command is issued determine the "
"result values. If results at another :ref:`shell` location are desired, "
"issue the new :ref:`shell` command and then re-issue the :ref:`cyccalc` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:87
msgid ""
"If a single node is input, the ``Item`` / ``Comp`` value at that location in"
" each sector is output. If a node component is given, then the maximum "
"``Item`` / ``Comp`` value within the set of nodes of each sector is output, "
"one value for each sector (the node of the maximum may vary from sector to "
"sector). For stress and strain items, only corner nodes are valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycspec:92
msgid ""
"For the displacement norm option ( ``Item`` = U, ``Comp`` = NORM), the L2 "
"norm computed from all the nodes in the component is output, one per sector."
msgstr ""

