msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `FSUM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_FSUM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:9
msgid "Coordinate system in which to perform summation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:11
msgid ""
"``(blank)`` - Sum all nodal forces in global Cartesian coordinate system "
"(default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:13
msgid ""
"``RSYS`` - Sum all nodal forces in the currently active RSYS coordinate "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:18
msgid ""
"``(blank)`` - Sum all nodal forces for all selected nodes (default), "
"excluding contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:20
msgid "``CONT`` - Sum all nodal forces for contact nodes only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:22
msgid ""
"``BOTH`` - Sum all nodal forces for all selected nodes, including contact "
"elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:38
msgid ""
"Sums and prints, in each component direction for the total selected node "
"set, the nodal force and moment contributions of the selected elements "
"attached to the node set. Selecting a subset of nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ) and "
"then issuing this command will give the total force acting on that set of "
"nodes (default), excluding surface-to-surface, node-to-surface, line-to-"
"line, and line-to-surface contact elements ( ``TARGE169``, ``TARGE170``, "
"``CONTA172``, ``CONTA174``, ``CONTA175``, and ``CONTA177`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:44
msgid ""
"Setting ``ITEM`` = CONT sums the nodal forces and moment contributions of "
"the selected contact elements ( ``CONTA172``, ``CONTA174``, ``CONTA175``, "
"and ``CONTA177`` ). Setting ``ITEM`` = BOTH sums the nodal forces for all "
"selected nodes, including contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:48
msgid ""
"Nodal forces associated with surface loads are not included. The effects of "
"nodal coupling and constraint equations are ignored. Moment summations are "
"about the global origin unless another point is specified with the "
":ref:`spoint` command. This vector sum is printed in the global Cartesian "
"system unless it is transformed ( :ref:`rsys` ) and a point is specified "
"with the :ref:`spoint` command. By default, the sum is done in global "
"Cartesian, and the resulting vector is transformed to the requested system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:55
msgid ""
"The ``LAB`` = RSYS option transforms each of the nodal forces into the "
"active coordinate system before summing and printing. The :ref:`force` "
"command can be used to specify which component (static, damping, inertia, or"
" total) of the nodal load is to be used. This command output is included in "
"the :ref:`nforce` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:60
msgid ""
"The command should not be used with axisymmetric elements because it might "
"calculate a moment where none exists. Consider, for example, the axial load "
"on a pipe modeled with an axisymmetric shell element. The reaction force on "
"the end of the pipe is the total force (for the full 360 degrees) at that "
"location. The net moment about the centerline of the pipe would be zero, but"
" the program would incorrectly calculate a moment at the end of the element "
"as the force multiplied by the radius."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:66
msgid ""
"The command is not valid for elements that operate solely within the nodal "
"coordinate system with 1D option activated and rotated nodes ( :ref:`nrotat`"
" )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:69
msgid ""
"**Using FSUM with the NLGEOM Command** If you have activated large "
"deflection ( :ref:`nlgeom`, ON ), the :ref:`fsum` command generates the "
"following message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:73
msgid ""
"Summations based on final geometry and will not agree with solution "
"reactions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:75
msgid ""
"The message warns that the moment summations may not equal the real moment "
"reactions. When calculating moment summations, the :ref:`fsum` command "
"assumes that the summation of rotations applies; however, it does not apply "
"for large rotations, which require pseudovector representation to sum the "
"rotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:80
msgid ""
"In contrast, the results for force reactions will be correct because they "
"depend upon linear displacement vectors (which can be added)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.fsum:83
msgid ""
"**Using FSUM in a Spectrum or PSD Analysis ( ANTYPE, SPECTR)** When using "
":ref:`fsum` in a spectrum analysis (after the combination file has been "
"input through :ref:`input`,,MCOM and when :ref:`spopt` has not been issued "
"with ``Elcalc`` = YES during the spectrum analysis), or in a PSD analysis "
"when postprocessing 1-sigma results (loadstep 3, 4, or 5), the following "
"message will display in the printout header:"
msgstr ""

