#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:52
msgid ""
"This function contains specificities regarding the argument definitions. "
"Please refer to the `command documentation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MACOPT.html>`_"
" for further explanations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:58
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rstmac` command calculates the MAC or FRF criteria values based on"
" the options specified via :ref:`macopt`. The :ref:`macopt` command must be "
"issued before the :ref:`rstmac` command. These commands enable you to "
"compare nodal solutions from two results files ( :file:`.rst` or "
":file:`.rstp` ) or from one results file and one Universal Format file ( "
":file:`.unv` ). Multiple :ref:`macopt` commands can be issued to specify "
"which results are compared and how."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:64
msgid ""
"As listed in the table above, model solutions can be compared using three "
"different mehtods: matching nodes based on location, matching nodes based on"
" node number, or by node mapping and solution interpolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:68
msgid ""
"When node mapping and solution interpolation is performed ( ``Option`` = "
"NODMAP), the following applies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:71
msgid ""
"``File1`` on :ref:`rstmac` must correspond to a model meshed in solid and/or"
" shell elements. Other types of elements can be present, but the node "
"mapping is not performed for these elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:74
msgid ""
"You should only compare solutions of models having the same dimension (both "
"models are 2D or both models are 3D). Comparing models with different "
"dimensions may lead to incorrect results if the solution at mapped/matched "
"nodes is not representative of the global solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:78
msgid "Interpolation is performed on UX, UY, and UZ degrees of freedom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:80
msgid ""
"Node pair MAC computation ( ``Option`` = NMAC) is only supported when a "
"matching procedure is used and a specific substep number is requested for "
"each solution ( ``Sbstep1``, ``Sbstep2`` on :ref:`rstmac` command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:84
msgid ""
"Non-structural degrees of freedom in coupled-field analyses are supported "
"for the matching methods ( ``Option`` = ABSTOLN or NUMMATCH). Multiple "
":ref:`macopt`, DOF commands can be issued consecutively to combine different"
" degrees of freedom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:88
msgid ""
"The FRF option is not compatible with any MAC calculation options (DOF, NMAC"
" and KEYMASS) and can only be used with node matching procedures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.macopt:95
msgid ""
"For a detailed discussion on using :ref:`macopt` with examples, see "
"`Comparing Nodal Solutions From Two Models or From One Model and "
"Experimental Data (RSTMAC) "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS5_4.html#>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/special_purpose.rst:57:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:2
msgid "Sums the nodal forces and moments of elements attached to nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NFORCE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NFORCE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:9
msgid ""
"Specifies the selected set of nodes for summing forces and moments for "
"contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:11
msgid ""
"``(blank)`` - Sums the nodal forces of elements for all selected nodes and "
"excludes contact elements (elements 169-177)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:14
msgid "``CONT`` - Sums the nodal forces of elements for contact nodes only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:16
msgid ""
"``BOTH`` - Sums the nodal forces of elements for all selected nodes, "
"including contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:32
msgid ""
"Sums and prints, in each component direction for each selected node, the "
"nodal force and moment contributions of the selected elements attached to "
"the node. If all elements are selected, the sums are usually zero except "
"where constraints or loads are applied. The nodal forces and moments may be "
"displayed ( :ref:`pbc`,FORC and :ref:`pbc`,MOME). Use :ref:`presol` to print"
" nodal forces and moments on an element-by-element basis. You can use the "
":ref:`force` command to specify which component (static, damping, inertia, "
"or total) of the nodal load is to be used. Nodal forces associated with "
"surface loads are not included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:40
msgid ""
"This vector sum is printed in the global Cartesian system. Moment summations"
" are about the global origin unless another point is specified with the "
":ref:`spoint` command. The summations for each node are printed in the "
"global Cartesian system unless transformed ( :ref:`rsys` ). This command is "
"generally not applicable to axisymmetric models because moment information "
"from the NFORCE command is not correct for axisymmetric elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:46
msgid ""
"Selecting a subset of elements ( :ref:`esel` ) and then issuing this command"
" will give the forces and moments required to maintain equilibrium of that "
"set of elements. The effects of nodal coupling and constraint equations are "
"ignored. The option ``ITEM`` = CONT provides the forces and moments for the "
"contact elements ( ``CONTA172``, ``CONTA174``, ``CONTA175``, and "
"``CONTA177`` ). Setting ``ITEM`` = BOTH provides the forces and moments for "
"all selected nodes, including contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:52
msgid ""
"This command also includes the :ref:`fsum` command function which "
"vectorially sums and prints, in each component direction for the total "
"selected node set, the nodal force and moment contributions of the selected "
"elements attached to the selected node set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:56
msgid ""
"**Using NFORCE in a Spectrum or PSD Analysis ( ANTYPE, SPECTR)** When using "
":ref:`nforce` in a spectrum analysis (after the combination file has been "
"input through :ref:`input`,,MCOM and when :ref:`spopt` has not been issued "
"with ``Elcalc`` = YES during the spectrum analysis), or in a PSD analysis "
"when postprocessing 1-sigma results (loadstep 3, 4, or 5), the following "
"message will display in the printout header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nforce:68
msgid ""
"The spectrum analysis summation is available when the element results are "
"written to the mode file, :file:`Jobname.MODE` ( ``MSUPkey`` = Yes on the "
":ref:`mxpand` command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/post1/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nldpost.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.post1.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.nldpost"
msgstr ""

