msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:78
msgid ""
"One result file ( :file:`.rst` ) and one universal format file ( "
":file:`.unv` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:80
msgid ""
"Either the modal assurance criterion (MAC) or the frequency response "
"function (FRF) correlation method is used. (For more details see `POST1 - "
"Modal Assurance Criterion (MAC) "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_post16.html#eqff29ac61-1393"
" - 4410-9090-572b02773534>`_ `POST1 - Frequency response function "
"correlation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thryFRF120.html#eqcaaee52b-1bb5-4b48-a411-6a162a579399>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:86
msgid ""
"The meshes read from ``File1`` and ``File2`` may be different. The nodes of "
"``File1`` are matched with the nodes of ``File2`` based on either node "
"location (default) or node number. The solutions are compared for the "
"identified pair of matched nodes. The nodes can also be mapped and the "
"solutions interpolated from ``File1``. See the :ref:`macopt` command for all"
" options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:91
msgid "Units and coordinate systems must be the same for both models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:93
msgid ""
"Results may be real or complex; however, if results in ``File1`` have a "
"different type than results in ``File2``, only the real parts of the "
"solutions are taken into account in MAC calculations. The analysis type can "
"be arbitrary for MAC while only harmonic analysis is supported for FRF "
"criteria calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:98
msgid ""
"Non-structural degrees of freedom can be considered. Degrees of freedom can "
"vary between ``File1`` and ``File2``, but at least one common degree of "
"freedom must exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:101
msgid ""
"The solutions read on the results files are not all written to the database;"
" therefore, subsequent plotting or printing of solutions is not possible. A "
":ref:`set` command must be issued after the :ref:`rstmac` command to post-"
"process each solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:105
msgid ""
"The corresponding database file ( :file:`.db` ) for :file:`File1` on "
":ref:`rstmac` must be resumed before running the command in the following "
"cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:108
msgid "A component ( ``Cname`` ) is used on :ref:`rstmac`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:110
msgid "The nodes are mapped ( :ref:`macopt`,NODMAP,YES)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:112
msgid ""
"The nodes are matched using a relative tolerance ( :ref:`macopt`,RELTOLN)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post1/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post1.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.rstmac:114
msgid ""
":ref:`rstmac` comparison on cyclic symmetry analysis works only if the "
"number of sectors on ``File1`` and ``File2`` are the same, and the database "
"is saved after the solution is finished. Also, a comparison cannot be made "
"between cyclic symmetry results and the full 360 degree model results ( "
"``File1`` - cyclic solution, ``File2`` - full 360 degree model solution). "
"Comparing cyclic symmetry solutions written on a selected set of nodes ( "
":ref:`outres` ) is not supported."
msgstr ""

