msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:9
msgid ""
"Name of the first vector that contains the noisy data set (that is, "
"independent variable). You must create and fill this vector before issuing "
":ref:`smooth`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:12
msgid "**vect2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:13
msgid ""
"Name of the second vector that contains the dependent set of data. Must be "
"the same length as the first vector. You must create and fill this vector "
"before issuing :ref:`smooth`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:16
msgid "**datap** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:17
msgid ""
"Number of data points to be fitted, starting from the beginning of the "
"vector. If left blank, the entire vector will be fitted. The maximum number "
"of data points is 100,000 (or greater, depending on the memory of the "
"computer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:21
msgid "**fitpt** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:22
msgid ""
"Order of the fitting curve that will be used as a smooth representation of "
"the data. This number should be less than or equal to the number of the data"
" points. Default (blank) is one-half the number of data points. Maximum "
"number of smoothed data fitting order is the number of data points up to 50."
" Depending on this number, the smoothed curve will be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:27
msgid "``1`` - Curve is the absolute average of all of the data points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:29
msgid "``2`` - Curve is the least square average of all of the data points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:31
msgid ""
"``3 or more`` - Curve is a polynomial of the order (n-1), where n is the "
"number of data fitting order points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:34
msgid "**vect3** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:35
msgid ""
"Name of the vector that contains the smoothed data of the independent "
"variable. This vector should have a length equal to or greater than the "
"number of smoothed data points. In batch (command) mode, you must create "
"this vector before issuing the :ref:`smooth` command. In interactive mode, "
"the GUI automatically creates this vector (if it does not exist). If you do "
"not specify a vector name, the GUI will name the vector smth_ind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:41
msgid "**vect4** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:42
msgid ""
"Name of the vector that contains the smoothed data of the dependent "
"variable. This vector must be the same length as ``Vect3``. In batch "
"(command) mode, you must create this vector before issuing the :ref:`smooth`"
" command. In interactive mode, the GUI automatically creates this vector (if"
" it does not exist). If you do not specify a vector name, the GUI will name "
"the vector smth_dep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
