"convenience, as well as in their standard dialog boxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:78
msgid ""
"You must always create ``Vect1`` and ``Vect2`` (using :ref:`dim` ) and fill "
"these vectors before smoothing the data. If working interactively, the "
"program automatically creates ``Vect3`` and ``Vect4``. If working in batch "
"(command) mode, you must create ``Vect3`` and ``Vect4`` (using :ref:`dim` ) "
"before issuing :ref:`smooth`. ``Vect3`` and ``Vect4`` are then filled "
"automatically by the program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:84
msgid ""
"The program also creates an additional TABLE type array that contains the "
"smoothed array and the unsmoothed data to enable plotting later with "
":ref:`starvplot`. Column 1 in the table corresponds to ``Vect1``, column 2 "
"to ``Vect2``, and column 3 to ``Vect4``. The array is named ``Vect3`` "
"_SMOOTH, up to a limit of 32 characters. For example, if the array name is "
"X1, the table name is X1_SMOOTH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.smooth:90
msgid "This command is also valid in PREP7 and SOLUTION."
msgstr ""

