"Defaults to the label formed by concatenating VPUT with the reference number"
" ``IR``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/post26/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.post26.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.vput:44
msgid ""
"At least one variable should be defined ( :ref:`nsol`, :ref:`esol`, "
":ref:`rforce`, etc.) before using this command. The starting array element "
"number must be defined. For example, :ref:`vput`,A(1),2 moves array "
"parameter A to variable 2 starting at time 0.0. Looping continues from array"
" element A(1) with the index number incremented by one until the variable is"
" filled. Unfilled variable locations are assigned a zero value. The number "
"of loops may be controlled with the :ref:`vlen` command (except that loop "
"skipping (NINC) is not allowed). For multi-dimensioned array parameters, "
"only the first (row) subscript is incremented."
msgstr ""

