msgid ""
"An attribute (TYPE, MAT, REAL, or ESYS) listed as a zero is unassigned; one "
"listed as a positive value indicates that the attribute was assigned with "
"the :ref:`aatt` command (and will not be reset to zero if the mesh is "
"cleared); one listed as a negative value indicates that the attribute was "
"assigned using the attribute pointer ( :ref:`type`, :ref:`mat`, :ref:`real`,"
" or :ref:`esys` ) that was active during meshing (and will be reset to zero "
"if the mesh is cleared). A \"-1\" in the \"nodes\" column indicates that the"
" area has been meshed but there are no interior nodes. The area size is "
"listed only if an :ref:`asum` command has been performed on the area."
msgstr ""

