"active coordinate system. ( RR, R θ, RZ for cylindrical; RR, R θ, R Φ for "
"spherical). Note that the R θ and R Φ scale factors are interpreted as "
"angular offsets. For example, if CSYS = 1, ``RX, RY, RZ`` input of "
"(1.5,10,3) would scale the specified keypoints 1.5 times in the radial and 3"
" times in the Z direction, while adding an offset of 10 degrees to the "
"keypoints. Zero, blank, or negative scale factor values are assumed to be "
"1.0. Zero or blank angular offsets have no effect."
