msgid ""
"Generates new volumes by subtracting the regions common to both the volumes "
"and areas (the intersection) from the ``NV`` volumes. The intersection will "
"be an area(s). If ``SEPO`` is blank, the volume is divided at the area and "
"the resulting volumes will be connected, sharing a common area where they "
"touch. If ``SEPO`` is set to SEPO, the volume is divided into two "
"unconnected volumes with separate areas where they touch. See the `Modeling "
"and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_"
