#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:68
msgid ""
"Repeat the :ref:`ce` command to add additional terms to the same equation. "
"To change only the constant term, repeat the command with no node terms "
"specified. Only the constant term can be changed during solution, and only "
"with the :ref:`cecmod` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:72
msgid ""
"Linear constraint equations may be used to relate the degrees of freedom of "
"selected nodes in a more general manner than described for nodal coupling ( "
":ref:`cp` ). The constraint equation is of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:80
msgid ""
"where U(I) is the degree of freedom (displacement, temperature, etc.) of "
"term (I). The following example is a set of two constraint equations, each "
"containing three terms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:83
msgid "0.0 = 3.0* (1 UX) + 3.0* (4 UX) + (-2.0)* (4 ROTY)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:85
msgid "2.0 = 6.0* (2 UX) + 10.0* (4 UY) + 1.0* (3 UZ)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:87
msgid ""
"The first unique degree of freedom in the equation is eliminated in terms of"
" all other degrees of freedom in the equation. A unique degree of freedom is"
" one which is not specified in any other constraint equation, coupled node "
"set, specified displacement set, or master degree of freedom set. It is "
"recommended that the first term of the equation be the degree of freedom to "
"be eliminated. The first term of the equation cannot contain a master degree"
" of freedom, and no term can contain coupled degrees of freedom. The same "
"degree of freedom may be specified in more than one equation but care must "
"be taken to avoid over-specification (over-constraint)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:95
msgid ""
"The degrees of freedom specified in the equation (that is, UX, UY, ROTZ, "
"etc.) must also be included in the model (as determined from the element "
"types ( :ref:`et` )). Also, each node in the equation must be defined on an "
"element (any element type containing that degree of freedom will do)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:99
msgid ""
"For buckling and modal analyses, the constant term of the equation will not "
"be taken into account (that is, ``CONST`` is always zero)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ce:102
msgid ""
"Note that under certain circumstances a constraint equation generated by "
":ref:`ce` may be modified during the solution. See for more information."
msgstr ""

