#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:9
msgid ""
"Tolerance about selected elements, based on a fraction of the element "
"dimension (defaults to 0.25 (25%)). Nodes outside the element by more than "
"the tolerance are not accepted as being on the interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:19
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:24
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:29
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:39
msgid ""
"Degrees of freedom for which constraint equations are written. Defaults to "
"all applicable DOFs. ``DOF1`` accepts ALL as a valid label, in which case "
"the rest are ignored (all DOFs are applied)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:43
msgid "**movetol** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:44
msgid ""
"The allowed \"motion\" of a node (see Note below). This distance is in terms"
" of the element coordinates (-1.0 to 1.0). A typical value is 0.05. Defaults"
" to 0 (do not move). ``MoveTol`` must be less than or equal to ``TOLER``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:62
msgid ""
"This command can be used to \"tie\" together two regions with dissimilar "
"mesh patterns by generating constraint equations that connect the selected "
"nodes of one region to the selected elements of the other region. At the "
"interface between regions, nodes should be selected from the more dense mesh"
" region, A, and the elements selected from the less dense mesh region, B. "
"The degrees of freedom of region A nodes are interpolated with the "
"corresponding degrees of freedom of the nodes on the region B elements, "
"using the shape functions of the region B elements. Constraint equations are"
" then written that relate region A and B nodes at the interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:70
msgid ""
"The ``MoveTol`` field lets the nodes in the previously mentioned region A "
"change coordinates when slightly inside or outside the elements of region B."
" The change in coordinates causes the nodes of region A to assume the same "
"surface as the nodes associated with the elements of region B. The "
"constraint equations that relate the nodes at both regions of the interface "
"are then written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:75
msgid ""
"Solid elements with six degrees of freedom should only be interfaced with "
"other six degree-of- freedom elements. The region A nodes should be near the"
" region B elements. A location tolerance based on the smallest region B "
"element length may be input. Stresses across the interface are not "
"necessarily continuous. Nodes in the interface region should not have "
"specified constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:80
msgid ""
"Use the :ref:`cpintf` command to connect nodes by coupling instead of "
"constraint equations. Use the :ref:`eintf` command to connect nodes by line "
"elements. See also the :ref:`nsel` and :ref:`esel` commands for selecting "
"nodes and elements. See the `Mechanical APDL Theory Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_biblio.html>`_"
" for a description of 3D space used to determine if a node will be "
"considered by this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.ceintf:87
msgid ""
"As an alternative to the :ref:`ceintf` command, you can use contact elements"
" and the internal multipoint constraint (MPC) algorithm to tie together two "
"regions having dissimilar meshes. See `Solid-Solid and Shell-Shell "
"Assemblies "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/Hlp_ctec_solsol.html#>`_"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

