msgid "Degrees of freedom associated with equations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:21
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - All applicable degrees of freedom (default). If 3D, generate 6 "
"equations based on UX, UY, UZ, ROTX, ROTY, ROTZ; if 2D, generate 3 equations"
" based on UX, UY, ROTZ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:24
msgid ""
"``UXYZ`` - Translational degrees of freedom. If 3D, generate 3 equations "
"based on the dependent nodes' UX, UY, and UZ DOFs and the independent node's"
" UX, UY, UZ, ROTX, ROTY, and ROTZ DOFs. If 2D, generate 2 equations based on"
" the dependent nodes UX and UY DOFs and the independent nodes UX, UY, and "
"ROTZ DOFs. No equations are generated for the rotational coupling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:29
msgid ""
"``RXYZ`` - Rotational degrees of freedom. If 3D, generate 3 equations based "
"on ROTX, ROTY, ROTZ; if 2D, generate 1 equation based on ROTZ. No equations "
"are generated for the translational coupling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:32
msgid "``UX`` - Dependent translational UX degree of freedom only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:34
msgid "``UY`` - Dependent translational UY degree of freedom only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:36
msgid "``UZ`` - Dependent translational UZ degree of freedom only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:38
msgid "``ROTX`` - Dependent rotational ROTX degree of freedom only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:40
msgid "``ROTY`` - Dependent rotational ROTY degree of freedom only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:42
msgid "``ROTZ`` - Dependent rotational ROTZ degree of freedom only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:44
msgid "**ldof2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:45
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:49
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:53
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:57
msgid ""
"Additional degrees of freedom. Used only if more than one degree of freedom "
"are required and ``Ldof`` is not ALL, UXYZ, or RXYZ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:48
msgid "**ldof3** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:52
msgid "**ldof4** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:56
msgid "**ldof5** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:74
msgid ""
"Defines a rigid region (link, area or volume) by automatically generating "
"constraint equations to relate nodes in the region. Nodes in the rigid "
"region must be assigned a geometric location before this command is used. "
"Also, nodes must be connected to elements having the required degree of "
"freedom set (see ``Ldof`` above). Generated constraint equations are based "
"on small deflection theory. Generated constraint equations are numbered "
"beginning from the highest previously defined equation number ( ``NEQN`` ) "
"plus 1. Equations, once generated, may be listed ( :ref:`celist` ) or "
"modified ( :ref:`ce` ) as desired. Repeat the :ref:`cerig` command for "
"additional rigid region equations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:83
msgid ""
"This command generates the constraint equations needed for defining rigid "
"lines in 2D or 3D space. Multiple rigid lines relative to a common point are"
" used to define a rigid area or a rigid volume. In 2D space, with ``Ldof =``"
" ALL, three equations are generated for each pair of constrained nodes. "
"These equations define the three rigid body motions in global Cartesian "
"space, that is, two in-plane translations and one in-plane rotation. These "
"equations assume the X-Y plane to be the active plane with UX, UY, and ROTZ "
"degrees of freedom available at each node. Other types of equations can be "
"generated with the appropriate ``Ldof`` labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:91
msgid ""
"Six equations are generated for each pair of constrained nodes in 3D space "
"(with ``Ldof =`` ALL). These equations define the six rigid body motions in "
"global Cartesian space. These equations assume that UX, UY, UZ, ROTX, ROTY, "
"and ROTZ degrees of freedom are available at each node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:95
msgid ""
"The UXYZ label allows generating a partial set of rigid region equations. "
"This option is useful for transmitting the bending moment between elements "
"having different degrees of freedom at a node. With this option only two of "
"the three equations are generated for each pair of constrained nodes in 2D "
"space. In 3D space, only three of the six equations are generated. In each "
"case the rotational coupling equations are not generated. Similarly, the "
"RXYZ label allows generating a partial set of equations with the "
"translational coupling equations omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:102
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.rbe3:58
msgid ""
"Applying this command to a large number of dependent nodes may result in "
"constraint equations with a large number of coefficients. This may "
"significantly increase the peak memory required during the process of "
"element assembly. If real memory or virtual memory is not available, "
"consider reducing the number of dependent nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:107
msgid ""
"Note that under certain circumstances the constraint equations generated by "
":ref:`cerig` may be modified during the solution. See for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:110
msgid ""
":ref:`cerig` is restricted to small-deflection analysis (large-deflection is"
" not supported). As an alternative to the :ref:`cerig` command, you can "
"define a similar type of rigid region using contact elements and the "
"internal multipoint constraint (MPC) algorithm. See `Surface-Based "
"Constraints "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/Hlp_ctec_surfcon.html#strbeamso1703>`_"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/constraint_equations.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.constraint_equations.ConstraintEquations.cerig:116
msgid ""
":ref:`cerig` cannot be deleted using :ref:`cedele`,ALL and then regenerated "
"in the second or higher load steps if the :ref:`lswrite` and :ref:`lssolve` "
"procedure is used. :ref:`cerig` writes constraint equations directly into "
"load step files. Deleting constraint equations ( :ref:`cedele`,ALL) cannot "
"always maintain the consistency among load steps."
msgstr ""

