#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/coupled_dof.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.coupled_dof.CoupledDof.cpintf:9
msgid ""
"Degree of freedom label for coupled nodes (in the nodal coordinate system). "
"If ALL, use all appropriate labels except HDSP. Valid labels are: Structural"
" labels: UX, UY, or UZ (displacements); ROTX, ROTY, or ROTZ (rotations, in "
"radians), HDSP (hydrostatic pressure). Thermal labels: TEMP, TBOT, TE2, "
"TE3,..., TTOP (temperature). Fluid labels: PRES (pressure); VX, VY, or VZ "
"(velocities). Electric labels: VOLT (voltage); EMF (electromotive force "
"drop); CURR (current). Magnetic labels: MAG (scalar magnetic potential); AZ "
"(vector magnetic potential); CURR (current). Diffusion label: CONC "
"(concentration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/coupled_dof.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.coupled_dof.CoupledDof.cpintf:18
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.cpcyc:16
msgid ""
"Tolerance for coincidence (based on maximum coordinate difference in each "
"global Cartesian direction for node locations and on angle differences for "
"node orientations). Defaults to 0.0001. Only nodes within the tolerance are "
"considered to be coincident for coupling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/coupled_dof.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.coupled_dof.CoupledDof.cpintf:36
msgid ""
"Defines coupled degrees of freedom between coincident nodes (within a "
"tolerance). May be used, for example, to \"button\" together elements "
"interfacing at a seam, where the seam consists of a series of node pairs. "
"One coupled set is generated for each selected degree of freedom for each "
"pair of coincident nodes. For more than two coincident nodes in a cluster, a"
" coupled set is generated from the lowest numbered node to each of the other"
" nodes in the cluster. Coupled sets are generated only within (and not "
"between) clusters. If fewer than all nodes are to be checked for "
"coincidence, use the :ref:`nsel` command to select nodes. Coupled set "
"reference numbers are incremented by one from the highest previous set "
"number. Use :ref:`cplist` to display the generated sets. Only nodes having "
"the same nodal coordinate system orientations (\"coincident\" within a "
"tolerance) are included. Use the :ref:`ceintf` command to connect nodes by "
"constraint equations instead of by coupling. Use the :ref:`eintf` command to"
" connect nodes by line elements instead of by coupling."
msgstr ""

