#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:440
msgid "**PATT: BEAM**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:442
msgid ""
"**Description:** Use this specialized input pattern for defining reinforcing"
" in regular constant and tapered beams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:447
msgid ""
"``V1`` and ``V2`` (or ``Y1`` and ``Z1`` ) -- Y and Z offsets with respect to"
" the section origin in the first beam section referenced by the base beam "
"element. The default value for Y1 and Z1 is 0.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:450
msgid ""
"``V3`` and ``V4`` (or ``Y2`` and ``Z2`` ) -- Y and Z offsets with respect to"
" the section origin in the second beam section referenced by the base beam "
"element. The default value for ``Y2`` is ``Y1``, and the default value for "
"``Z2`` is ``Z1``. (Because ``V3`` and ``V4`` values apply only to tapered "
"beams, the program ignores them if the base beam has a constant section.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:459
msgid "**Type: REINF, Subtype: SMEAR**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:461
msgid ""
"Suitable for layers of reinforcing fibers with uniform cross-section area "
"and spacing. Each :ref:`secdata` command defines the one reinforcing layer "
"in the section. When referenced by a ``MESH200`` element, only one "
":ref:`secdata` command per section is allowed. When referenced by "
"reinforcing elements ( ``REINF263`` and ``REINF265`` ), this limitation does"
" not apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:467
msgid "``MAT, A, S, KCN, THETA, PATT, V1, V2, V3, V4, V5``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:469
msgid ""
"``MAT`` = Material ID for layer. (See ``REINF263`` or ``REINF265`` for "
"available material models.) When the section is referenced by a ``MESH200`` "
"element, the default is the ``MESH200`` element material ID ( :ref:`mat` ). "
"When the section is referenced by reinforcing elements, the material ID is "
"required for all fibers, and no default for this value is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:473
msgid ""
"``A`` = Cross-section area of a single reinforcing fiber ( or the thickness "
"of the reinforcing layer for homogeneous reinforcing membranes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:475
msgid ""
"``S`` = Distance between two adjacent reinforcing fibers (ignored for "
"homogeneous reinforcing membranes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:477
msgid ""
"**Note:** If the section is used to model the reinforcing layers with a "
"uniaxial stress state ( :ref:`seccontrol`,,,0), the equivalent thickness h "
"of the reinforcing layer is determined by h = ``A`` / ``S``, where ``A`` is "
"the cross-section area of a single fiber and ``S`` is the distance between "
"two adjacent fibers. If the section is used to model homogeneous reinforcing"
" membranes ( :ref:`seccontrol`,,,1), the cross-section area input ``A`` is "
"the thickness of the reinforcing layer and the distance input ``S`` is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:483
msgid ""
"``KCN`` = Local coordinate system reference number for this layer. (See "
":ref:`local` for more information.) When the section is referenced by a "
"``MESH200`` element, the default ``KCN`` value is the ``MESH200`` element "
"coordinate system ID ( :ref:`esys` ). For the 2D smeared reinforcing element"
" ``REINF263``, ``KCN`` input is not required. When ``KCN`` is not specified,"
" the program uses a default layer coordinate system (described in "
"``REINF263`` and ``REINF265`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:488
msgid ""
"``THETA`` = Angle (in degrees) of the final layer coordinate system with "
"respect to the default layer system or the layer system specified in the "
"``KCN`` field. This value is ignored for ``REINF263`` when that element is "
"embedded in 2D plane strain or plane stress base elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:494
msgid ""
"``V1, V2, V3, V4, V5`` = Values to define the location of the reinforcing "
"layer, as shown:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:505
msgid ""
"**Description:** The smeared reinforcing layer is placed in the middle of a "
"layer in a layered base element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:508
msgid ""
"**Required input:**``V1`` (or ``n`` ) -- The number of the layer in the base"
" element on which to apply the reinforcing layer. The default value is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:515
msgid ""
"**Description:** This pattern applies only to 2D smeared reinforcing element"
" ``REINF263``. The smeared reinforcing layer is represented by a line in 2D."
" The orientation of the 2D smeared reinforcing layer is similar to one of "
"the specified element edges. The fiber orientation can be further adjusted "
"via offsets with respect to the specified element edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:524
msgid ""
"``V2`` (or ``Y1`` ) -- The normalized distances from the reinforcing layer "
"to the first end of the specified element edge. Valid values for Y1 are 0.0 "
"through 1.0. The default value for ``Y1`` is 0.5. ``V3`` (or ``Z1`` ) input "
"is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:527
msgid ""
"``V4`` (or ``Y2`` ) -- The normalized distances from the reinforcing layer "
"to the second end of the specified element edge. Valid value values for "
"``Y2`` are 0.0 through 1.0. The default value for ``Y2`` is ``Y1``. ``V4`` "
"(or ``Y2`` ) is ignored for axisymmetric shell elements. ``V5`` (or ``Z2``` "
") input is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:535
msgid "**PATT: ELEF**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:537
msgid ""
"**Description:** The smeared reinforcing layer is oriented parallel to one "
"of three adjacent element faces. (This pattern does not apply to 2D smeared "
"reinforcing element ``REINF263``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:543
msgid ""
"``V1`` (or ``F`` ) -- The number to indicate the base element face. The "
"default value is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:544
msgid ""
"``V2`` (or ``d1`` ) -- The normalized distance from the layer to the "
"specified base element face. Valid values for ``d1`` are 0.0 through 1.0. "
"The default value is 0.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:546
msgid ""
"``V3`` (or ``d2`` ) -- The normalized distance from corners JJ and KK of the"
" layer to the specified base element face (applicable to 8-node or 20-node "
"solid elements only). Valid values for ``d2`` are 0.0 through 1.0. The "
"default value is ``d1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:569
msgid ""
"Shell sections are referenced by the ``SHELL131``, ``SHELL132``, "
"``SHELL181``, ``SOLID185`` Layered Solid, ``SOLID186`` Layered Solid, "
"``SOLSH190``, ``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, ``SOLID278`` Layered Solid, "
"``SOLID279`` Layered Solid, and ``SHELL281`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:574
msgid "``TK``, ``MAT``, ``THETA``, ``NUMPT``, ``LayerName``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:576
msgid ""
"``TK`` = Thickness of shell layer. Zero thickness (not valid for "
"``SHELL131`` and ``SHELL132`` ) indicates a dropped layer. The sum of all "
"layer thicknesses must be greater than zero. The total thickness can be "
"tapered via the :ref:`secfunction` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:579
msgid ""
"``MAT`` = Material ID for layer (any current-technology material model is "
"available for ``SHELL181``, ``SOLID185`` Layered Solid, ``SOLID186`` Layered"
" Solid, ``SOLSH190``, ``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, ``SOLID278`` Layered Solid"
" and ``SOLID279`` Layered Solid [including `UserMat "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_prog/Z7K4r1e5lcd.html#>`_"
" ], and ``SHELL281`` ). ``MAT`` is required for a composite (multi-layered) "
"laminate. For a homogeneous (single-layered) shell, the default is the "
"`element material attribute "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD7_2.html#ad77wq1a7lcd>`_."
" You can also address multiple reference temperatures ( :ref:`tref` and/or "
":ref:`mp`,REFT)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:588
msgid ""
"``THETA`` = Angle (in degrees) of layer element coordinate system with "
"respect to element coordinate system (ESYS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:590
msgid ""
"``NUMPT`` = Number of integration points in layer. The user interface offers"
" 1, 3 (default), 5, 7, or 9 points; however, you can specify a higher number"
" on the :ref:`secdata` command. The integration rule used is Simpson's Rule."
" ( ``NUMPT`` is not used by ``SHELL131`` and ``SHELL132``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:598
msgid "Type: SUPPORT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:600
msgid ""
"Support sections are referenced by ``SOLID185`` and ``SOLID186`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:602
msgid "**Type: SUPPORT, Subtype: BLOCK**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:604
msgid "Data to provide in the value fields for ``Subtype`` = BLOCK:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:605
msgid "``T``, ``L``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:607
msgid "``T`` = Thickness of the block wall."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:608
msgid "``L`` = Spacing distance of the block walls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:610
msgid "**Type: SUPPORT, Subtype: ASEC**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:612
msgid "Data to provide in the value fields for ``Subtype`` = ASEC:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:617
msgid ""
"The multiplication factors are homogenization factors, and in each direction"
" reflect the ratio of the support area projected onto the area of a fully "
"solid support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:619
msgid "Values default to 1.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:620
msgid "Y and Z values default to X values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:621
msgid "GXY value defaults to EX value, GYZ to EY, and GXZ to EZ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:626
msgid "Type: TAPER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:628
msgid ""
"Tapered sections are referenced by ``BEAM188``, ``BEAM189`` and ``ELBOW290``"
" elements. After specifying the tapered section type ( "
":ref:`sectype`,,TAPER), issue separate :ref:`secdata` commands to define "
"each end of the tapered beam or pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:633
msgid "``Sec_IDn``, ``XLOC``, ``YLOC``, ``ZLOC``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:636
msgid "``Sec_IDn`` = Previously defined beam or pipe section at ends 1 and 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:637
msgid ""
"``XLOC``, ``YLOC``, ``ZLOC`` = The location of Sec_ID n in the global "
"Cartesian coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secdata:639
msgid ""
"For more information about tapered beams and pipes, including assumptions "
"and example command input, see `Defining a Tapered Beam or Pipe "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/Hlp_G_STR15_4.html#>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.cross\\_sections.CrossSections.secfunction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/cross_sections.rst:54:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:2
msgid "Specifies shell section thickness as a tabular function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SECFUNCTION "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SECFUNCTION.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:8
msgid "**table** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:9
msgid "Name of table parameter or array parameter for specifying thickness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:11
msgid "**pattern** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:12
msgid "Interpretation pattern for array parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:28
msgid ""
"The :ref:`secfunction` command is associated with the section most recently "
"defined via the :ref:`sectype` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:31
msgid ""
"A table parameter can define tabular thickness as a function of coordinates."
" Alternatively, you can use an array parameter (indexed by node number) that"
" expresses the function to be mapped. (See ``PATTERN`` of NOD2 for array "
"content.) Enclose the table or array name in percent signs (%) ( "
":ref:`secfunction`,``tablename``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:36
msgid "Issue the :ref:`dim` command to define a table or array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:38
msgid ""
"The table or array defines the total shell thickness at any point in space. "
"In multilayered sections, the total thickness and each layer thickness are "
"scaled accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:41
msgid ""
"The `Function Tool "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BASFUNCGRAPH.html>`_"
" is a convenient way to define your thickness tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:45
msgid ""
"Refer to the :ref:`dim` command for interpreting a table in a local "
"coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:47
msgid ""
"When ``PATTERN`` = NODE, ``TABLE`` should be a 1D array parameter (indexed "
"by node number) that expresses the function to be mapped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.secfunction:50
msgid ""
