#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.sload:76
msgid ""
"The :ref:`sload` command applies pretension loads to specified pretension "
"sections ( ``PRETS179`` -based) created via the :ref:`psmesh` command. A "
"pretension load is ramp-applied ( :ref:`kbc` = 0) if it is a force ( ``KFD``"
" = FORC), and step-applied ( :ref:`kbc` = 1) if it is a displacement ( "
"``KFD`` = DISP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/cross_sections.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.cross_sections.CrossSections.sload:81
msgid ""
"You can lock the load value at a specified load step. When locked, the load "
"changes from a force to a displacement, and the program applies the load as "
"a constant displacement in all future load steps. Locking is useful when "
"applying additional loadings. The additional loadings alter the effect of "
"the initial load value, but because locking transforms the load into a "
"displacement, it preserves the initial load's effect."
msgstr ""

