#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:267
msgid ""
"The data may be reread (on a different machine, for example) with the "
":ref:`cdread` command. Caution: When the file is read in, the "
":ref:`numoff`,MAT command may cause a mismatch between material definitions "
"and material numbers referenced by certain loads and element real constants."
" See :ref:`numoff` for details. Also, be aware that the files created by the"
" :ref:`cdwrite` command explicitly set the active coordinate system to "
"Cartesian ( :ref:`csys`,0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:273
msgid ""
"You should generally use the blocked format ( ``Fmat`` = BLOCKED) when "
"writing out model data with :ref:`cdwrite`. This is a compressed data format"
" that greatly reduces the time required to read large models through the "
":ref:`cdread` command. The blocked and unblocked formats are described in "
"`The CDWRITE (CDB) File Format "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_prog/Hlp_P_INT3_3.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:279
msgid ""
"If you use :ref:`cdwrite` in any of the derived products (Ansys Mechanical "
"Pro, Ansys Mechanical Premium), then before reading the file, you must edit "
"the :file:`Jobname.cdb` file to remove commands that are not available in "
"the respective component product."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:284
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cdwrite` command does not support (for beam meshing) any line "
"operation that relies on solid model associativity. For example, meshing the"
" areas adjacent to the meshed line, plotting the line that contains the "
"orientation nodes, or clearing the mesh from the line that contains "
"orientation nodes may not work as expected. For more information about beam "
"meshing, see `Meshing Your Solid Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD7_8.html>`_"
" in the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:293
msgid ""
"If you issue :ref:`cdwrite` to write a :file:`.cdb` file containing a user-"
"defined element, manually insert :ref:`usrelem` and :ref:`usrdof` commands "
"in the :file:`.cdb` file to provide the user- defined element "
"characteristics. Insert the two commands after the :ref:`et` command "
"(defining the user-defined element) and before the ``EBLOCK``  command. (If "
"multiple element types are defined in the :file:`.cdb` file, insert the "
":ref:`type` command to select the user-defined element. Place it before  "
":ref:`usrelem` and :ref:`usrdof`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:300
msgid ""
"If radiosity surface elements ( ``SURF251`` or ``SURF252`` ) are present in "
"the model, a radiosity mapping data file, :file:`Fname.RSM,` is also saved "
"when the :ref:`cdwrite` command is issued. For more information, see "
"`Advanced Radiosity Options "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_the/Hlp_G_THEadvrad.html#themultrsymm>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:305
msgid "*\\*IGES and ANF File Formats for Solid Model Geometry Information**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:307
msgid ""
"The format used for solid model geometry information is determined by the "
"current :ref:`cdopt` command setting. The default format is IGES."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:310
msgid ""
"IGES option (default) to write solid model information ( :ref:`cdopt`, IGS):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:312
msgid ""
"Before writing solid model entities, select all corresponding lower level "
"entities ( :ref:`allsel`,BELOW,ALL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:315
msgid ""
"Section properties assigned to areas, lines and other solid model entities "
"are not maintained when the model is exported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:318
msgid ""
"If you issue :ref:`cdwrite` after generating a beam mesh with orientation "
"nodes, the database file will contain all of the nodes for every beam "
"element, including the orientation nodes; however, the orientation keypoints"
" that were specified for the line ( :ref:`latt` ) are no longer associated "
"with the line and won't be written out to the geometry file. All "
"associativity between the line and the orientation keypoints is lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:324
msgid ""
"For beam meshing, this option does not support any line operation that "
"relies on solid model associativity. For example, meshing the areas adjacent"
" to the meshed line, plotting the line that contains the orientation nodes, "
"or clearing the mesh from the line that contains orientation nodes may not "
"work as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:329
msgid ""
"Concatenated lines are not written. The line segments that make up the "
"concatenated lines are written; however, if the command encounters an area "
"that contains a concatenated line, the write operation halts (that area "
"cannot be recreated during the read operation). If your model has areas that"
" contain concatenated lines, you must first list these and then "
"unconcatenate them before issuing the :ref:`cdwrite` command. Similarly, "
"hardpoint information cannot be written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:335
msgid "ANF option to write solid model information ( :ref:`cdopt`, ANF):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:337
msgid ""
"Writes all model information in the database (regardless of select status) "
"to the archive file; however, when you restore the database using this "
"archived file, the select status of entities is also restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:341
msgid ""
"Restores all line attributes, including orientation keypoints. It also "
"writes out any components (not assemblies) that consist of solid model "
"entities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:344
msgid ""
"Halts :ref:`cdwrite` when a concatenated line or an area that contains a "
"concatenated line is detected. You must delete the concatenated lines before"
" issuing :ref:`cdwrite`. Similarly, hardpoint information cannot be written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:353
msgid "Create a basic block and save it to disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cdwrite:371
msgid "Optionally load the mesh into Python using the archive reader."
msgstr ""

