#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:11
msgid "``DETAIL`` - List all contact pair properties (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:13
msgid "``SUMMARY`` - List only the open/closed status for each contact pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:15
msgid ""
"``POST`` - Execute a partial solution to write the initial contact "
"configuration to the :file:`jobname.rcn` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:18
msgid ""
"``ADJUST`` - Physically move contact nodes to the target in order to close a"
" gap or reduce penetration. The initial adjustment is converted to "
"structural displacement values (UX, UY, UZ) and stored in the "
":file:`jobname.rcn` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:22
msgid ""
"``MORPH`` - Physically move contact nodes to the target in order to close a "
"gap or reduce penetration, and also morph the underlying solid mesh. The "
"initial adjustment of contact nodes and repositioning of solid element nodes"
" due to mesh morphing are converted to structural displacement values (UX, "
"UY, UZ) and stored in the :file:`jobname.rcn` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:27
msgid ""
"``TADJUST`` - Physically move target body to the contact surface in order to"
" close a gap or reduce penetration. The initial adjustment is converted to "
"structural displacement values (UX, UY, UZ) and stored in the "
":file:`jobname.rcn` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:31
msgid ""
"``RESET`` - Reset target element and contact element key options and real "
"constants to their default values. This option is not valid for general "
"contact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:34
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Automatically sets certain real constants and key options to "
"recommended values or settings in order to achieve better convergence based "
"on overall contact pair behaviors. This option is not valid for general "
"contact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:38
msgid ""
"``TRIM`` - Trim contact pair (remove certain contact and target elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:40
msgid "``UNSE`` - Unselect certain contact and target elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:42
msgid ""
"``SPLIT`` - Split base (original) contact pairs into smaller sub-pairs at "
"the preprocessing ( :ref:`prep7` ) level. The main intent of this option is "
"to achieve better scalability in a distributed-memory parallel (DMP) run. "
"The splitting operation may create additional overlapping contact elements "
"at the split boundaries. Contact pairs can only be split once; repeated use "
"of this option results in no further splitting for those contact pairs "
"already split."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:48
msgid ""
"``DMP`` - This option is similar to the SPLIT, but it is more automatic and "
"contact pair splitting is done at the solution level ( :ref:`solve` ) of the"
" first load step, not at the preprocessing level. This option is activated "
"only in a distributed-memory parallel (DMP) run. For this option, "
"``TRlevel`` and ``InterType`` are valid; all other arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/database.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.database.Database.cncheck:53
msgid ""
"``MERGE`` - Merge all contact sub-pairs that were previously split (by prior"
" ``Option`` = SPLIT or DMP operations) back to their original pairs. Any "
"contact and target elements deleted due to the trim logic of the splitting "
"operation cannot be recovered by the MERGE operation. All other arguments "
"are ignored."
msgstr ""

