#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.cpcyc:37
msgid "**knonrot** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eintf:48
msgid ""
"When ``KNONROT`` = 0, the nodes coordinate system is not rotated. When "
"``KNONROT`` = 1, the nodes belonging to the elements created are rotated "
"into coordinate system ``KCN`` (see :ref:`nrotat` command description)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eintf:66
msgid ""
"Defines 2-node elements (such as gap elements) between coincident or offset "
"nodes (within a tolerance). May be used, for example, to \"hook\" together "
"elements interfacing at a seam, where the seam consists of a series of node "
"pairs. One element is generated for each set of two coincident nodes. For "
"more than two coincident or offset nodes in a cluster, an element is "
"generated from the lowest numbered node to each of the other nodes in the "
"cluster. If fewer than all nodes are to be checked for coincidence, use the "
":ref:`nsel` command to select the nodes. Element numbers are incremented by "
"one from the highest previous element number. The element type must be set ("
" :ref:`et` ) to a 2-node element before issuing this command. Use the "
":ref:`cpintf` command to connect nodes by coupling instead of by elements. "
"Use the :ref:`ceintf` command to connect the nodes by constraint equations "
"instead of by elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eintf:77
msgid ""
"For contact element ``CONTA178``, the tolerance is based on the maximum "
"Cartesian coordinate difference for node locations only. The angle "
"differences for node orientations are not checked."
msgstr ""

