msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:9
msgid "Increment to be added to element numbers in pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:12
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:17
msgid ""
"Do this generation operation a total of ``ITIME`` s, incrementing all nodes "
"in the given pattern by ``NINC`` each time after the first. ``ITIME`` must "
"be > 1 if generation is to occur. ``NINC`` may be positive, zero, or "
"negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:22
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:32
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:42
msgid ""
"Generate elements from the pattern that begins with ``IEL1`` to ``IEL2`` "
"(defaults to ``IEL1`` ) in steps of ``IEINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``IEL1`` "
"is negative, ``IEL2`` and ``IEINC`` are ignored and use the last \\| "
"``IEL1`` \\| elements (in sequence backward from the maximum element number)"
" as the pattern to be repeated. If ``IEL1`` = ALL, ``IEL2`` and ``IEINC`` "
"are ignored and all selected elements ( :ref:`esel` ) are used as the "
"pattern to be repeated. If ``IEL1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and "
"all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A "
"component name may also be substituted for ``IEL1`` ( ``IEL2`` and ``IEINC``"
" are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:56
msgid "Increment type number by ``TINC``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:68
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:73
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:78
msgid ""
"Define nodes that do not already exist but are needed by generated elements "
"( :ref:`ngen`, ``ITIME,INC,NODE1,,,DX,DY,DZ`` ). Zero is a valid value. If "
"blank, ``DX``, ``DY``, and ``DZ`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.engen:96
msgid ""
"Same as the :ref:`egen` command except it allows element numbers to be "
"explicitly incremented ( ``IINC`` ) from the generated set. Any existing "
"elements already having these numbers will be redefined."
msgstr ""

