msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ENORM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ENORM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:8
msgid "**enum** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:9
msgid ""
"Element number having the normal direction that the reoriented elements are "
"to match. If ``ENUM`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining "
"command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:27
msgid ""
"Reorients shell elements so that their outward normals are consistent with "
"that of a specified element. :ref:`enorm` can also be used to reorder nodal "
"connectivity of line elements so that their nodal ordering is consistent "
"with that of a specified element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:31
msgid ""
"For shell elements, the operation reorients the element by reversing and "
"shifting the node connectivity pattern. For example, for a 4-node shell "
"element, the nodes in positions I, J, K and L of the original element are "
"placed in positions J, I, L and K of the reoriented element. All 3D shell "
"elements in the selected set are considered for reorientation, and no "
"element is reoriented more than once during the operation. Only shell "
"elements adjacent to the lateral (side) faces are considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:38
msgid ""
"The command reorients the shell element normals on the same panel as the "
"specified shell element. A panel is the geometry defined by a subset of "
"shell elements bounded by free edges or T-junctions (anywhere three or more "
"shell edges share common nodes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:42
msgid ""
"Reorientation progresses within the selected set until either of the "
"following conditions is true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:44
msgid "The edge of the model is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:46
msgid ""
"More than two elements (whether selected or unselected) are adjacent to a "
"lateral face."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:48
msgid ""
"In situations where unselected elements might undesirably cause case b to "
"control, consider using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:49
msgid ""
":ref:`ensym`,0,,0,ALL instead of :ref:`enorm`. It is recommended that "
"reoriented elements be displayed and graphically reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:51
msgid ""
"You cannot use the :ref:`enorm` command to change the normal direction of "
"any element that has a body or surface load. We recommend that you apply all"
" of your loads only after ensuring that the element normal directions are "
"acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.enorm:55
msgid ""
"Real constant values are not reoriented and may be invalidated by an element"
" reversal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:2
msgid "Generates elements by symmetry reflection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ENSYM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ENSYM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:9
msgid "Increment to be added to element numbers in existing set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:12
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:9
msgid "Increment nodes in the given pattern by ``NINC``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:15
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:22
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:29
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:12
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:19
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:26
msgid ""
"Reflect elements from pattern beginning with ``IEL1`` to ``IEL2`` (defaults "
"to ``IEL1`` ) in steps of ``IEINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``IEL1`` = ALL, "
"``IEL2`` and ``IEINC`` are ignored and pattern is all selected elements ( "
":ref:`esel` ). If ``IEL1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``IEL1`` ( ``IEL2`` and ``IEINC`` are "
"ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:49
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ensym` command is similar to the :ref:`esym` command except that "
"it enables explicitly assigned element numbers to the generated set (in "
"terms of an increment ``IINC`` ). Any existing elements already having these"
" numbers are redefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:53
msgid ""
"The operation generates a new element by incrementing the nodes on the "
"original element, and reversing and shifting the node connectivity pattern. "
"For example, for a 4-node 2D element, the nodes in positions I, J, K and L "
"of the original element are placed in positions J, I, L and K of the "
"reflected element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:58
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:52
msgid ""
"Similar permutations occur for all other element types. For line elements, "
"the nodes in positions I and J of the original element are placed in "
"positions J and I of the reflected element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:63
msgid ""
"This command also provides a convenient way to reverse shell element "
"normals. If the ``IINC`` and ``NINC`` argument fields are left blank, the "
"effect of the reflection is to reverse the direction of the outward normal "
"of the specified elements. You cannot use this command to change the normal "
"direction of any element that has a body or surface load. It is best to "
"apply all loading only after ensuring that the element normal directions are"
" acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ensym:72
msgid ""
"For more information about controlling element normals, see `Revising Your "
"Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD8_6.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eplot.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eplot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eplot:2
msgid "Produces an element display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eplot:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EPLOT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EPLOT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eplot:21
msgid ""
"Produces an element display of the selected elements. In full graphics, only"
" those elements faces with all of their corresponding nodes selected are "
"plotted. In PowerGraphics, all element faces of the selected element set are"
" plotted irrespective of the nodes selected. However, for both full graphics"
" and PowerGraphics, adjacent or otherwise duplicated faces of 3D solid "
"elements will not be displayed in an attempt to eliminate plotting of "
"interior facets. See the :ref:`dsys` command for display coordinate system "
"issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eplot:28
msgid ""
"This command will display curvature in midside node elements when "
"PowerGraphics is activated ( :ref:`graphics` ,POWER) and :ref:`efacet`,2 or "
":ref:`efacet`,4 are enabled. (To display curvature, two facets per edge is "
"recommended ( :ref:`efacet`,2)). When you specify :ref:`efacet`,1, "
"PowerGraphics does not display midside nodes. :ref:`efacet` has no effect on"
" :ref:`eplot` for non- midside node elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:2
msgid "Reads elements from a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EREAD "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EREAD.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:16
msgid ""
"Filename extension (eight-character maximum). The extension defaults to ELEM"
" if ``Fname`` is blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:31
msgid ""
"This read operation is not necessary in a standard anlaysis run but is "
"provided as a convenience for those wanting to read a coded element file, "
"such as from another mesh generator or from a CAD/CAM program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:35
msgid "Data should be formatted as generated via :ref:`ewrite`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:37
msgid ""
"If issuing :ref:`eread` to acquire element information generated from "
":ref:`ewrite`, you must also issue :ref:`nread` before the :ref:`eread` "
"command. The element types ( :ref:`et` ) must be defined before the file is "
"read so that the file may be read properly. Only elements that are specified"
" via :ref:`errang` are read from the file. Also, only elements that are "
"fully attached to the nodes specified via :ref:`nrrang` are read from the "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.eread:43
msgid ""
"Elements are assigned numbers consecutively as read from the file, beginning"
" with the current highest database element number plus one. The file is "
"rewound before and after reading. Reading continues until the end of the "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:2
msgid "Generates reinforcing elements from selected existing (base) elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EREINF "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EREINF.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:8
msgid "**koffalim** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:9
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the limit of the angle between a ``MESH200`` element and a"
" base element. Valid for the `mesh-independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
" only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:13
msgid "0 - Enable the angle limit (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:14
msgid "1 - Disable the angle limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:16
msgid "**ktri** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:17
msgid ""
"Specify the shape of 3D smeared reinforcing members. Valid for the `mesh-"
"independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
" only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:20
msgid ""
"0 - Generate quad-dominant (mixed quadrilateral and triangular) reinforcing "
"members (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:21
msgid "1 - Generate triangular reinforcing members only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:35
msgid ""
":ref:`ereinf` generates reinforcing elements ( ``REINF263``, ``REINF264`` "
"and ``REINF265`` ) directly from selected base elements (that is, existing "
"standard structural elements in your model). The command scans all selected "
"base elements and generates (if necessary) a compatible reinforcing element "
"type for each base element. (You can select a combination of different base "
"element types.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:40
msgid ""
"Before issuing :ref:`ereinf`, first define the reinforcing geometry, "
"material, and orientation via one of two methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:43
msgid ""
"`Mesh-Independent Method: "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
"  Use ``MESH200`` elements to temporarily represent the geometry of the "
"reinforcing fibers or smeared reinforcing surfaces. Define additional data "
"including material, fiber cross-section area, fiber spacing, and fiber "
"orientation via reinforcing sections with the mesh pattern ( :ref:`secdata` "
") and assign the sections to corresponding ``MESH200`` elements. "
"(Predefining the reinforcing element type ( :ref:`et` ) is not required.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:51
msgid ""
"`Standard Method: "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
"  Define reinforcing section types ( :ref:`sectype` ) with standard "
"reinforcing location patterns ( :ref:`secdata` ). The standard reinforcing "
"location input are given with respect to the selected base elements; "
"therefore, a change in the base mesh may require redefining the (mesh-"
"dependent) reinforcing section types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:58
msgid ""
"Standard element-definition commands (such as :ref:`et` and :ref:`e` ) are "
"not used for defining reinforcing elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:61
msgid ""
":ref:`ereinf` creates no new nodes. The reinforcing elements and the base "
"elements share the common nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:64
msgid ""
"Elements generated by :ref:`ereinf` are not associated with the solid model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:66
msgid ""
"After :ref:`ereinf` executes, you can issue :ref:`etlist`, :ref:`elist`, or "
":ref:`eplot` to verify the newly created reinforcing element types and "
"elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:69
msgid ""
"Reinforcing elements do not account for any subsequent modifications made to"
" the base elements. Ansys, Inc. recommends issuing :ref:`ereinf` only after "
"the base elements are finalized. If you delete or modify base elements (via "
":ref:`edele`, :ref:`emodif`, :ref:`etchg`, :ref:`emid`, :ref:`eorient`, "
":ref:`nummrg`, or :ref:`numcmp`, for example), remove all affected "
"reinforcing elements and reissue :ref:`ereinf` to avoid inconsistencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:75
msgid ""
"If you define reinforcing via the `mesh-independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_,"
" :ref:`ereinf` creates new reinforcing sections containing details of the "
"created reinforcing elements, then applies them to all newly generated "
"reinforcing elements. The number of new reinforcing sections depends on the "
"number of new reinforcing elements. (You can examine the properties of new "
"sections ( :ref:`slist` ).) The program sets the ID number of the newest "
"reinforcing section to the highest section ID number in the model. After "
"issuing :ref:`ereinf`, the command shows the highest-numbered IDs (element "
"type, element, and section). Do not overwrite a new reinforcing section when"
" defining subsequent sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:85
msgid ""
"For the 3D smeared-reinforcing element ( ``REINF265`` ) with the `mesh-"
"independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_,"
" you can select the shape of the reinforcing members via ``KTri``. The "
"default behavior ( ``KTri`` = 0) generates quad-dominant members (primarily "
"quadrilaterals but with some triangles)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:90
msgid ""
":ref:`ereinf` can generate the reinforcing elements with thermal properties "
"if the base elements are thermal solid elements ( ``SOLID278`` or "
"``SOLID279`` ):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:93
msgid ""
"If using the `mesh-independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
" for defining reinforcing, apply element body-force loading ( "
":ref:`bfe`,,HGEN) or nodal body-force loading ( :ref:`bf`,,HGEN) on the "
"``MESH200`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:98
msgid ""
"If using the `standard method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
" for defining reinforcing, apply element body-force loading ( "
":ref:`bfe`,,HGEN) on the reinforcing members directly. (Do not apply nodal "
"body-force loading ( :ref:`bf`,,HGEN).)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:103
msgid ""
"If performing a subsequent structural analysis after the thermal analysis, "
":ref:`ereinf` can convert the reinforcing elements for the structural "
"analysis: Convert the thermal base elements to the appropriate structural "
"element ( :ref:`et` or :ref:`emodif` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:107
msgid "Select the reinforcing elements only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:109
msgid "Issue :ref:`ereinf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:111
msgid ""
"Result : The selected reinforcing elements are converted to elements "
"compatible with the converted base elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ereinf:114
msgid ""
"Solution accuracy can be affected if the volume ratio between reinforcing "
"elements and base elements is high, particularly when body loading (such as "
"heat generation) is applied via the reinforcing elements. If the program "
"detects a high volume ratio of reinforcing elements generated via the `mesh-"
"independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_,"
" it issues a warning message and saves affected base and ``MESH200`` "
"elements (used to generate the reinforcing elements) into a component for "
"close model inspection. Only the volume of reinforcing elements created by "
"the current  :ref:`ereinf` command is considered in the volume-ratio "
"calculation (that is, no volume accumulation occurs over multiple "
":ref:`ereinf` commands)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:2
msgid "Specifies the element range to be read from a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ERRANG "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ERRANG.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:8
msgid "**emin** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:17
msgid ""
"Elements with numbers from ``EMIN`` (defaults to 1) to ``EMAX`` (defaults to"
" 999999999) in steps of ``EINC`` (defaults to 1) will be read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:12
msgid "**emax** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/piping.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.piping.Piping.bend:27
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/piping.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.piping.Piping.miter:27
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/piping.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.piping.Piping.run:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/piping.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.piping.Piping.tee:39
msgid "**einc** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.errang:34
msgid ""
"Defines the element number range to be read ( :ref:`eread` ) from the "
"element file. If a range is also implied from the :ref:`nrrang` command, "
"only those elements satisfying both ranges will be read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:2
msgid "Generates elements overlaid on the free faces of selected nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ESURF "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ESURF.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:8
msgid "**xnode** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:9
msgid "Node number that is used only in the following two cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:11
msgid ""
"``XNODE`` is a single extra node number (ID) used for generating SURF151 or "
"SURF152 elements when KEYOPT(5)=1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:13
msgid ""
"``XNODE`` is a single pressure node number (ID) used for generating "
"``HSFLD241`` or ``HSFLD242`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:16
msgid ""
"There is no default. ``XNODE`` must be specified for the above cases. If "
"``XNODE`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields"
" are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A parameter or parametric expression "
"can be substituted for ``XNODE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:21
msgid ""
"Generates target, contact, and hydrostatic fluid elements with correct "
"direction of normals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:23
msgid ""
"This option is valid only with ``TARGE169``, ``TARGE170``, ``CONTA172``, "
"``CONTA174``, ``CONTA177``, ``HSFLD241``, and ``HSFLD242`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:25
msgid ""
"``TOP`` - Generates target and contact elements over beam and shell "
"elements, or hydrostatic fluid elements over shell elements, with the "
"normals the same as the underlying beam and shell elements (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:29
msgid ""
"``BOTTOM`` - Generates target and contact elements over beam and shell "
"elements, or hydrostatic fluid elements over shell elements, with the "
"normals opposite to the underlying beam and shell elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:33
msgid ""
"If target or contact elements and hydrostatic fluid elements are defined on "
"the same underlying shell elements, you only need to use this option once to"
" orient the normals opposite to the underlying shell elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:37
msgid ""
"``REVERSE`` - Reverses the direction of the normals on existing selected "
"target elements, contact elements, and hydrostatic fluid elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:40
msgid ""
"If target or contact elements and hydrostatic fluid elements are defined on "
"the same underlying shell elements, you only need to use this option once to"
" reverse the normals for all selected elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:44
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.tshap:8
msgid "**shape** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:45
msgid ""
"Used to specify the element shape for target element ``TARGE170`` ( "
"``Shape`` = LINE or POINT) or ``TARGE169`` elements ( ``Shape`` = POINT)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:47
msgid ""
"``(blank)`` - The target element takes the same shape as the external "
"surface of the underlying element (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:50
msgid ""
"``LINE`` - Generates LINE or PARA (parabolic) segments on exterior of "
"selected 3D elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:52
msgid "``POINT`` - Generates POINT segments on selected nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:68
msgid ""
"The :ref:`esurf` command generates elements of the currently active element "
"type overlaid on the free faces of existing elements. For example, surface "
"elements (such as ``SURF151``, ``SURF152``, ``SURF153``, ``SURF154``, or "
"``SURF159`` ) can be generated over solid elements (such as ``PLANE55``, "
"``SOLID70``, ``PLANE182``, ``SOLID185``, or ``SOLID272``, respectively)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:73
msgid ""
"Element faces are determined from the selected node set ( :ref:`nsel` ) and "
"the load faces for that element type. The operation is similar to that used "
"for generating element loads from selected nodes via the :ref:`sf`,ALL "
"command, except that elements (instead of loads) are generated. All nodes on"
" the face must be selected for the face to be used. For shell elements, only"
" face one of the element is available. If nodes are shared by adjacent "
"selected element faces, the faces are not free and no element is generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:80
msgid ""
"Elements created by :ref:`esurf` are oriented such that their surface load "
"directions are consistent with those of the underlying elements. Carefully "
"check generated elements and their orientations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:83
msgid ""
"Generated elements use the existing nodes and the active :ref:`mat`, "
":ref:`type`, :ref:`real`, and :ref:`esys` attributes. The exception is when "
"``Tlab`` = REVERSE. The reversed target and contact elements have the same "
"attributes as the original elements. If the underlying elements are solid "
"elements, ``Tlab`` = TOP or BOTTOM has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:88
msgid ""
"When the command generates a target element, the shape is by default the "
"same as that of the underlying element. Issue :ref:`esurf`,,,LINE or "
":ref:`esurf`,,,POINT to generate LINE, PARA, and POINT segments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:92
msgid ""
"The :ref:`esurf` command can also generate the 2D or 3D node-to-surface "
"element ``CONTA175``, based on the selected node components of the "
"underlying solid elements. When used to generate ``CONTA175`` elements, all "
":ref:`esurf` arguments are ignored. (If ``CONTA175`` is the active element "
"type, the path Main Menu> Preprocessor> Modeling> Create> Elements> Node-to-"
"Surf uses :ref:`esurf` to generate elements.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:98
msgid ""
"To generate ``SURF151`` or ``SURF152`` elements that have two extra nodes "
"from ``FLUID116`` elements, KEYOPT(5) for ``SURF151`` or ``SURF152`` is "
"first set to 0 and :ref:`esurf` is issued. Then KEYOPT(5) for ``SURF151`` or"
" ``SURF152`` is set to 2 and :ref:`mstole` is issued. For more information, "
"see `Using the Surface Effect Elements "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_the/Hlp_G_THE2_5.html#>`_"
" in the `Thermal Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_the/Hlp_G_THE4.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esurf:106
msgid ""
"For hydrostatic fluid elements ``HSFLD241`` and ``HSFLD242``, the "
":ref:`esurf` command generates triangular (2D) or pyramid-shaped (3D) "
"elements with bases that are overlaid on the faces of selected 2D or 3D "
"solid or shell elements. The single vertex for all generated elements is at "
"the pressure node specified as ``XNODE``. The generated elements fill the "
"volume enclosed by the solid or shell elements. The nodes on the overlaid "
"faces have translational degrees of freedom, while the pressure node shared "
"by all generated elements has a single hydrostatic pressure degree of "
"freedom, HDSP (see ``HSFLD241`` and ``HSFLD242`` for more information about "
"the pressure node)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:2
msgid "Generates elements from a pattern by a symmetry reflection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ESYM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ESYM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:46
msgid ""
"Generates additional elements from a given pattern (similar to :ref:`egen` )"
" except with a symmetry reflection. The operation generates a new element by"
" incrementing the nodes on the original element, and reversing and shifting "
"the node connectivity pattern. For example, for a 4-node 2D element, the "
"nodes in positions I, J, K, and L of the original element are placed in "
"positions J, I, L, and K of the reflected element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:55
msgid ""
"It is recommended that symmetry elements be displayed and graphically "
"reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:57
msgid ""
"If the nodes are also reflected (as with the :ref:`nsym` command), this "
"pattern is such that the orientation of the symmetry element remains similar"
" to the original element (that is, clockwise elements are generated from "
"clockwise elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:61
msgid ""
"For a non-reflected node pattern, the reversed orientation has the effect of"
" reversing the outward normal direction (clockwise elements are generated "
"from counterclockwise elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.esym:64
msgid ""
"Because nodes may be defined anywhere in the model independently of this "
"command, any orientation of the symmetry elements is possible. See also the "
":ref:`ensym` command for modifying existing elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:2
msgid "Writes elements to a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EWRITE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EWRITE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:9
msgid ""
"File name and directory path (up to 248 characters, including the characters"
" needed for the directory path). An unspecified directory path defaults to "
"the working directory; in this case, you can use all 248 characters for the "
"file name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:19
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:17
msgid "**kappnd** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:20
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:18
msgid "Append key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:22
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:20
msgid "``0`` - Rewind file before the write operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:24
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:22
msgid "``1`` - Append data to the end of the existing file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:27
msgid "Format key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:29
msgid "``SHORT`` - I6 format (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:31
msgid ""
"``LONG`` - I8 format. Switches automatically to I10 if entity IDs are large."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:47
msgid ""
"Writes the selected elements to a file. The write operation is unnecessary "
"in a standard Mechanical APDL run but is provided as convenience to users "
"wanting a coded element file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:51
msgid ""
"If issuing :ref:`ewrite` from Mechanical APDL to be used in Mechanical APDL,"
" issue :ref:`nwrite` to store nodal information for later use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:55
msgid ""
"Only elements having all of their nodes defined (and selected) are written. "
"Data are written in a coded format. The data description of each record is: "
"I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P, MAT, TYPE, REAL, SECNUM, ESYS, IEL, where MAT, TYPE,"
" REAL, and ESYS are attribute numbers, SECNUM is the beam section number, "
"and IEL is the element number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:60
msgid ""
"The format is (14I6) if ``Format`` = SHORT, and (14I8 or 14I10) if "
"``Format`` = LONG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.ewrite:62
msgid ""
"One element description per record is written for elements having <= 8 "
"nodes. For elements having > 8 nodes, nodes 9 and above are written on a "
"second record using the same format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:2
msgid "Defines interface interactions between general contact surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `GCDEF "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_GCDEF.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:9
msgid "Option to be performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:11
msgid ""
"``(blank)`` - Retain the previous ``Option`` setting between ``SECT1`` and "
"``SECT2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:13
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Define auto asymmetric contact between surfaces ``SECT1`` and "
"``SECT2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:15
msgid ""
"``SYMM`` - Define symmetric contact between surfaces ``SECT1`` and "
"``SECT2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:17
msgid ""
"``ASYM`` - Define asymmetric contact with ``SECT1`` as the source (contact) "
"surface and ``SECT2`` as the target surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:20
msgid ""
"``EXCL`` - Exclude contact between surfaces ``SECT1`` and ``SECT2``. "
"``MATID``, ``REALID``, ``SECT1END``, and ``SECT2END`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:23
msgid ""
"``DELETE`` - Remove the given definition from the :ref:`gcdef` table. "
"``MATID``, ``REALID``, ``SECT1END``, and ``SECT2END`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:26
msgid ""
"Note that :ref:`gcdef`,DELETE,ALL,ALL does not remove the entire "
":ref:`gcdef` table; it merely removes any existing :ref:`gcdef`,,ALL,ALL "
"definitions, while leaving intact any existing :ref:`gcdef` definitions that"
" are more specific."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:30
msgid ""
"To remove the entire :ref:`gcdef` table, issue :ref:`gcdef`,DELETE,TOTAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:32
msgid ""
"It is good practice to list all definitions using :ref:`gcdef`,LIST before "
"and after a :ref:`gcdef`,DELETE command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:35
msgid ""
"``LIST`` - List stored :ref:`gcdef` data entries. ``MATID`` and ``REALID`` "
"are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:37
msgid ""
":ref:`gcdef`,LIST lists all defined interactions. :ref:`gcdef`,LIST, "
"``SECT1``, ``SECT2`` lists the entry for the specific ``SECT1`` / ``SECT2`` "
"interaction. :ref:`gcdef`,LIST,ALL,ALL lists only the ALL,ALL entry (if "
"any)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:41
msgid ""
"``TABLE`` - List interpreted general contact definitions in tabular format. "
"``MATID`` and ``REALID`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:44
msgid ""
"By default, rows/columns of the table that match neighboring rows/columns "
"are compressed to simplify the table. Issue :ref:`gcdef`,TABLE,TOTAL to list"
" the entire :ref:`gcdef` table without removal of duplicate rows and "
"columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:48
msgid ""
"``TABLESOL`` - List a table showing actual interactions considered during "
"solution. This option is only available after the :ref:`solve` command. "
"``MATID`` and ``REALID`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:51
msgid ""
"The table shows MAT and REAL entries considered during the solution (actual "
"contact may or may not have occurred). This is in contrast to "
":ref:`gcdef`,TABLE, which shows the user specifications. For auto asymmetric"
" contact, TABLESOL indicates which of the possible contact versus target "
"surface combinations was considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:56
msgid "**sect1** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:57
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:96
msgid ""
"Section numbers representing contact ( ``SECT1`` ) and target ( ``SECT2`` ) "
"general contact surfaces (no defaults). (In most cases, the actual "
"determination of contact versus target surfaces takes place during "
":ref:`solve`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:61
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:100
msgid ""
"A node component name is also valid input for ``SECT1`` and ``SECT2``. The "
"component name is not stored. Instead, the program loops through all valid "
"section IDs found in the component and creates :ref:`gcdef` entries for all "
"possible SECT1/SECT2 combinations that result. These entries are reflected "
"in the ``Option`` = LIST and TABLE output. Section IDs can be further "
"controlled by adding an extension (_EDGE, _FACE, _VERT, _TOP, or _BOT) to "
"the end of the component name. See in the `Contact Technology Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/ctec_flpressexamp.html>`_"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:68
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:107
msgid "The following labels are also valid input:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:70
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:109
msgid "``SELF`` - Self contact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:72
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:111
msgid "``ALL`` - All general contact sections IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:74
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:113
msgid ""
"``ALL_EDGE`` - Section IDs of all ``CONTA177`` general contact line elements"
" (which may be on the edges of 3D solid and shell base elements, or on beam "
"base elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:77
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:116
msgid ""
"``ALL_FACE`` - Section IDs of all general contact elements on faces of solid"
" or shell base elements (both top and bottom faces of shell elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:80
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:119
msgid ""
"``ALL_VERT`` - Section IDs of all ``CONTA175`` general contact vertex "
"elements (which may be on convex corners of solid and shell base elements, "
"and on endpoints of beam base elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:83
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:122
msgid ""
"``ALL_TOP`` - Section IDs of all general contact elements on top faces of "
"shell base elements, and faces of solid base elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:86
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:125
msgid ""
"``ALL_BOT`` - Section IDs of general contact elements on bottom faces of "
"shell base elements, and faces of solid base elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:89
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:128
msgid ""
"The ALL labels apply to all defined general contact element section IDs in "
"the model without regard to the select status of the elements or attached "
"nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:92
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:131
msgid ""
"See :ref:`sect12interact` ``SECT1`` / ``SECT2`` Interactions for a "
"description of how the various inputs for ``SECT1`` and ``SECT2`` are "
"interpreted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:95
msgid "**sect2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:135
msgid ""
"Material ID number for general contact interaction properties at the "
"``SECT1`` / ``SECT2`` interface. If zero or blank, the previous setting of "
"``MATID`` for ``SECT1`` / ``SECT2`` (if any) is retained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:139
msgid ""
"As an example, you could specify \"always bonded\" contact behavior at the "
"interface by setting ``MATID`` to 2 and issuing the command "
":ref:`tb`,INTER,2,,,ABOND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:142
msgid ""
"The coefficient of friction MU is also defined by ``MATID``. Since the "
"default is ``MATID`` = 0, frictionless contact (MU = 0) is assumed by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:145
msgid "**realid** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:146
msgid ""
"Real constant ID number for general contact interaction properties at the "
"``SECT1`` / ``SECT2`` interface. If zero or blank, the previous setting of "
"``REALID`` for ``SECT1`` / ``SECT2`` (if any) is retained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:150
msgid ""
"As an example, you could specify contact stiffness (FKN) = 10 at the "
"interface by setting ``REALID`` to 14 and issuing the command "
":ref:`r`,14,,,10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:153
msgid "**sect1end** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:154
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:160
msgid ""
"Last section number in the range. For ``Option`` = LIST, TABLE, or TABLESOL,"
" data entries are processed for contact section numbers in the range from "
"``SECT1`` to ``SECT1END``, and target section numbers in the range from "
"``SECT2`` to ``SECT2END``. ``SECT1END`` and ``SECT2END`` are ignored for all"
" other ``Option`` labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:159
msgid "**sect2end** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:179
msgid ""
":ref:`gcdef` defines the interface interaction between general contact "
"surfaces identified by ``SECT1`` and ``SECT2``. :ref:`gcdef` commands are "
"order independent in most cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:182
msgid ""
":ref:`gcdef` definitions should be issued after :ref:`gcgen`. They are saved"
" in the database and are written to and read from :file:`.CDB` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:185
msgid ""
"See `General Contact "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/ctec_toolsgencont.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:191
msgid "**SECT1/ SECT2 Interactions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:192
msgid ""
"The most specific types of general contact definitions are those described "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:194
msgid ""
"``SECT1`` = any valid general surface section ID and ``SECT2`` = any "
"different valid general surface section ID: ``Option``, ``MATID``, and "
"``REALID`` apply to general surface interactions between ``SECT1`` and "
"``SECT2``. This is one of the most specific types of general contact "
"definitions and is never overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:198
msgid ""
"``SECT1`` = any valid general surface section ID and ``SECT2`` = ``SECT1`` :"
" ``Option``, ``MATID``, and ``REALID`` apply to general surface self contact"
" interactions involving ``SECT1``. This is one of the most specific types of"
" general contact definitions and is never overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:202
msgid ""
"The remaining general contact definition types can be overridden by the "
"above two general contact definition types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:205
msgid ""
"``SECT1`` = ALL and ``SECT2`` = ALL: ``Option``, ``MATID``, and ``REALID`` "
"apply to all general surface interactions, except where overridden by a more"
" specific :ref:`gcdef` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:207
msgid ""
"``SECT1`` = ALL and ``SECT2`` = SELF or ``SECT1`` = SELF and ``SECT2`` = "
"ALL: ``Option``, ``MATID``, and ``REALID`` apply to all general surface self"
" contact interactions, except where overridden by a more specific "
":ref:`gcdef` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:210
msgid ""
"``SECT1`` = ALL and ``SECT2`` = any valid general surface section ID: "
"``Option``, ``MATID``, and ``REALID`` apply to all general surface "
"interactions that include ``SECT2``, except where overridden by a more "
"specific :ref:`gcdef` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcdef:213
msgid ""
"``SECT1`` = any valid general surface section ID and ``SECT2`` = ALL: "
"``Option``, ``MATID``, and ``REALID`` apply to all general surface "
"interactions that include ``SECT1``, except where overridden by a more "
"specific :ref:`gcdef` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/elements.rst:63:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:2
msgid "Creates contact elements for general contact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `GCGEN "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_GCGEN.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:11
msgid ""
"``NEW`` - Create a new general contact definition. This option removes all "
"existing general contact elements and generates new elements with new "
"section IDs. Any existing :ref:`gcdef` specifications, general contact "
":ref:`sectype` / :ref:`secdata` data, and general contact element types are "
"also removed. If no general contact elements or data exist, this option "
"behaves the same as ``Option`` = UPDATE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:17
msgid ""
"``UPDATE`` - Generate general contact elements on newly added (or selected) "
"base elements. Newly generated contact elements are assigned new Section "
"IDs. Existing general contact elements remain with their previously assigned"
" section IDs and element attributes. Existing :ref:`gcdef` and "
":ref:`sectype` / :ref:`secdata` general contact data are respected. (This is"
" the default option.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:22
msgid ""
"``DELETE`` - Remove all existing general contact elements. Existing "
":ref:`gcdef` specifications, general contact :ref:`sectype` / :ref:`secdata`"
" data, and general contact element types are also removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:26
msgid "``SELECT`` - Select all existing general contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:28
msgid "**featureangle** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:29
msgid ""
"Angle tolerance for determining feature edges ( ``EdgeKEY`` ) and general "
"surfaces ( ``SplitKey`` ). Default = 42 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:32
msgid "**edgekey** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:33
msgid ""
"Key that controls creation of general contact line and vertex elements ( "
"``CONTA177``, ``CONTA175`` ) on base elements. Line elements are overlaid on"
" feature edges of 3D deformable bodies and on perimeter edges of 3D shell "
"structures; vertex elements are overlaid on convex corners of deformable "
"bodies and shell structures (2D or 3D), and on endpoints of 3D beam "
"structures. See :ref:`Understanding <usingfeatang>` ``FeatureANGLE`` for an "
"explanation of the feature edge criteria."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:35
msgid "``0`` - Exclude all edges and vertices (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:37
msgid "``1`` - Include ``CONTA177`` elements on feature edges only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:39
msgid "``2`` - Include ``CONTA177`` elements on shell perimeter edges only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:41
msgid ""
"``3`` - Include ``CONTA177`` elements on feature edges and shell perimeter "
"edges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:43
msgid ""
"``4`` - Include ``CONTA177`` elements on feature edges and shell perimeter "
"edges, and ``CONTA175`` elements on vertices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:46
msgid "``5`` - Include ``CONTA175`` elements on vertices only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:48
msgid ""
"``EdgeKey`` > 0 is intended to add extra contact constraint between an edge "
"or vertex of one surface and other 3D surfaces. Both edge and vertex contact"
" always use the penalty method and only include structural degrees of "
"freedom (UX, UY, UZ)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:52
msgid ""
":ref:`gcgen` always creates ``CONTA177`` elements on base beam elements, "
"regardless of the ``EdgeKEY`` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:55
msgid "**splitkey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:56
msgid ""
"Key that controls how section IDs and contact element type IDs are assigned "
"to surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:58
msgid ""
"``SPLIT`` - Assign a different section ID and contact element type ID for "
"every general surface of the selected base elements (default). See "
":ref:`Understanding <usingfeatang>` ``FeatureANGLE`` for an explanation of "
"the split criteria. Different section IDs are assigned to the top and bottom"
" surfaces of 2D shell and 3D shell bodies. This allows different "
":ref:`gcdef` specifications for different portions of the assembly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:64
msgid ""
"``PART`` - Assign a different section ID and contact element type ID for "
"every general surface which covers a physical part. Compared to the SPLIT "
"option, this option produces fewer unique section IDs, which can make it "
"easier to specify interactions via :ref:`gcdef`. However, it may also result"
" in a less accurate and/or less efficient solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:69
msgid "**selopt** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:70
msgid ""
"Key that controls which base elements are considered for general contact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:72
msgid ""
"``ATTACH`` - Use a recursive adjacency selection to obtain complete physical"
" parts (default). This selection starts from the selected base elements, "
"progressively adding elements adjacent to the faces of selected elements "
"until the edge of a part is reached. Then general contact elements are "
"generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:77
msgid ""
"``SELECT`` - Use only the initially selected base elements to generate "
"general contact elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:93
msgid ""
":ref:`gcgen` creates general contact elements on the exterior faces of "
"selected base elements. The base elements can be 2D or 3D solids, 3D beams, "
"2D shells (top and bottom), or 3D shells (top and bottom). The contact "
"element types can be ``CONTA172``, ``CONTA174``, ``CONTA175``, and/or "
"``CONTA177``, depending upon the types of base elements in the model and the"
" specified :ref:`gcgen` options. General contact elements are identified by "
"a real constant ID equal to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:99
msgid ""
"You can control contact interactions between specific general contact "
"surfaces that could potentially be in contact by using the :ref:`gcdef` "
"command. See `General Contact "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/ctec_toolsgencont.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:106
msgid "**Understanding FeatureANGLE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:107
msgid ""
"The exterior facets of the selected base solid and shell elements are "
"divided into subsets based on the angle between the normals of neighboring "
"faces. On a flat or smooth surface, adjacent exterior element faces have "
"normals that are parallel or nearly parallel; that is, the angle between the"
" adjacent normals is near zero degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/elements.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.elements.Elements.gcgen:112
msgid ""
"When the angle between the normals of two adjacent faces is greater than "
"``FeatureANGLE``, the two faces are considered to be on two separate "
"surfaces ( ``SplitKey`` = SPLIT). The edge between the faces may be convex "
"or concave. A convex (or outside) edge is considered to be a feature edge "
"and may be affected by the ``EdgeKEY`` setting. For more information, see "
"`Feature Angle ( FeatureANGLE) "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/ctec_generategc.html#gencontsurf>`_"
msgstr ""

