#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcrb:49
msgid ""
"EDCRB is valid only for materials defined as rigid bodies with the "
"EDMP,RIGID command. EDCRB automatically generates a constraint equation to "
"force the specified rigid bodies to behave as a single rigid body. The slave"
" rigid body takes on the material properties and loading of the master rigid"
" body. Any loads [EDLOAD] existing on the slave rigid body are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcrb:56
msgid ""
"To create a single large rigid body from several smaller bodies, use a "
"series of EDCRB commands. With the first command, specify a master and slave"
" to create the first combined rigid body. Then, using that body as the "
"master, specify another slave to create a larger rigid body. Continue the "
"process, using the expanding rigid body as the master and adding slave "
"bodies until you have defined the desired large rigid body. All slave rigid "
"bodies will take on the material properties and loading of the original "
"master rigid body. Note that you will need to use different NEQN values for "
"each pair of PARTM and PARTS.  This command will be ignored if you specify "
"the previously-defined master rigid body as a slave rigid body in the same "
"analysis. To change the master and slave definitions, first use the DELE "
"option to delete all master and slave definitions, and then use the ADD "
"option to redefine them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcrb:71
msgid ""
"The equation number, NEQN, is a reference number by which the constrained "
"bodies can be identified for listing and deleting purposes on the EDCRB "
"command. For any other reference to the constrained bodies (loading, contact"
" definitions, etc.), use the master body part number (PARTM)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.explicit\\_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.rst:57:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc:2
msgid "Specifies whether to use subcycling in an explicit dynamics analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc:4
msgid "APDL Command: EDCSC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc:9
msgid "Subcycling key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc:11
msgid "OFF - Do not use subcycling (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc:13
msgid "ON - Use subcycling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcsc:27
msgid ""
"Subcycling can be used to speed up an analysis when element sizes within a "
"model vary significantly. Relatively small elements will result in a small "
"time step size. When subcycling is on, the minimum time step size is "
"increased for the smallest elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.explicit\\_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.rst:57:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:2
msgid "Specifies mass scaling and scale factor of computed time step for an"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:4
msgid "APDL Command: EDCTS explicit dynamics analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:9
msgid "**dtms**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:10
msgid "Time step size for mass scaled solutions (defaults to 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:12
msgid "**tssfac**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:13
msgid ""
"Scale factor for computed time step. Defaults to 0.9; if high explosives are"
" used, the default is lowered to 0.67."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:28
msgid ""
"If DTMS is positive, the same time step size will be used for all elements "
"and mass scaling will be done for all elements.  Therefore, positive values "
"should only be used if inertial effects are insignificant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:33
msgid ""
"If DTMS is negative, mass scaling is applied only to elements whose "
"calculated time step size is smaller than DTMS.  Negative values should only"
" be used in transient analyses if the mass increases are insignificant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcts:38
msgid ""
"In order to use mass scaling in an explicit dynamic small restart analysis "
"(EDSTART,2) or full restart analysis (EDSTART,3), mass scaling must have "
"been active in the original analysis. The time step and scale factor used in"
" the original analysis will be used by default in the restart. You can issue"
" EDCTS in the restart analysis to change these settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.explicit_dynamics.ExplicitDynamics.edcurve.rst:2
