msgid ""
"The EDRUN command specifies either serial (one CPU) processing or shared "
"(multiple CPU) memory parallel processing (SMP). When using SMP, the "
"calculations may be executed in a different order, depending on CPU "
"availability and the load on each CPU. You may therefore see slight "
"differences in the results when running the same job multiple times, either "
"with the same number or a different number of processors. Comparing nodal "
"accelerations often shows wider discrepancies. To avoid such differences, "
"you can specify that consistency be maintained by setting CONS = 1. "
"Maintaining consistency can result in an increase of up to 15 percent in CPU"
" time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/explicit_dynamics.pydocstring
