msgid ""
"Generates a scaled set of (meshed) keypoints from a pattern of keypoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `KPSCALE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_KPSCALE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:23
msgid ""
"Set of keypoints ( ``NP1`` to ``NP2`` in steps of ``NINC`` ) that defines "
"the pattern to be scaled. ``NP2`` defaults to ``NP1``, ``NINC`` defaults to "
"1. If ``NP1`` = ALL, ``NP2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is "
"defined by all selected keypoints. If ``NP1`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may also be substituted for ``NP1`` ( ``NP2`` and "
"``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:38
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:46
msgid ""
"Scale factors to be applied to the X, Y, Z keypoint coordinates in the "
"active coordinate system (RR, Rθ, RZ for cylindrical; RR, Rθ, RΦ for "
"spherical). The Rθ and RΦ scale factors are interpreted as angular offsets. "
"For example, if CSYS = 1, an ``RX``, ``RY``, ``RZ`` input of (1.5,10,3) "
"would scale the specified keypoints 1.5 times in the radial and 3 times in "
"the Z direction, while adding an offset of 10 degrees to the keypoints.) "
"Zero, blank, or negative scale factor values are assumed to be 1.0. Zero or "
"blank angular offsets have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:54
msgid ""
"Increment to be applied to the keypoint numbers for generated set. If zero, "
"the lowest available keypoint numbers will be assigned ( :ref:`numstr` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:60
msgid ""
"``0`` - Nodes and point elements associated with the original keypoints will"
" be generated (scaled) if they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:63
msgid "``1`` - Nodes and point elements will not be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:68
msgid "``0`` - Additional keypoints will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:70
msgid ""
"``1`` - Original keypoints will be moved to new position ( ``KINC`` and "
"``NOELEM`` are ignored). Use only if the old keypoints are no longer needed "
"at their original positions. Corresponding meshed items are also moved if "
"not needed at their original position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/keypoints.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kpscale:88
msgid ""
"Generates a scaled set of keypoints (and corresponding mesh) from a pattern "
"of keypoints. The MAT, TYPE, REAL, and ESYS attributes are based on the "
"keypoints in the pattern and not the current settings. Scaling is done in "
"the active coordinate system. Keypoints in the pattern could have been "
"generated in any coordinate system. However, solid modeling in a toroidal "
"coordinate system is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kscale.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.keypoints.Keypoints.kscale"
msgstr ""

