"negative, assume ``P1`` (see below) is the second keypoint of the line "
"instead of the first. If ``NL1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ltan:14
msgid "Keypoint at which generated line must end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:16
msgid "**ang** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:17
msgid ""
"Angle of intersection of generated line ``PHIT`` - ``P3`` with tangent to "
"line ``P1`` - ``P2`` at ``PHIT``. If 0 (default), the generated line is "
"tangent to ``NL1`` toward end P1; if 90, the generated line is perpendicular"
" to ``NL1``. If 180, the generated line is tangent to NL1 toward end P2. "
"``ANG`` can be any value, but is adjusted to the corresponding acute angle "
"with respect to ``LOCAT``. See :ref:`LANG_notes` for a discussion of "
"accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:23
msgid "**phit** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:24
msgid ""
"Number to be assigned to keypoint generated at hit location (defaults to "
"lowest available keypoint number ( :ref:`numstr` ))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:27
msgid "**locat** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:28
msgid ""
"Approximate location of ``PHIT`` in terms of the ratio of the distance along"
" the line ( ``NL1`` ) to the length of the line. ``LOCAT`` can range from 0 "
"to 1. If ``LOCAT`` is blank, the point will be located with less speed and "
"accuracy, and an arbitrary location may result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:50
msgid ""
"Generates a straight line ( ``PHIT`` - ``P3`` ) at an angle ( ``ANG`` ) with"
" a line ``NL1`` ( ``P1`` - ``P2`` ). The location of ``PHIT`` on the line is"
" automatically calculated. Line ``P1`` - ``P2`` becomes ``P1`` - ``PHIT`` "
"and new lines ``PHIT`` - ``P2`` and ``PHIT`` - ``P3`` are generated. Line "
"divisions are set to zero (use :ref:`lesize`, etc. to modify)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:55
msgid ""
"``PHIT`` is positioned closest to ``LOCAT`` for the given angle, ``ANG``. To"
" ensure better performance, it is recommended that ``LOCAT`` be input, even "
"if it is 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:58
msgid ""
"The program uses an iterative procedure to position ``PHIT``. The procedure "
"is not exact, with the result that the actual value of ``ANG`` will "
"sometimes differ slightly from the specified value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lang:64
msgid ""
"Create a line from a line from (0, 0, 0) to (1, 0, 0) to a keypoint at (1, "
"1, 1) at an angle of 60 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/lines.rst:45:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:2
msgid "Defines a circular arc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LARC "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LARC.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:9
msgid ""
"Keypoint at one end of circular arc line. If ``P1`` = P, graphical picking "
"is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:13
msgid "Keypoint at other end of circular arc line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:15
msgid "**pc** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:16
msgid ""
"Keypoint defining plane of arc and center of curvature side (with positive "
"radius). Must not lie along the straight line from ``P1`` to ``P2``. ``PC`` "
"need not be at the center of curvature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:20
msgid ""
"Radius of curvature of the arc. If negative, assume center of curvature side"
" is opposite to that defined by ``PC``. If ``RAD`` is blank, ``RAD`` will be"
" calculated from a curve fit through ``P1``, ``PC``, and ``P2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:29
msgid "Line number of the arc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:42
msgid ""
"Defines a circular arc line from ``P1`` to ``P2``. The line shape is "
"generated as circular, regardless of the active coordinate system. The line "
"shape is invariant with coordinate system after it is generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:46
msgid ""
"When dealing with a large radius arc (1e3), or if the location of the arc "
"you create is far away from the origin of your coordinate system, anomalies "
"may occur. You can prevent this by creating the arc at a smaller scale, and "
"then scaling the model back to full size ( :ref:`lsscale` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larc:53
msgid ""
"Create a circular arc that travels between (0, 0, 0) and (1, 1, 0) with a "
"radius of curvature of 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/lines.rst:45:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:2
msgid "Generates the shortest line between two keypoints on an area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LAREA "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LAREA.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:9
msgid ""
"First keypoint of line to be generated. If ``P1`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:13
msgid "Second keypoint of line to be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:16
msgid ""
"Area containing ``P1`` and ``P2``, or area to which generated line is to be "
"parallel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:36
msgid ""
"Generates the shortest line between two keypoints, ``P1`` and ``P2``, both "
"of which lie on an area. The generated line will also lie on the area. "
"``P1`` and ``P2`` may also be equidistant (in global Cartesian space) from "
"the area (and on the same side of the area), in which case a line parallel "
"to the area is generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.larea:44
msgid "Generate a line on a square between its two corners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/lines.rst:45:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:2
msgid "Combines adjacent lines into one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LCOMB "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LCOMB.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:9
msgid ""
"Number of the first line to be combined. If ``NL1`` = ALL, ``NL2`` is "
"ignored and all selected lines ( :ref:`lsel` ) are combined. If ``NL1`` = P,"
" graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI). A component name may also be substituted for "
"``NL1`` ( ``NL2`` is ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:15
msgid "Number of the second line to be combined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:17
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:29
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lextnd:18
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:8
msgid "**keep** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:18
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lextnd:19
msgid "Specifies whether to keep the input entities:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:20
msgid ""
"``0`` - Delete lines ``NL1`` and ``NL2`` and their common keypoint. "
"Keypoints will not be deleted if they are meshed or if they are attached to "
"other lines. Lines will not be deleted if they are attached to different "
"areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:24
msgid ""
"``1`` - Keep ``NL1``, ``NL2``, and their common keypoint. (The common "
"keypoint will not be attached to the output line.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:32
msgid "Line number of the combined line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:45
msgid ""
"Combines adjacent lines into one line (the output line). This operation will"
" effectively \"undo\" the :ref:`ldiv` operation. Line divisions are set to "
"zero (use :ref:`lesize`, etc. to modify). Lines attached to the same area(s)"
" can also be combined. See also the :ref:`lccat` command for line "
"concatenation capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lcomb:53
msgid "Create two lines and combine them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/lines.rst:45:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:2
msgid "Deletes unmeshed lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LDELE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LDELE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:23
msgid ""
"Delete lines from ``NL1`` to ``NL2`` (defaults to ``NL1`` ) in steps of "
"``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NL1`` = ALL, ``NL2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored"
" and all selected lines ( :ref:`lsel` ) are deleted. If ``NL1`` = P, "
"graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI). A component name may also be substituted for "
"``NL1`` ( ``NL2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:30
msgid "Specifies whether keypoints are also to be deleted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:32
msgid "``0`` - Delete lines only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:34
msgid ""
"``1`` - Delete lines, as well as keypoints attached to lines but not "
"attached to other lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldele:50
msgid ""
"A line attached to an area cannot be deleted unless the area is first "
"deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/lines.rst:45:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:2
msgid "Divides a single line into two or more lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LDIV "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LDIV.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:9
msgid ""
"Number of the line to be divided. If negative, assume ``P1`` (see below) is "
"the second keypoint of the line instead of the first for ``RATIO``. If ALL, "
"divide all selected lines ( :ref:`lsel` ). If ``NL1`` = P, graphical picking"
" is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may also be substituted for ``NL1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:15
msgid ""
"Ratio of line length ``P1`` - ``PDIV`` to line length ``P1`` - ``P2``. Must "
"be between 0.0 and 1.0. Input ignored if ``NDIV`` > 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:18
msgid "**pdiv** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:19
msgid ""
"Number to be assigned to keypoint generated at division location (defaults "
"to lowest available keypoint number ( :ref:`numstr` )). Input ignored if "
"``NL1`` = ALL or ``NDIV`` > 2. If ``PDIV`` already exists and lies on line "
"``NL1``, divide line at ``PDIV`` ( ``RATIO`` must also be 0.0). If ``PDIV`` "
"already exists and does not lie on line ``NL1``, ``PDIV`` is projected and "
"moved to the nearest point on line ``NL1`` (if possible). ``PDIV`` cannot be"
" attached to another line, area, or volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:27
msgid "The number of new lines to be generated from old line (defaults to 2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:32
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lextnd:21
msgid "``0`` - Modify old line to use new keypoints and slopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:34
msgid ""
"``1`` - Do not modify old line. New lines will overlay old line and have "
"unique keypoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldiv:50
msgid ""
"Divides a single line ``NL1`` (defined from keypoint ``P1`` to keypoint "
"``P2`` ) into two or more lines. Line ``NL1`` becomes the new line beginning"
" with keypoint ``P1`` and new lines are generated ending at keypoint ``P2``."
" If the line is attached to an area, the area will also be updated. Line "
"divisions are set to zero (use :ref:`lesize`, etc. to modify)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/lines.rst:45:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:2
msgid "Generates lines by sweeping a keypoint pattern along path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LDRAG "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LDRAG.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:15
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:27
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:33
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:39
msgid ""
"List of keypoints in the pattern to be dragged (6 maximum if using keyboard "
"entry). If ``NK1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining "
"command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). If ``NK1`` = ALL, all "
"selected keypoints (except those that define the drag path) will be swept "
"along the path. A component name may also be substituted for ``NK1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.ldrag:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/lines.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.lines.Lines.lrotat:14
msgid "**nk2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

