#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.rsmesh:24
msgid "**kdir** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:21
msgid ""
"Direction (x, y, or z) normal to separation surface in the ``KCN`` "
"coordinate system (if ``ecomps1`` and ``ecomps2`` not specified)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:25
msgid ""
"Coordinate value along the ``KDIR`` axis at which to locate the interface "
"(if ``ecomps1`` and ``ecomps2`` not specified)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:28
msgid "**cztol** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:29
msgid ""
"Optional absolute tolerance about ``VALUE`` (if ``ecomps1`` and ``ecomps2`` "
"not specified). Allows nodes occurring slightly above or below the "
"separation to be grouped properly. The following expression represents the "
"default value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:33
msgid "equation not available  ``max`` - X ``min`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:51
msgid ":ref:`czmesh` is used on a mesh with shared nodes at the interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:53
msgid ""
"If ``ecomps1`` and ``ecomps2`` are specified, the :ref:`czmesh` command "
"creates/meshes interface elements ( ``INTER202``, ``INTER203``, "
"``INTER204``, ``INTER205`` ) along the boundary between the two components "
"or groups of elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:57
msgid ""
"The elements in each of the components or groups of elements share nodes "
"with each other and also with the interface elements. This one-element thick"
" boundary of interface elements splits the body between the two components "
"or groups of elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:61
msgid ""
"Subsequent separation (delamination and failure) of the interface zone "
"results in an increasing displacement between the nodes (within the "
"interface element) along the cohesive zone elements. Unless otherwise "
"specified, the :ref:`czmesh` command analyzes the configuration and geometry"
" of the adjacent structural elements and provides the appropriate interface "
"element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:66
msgid ""
"The :ref:`czmesh` operation copies any nodal temperatures that you have "
"defined on the split surface of the original mesh from the original nodes to"
" the newly created coincident duplicate nodes. Displacements, forces, and "
"other boundary conditions, however, are not copied; therefore, apply "
"boundary conditions and loadings after issuing :ref:`czmesh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:71
msgid ""
"If using :ref:`czmesh` to generate interface elements ( ``INTER202`` and "
"``INTER205`` ) in a `VCCT- based crack-growth simulation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_frac/Hlp_G_STR_VCCT.html#vcctsimassum>`_,"
" be aware that those elements do not support degenerate shapes. Examine the "
"resulting mesh, therefore, to verify correct element connectivity around the"
" crack tip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:77
msgid ""
"This command does not support mesh regions with non-solid elements (such as "
"surface-effect and shell elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.czmesh:80
msgid "This command is valid for structural analyses only."
msgstr ""

