#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:2
msgid ""
"Generates nodes and tetrahedral volume elements from detached exterior area "
"elements (facets)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `FVMESH "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_FVMESH.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:9
msgid ""
"Specifies whether to keep the area elements after the tetrahedral meshing "
"operation is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:11
msgid "``0`` - Delete area elements (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:13
msgid "``1`` - Keep area elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:29
msgid ""
"The :ref:`fvmesh` command generates a tetrahedral volume mesh from a "
"selected set of detached exterior area elements (facets). (Detached elements"
" have no solid model associativity.) The area elements can be triangular-"
"shaped, quadrilateral-shaped, or a mixture of the two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:33
msgid ""
"The :ref:`fvmesh` command is in contrast to the :ref:`vmesh` command, which "
"requires a volume to be input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:36
msgid ""
"The main tetrahedra mesher ( :ref:`mopt`,VMESH,MAIN) is the only tetrahedra "
"mesher that supports the :ref:`fvmesh` command. The alternate tetrahedra "
"mesher ( :ref:`mopt`,VMESH,ALTERNATE) does not support :ref:`fvmesh`. "
"``MESH200`` elements do not support :ref:`fvmesh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:40
msgid ""
"Tetrahedral mesh expansion ( :ref:`mopt`,TETEXPND, ``Value`` ) is supported "
"for both the :ref:`fvmesh` and :ref:`vmesh` commands. Tet-mesh expansion is "
"the only mesh control supported by :ref:`fvmesh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:44
msgid ""
"Triangle- or quadrilateral-shaped elements may be used as input to the "
":ref:`fvmesh` command. Where quadrilaterals are used, the default behavior "
"is for the pyramid-shaped elements to be formed at the boundary when the "
"appropriate element type is specified. See the :ref:`mopt`,PYRA command for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:49
msgid ""
"The :ref:`fvmesh` command does not support multiple \"volumes.\" If you have"
" multiple volumes in your model, select the surface elements for one "
"\"volume,\" while making sure that the surface elements for the other "
"volumes are deselected. Then use :ref:`fvmesh` to generate a mesh for the "
"first volume. Continue this procedure by selecting one volume at a time and "
"meshing it, until all of the volumes in the model have been meshed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.fvmesh:55
msgid ""
"If an error occurs during the meshing operation, the area elements are kept "
"even if ``KEEP`` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.gsgdata.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.gsgdata"
msgstr ""

