#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.smrtsize:236
msgid ""
"Where appropriate, SmartSizing will start with :ref:`aesize` settings. "
"Elsewhere, it will start with any defined :ref:`esize`,SIZE setting. It will"
" locally override :ref:`aesize` or :ref:`esize` for proximity and curvature."
" SmartSizing ignores any :ref:`esize`,,NDIV setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.smrtsize:240
msgid ""
":ref:`lesize` line division and spacing specifications will be honored by "
"SmartSizing, unless you give permission for SmartSizing to override them "
"(for proximity or curvature) by setting KYNDIV to 1. Lines not having an "
":ref:`lesize` specification are meshed as well as they can be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:2
msgid ""
"Converts 20-node degenerate tetrahedral elements to their 10-node non-"
"degenerate counterparts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `TCHG "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_TCHG.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:8
msgid "**ename1** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:9
msgid ""
"Name (or the number) of the 20-node tetrahedron element that you want to "
"convert. This argument is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:12
msgid "**ename2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:13
msgid ""
"Name (or the number) of the 10-node tetrahedron element to which you want to"
" convert the ``ENAME`` elements. This argument is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:16
msgid "**etype2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:17
msgid ""
"Element TYPE reference number for ``ENAME2``. If ``ETYPE2`` is 0 or is not "
"specified, the program selects the element TYPE reference number for "
"``ENAME2``. See the :ref:`TCHG_notes` section for details. This argument is "
"optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:35
msgid ""
"The :ref:`tchg` command allows you to specify conversion of any selected "
"20-node brick that is degenerated into a tetrahedron to a 10-node "
"tetrahedron."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:38
msgid ""
"The :ref:`tchg` command is useful when used in with the :ref:`mopt`,PYRA "
"command. Twenty-node pyramid shaped elements may be used in the same volume "
"with 10-node tetrahedra."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:41
msgid ""
"Performing a conversion is likely to create circumstances in which more than"
" one element type is defined for a single volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:44
msgid ""
"If specified, ``ETYPE2`` will usually be the same as the local element TYPE "
"number ( :ref:`et`, ``ITYPE`` ) that was assigned to ``ENAME2`` with the "
":ref:`et` command. You can specify a unique number for ``ETYPE2`` if you "
"prefer. Although ``ETYPE2`` is optional, it may be useful when two or more "
"``ITYPE`` s have been assigned to the same element (for example, if two "
"``SOLID187`` elements have been established in the element attribute tables "
"for the current model, use the ``ETYPE2`` argument to distinguish between "
"them). If ``ETYPE2`` is nonzero and it has not already been assigned to an "
"element via :ref:`et`, the program assigns the ``ETYPE2`` value to "
"``ENAME2`` as its element TYPE reference number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:53
msgid ""
"If ``ETYPE2`` is 0 or is not specified, the program determines the element "
"TYPE reference number for ``ENAME2`` in one of these ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:56
msgid ""
"If ``ETYPE2`` is 0 or is not specified, and ``ENAME2``  does not appear in "
"the element attribute tables, the program uses the next available (unused) "
"location in the element attribute tables to determine the element TYPE "
"reference number for ``ENAME2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:60
msgid ""
"If ``ETYPE2`` is 0 or is not specified, and ``ENAME2``  appears in the "
"element attribute tables, the program uses ``ENAME2`` 's existing element "
"TYPE reference number for ``ETYPE2``. (If there is more than one occurrence "
"of ``ENAME2`` in the element attribute tables (each with its own TYPE "
"reference number), the program uses the first ``ENAME2`` reference number "
"for ``ETYPE2``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:65
msgid ""
"You cannot use element conversion if boundary conditions or loads are "
"applied directly to any selected elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.tchg:68
msgid ""
"For more information about converting degenerate tetrahedral elements, see "
"`Meshing Your Solid Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD7_8.html>`_"
" in the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_"
msgstr ""

