msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:9
msgid ""
"Identifies the tetrahedral elements to be improved. Valid values are ALL and"
" P. If ``ELEM`` = ALL (default), improve all selected tetrahedral elements. "
"If ``ELEM`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command "
"fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:14
msgid "**chgbnd** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:14
msgid ""
"Specifies whether to allow boundary modification. Boundary modification "
"includes such things as changes in the connectivity of the element faces on "
"the boundary and the addition of boundary nodes. (Also see the Notes section"
" below for important usage information for ``CHGBND``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:18
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:19
msgid "``0`` - Do not allow boundary modification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:20
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:21
msgid "``1`` - Allow boundary modification (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:22
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:23
msgid "**implevel** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:23
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:24
msgid ""
"Identifies the level of improvement to be performed on the elements. "
"(Improvement occurs primarily through the use of face swapping and node "
"smoothing techniques.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:26
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:27
msgid "``0`` - Perform the least amount of swapping/smoothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:28
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:29
msgid "``1`` - Perform an intermediate amount of swapping/smoothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:31
msgid "``2`` - Perform the greatest amount of swapping/smoothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:32
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:33
msgid ""
"``3`` - Perform the greatest amount of swapping/smoothing, plus additional "
"improvement techniques (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:49
msgid ""
"The :ref:`timp` command enables you to improve a given tetrahedral mesh by "
"reducing the number of poorly-shaped tetrahedral elements (in particular, "
"the number of sliver tetrahedral elements)--as well as the overall number of"
" elements--in the mesh. It also improves the overall quality of the mesh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:54
msgid ""
":ref:`timp` is particularly useful for an imported tetrahedral mesh for "
"which no geometry information is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:57
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:58
msgid ""
"Regardless of the value of the ``CHGBND`` argument, boundary mid-nodes can "
"be moved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:59
msgid ""
"When loads or constraints have been placed on boundary nodes or mid-nodes, "
"and boundary mid-nodes are later moved, the program issues a warning message"
" to let you know that it will not update the loads or constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.timp:63
msgid ""
"No boundary modification is performed if shell or beam elements are present "
"in the mesh, even when ``CHGBND`` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type:2
msgid "Sets the element type attribute pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `TYPE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_TYPE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type:9
msgid "Assign a type number to the elements (defaults to 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type:25
msgid ""
"Assigns an element-type number to subsequently defined elements. The number "
"refers to the element- type number ( ``ITYPE`` ) defined with via :ref:`et`."
" You can display type numbers ( :ref:`pnum` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.type:28
msgid ""
"In some cases, the program can proceed with a meshing operation even when no"
" logical element type has been assigned via :ref:`type` or **XATT**, "
"``TYPE``. For more information, see the discussion for setting element "
"attributes in `Meshing Your Solid Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD7_8.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:2
msgid "Associates element attributes with the selected, unmeshed volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VATT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VATT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:17
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:25
msgid ""
"Material number, real constant set number, type number, coordinate system "
"number, and section number to be associated with selected, unmeshed volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:42
msgid ""
"These element attributes will be used when the volumes are meshed. If a "
"volume does not have attributes associated with it (by this command) at the "
"time it is meshed, the attributes are obtained from the then current "
":ref:`mat`, :ref:`real`, :ref:`type`, :ref:`esys`, and :ref:`secnum` command"
" settings. Reissue the :ref:`vatt` command (before volumes are meshed) to "
"change the attributes. A zero (or blank) argument removes the corresponding "
"association."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:48
msgid ""
"If any of the arguments ``MAT``, ``REAL``, ``TYPE``, ``ESYS`` or ``SECNUM`` "
"are defined as -1, then that value will be left unchanged in the selected "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vatt:51
msgid ""
"In some cases, the program can proceed with a volume meshing operation even "
"when no logical element type has been assigned via :ref:`vatt`, ``TYPE`` or "
":ref:`type`. For more information, see the discussion on setting element "
"attributes in `Meshing Your Solid Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD7_8.html>`_"
"  of the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear:2
msgid "Deletes nodes and volume elements associated with selected volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VCLEAR "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VCLEAR.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear:23
msgid ""
"Delete mesh for volumes ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to ``NV1`` ) in steps "
"of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL, ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored and mesh for all selected volumes ( :ref:`vsel` ) is deleted. If "
"``NV1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields "
"are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component name may also be "
"substituted for ``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vclear:43
msgid ""
"Deletes all nodes and volume elements associated with selected volumes "
"(regardless of whether the nodes or elements are selected). Nodes shared by "
"adjacent meshed volumes and nodes associated with non-volume elements will "
"not be deleted. Attributes assigned as a result of :ref:`vatt` are "
"maintained. In the program's response to the command, if a volume, area, "
"line, or keypoint is tallied as \"cleared,\" it means either its node or "
"element reference was deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:2
msgid ""
"Specifies brick element orientation for volume mapped (hexahedron) meshing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VEORIENT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VEORIENT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:6
msgid "**Command default:** Elements are not oriented in any specific manner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:11
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:9
msgid "**vnum** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:12
msgid ""
"Number identifying volume for which elements are to be oriented (no "
"default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:15
msgid "Option for defining element orientation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:17
msgid ""
"``KP`` - Orientation is determined by two keypoints on the volume. Input the"
" keypoint numbers (KZ1 and KZ2) in fields ``VALUE1`` and ``VALUE2``, "
"respectively. The element z-axis points from KZ1 toward KZ2. Element x and y"
" directions point away from KZ1 along edges of the volume to make a right-"
"hand triad. (The element x- and y-axes are uniquely determined by this "
"specification.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:22
msgid ""
"``LINE`` - Orientation is determined by one of the lines defining the "
"volume. Input the line number in field ``VALUE1``. The element z direction "
"follows the direction of the line. Input a negative value if the desired z "
"direction is opposite to the direction of the specified line. (The element "
"x- and y-axes are uniquely determined by this specification.) ( ``VALUE2`` "
"is not used.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:27
msgid ""
"``AREA`` - Orientation is determined by one of the areas defining the "
"volume. The area represents the desired element top surface. Input the area "
"number as ``VALUE1``. The shortest line in the volume connected to the area "
"will be used to specify the element z direction. (If more than one shortest "
"line exists, the lowest numbered of those is used.) Element x and y "
"directions are not uniquely specified by this option. ( ``VALUE2`` is not "
"used.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:33
msgid ""
"``THIN`` - Align the element z normal to the thinnest dimension of the "
"volume. The shortest line in the volume is used to specify the element z "
"direction. (If more than one shortest line exists, the lowest numbered of "
"those is used.) Element x and y directions are not uniquely specified by "
"this option. ( ``VALUE1`` and ``VALUE2`` are not used.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:38
msgid ""
"``DELE`` - Delete the previously defined volume orientation for the "
"specified volume ( ``VNUM`` ). ( ``VALUE1`` and ``VALUE2`` are not used.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:42
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:47
msgid ""
"Parameters required for the element z-axis direction specification. The "
"meaning of ``VALUE1`` and ``VALUE2`` will depend on the chosen ``Option``. "
"See the description of ``Option`` above for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:63
msgid ""
"Use :ref:`veorient` before the :ref:`vmesh` command to specify the desired "
"orientation of brick elements in a mapped mesh. :ref:`veorient` has no "
"effect on tetrahedron meshes, extruded meshes ( :ref:`vrotat`, :ref:`vdrag`,"
" :ref:`vext`, etc.), or swept meshes ( :ref:`vsweep` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:67
msgid ""
"Proper brick orientation is essential for certain element types such as "
"``SOLID185`` Layered Solid, ``SOLID186`` Layered Solid, and ``SOLSH190``. In"
" such cases, use :ref:`veorient` or :ref:`eorient` to achieve the desired "
"orientation. For other brick element types, you may need to specify element "
"orientation to control orthotropic material property directions without "
"concern for the element connectivity. For those cases, the :ref:`esys` "
"command is the preferred method of specifying the material property "
"directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.veorient:74
msgid ""
"For ``Option`` = LINE, AREA, and THIN, the orientation will be internally "
"converted to an equivalent ``Option`` = KP specification (KP,KZ1,KZ2). Use "
"the :ref:`vlist` command to view the element orientations (in terms of KZ1 "
"and KZ2) associated with each volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:2
msgid ""
"Improves the quality of the tetrahedral elements in the selected volume(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VIMP "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VIMP.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:8
msgid "**vol** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:9
msgid ""
"Number of the volume containing the tetrahedral elements to be improved. If "
"``VOL`` = ALL (default), improve the tetrahedral elements in all selected "
"volumes. If ``VOL`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining "
"command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component name may "
"also be substituted for ``VOL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:15
msgid ""
"Specifies whether to allow boundary modification. Boundary modification "
"includes such things as changes in the connectivity of the element faces on "
"the boundary and the addition of boundary nodes. (Also see :ref:`VIMP_notes`"
" below for important usage information for ``CHGBND``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:50
msgid ""
":ref:`vimp` is useful for further improving a volume mesh created in "
"Mechanical APDL ( :ref:`vmesh` ), especially quadratic tetrahedral element "
"meshes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:54
msgid ""
"The command enables you to improve a given tetrahedral mesh by reducing the "
"number of poorly-shaped tetrahedral elements (in particular, the number of "
"sliver tetrahedral elements)--as well as the overall number of elements--in "
"the mesh. It also improves the overall quality of the mesh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:60
msgid ""
"When loads or constraints have been placed on boundary nodes or mid-nodes, "
"and boundary mid-nodes are later moved, the program issues a warning message"
" indicating that it will not update the loads or constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vimp:64
msgid ""
"Even when ``CHGBND`` = 1, no boundary modification is performed on areas and"
" lines that are not modifiable. For example, areas that are adjacent to "
"other volumes or that contain shell elements, or lines that are not incident"
" on modifiable areas, contain beam elements, or have line divisions "
"specified for them ( :ref:`lesize` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh.rst:2
