msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:2
msgid "Generates nodes and volume elements within volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VMESH "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VMESH.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:23
msgid ""
"Mesh volumes from ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to ``NV1`` ) in steps of "
"``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL, ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored"
" and all selected volumes ( :ref:`vsel` ) are meshed. If ``NV1`` = P, "
"graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI). A component name may also be substituted for "
"``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:43
msgid ""
"Missing nodes required for the generated elements are created and assigned "
"the lowest available numbers ( :ref:`numstr` ). During a batch run and if "
"elements already exist, a mesh abort will write an alternative database file"
" ( :file:`File.DBE` ) for possible recovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vmesh:47
msgid ""
"Tetrahedral mesh expansion ( :ref:`mopt`,TETEXPND, ``Value`` ) is supported "
"for both the :ref:`vmesh` and :ref:`fvmesh` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/meshing.rst:74:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:2
msgid ""
"Fills an existing unmeshed volume with elements by sweeping the mesh from an"
" adjacent area through the volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:5
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VSWEEP "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VSWEEP.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:10
msgid ""
"Number identifying the volume that is to be meshed by :ref:`vsweep`. If "
"``VNUM`` = P, graphical picking is enabled, you will be prompted to choose "
"the volume or volumes based on the setting of :ref:`extopt`,VSWE,AUTO. This "
"argument is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:14
msgid ""
"\"ALL\" is a valid input value that when selected sends all the selected "
"volumes to the sweeper. If ``VNUM`` = ALL, each volume that can be swept "
"will be and those not able to be swept will be unmeshed or meshed with tets "
"depending upon the setting of :ref:`extopt`,VSWE,TETS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:18
msgid ""
"A component name is a valid input value. All volumes that are part of the "
"specified component will be sent to the sweeper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:21
msgid "**srca** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:22
msgid ""
"Number identifying the source area. This is the area whose mesh will provide"
" the pattern for the volume elements. (If you do not mesh the source area "
"prior to volume sweeping, the program meshes it internally when you initiate"
" volume sweeping.) The program sweeps the pattern of the area elements "
"through the volume to create the mesh of volume elements. You cannot "
"substitute a component name for ``SRCA``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:28
msgid ""
"This argument is optional. If ``VNUM`` = ALL or is a component containing "
"more than one volume, ``SRCA`` is ignored. If ``SRCA`` is not provided or if"
" it is ignored, :ref:`vsweep` attempts to automatically determine which area"
" should be the target area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:32
msgid "**trga** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:33
msgid ""
"Number identifying the target area. This is the area that is opposite the "
"source area specified by ``SRCA``. You cannot substitute a component name "
"for ``TRGA``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:36
msgid ""
"This argument is optional. If ``VNUM`` = ALL or component containing more "
"than one volume, ``TRGA`` is ignored. If ``TRGA`` is not provided or if it "
"is ignored, :ref:`vsweep` attempts to automatically determine which area "
"should be the target area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:40
msgid "**lsmo** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:41
msgid ""
"Value specifying whether the program should perform line smoothing during "
"volume sweeping. (The value of this argument controls line smoothing for the"
" :ref:`vsweep` command only; it has no effect on the setting of the "
":ref:`mopt` command's LSMO option.) This argument is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:44
msgid "``0`` - Do not perform line smoothing. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:46
msgid ""
"``1`` - Always perform line smoothing. This setting is not recommended for "
"large models due to speed considerations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:63
msgid ""
"If the source mesh consists of quadrilateral elements, the program fills the"
" volume with hexahedral elements. If the source mesh consists of triangles, "
"the program fills the volume with wedges. If the source mesh consists of a "
"combination of quadrilaterals and triangles, the program fills the volume "
"with a combination of hexahedral and wedge elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:68
msgid ""
"In the past, you may have used the :ref:`vrotat`, :ref:`vext`, "
":ref:`voffst`, and/or :ref:`vdrag` commands to extrude a meshed area into a "
"meshed volume. However, those commands create the volume and the volume mesh"
" simultaneously. In contrast, the :ref:`vsweep` command is intended for use "
"in an existing unmeshed volume. This makes :ref:`vsweep` particularly useful"
" when you have imported a solid model that was created in another program, "
"and you want to mesh it in Mechanical APDL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/meshing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.meshing.Meshing.vsweep:74
msgid ""
"For related information, see the description of the :ref:`extopt` command "
"(although :ref:`extopt` sets volume sweeping options, it does not affect "
"element spacing). Also see the detailed discussion of volume sweeping in "
"`Meshing Your Solid Model "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD7_5.html#modmeshvaidck31400>`_"
" of the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.damorph.rst:2
