" picking is enabled. A component may be substituted for ``VOLU``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:13
msgid "**xarea** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:14
msgid ""
"Areas to be excluded from morphing. If ALL, exclude all selected areas ( "
":ref:`asel` ). If ``XAREA`` = P, graphical picking is enabled. A component "
"may be substituted for ``XAREA``. If ``XAREA`` is blank (default), allow "
"morphing of nodes attached to areas of the selected volumes ( ``VOLU`` ) "
"which are not shared by unselected volumes. (See Notes for clarification)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:22
msgid ""
"``0`` - Remesh the selected non-structural volumes only if mesh morphing "
"fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:24
msgid ""
"``1`` - Remesh the selected non-structural volumes and bypass mesh morphing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:42
msgid ""
"The selected volumes should include only non-structural regions adjacent to "
"structural regions. DVMORPH will morph the non-structural volumes to "
"coincide with the deflections of the structural regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:46
msgid ""
"Nodes in the structural regions move in accordance with computed "
"displacements. Displacements from a structural analysis must be in the "
"database prior to issuing DVMORPH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:49
msgid ""
"By default, nodes attached to areas can move along the areas. You can use "
"``XAREA`` to restrain nodes on certain areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:52
msgid ""
"By default ( ``RMSHKY`` = 0), DVMORPH will remesh the selected non-"
"structural volumes entirely if a satisfactory morphed mesh cannot be "
"provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:55
msgid ""
"If boundary conditions and loads are applied directly to nodes and elements,"
" the DVMORPH command requires that these be removed before remeshing can "
"take place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.dvmorph:58
msgid ""
"Exercise care with initial conditions defined by the :ref:`ic` command. "
"Before a structural analysis is performed for a sequentially coupled "
"analysis, the DVMORPH command requires that initial conditions be removed "
"from all null element type nodes in the non-structural regions. Use "
":ref:`icdele` to delete the initial conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/morphing.rst:22:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:2
msgid "Specifies morphing and remeshing controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MORPH "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MORPH.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:9
msgid "``OFF`` - Turns off morphing for field elements (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:11
msgid "``ON`` - Turns on morphing for field elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:13
msgid "**remeshopt** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:14
msgid "``OFF`` - Do not remesh (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:16
msgid ""
"``ON`` - Remesh when element qualities fall below values specified by "
"``ARMAX``, ``VOCH``, or ``ARCH`` as explained below. Valid only when "
"``Option`` is ON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:19
msgid "**elemset** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:20
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - Remesh all selected elements if the quality of the worst defined "
"element falls below any quality requirement (default when ``Remeshopt`` = "
"ON)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:23
msgid ""
"``CompName`` - Specify a component name, up to 256 characters. All elements "
"included in this component name are remeshed if the quality of the worst "
"element falls below any quality requirement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:26
msgid "**armax** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:27
msgid "The maximum allowable element generalized aspect ratio. Defaults to 5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:29
msgid "**voch** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:30
msgid ""
"The maximum allowable change of element size (area or volume). Defaults to "
"3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:32
msgid "**arch** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:33
msgid "The maximum allowable element aspect ratio change. Defaults to 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:35
msgid "**step** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:36
msgid ""
"The frequency of element quality checking, based on time steps. A quality "
"check takes place at the intervals defined by ``STEP``. Defaults to 1 "
"(quality check at every step)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:40
msgid ""
"A quality check takes place at the time point specified. Defaults to -1 (a "
"quality check at every time point)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:43
msgid "**stropt** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:44
msgid "``NO`` - There are no structural elements in the model (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:46
msgid ""
"``YES`` - There are structural elements in the model and the morphing "
"happens after the structural solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:63
msgid ""
":ref:`morph` is applicable to any non-structural field analysis. It "
"activates displacement degrees of freedom for non-structural elements so "
"that boundary conditions may be placed on the field mesh to constrain the "
"movement of the non-structural mesh during morphing. It morphs the non-"
"structural mesh using displacements transferred at the surface interface "
"between the structural field and the non-structural field. The displacements"
" of non-structural elements are mesh displacements to avoid mesh distortion,"
" but have no physical meaning except at the interface. :ref:`morph` does not"
" support surface, link, or shell elements, or any element shape other than "
"triangles, quads, tets, and bricks. Morphed fields must be in the global "
"Cartesian system ( :ref:`csys` = 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/morphing.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.morphing.Morphing.morph:72
msgid ""
"If ``StrOpt`` = YES, the following non-structural element types will be "
"morphed:"
msgstr ""

