msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `CENTER "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CENTER.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:9
msgid ""
"Number to be assigned to the node generated at the center of curvature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:12
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:15
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:18
msgid ""
"Three nodes used to calculated the center of curvature, as described under "
"``RADIUS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:20
msgid "**radius** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:21
msgid ""
"Used to control the interpretation of ``NODE1``, ``NODE2`` and ``NODE3`` :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:23
msgid ""
"``0`` - ``NODE1``, ``NODE2`` and ``NODE3`` lie on a circular arc. The "
"program will calculate the center of curvature (and radius) (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.center:26
msgid ""
"``≠, 0`` - ``NODE1`` and ``NODE2`` are the endpoints of an arc, and "
"``RADIUS`` is the radius of curvature. The program will locate the center of"
" curvature on the ``NODE3`` side of the ``NODE1`` - ``NODE2`` line if "
"``RADIUS`` > 0, and opposite to ``NODE3`` if ``RADIUS`` < 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:2
msgid "Extrudes 2D plane elements into 3D solids during a 2D to 3D analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EEXTRUDE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EEXTRUDE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.naxis:9
msgid "Specifies one of the following command behaviors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:11
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Extrudes plane elements ( ``PLANE182`` and ``PLANE183`` ) `Notes "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EEXTRUDE.html#>`_"
" based on the KEYOPT(3) setting. Complementary elements are also extruded. "
"(See `Notes "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EEXTRUDE.html#>`_"
" Notes for more information.) This behavior is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:17
msgid ""
"``PLANE`` - Extrudes elements in the global Z direction. KEYOPT(3) of the "
"parent plane elements is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:20
msgid ""
"``AXIS`` - Extrudes elements about the global Y axis. KEYOPT(3) of the "
"parent plane elements is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:23
msgid ""
"``TANGENT`` - Extrudes plane and contact elements about the global Y axis. "
"Target elements are extruded in the global Z direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:26
msgid ""
"``TIRE`` - Extrudes plane and contact elements about the global Y axis in a "
"360-degree span. Target elements are extruded in the global Z direction if "
"outside the plane elements. Mesh refinement is adapted specifically for tire"
" analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:30
msgid "See :ref:`actionbehavior`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:32
msgid "**nelem** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:33
msgid ""
"Number of elements to generate in the extruded direction. If you do not "
"specify a number, the program calculates a number automatically based on the"
" average element size and extrusion distance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:38
msgid ""
"Spacing ratio. If positive, this value is the nominal ratio of the last "
"division size to the first division size (if > 1.0, sizes increase, if < "
"1.0, sizes decrease). If negative, \\|SPACE\\| is the nominal ratio of the "
"center division size to the end division size. Default = 1.0 (uniform "
"spacing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:44
msgid ""
"Distance to extrude in the global Z direction for the plane strain case ( "
"``Action`` = PLANE). The default is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:48
msgid "Angle (in degrees) depending on ``Action`` :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:50
msgid ""
"``Action`` = AXIS - Ending angle to extrude about the global Y axis for the "
"axisymmetric case. Default = 360. (The beginning angle is always 0 degrees.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:52
msgid ""
"``Action`` = TIRE - Span of the contact patch for mesh refinement. The "
"program generates an abrupt mesh transition from fine to coarse. Default = "
"0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:55
msgid "**tfact** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:56
msgid ""
"Factor for increasing the rigid target size. The size of the extruded rigid "
"target elements is determined automatically based on the size of the contact"
" elements. Default = 0.2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:59
msgid "**bckey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:60
msgid ""
"Controls the nodal orientation in the third direction and boundary-condition"
" mapping ( ``Action`` = AXIS or TIRE only):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:62
msgid ""
"``0`` - All nodes are rotated to a local Cartesian coordinate system where X"
" is the radial, Y axial and Z circumferential direction. All loads and "
"displacements are mapped from the 2D model to the 3D model in the local "
"coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:66
msgid ""
"If applying rotation ROTY in axisymmetric cases with torsion on the 2D "
"model, this value sets UZ = 0 at all corresponding 3D nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:69
msgid "This value is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:71
msgid ""
"``1`` - Only nodes with applied loads and/or displacements are rotated to a "
"local Cartesian coordinate system where X is the radial, Y axial and Z "
"circumferential direction. All loads are mapped to the 3D model and all "
"applied displacements are reset to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:75
msgid "See :ref:`bckeybehavior`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:91
msgid ""
"The :ref:`eextrude` command extrudes elements ``PLANE182`` and ``PLANE183``."
" Complementary elements ``TARGE169``, ``CONTA172``, and ``REINF263``  also "
"extrude. Extrusion operates automatically on elements in the selected "
"element set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:95
msgid ""
"``Action`` = TIRE determines if target elements are in the middle (rim) part"
" of the model or on the outside (road) part. The middle elements extrude "
"axisymmetrically about the Y axis, and the outside elements extrude in the Z"
" direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:99
msgid ""
"Example Command Actions If interference exists between road and tire, the "
"command extrudes outside elements within the specified tolerance ( "
":ref:`seltol` ) in the global Z direction. For more information, see `2D to "
"3D analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_adv/Hlp_G_ADV2DTO3DREST.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:105
msgid ""
"The ``BCKEY`` value is valid only within the 2D to 3D analysis environment "
"(that is, after issuing :ref:`map2dto3d`,START and before issuing "
":ref:`map2dto3d`,FINISH)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:108
msgid ""
"Use the default ``BCKEY`` = 0 setting if you intend to apply minimal new "
"loads or constraints during the 3D analysis phase; otherwise, set ``BCKEY`` "
"= 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:111
msgid ""
"For more information, including how boundary conditions and loads are mapped"
" from the 2D model to the 3D model, see `2D to 3D Analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_adv/Hlp_G_ADV2DTO3DREST.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:115
msgid ""
"Boundary Condition Key Behavior This command is valid in the PREP7 ( "
":ref:`prep7` ) and SOLUTION ( :ref:`slashsolu` ) processors. Some options "
"are valid within the 2D to 3D analysis environment only (between "
":ref:`map2dto3d` ,START and :ref:`map2dto3d`,FINISH)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:120
msgid ""
"For automatic ``PLANE182`` and ``PLANE183`` extrusion ( ``Action`` = AUTO), "
"based on the element behavior of the plane elements, the command performs as"
" follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:123
msgid "``KEYOPT(3) = 0`` - Plane stress; the element is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:125
msgid ""
"``KEYOPT(3) = 1`` - Axisymmetric; the element is extruded 360 degrees about "
"the Y-axis. ``THETA`` is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:128
msgid ""
"``KEYOPT(3) = 2`` - Plane strain (Z strain = 0.0); the element is extruded a"
" unit distance in the global Z direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:131
msgid ""
"``KEYOPT(3) = 3`` - Plane stress with thickness input; the element is "
"extruded in the Z-direction as specified by the thickness input via a real "
"constant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:134
msgid "``KEYOPT(3) = 5`` - Generalized plane strain; the element is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:136
msgid ""
"``KEYOPT(3) = 6`` - Axisymmetric with torsion; the element is extruded 360 "
"degrees about the Y-axis. ``THETA`` is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:139
msgid ""
"For an axisymmetric extrusion ( ``Action`` = AUTO with KEYOPT(3) = 1, "
"``Action`` = AXIS, or ``Action`` = TANGENT), the command merges any nodes "
"within the specified tolerance ( :ref:`seltol`, ``TOLER`` ) of the axis into"
" a single node, then forms degenerate tetrahedrons, pyramids, or wedges. The"
" default tolerance value is 1.0E-6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:144
msgid ""
"For an axisymmetric extrusion, ``SHELL208`` and ``SHELL209`` will extrude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:146
msgid "You can control shape-checking options via the :ref:`shpp` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:148
msgid ""
"The extrusion behavior of accompanying contact ( ``CONTA172`` ) is "
"determined by the plane element settings. Rigid target ( ``TARGE169`` ) "
"elements are extruded in the global Z direction unless axisymmetric "
"extrusion ( ``Action`` = AXIS or ``Action`` = TIRE) is in effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:152
msgid ""
"Within the 2D to 3D analysis environment (between :ref:`map2dto3d`,START and"
" :ref:`map2dto3d`,FINISH), ``PLANE182``, ``PLANE183``, and associated "
"contact/target/reinforcing elements are supported for the axisymmetric (with"
" or without torsion) and plane-strain options only. For ``REINF263`` "
"reinforcing elements, if the fibers have an orientation angle that causes "
"torsion in an axisymmetric analysis, use the axsiymmetrixc-with-torsion "
"option (KEYOPT(3) = 6) for the base elements. For more information, see `2D "
"to 3D Analysis Requirements and Limitations "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_adv/Hlp_G_ADV2DTO3DREQ.html#fnconta172173>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:160
msgid ""
"The following table shows each 2D element capable of extrusion and its "
"corresponding post-extrusion 3D element:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.eextrude:166
msgid ""
"All element properties are also transferred consistently during extrusion. "
"For example, a :math:`equation not available`  2D element is extruded to a  "
":math:`equation not available`  3D element, and a mixed u-P 2D element is "
"extruded to a mixed u-P 3D    element. Element and node components are "
"passed over the 3D elements and extruded nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:2
msgid "Generates a line of nodes between two existing nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `FILL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_FILL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:14
msgid ""
"Beginning and ending nodes for fill-in. ``NODE1`` defaults to next to last "
"node specified, ``NODE2`` defaults to last node specified. If ``NODE1`` = P,"
" graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:19
msgid ""
"Fill ``NFILL`` nodes between ``NODE1`` and ``NODE2`` (defaults to \\| "
"``NODE2`` - ``NODE1`` \\|-1). ``NFILL`` must be positive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:23
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:25
msgid ""
"Node number assigned to first filled-in node (defaults to ``NODE1`` + "
"``NINC`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:26
msgid ""
"Add this increment to each of the remaining filled-in node numbers (may be "
"positive or negative). Defaults to the integer result of ( ``NODE2`` - "
"``NODE1`` )/( ``NFILL`` + 1), that is, linear interpolation. If the default "
"evaluates to zero, or if zero is input, ``NINC`` is set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:32
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:36
msgid ""
"Do fill-in operation a total of ``ITIMEs``, incrementing ``NODE1``, "
"``NODE2`` and ``NSTRT`` by ``INC`` each time after the first. ``ITIME`` and "
"``INC`` both default to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.fill:57
msgid ""
"Generates a line of nodes (in the active coordinate system) between two "
"existing nodes. The two nodes may have been defined in any coordinate "
"system. Nodal locations and rotation angles are determined by interpolation."
" Any number of nodes may be filled-in and any node number sequence may be "
"assigned. See the :ref:`cscir` command when filling across the 180° "
"singularity line in a non- Cartesian system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:2
msgid "Calculates and moves a node to an intersection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MOVE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MOVE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:9
msgid ""
"Move this node. If ``NODE`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``NODE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:26
msgid ""
"Input one or two values defining the location of the node in this coordinate"
" system. Input \"U\" for unknown value(s) to be calculated and input \"E\" "
"to use an existing coordinate value. Fields are R1, θ1, Z1 for cylindrical, "
"or R1, θ1, Φ1 for spherical or toroidal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:39
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:44
msgid ""
"Input two or one value(s) defining the location of the node in this "
"coordinate system. Input \"U\" for unknown value(s) to be calculated and "
"input \"E\" to use an existing coordinate value. Fields are R2, θ2, Z2 for "
"cylindrical, or R2, θ2, Φ2 for spherical or toroidal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:62
msgid ""
"Calculates and moves a node to an intersection location. The node may have "
"been previously defined (at an approximate location) or left undefined (in "
"which case it is internally defined at the :ref:`source` location). The "
"actual location is calculated from the intersection of three surfaces "
"(implied from three coordinate constants in two different coordinate "
"systems). The three (of six) constants easiest to define should be used. The"
" program will calculate the remaining three coordinate constants. All "
"arguments, except ``KC1``, must be input. Use the repeat command ( "
"``*REPEAT`` ) after the :ref:`move` command to define a line of intersection"
" by repeating the move operation on all nodes of the line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:71
msgid ""
"Surfaces of constant value are implied by some commands by specifying a "
"single coordinate value. Implied surfaces are used with various commands ( "
":ref:`move`, :ref:`kmove`, :ref:`nsel`, etc.). Three surfaces are available "
"with each of the four coordinate system types. Values or X, Y, or Z may be "
"constant for the Cartesian coordinate system; values of R, θ, or Z for the "
"cylindrical system; and values of R, θ, Φ for the spherical and toroidal "
"systems. For example, an X value of 3 represents the Y-Z plane (or surface) "
"at X=3. In addition, the parameters for the cylindrical and spherical "
"coordinate systems may be adjusted ( :ref:`cs`, :ref:`local` ) to form "
"elliptical surfaces. For surfaces in elliptical coordinate systems, a "
"surface of \"constant\" radius is defined by the radius value at the X-axis."
" Surfaces of constant value may be located in local coordinate systems ( "
":ref:`local`, :ref:`clocal`, :ref:`cs`, or :ref:`cskp` ) to allow for any "
"orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:82
msgid ""
"The intersection calculation is based on an iterative procedure (250 "
"iterations maximum) and a tolerance of 1.0E-4. The approximate location of a"
" node should be sufficient to determine a unique intersection if more than "
"one intersection point is possible. Tangent \"intersections\" should be "
"avoided. If an intersection is not found, the node is placed at the last "
"iteration location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.move:87
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
