#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:2
msgid "Calculates and lists the distance between two nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NDIST "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NDIST.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:8
msgid "**nd1** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:9
msgid ""
"First node in distance calculation. If ``ND1`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:12
msgid "**nd2** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:13
msgid "Second node in distance calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:22
msgid "``[DIST, X, Y, Z]`` :obj:`distance` :obj:`between` :obj:`two` nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:36
msgid ""
":ref:`ndist` lists the distance between nodes ``ND1`` and ``ND2``, as well "
"as the current coordinate system offsets from ``ND1`` to ``ND2``, where the "
"X, Y, and Z locations of ``ND1`` are subtracted from the X, Y, and Z "
"locations of ``ND2`` (respectively) to determine the offsets. :ref:`ndist` "
"is valid in any coordinate system except toroidal ( :ref:`csys`,3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:41
msgid ""
":ref:`ndist` returns a variable, called \" ``_RETURN``,\" which contains the"
" distance value. You can use this value for various purposes, such as the "
"calculation of distributed loads. In interactive mode, you can access this "
"command by using the Model Query Picker ( Utility Menu> List> Picked "
"Entities ), where you can also access automatic annotation functions and "
"display the value on your model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ndist:52
msgid "Compute the distance between two nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:2
msgid "Generates additional nodes from a pattern of nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NGEN "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NGEN.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:13
msgid ""
"Do this generation operation a total of ``ITIME`` times, incrementing all "
"nodes in the given pattern by ``INC`` each time after the first. ``ITIME`` "
"must be > 1 for generation to occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:17
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:24
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:31
msgid ""
"Generate nodes from the pattern of nodes beginning with ``NODE1`` to "
"``NODE2`` (defaults to ``NODE1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If "
"``NODE1`` = ALL, ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is all "
"selected nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ). If ``NODE1`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may also be substituted for ``NODE1`` ( ``NODE2`` and"
" ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:53
msgid ""
"The average spacing ratio remains 1.0, such that the location of the last "
"generated set will be the same regardless of ``SPACE``. ``SPACE`` only "
"serves to skew the position of the nodes between the pattern set and the "
"last set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.ngen:71
msgid ""
"Generates additional nodes from a given node pattern. Generation is done in "
"the active coordinate system. Nodes in the pattern may have been generated "
"in any coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nkpt.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nkpt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
