#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NROTAT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NROTAT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:23
msgid ""
"Rotate nodes from ``NODE1`` to ``NODE2`` (defaults to ``NODE1`` ) in steps "
"of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NODE1`` = ALL, ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored and all selected nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ) are rotated. If ``NODE1`` = "
"P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored"
" (valid only in the GUI). A component name may also be substituted for "
"``NODE1`` ( ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:43
msgid ""
"Rotates nodal coordinate systems into the active coordinate system. Nodal "
"coordinate systems may be automatically rotated into the active (global or "
"local) coordinate system as follows: Rotations in Cartesian systems will "
"have nodal x directions rotated parallel to the Cartesian X direction. "
"Rotations in cylindrical, spherical or toroidal systems will have the nodal "
"x directions rotated parallel to the R direction. Nodes at (or near) a zero "
"radius location should not be rotated. Nodal coordinate directions may be "
"displayed ( :ref:`psymb` ). Nodal forces and constraints will also appear "
"rotated when displayed if the nodal coordinate system is rotated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:51
msgid ""
"When the nodal coordinate systems are defined, they remain parallel to the "
"global Cartesian system unless subsequently rotated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:54
msgid "Previously specified rotations on the specified nodes are overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrotat:56
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`nmodif`, :ref:`nang`, and :ref:`nora` commands for other "
"rotation options."
msgstr ""

