"Node range is defined from ``NMIN`` (defaults to 1) to ``NMAX`` (defaults to"
" 999999999) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrrang:12
msgid "**nmax** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nrrang:34
msgid ""
"Defines the range of nodes to be read ( :ref:`nread` ) from the node file. "
"Also implies an element range since only elements fully attached to these "
"nodes will be read from the element file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:2
msgid "Generates a scaled set of nodes from a pattern of nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NSCALE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NSCALE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:9
msgid ""
"Do this scaling operation one time, incrementing all nodes in the given "
"pattern by ``INC``. If ``INC`` = 0, nodes will be redefined at the scaled "
"locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:20
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:27
msgid ""
"Scale nodes from pattern of nodes beginning with ``NODE1`` to ``NODE2`` "
"(defaults to ``NODE1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NODE1`` "
"= ALL, ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and pattern is all selected nodes "
"( :ref:`nsel` ). If ``NODE1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``NODE1`` ( ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:39
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:44
msgid ""
"Scale factor ratios. Scaling is relative to the origin of the active "
"coordinate system (RR, Rθ, RZ for cylindrical, RR, Rθ, RΦ for spherical or "
"toroidal). If absolute value of ratio > 1.0, pattern is enlarged. If < 1.0, "
"pattern is reduced. Ratios default to 1.0 (each)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nscale:62
msgid ""
"Generates a scaled pattern of nodes from a given node pattern. Scaling is "
"done in the active coordinate system. Nodes in the pattern may have been "
"generated in any coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth:2
msgid "Smooths selected nodes among selected elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NSMOOTH "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NSMOOTH.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth:8
msgid "**npass** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth:9
msgid "Number of smoothing passes. Defaults to 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsmooth:25
msgid ""
"Repositions each selected node at the average position of its immediate "
"neighbors on the selected elements. The node positions converge after some "
"number of smoothing passes. For some initial conditions, ``NPASS`` may need "
"to be much larger than 3. If the boundary of a mesh is to be undisturbed "
"(usually desirable), the boundary nodes should be unselected before issuing "
":ref:`nsmooth`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:2
msgid "Generates a reflected set of nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NSYM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NSYM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:18
msgid ""
"Increment all nodes in the given pattern by ``INC`` to form the reflected "
"node pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:28
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:35
msgid ""
"Reflect nodes from pattern beginning with ``NODE1`` to ``NODE2`` (defaults "
"to ``NODE1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NODE1`` = ALL, "
"``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and pattern is all selected nodes ( "
":ref:`nsel` ). If ``NODE1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``NODE1`` ( ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:55
msgid ""
"Generates nodes from a given node pattern by a symmetry reflection. "
"Reflection is done in the active coordinate system by changing a particular "
"coordinate sign. Nodes in the pattern may have been generated in any "
"coordinate system. Nodal rotation angles are not reflected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nsym:59
msgid ""
"Symmetry reflection may be used with any node pattern, in any coordinate "
"system, as many times as desired. Reflection is accomplished by a coordinate"
" sign change (in the active coordinate system). For example, an X-reflection"
" in a Cartesian coordinate system generates additional nodes from a given "
"pattern, with a node increment added to each node number, and an X "
"coordinate sign change. An R-reflection in a cylindrical coordinate system "
"gives a reflected \"radial\" location by changing the \"equivalent\" "
"Cartesian (that is, the Cartesian system with the same origin as the active "
"cylindrical system) X and Y coordinate signs. An R-reflection in a spherical"
" coordinate system gives a reflected \"radial\" location by changing the "
"equivalent Cartesian X, Y, and Z coordinate location signs. Nodal coordinate"
" system rotation angles are not reflected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:2
msgid "Writes nodes to a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NWRITE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NWRITE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:38
msgid ""
"Writes selected nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ]) to a file. The write operation is not"
" necessary in a standard Mechanical APDL run but is provided as a "
"convenience to those who want coded node file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:41
msgid ""
"Data are written in a coded format. The format used is (I9, 6G21.13E3) to "
"write out ``NODE``, ``X``, ``Y``, ``Z``, ``THXY``, ``THYZ``, ``THZX``. If "
"the last number is zero ( ``THZX`` = 0), or the last set of numbers are "
"zero, they are not written but are left blank. Therefore, use a formatted "
"read to process this file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.nwrite:46
msgid "Coordinate values are in the global Cartesian system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:2
msgid "Generates a quadratic line of nodes from three nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `QUAD "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_QUAD.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:9
msgid ""
"Begin fill-in from this node location. If ``NODE1`` = P, graphical picking "
"is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:12
msgid "**nintr** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:13
msgid ""
"Intermediate or guiding node. Quadratic curve will pass through this "
"location. ``NINTR`` may have any node number and any location. If the "
"quadratic line also generates a node with number ``NINTR``, the generated "
"location overrides the previous ``NINTR`` location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:18
msgid "End quadratic fill-in at this node location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:21
msgid ""
"Fill-in ``NFILL`` nodes between ``NODE1`` and ``NODE2`` (defaults to | "
"``NODE2`` - ``NODE1`` |-1). ``NFILL`` must be positive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:28
msgid ""
"Add this increment to each of the remaining filled-in node numbers (may be "
"positive or negative). Defaults to ( ``NODE2`` - ``NODE1`` )/( ``NFILL`` + "
"1), that is, linear interpolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:32
msgid "**pkfac** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:33
msgid ""
"Peak location factor. If ``PKFAC`` =0.5, the peak of the quadratic shape "
"occurs at the ``NINTR`` location. If 0.0 < ``PKFAC`` < 0.5, the peak occurs "
"to the ``NODE2`` side of the ``NINTR`` location. If 0.5 < ``PKFAC`` < 1.0, "
"the peak occurs to the ``NODE1`` side of the ``NINTR`` location. Defaults to"
" 0.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:52
msgid ""
"Generates a quadratic line of nodes (in the active coordinate system) from "
"three nodes. The three nodes determine the plane of the curve and may have "
"been defined in any coordinate system. Any number of nodes may be filled-in "
"and any node number sequence may be assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:56
msgid ""
"The quadratic line feature uses three nodes ( ``NODE1``, ``NINTR``, "
"``NODE2`` ) to determine the plane of the curve. The curve passes through "
"the three points, beginning from ``NODE1``, through the intermediate (or "
"guiding) point ``NINTR``, and toward ``NODE2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:60
msgid ""
"Generated nodes are also quadratically spaced. If the guiding node number is"
" within the set being generated, it will be relocated according to the "
"quadratic spacing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.quad:63
msgid ""
"The peak location factor is used to determine how the quadratic fits through"
" the three points. Various nodal progressions can be obtained by different "
"combinations of ``PKFAC`` and the guiding node location. If the guiding node"
" is at mid-length between ``NODE1`` and ``NODE2``, 0.293 :math:`equation not"
" available`   ``PKFAC`` < 0.707 will ensure that all generated nodes fall "
"within the ``NODE1``, ``NODE2`` bounds. In the limit, as ``PKFAC`` "
"approaches 0.0, the peak approaches the line through ``NODE1`` and ``NINTR``"
" at an infinite distance from ``NODE1``. The :ref:`quad` command generates "
"quadratic lines of nodes, which in turn may be used as a base line for "
"generating irregular surfaces of nodes (by repeating ( ``*REPEAT`` ), "
"generating ( :ref:`ngen`, :ref:`nscale` ), etc.). Irregular surfaces may "
"also be generated with the meshing commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/nodes.rst:43:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:2
msgid "Transfers a pattern of nodes to another coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `TRANSFER "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_TRANSFER.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:13
msgid ""
"Increment all nodes in the given pattern by ``INC`` to form the transferred "
"node pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:23
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:30
msgid ""
"Transfer nodes from pattern beginning with ``NODE1`` to ``NODE2`` (defaults "
"to ``NODE1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NODE1`` = ALL, "
"``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is all selected nodes ( "
":ref:`nsel` ). If ``NODE1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"may be substituted for ``NODE1`` ( ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:50
msgid ""
"Transfers a pattern of nodes from one coordinate system to another. "
"Coordinate systems may be translated and rotated relative to each other. "
"Initial pattern may be generated in any coordinate system. Coordinate values"
" are interpreted in the active coordinate system and are transferred "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/nodes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.nodes.Nodes.transfer:55
msgid ""
"A model generated in one coordinate system may be transferred to another "
"coordinate system. The user may define several coordinate systems "
"(translated and rotated from each other), generate a model in one coordinate"
" system, and then repeatedly transfer the model to other coordinate systems."
" The model may be generated in any type of coordinate system (Cartesian, "
"cylindrical, etc.) and transferred to any other type of coordinate system. "
"Coordinate values (X, Y, Z, or R, θ, Z, or etc.) of the model being "
"transferred are interpreted in the active coordinate system type, regardless"
" of how they were generated. Values are transferred directly and are "
"interpreted according to the type of coordinate system being transferred to."
" For example, transferring from a Cartesian coordinate system to a "
"cylindrical coordinate system (not recommended) would cause X = 2.0 and Y = "
"3.0 values to be directly interpreted as R = 2.0 and θ = 3.0 values, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.piping.Piping.bellow.rst:2
