"file. No other postprocessing is available for this modal solve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycfreq:180
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`cycfreq`,RESTART, only mistuning parameters or frequency "
"range may be changed. All other changes in parameters are ignored. This type"
" of restart can only be performed by exiting the current mistuning solution "
"using :ref:`finish` and re-entering the solution phase using "
":ref:`slashsolu` and then calling the desired :ref:`cycfreq`,RESTART "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycfreq:192
msgid ""
"`Analysis and Solution Controls section of the Technology Showcase Example "
"Problem: Forced-response analysis of a mistuned bladed disk with aerodamping"
" "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_tec/tecmistuninganalysis.html#tecmistuning_nonlinmsup_mistuned>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycfreq:196
msgid ""
"For an example demonstrating how to apply modal loads directly in the cyclic"
" harmonic analysis step of a mode-superposition harmonic cyclic symmetry "
"analysis, see."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/special_purpose.rst:35:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:2
msgid "Specifies a cyclic symmetry analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `CYCLIC "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CYCLIC.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:10
msgid ""
"The default :ref:`cyclic` command (issuing the command with no arguments) "
"detects the number of sectors ( ``NSECTOR`` ), the sector angle ( ``ANGLE`` "
"), and the coordinate system ( ``KCN`` ) based upon the existing solid or "
"finite-element model. The command also detects sector low- and high-edge "
"components in most cases and assigns the default root name CYCLIC to the "
"components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:18
msgid ""
"The number of sectors in the full 360 degrees, or one of the following "
"options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:20
msgid "``STATUS`` - Indicates the current cyclic status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:22
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - Resets model to normal (non-cyclic) status and removes the "
"duplicate sector if it exists. This option also deletes automatically "
"detected edge components (generated when ``USRCOMP`` = 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:26
msgid ""
"``UNDOUBLE`` - Removes the duplicate sector if it exists. The duplicate "
"sector is created during the solution ( :ref:`solve` ) stage of a modal "
"cyclic symmetry analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:29
msgid ""
"The duplicate sector is necessary for displaying cyclic symmetry analysis "
"results during postprocessing ( :ref:`post1` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:32
msgid ""
"If you specify a value of STATUS, OFF or UNDOUBLE, the command ignores all "
"remaining arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:35
msgid "The sector angle in degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:38
msgid ""
"An arbitrary reference number assigned to the cyclic coordinate system. The "
"default value of 0 specifies automatic detection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:42
msgid ""
"The root name of sector low- and high-edge components (line, area, or node "
"components). The default root name (when ``USRCOMP`` = 0) is CYCLIC. A root "
"name that you specify can contain up to 11 characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:46
msgid ""
"The naming convention for each low- and high-edge component pair is either "
"of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:48
msgid ""
"``Name`` _m ``xx`` l, ``Name`` _m ``xx`` h (potentially matched node "
"patterns)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:49
msgid ""
"``Name`` _u ``xx`` l, ``Name`` _u ``xx`` h (potentially unmatched node "
"patterns)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:51
msgid ""
"The ``Name`` value is the default ( CYCLIC ) or specified root name and "
"``xx`` is the component pair ID number (sequential, starting at 01)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:54
msgid "**usrcomp** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:55
msgid ""
"The number of pairs of user-defined low- and high-edge components on the "
"cyclic sector (if any). The default value of 0 specifies automatic detection"
" of sector edges; however, the automatic setting is not valid in all cases. "
"(For more information, see the Notes section below.) If the value is greater"
" than 0, no verification of user-defined components occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:61
msgid ""
"The name of a user-defined array specifying the matching node pairs between "
"the sector low and high edges. Valid only when ``USRCOMP`` = 0. Skips the "
"automatic detection of sector edges. Node pairs may be input in any order, "
"but the low edge node must be the first entry in each pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:88
msgid ""
"You can input your own value for ``NSECTOR``, ``ANGLE`` or ``KCN`` ; if you "
"do so, the command verifies argument values before executing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:91
msgid ""
"When ``USRCOMP`` = 0 and ``UsrNMap`` = blank (default), the :ref:`cyclic` "
"command automatically detects `low- and high-edge components "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycedgecomp.html#>`_"
" for models that consist of any combination of line, area, or volume "
"elements. If a solid model exists, however, the command uses only the lines,"
" areas, and/or volumes to determine the low- and high-edge components; the "
"elements, if any, are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:98
msgid ""
"Nodes will be automatically rotated unless :ref:`cycopt`,USRROT,YES has been"
" specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:100
msgid ""
"If you issue a :ref:`cycopt`,TOLER command to set a tolerance for edge-"
"component pairing before issuing the :ref:`cyclic` command, the "
":ref:`cyclic` command uses the specified tolerance when performing automatic"
" edge-component detection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:104
msgid ""
"For 2D models, autodetection does not consider the :ref:`csys`,5 or "
":ref:`csys`,6 coordinate system specification. Autodetection for 180 degree "
"(two-sector) models is not possible unless a central hole exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:108
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cyclic` command sets values and keys so that, if possible, the "
"area-mesh ( :ref:`amesh` ) or volume-mesh ( :ref:`vmesh` ) command meshes "
"the sector with matching node and element face patterns on the low and high "
"edges. (The command has no effect on any other element-creation command.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:113
msgid ""
"Issue the :ref:`cyclic` command prior to the meshing command to, if "
"possible, produce a mesh with identical node and element patterns on the low"
" and high sector edges. Only the :ref:`amesh` or :ref:`vmesh` commands can "
"perform automated matching. (Other meshing operation commands such as "
":ref:`vsweep` cannot.) If you employ a meshing operation other than "
":ref:`amesh` or :ref:`vmesh`, you should ensure that node and element face "
"patterns match, if desired. The :ref:`cyclic` command output indicates "
"whether each edge-component pair has or can produce a matching node pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:120
msgid ""
"A cyclic solution (via the :ref:`solve` command) allows dissimilar mesh "
"patterns on the extreme boundaries of a cyclically symmetric model. The "
"allowance for dissimilar patterns is useful when you have only finite-"
"element meshes for your model but not the geometry data necessary to remesh "
"it to obtain identical node patterns. In such cases, it is possible to "
"obtain solution results, although perhaps at the expense of accuracy. A "
"warning message appears because results may be degraded near the sector "
"edges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:127
msgid ""
"The constraint equations (CEs) that tie together the low and high edges of "
"your model are generated at the solution stage of the analysis from the low-"
" and high-edge components (and nowhere else). You should verify that "
"automatically detected components are in the correct locations and that you "
"can account for all components; to do so, you can list ( :ref:`cmlist` ) or "
"plot ( :ref:`cmplot` ) the components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:133
msgid ""
"If you issue the :ref:`cyclic` command after meshing and have defined "
"element types with rotational degrees of freedom (DOFs), Mechanical APDL "
"generates cyclic CEs for rotational DOFs that may not exist on the sector "
"boundaries. Issue :ref:`cycopt`,DOF to prevent unused rotational terms from "
"being generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:139
msgid ""
"Modal cyclic symmetry analysis is supported by the following eigensolvers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:141
msgid "Block Lanczos ( :ref:`modopt`,LANB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:143
msgid "PCG Lanczos ( :ref:`modopt`,LANPCG)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:145
msgid "Super Node ( :ref:`modopt`,SNODE)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:147
msgid "Subspace ( :ref:`modopt`,SUBSP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cyclic:152
msgid ""
"When using the :ref:`cyclic` command to automatically detect the sector, if "
"an area is defined with the :ref:`al` command, the lines need to be oriented"
" to form the closed curve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/special_purpose.rst:35:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:2
msgid "Specifies solution options for a cyclic symmetry analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `CYCOPT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CYCOPT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:9
msgid ""
"Cyclic symmetry analysis option. There is no default. You must choose o ne "
"of the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:11
msgid ""
"``BCMULT`` - Controls whether cyclic sector array parameter names are reused"
" or created new for multiple entities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:27
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:118
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:130
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:184
msgid "``Value1`` - The flag value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:16
msgid "``0 (OFF or NO)`` - Create new array parameter names (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:18
msgid "``1(ON or YES)`` - Reuse array parameter names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:20
msgid ""
"``COMBINE`` - For linear `static cyclic symmetry analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycstaticans.html#cycsym_postproc_stat>`_"
" with `non-cyclically symmetric loading "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycsolarch.html#>`_"
" only, expands and combines all harmonic index solutions and writes them to "
"the results file during the solution phase of the analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:29
msgid ""
"``0 (OFF or NO)`` - Disable combining of harmonic index solutions (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:31
msgid "``1 (ON or YES)`` - Enable combining of harmonic index solutions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:33
msgid "``DEFAULT`` - Set the default cyclic solution settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:35
msgid ""
"``DOF`` - The degrees of freedom to couple from the nodes on the low sector "
"boundary to nodes on the high boundary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:38
msgid "``Value1`` - The component pair ID number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:40
msgid ""
"``Value2, Value3, Value4, ..., Value7`` - The constraint-equation/-coupling "
"degree of freedom (DOF) for this pair. Repeat the command to add other DOFs."
" The default is constraint- equation/-coupling all applicable DOFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:44
msgid ""
"``FACETOL`` - Tolerance for inclusion of surface nodes into your base "
"sector. Autodetect defaults to 15°, accommodating most sections. Specify a "
"new ``Value1`` only when extreme cut angles or complex model geometry cause "
"surface nodes to be excluded. See Notes (below) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:48
msgid ""
"Ansys, Inc. recommends that successful auto-detection depends more on the "
"value of ANGTOL than the value of FACETOL. Please refer to `CYCOPTAuto "
"Detection Tolerance Adjustments for Difficult Cases "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycedgecomp.html#gadvcycopttol7>`_"
" :ref:`cycopt` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:54
msgid ""
"``Value1`` - The face tolerance applies only to auto detection from "
"node/element models (already meshed and no solid model), and it defaults to "
"15°."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:57
msgid ""
"``HINDEX`` - The `harmonic index "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#harmindex>`_"
" ranges to be solved. Applies to static and harmonic analyses only if "
":ref:`CYCOPT_HINDEXValue5` ``Value5`` = STATIC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:62
msgid ""
"By default, the :ref:`solve` command loops through all available harmonic "
"indices. `Static "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycstaticans.html#cycsym_postproc_stat>`_"
" and `harmonic "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#harmindex>`_"
" analyses only solve harmonic indices required for the applied loads. All "
"other analyses solve them all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:69
msgid ""
"``EVEN / ODD`` - For low-frequency electromagnetic analysis only, EVEN "
"specifies a symmetric solution and ODD specifies an antisymmetric solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:72
msgid ""
"The value you specify is based on the `harmonic index "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#harmindex>`_"
" : EVEN (default) indicates harmonic index = 0, and ODD indicates harmonic "
"index = ``N`` / 2 (where ``N`` is an integer representing the number of "
"sectors in 360°). A value of ODD applies only when ``N`` is an even number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:78
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cycopt` command with this HINDEX option is cumulative. To remove "
"an option (for example, EVEN), issue this command: "
":ref:`cycopt`,HINDEX,EVEN,,,-1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:81
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - Solve all applicable harmonic indices. ``Value2`` must be blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:83
msgid ""
"``Value1, Value2, Value3`` - Solve harmonic indices in range ``Value1`` "
"through ``Value2`` in steps of ``Value3``. Repeat the command to add other "
"ranges. The default solves all applicable harmonic indices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:87
msgid ""
"``Value4`` - The only valid value is -1. If specified, it removes ``Value1``"
" through ``Value2`` in steps of ``Value3`` from the set to solve. By "
"default, if ``Value4`` = -1 then ``Value1`` = 0, ``Value2`` = 0, and "
"``Value3`` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:91
msgid ""
"``Value5`` - For `static "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycstaticans.html#cycsym_postproc_stat>`_"
" and `harmonic "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#harmindex>`_"
" analyses, enter either a number or STATIC:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:97
msgid ""
"If ``Value5`` = <number>  the number entered sets the tolerance for "
"determining if the Fourier contribution of a load is significant (default = "
"1.0E-5). In this case, the harmonic index selection is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:101
msgid ""
"If ``Value5`` = STATIC the harmonic index selection is enabled, and no "
"verification is done on the significance of unselected harmonic indicies. "
"Improper selection of the harmonic index range may produce incomplete "
"(incorrect) results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:105
msgid ""
"``LDSECT`` - Restricts subsequently defined force loads and surface loads to"
" a specified sector. The restriction remains in effect until you change or "
"reset it. This option is not available for harmonic analyses based on mode-"
"superposition ( :ref:`cycopt`,MSUP,1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:109
msgid ""
"``Value1`` - The sector number. A value other than 0 (default) is valid for "
"a cyclic symmetry analysis with `non- cyclically symmetric loading "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycsolarch.html#>`_"
" only. A value of 0 (or ALL) resets the default behavior for cyclic loading "
"(where the loads are identical on all sectors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:115
msgid ""
"``MOVE`` - Specifies if the program should move high- or low-edge component "
"nodes paired within the specified tolerance (TOLER) to create precisely "
"matching pairs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:120
msgid "``0`` - Do not move edge component nodes (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:122
msgid ""
"``1 or HIGH`` - Move the high-edge component nodes to precisely match the "
"low-edge component nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:124
msgid ""
"``-1 or LOW`` - Move the low-edge component nodes to precisely match the "
"high-edge component nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:126
msgid ""
"``MSUP`` - This flag is used to limit the results written to the "
":file:`Jobname.MODE` and :file:`Jobname.RST` files in a modal cyclic "
"symmetry analysis. In a linear perturbation analysis, the modal analysis and"
" the first load step of the preceding base analysis must be set to the same "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:132
msgid ""
"``0 (OFF or NO)`` - Write results for the base and duplicate sectors to the "
":file:`Jobname.MODE` and :file:`Jobname.RST` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:135
msgid ""
"``1 (ON or YES)`` - Write only the base sector results to the "
":file:`Jobname.MODE` and :file:`Jobname.RST` files for use in a subsequent "
"mode-superposition-based analysis. Default, except for cyclic unsymmetric "
"modal, LANPCG, and SNODE solutions, which use ``Value1`` = 0 as the default."
" This option is not valid for cyclic unsymmetric modal, LANPCG, and SNODE "
"solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:140
msgid ""
"``STATUS`` - List the solution option settings active for the cyclic model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:142
msgid ""
"``TOLER`` - The tolerance used to determine whether a node on the low edge "
"is paired with a node on the high edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:145
msgid "``Value1`` - The tolerance value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:147
msgid ""
"``Greater than 0`` - The absolute distance tolerance for automatic sector-"
"boundary detection and low-/high-edge component node pairing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:150
msgid ""
"``Less than 0`` - The relative tolerance for automatic sector-boundary "
"detection and low-/high-edge component node pairing. In this case, the "
"tolerance is ``Value1`` \\* ``Length``, where ``Length`` is the length of "
"the diagonal of an imaginary box enclosing the model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:153
msgid "``0`` - Tolerance is set to -1.0 x 10 :sup:`-4` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:155
msgid ""
"``Value2`` - ``ANGTOL`` = Maximum allowable angle tolerance. (default = "
"0.01°)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:157
msgid "The valid range for ``ANGTOL`` is model dependent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:159
msgid ""
"If you input both the number of sectors and a sector angle, the angle must "
"match 360/(number of sectors) within ``ANGTOL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:162
msgid ""
"If you input only a sector angle, it must divide evenly into 360° within "
"``ANGTOL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:164
msgid ""
"If you input a sector angle, the final cyclic sector must span that angle "
"within ``ANGTOL``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:166
msgid ""
"For auto detected sector angle, the final cyclic sector must span "
"360/(number of sectors) within ``ANGTOL``, everywhere along the LOW/HIGH "
"boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:169
msgid ""
"If ``ANGTOL`` is too small, your CAD or FEA model may not be accurate enough"
" to allow auto detection or verification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:172
msgid ""
"If ``ANGTOL`` is too large, you may get an unexpected or incorrect boundary "
"definition, or in other cases fail to detect the boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:175
msgid ""
"For some difficult cases from FEA models (not solid models), you may need to"
" change the value of ``FACETOL`` to achieve auto detection. Please refer to "
"`CYCOPTAuto Detection Tolerance Adjustments for Difficult Cases "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycedgecomp.html#gadvcycopttol7>`_"
" :ref:`cycopt` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:181
msgid ""
"``USRROT`` - Flag specifying whether the program should override automatic "
"nodal rotations to edge components and allow you to apply nodal rotations "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:186
msgid "``0 (OFF or NO)`` - Allow automatic node rotation (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:188
msgid ""
"``1 (ON or YES)`` - Suppress automatic node rotation. If you select this "
"option, you must apply appropriate nodal rotations to all edge component "
"nodes; otherwise, your analysis will yield incorrect solution results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:192
msgid ""
"``LOW`` - Suppresses automatic rotation of low-edge component nodes only, "
"allowing you to apply them manually. Automatic rotation of high-edge "
"component nodes occurs to produce the matching edge nodes required for a "
"valid cyclic solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:196
msgid ""
"``HIGH`` - Suppresses automatic rotation of high-edge component nodes only, "
"allowing you to apply them manually. Automatic rotation of low-edge "
"component nodes occurs to produce the matching edge nodes required for a "
"valid cyclic solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:201
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:207
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:213
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:219
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:225
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:231
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:237
msgid ""
"The description of the argument is missing in the Python function. Please, "
"refer to the `command documentation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CYCOPT.html>`_"
" for further information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:230
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:111
msgid "**value6** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:236
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:117
msgid "**value7** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:259
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cycopt`,COMBINE option is an alternative to the :ref:`cycexpand` "
"command and is especially useful for testing purposes. However, Ansys, Inc. "
"recommends specifying COMBINE only when the number of sectors is relatively "
"small. (The option expands nodes and elements into the full 360° and can "
"slow postprocessing significantly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:264
msgid ""
"If you issue a :ref:`cycopt`,TOLER command to set a tolerance for `edge-"
"component "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycedgecomp.html#>`_"
" pairing before issuing the :ref:`cyclic` command, the :ref:`cyclic` command"
" uses the specified tolerance when performing automatic edge-component "
"detection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:269
msgid ""
"In cases involving `non-cyclically symmetric loading "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycsolarch.html#>`_"
" (that is, when LDSECT > 0), the underlying command operations create or "
"modify the required SECTOR tabular boundary condition (BC) data to apply on "
"the appropriate sector. Therefore, it is not necessary to manipulate tables "
"for situations where the applied BC is not a function of other tabular BC "
"variables such as TIME, X, Y, Z, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:276
msgid ""
"To delete a previously applied load on a specified sector, issue an "
":ref:`fdele` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:278
msgid ""
"Because edge nodes are rotated into the cyclic coordinate system during "
"solution, any applied displacements or forces on sector edges will be in the"
" cyclic coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:281
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cycopt` command is valid in the preprocessing and solution stages "
"of an analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.cycopt:286
msgid ""
"Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction The COMBINE option is not "
"supported in a DMP solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/special_purpose.rst:35:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym:2
msgid "Specifies circular symmetry for electromagnetic sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EMSYM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EMSYM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym:8
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:52
msgid "**nsect** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym:9
msgid "The number of circular symmetry sections (defaults to 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.emsym:25
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of times to repeat electromagnetic sources for circular"
" symmetry. Applies to ``SOURC36`` elements and to coupled-field elements "
"with electric current conduction results in the database. Sources are "
"assumed to be equally spaced over 360° about the global Cartesian Z axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.special\\_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/special_purpose.rst:35:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:2
msgid ""
"Specifies solution options for a `multistage cyclic symmetry analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mstag/ans_mstag_introTheory.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:5
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MSOPT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MSOPT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:10
msgid ""
"Multistage cyclic symmetry analysis option. There is no default. You must "
"choose one of the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:13
msgid ""
"``CSYS`` - Activates a previously defined cyclic coordinate system by the "
"reference number specified in ``Value1``. ``Sname`` is ignored. This option "
"is only valid in the /PREP7 processor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:16
msgid ""
"``Value1`` - Cylindrical coordinate system reference number. You must have "
"already created the coordinate system by issuing prior commands like "
":ref:`cs` or :ref:`local` to define it. Defaults to 1 where the global "
"Cartesian Z axis is the cyclic symmetry axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:20
msgid "You must define the coordinate system before defining the stages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:22
msgid ""
"``NEW`` - Creates a new stage with the name entered in ``Sname`` and the "
"``Value1`` - ``Value6`` specifications listed in the table below. This "
"option is only valid in the /PREP7 processor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:25
msgid ""
"``Sname`` - An alphanumeric name used to identify the stage. ``Sname`` may "
"be up to 32 characters, beginning with a letter and containing only letters,"
" numbers, and underscores. Names beginning with an underscore (for example, "
"_LOOP) are reserved for use by Mechanical APDL and should be avoided. The "
"component name ALL is not permitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:33
msgid ""
"When creating a new stage, the base and duplicate sector meshes should be "
"coincident. The offset between the number of base and duplicate coincident "
"nodes is constant throughout the whole model. The same is true for the "
"element numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:37
msgid "``DELETE`` - Deletes the stage identified by ``Sname``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:39
msgid ""
"``Sname`` - The name of the stage to be deleted. Entities such as nodes and "
"elements contained in the stage are unaffected. Only the grouping and the "
"related constraint equations are concerned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:42
msgid ""
"``EXPAND`` - Specifies stages (identified by ``Sname`` ) and sectors (sector"
" number specified in ``Value1`` ) for subsequent expansion. This option is "
"only valid in the /POST1 processor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:45
msgid ""
"``Sname`` - The name of the stage to be expanded. A value of 0 resets all "
"expansion settings. A value of ALL means all existing stages will be "
"expanded (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:48
msgid ""
"``Value1`` - The sector number. A value of 0 resets all sector settings. A "
"value of ALL means all sectors will be expanded (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:51
msgid ""
"``LIST`` - Lists the stage identified by ``Sname`` with the level of detail "
"specified in ``Value1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:53
msgid ""
"``Sname`` - The name of the stage to be listed. If blank, list all stages "
"(default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:55
msgid "``Value1`` - Key for specifying the level of detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:57
msgid "``0 (, or OFF)`` - Basic listing (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:59
msgid ""
"``1 (, or ON)`` - Detailed listing, including constraint equations "
"information. Note that the interstage constraint equations number "
"information is only listed for the stage with the smallest number of "
"sectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:63
msgid ""
"``MODIFY`` - Sets the `harmonic index "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#harmindex>`_"
" of a stage identified by ``Sname`` to the integer specified in ``Value1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:67
msgid "``Sname`` - The name of the stage to be modified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:69
msgid ""
"``Value1`` - The new `harmonic index "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cycsym/advcycmodalans.html#harmindex>`_."
" Existing cyclic and multistage interface constraint equations will be "
"deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:73
msgid ""
"``RESET`` - Deletes all stages and resets all multistage analysis settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/special_purpose.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.special_purpose.SpecialPurpose.msopt:75
msgid "**sname** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

