#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SETRAN "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SETRAN.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:9
msgid ""
"The name (case-sensitive) of the file containing the original superelement "
"matrix created by the generation pass ( :file:`Sename.SUB` ). The default is"
" the current :file:`Jobname`. If ``Sename`` is a number, it is the element "
"number of a previously defined superelement in the current use pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:15
msgid ""
"The reference number of the coordinate system to where the superelement is "
"to be transferred. The default is the global Cartesian system. Transfer "
"occurs from the active coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:19
msgid ""
"The node offset. The default is zero. All new element node numbers are "
"offset from those on the original by ``INC``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:23
msgid ""
"File name and directory path (248 characters maximum, including the "
"characters needed for the directory path). An unspecified directory path "
"defaults to the working directory; in this case, you can use all 248 "
"characters for the file name. This field requires input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:31
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:37
msgid ""
"Node location increments in the global Cartesian coordinate system. Defaults"
" to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:39
msgid "**norot** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:40
msgid "Node rotation :ref:`key: <NOROTnotes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:42
msgid ""
"``0`` - The nodal coordinate systems of the transferred superelement rotate "
"into the ``KCNTO`` system. (That is, the nodal coordinate systems rotate "
"with the superelement.) The superelement matrices remain unchanged. This "
"value is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:46
msgid ""
"``1`` - The nodal coordinate systems do not rotate. (That is, they remain "
"fixed in their original global orientation.) The superelement matrices and "
"load vectors are modified if any rotations occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:63
msgid ""
"The :ref:`setran` command creates a superelement from an existing "
"superelement and writes the new element to a file. You can then issue an "
":ref:`se` command to read the new element (during the `use pass "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_substr/an9Auq1d6ldm.html#advobsl5jla062999>`_"
" )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:69
msgid "You can create a superelement from an original by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:71
msgid ""
"Transferring the original's geometry from the active coordinate system into "
"another coordinate system ( ``KCNTO`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:74
msgid ""
"Offsetting its geometry in the global Cartesian coordinate system ( ``DX``, "
"``DY``, and ``DZ`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:76
msgid "Offsetting its node numbers ( ``INC`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:78
msgid ""
"A combination of methods is valid. If you specify both the geometry transfer"
" and the geometry offset, the transfer occurs first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:81
msgid ""
"If you specify rotation of the transferred superelement's nodal coordinate "
"systems into the ``KCNTO`` system ( ``NOROT`` = 0), the rotated nodes cannot"
" be coupled via the :ref:`cp` command; in this case, issue the :ref:`ce` "
"command instead. If you specify no rotation of the nodal coordinate systems "
"( ``NOROT`` = 1) for models with displacement degrees of freedom, and "
"``KCNTO`` is not the active system, the superelement ``Sename`` must have "
"six MDOF at each node that has MDOF; therefore, only elements with all six "
"structural DOFs are valid in such cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/superelements.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.superelements.Superelements.setran:88
msgid ""
"There is no limit to the number of copies that can be made of a "
"superelement, provided the copies are all generated from the same original "
"superelement. However, nested copies are limited to five. In other words, "
"the total number of different ``Sename`` usages on the :ref:`setran` and "
":ref:`sesymm` commands is limited to five."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.extopt.rst:2
