#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdele:34
msgid ""
"``1`` - Delete volumes, as well as keypoints, lines, and areas attached to "
"the specified volumes but not shared by other volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl:2
msgid "Lists keypoints of a volume that lie on a parametric degeneracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VDGL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VDGL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl:17
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl:25
msgid ""
"List keypoints that lie on a parametric degeneracy on volumes from ``NV1`` "
"to ``NV2`` (defaults to ``NV1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If "
"``NV1`` = ALL (default), ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` will be ignored and keypoints "
"on all selected volumes ( :ref:`vsel` ) will be listed. If ``NV1`` = P, "
"graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI). You may also substitute a component name for "
"``NV1`` (ignore ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdgl:46
msgid ""
"See the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_"
" for details about parametric degeneracies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:2
msgid "Generates volumes by dragging an area pattern along a path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VDRAG "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VDRAG.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:15
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:27
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:33
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:39
msgid ""
"List of areas in the pattern to be dragged (6 maximum if using keyboard "
"entry). If ``NA1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining "
"command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). If ``NA1`` = ALL, all "
"selected areas will be swept along the path. A component name may also be "
"substituted for ``NA1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:45
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:51
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:57
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:63
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:69
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:75
msgid ""
"List of lines defining the path along which the pattern is to be dragged (6 "
"maximum if using keyboard entry). Must be a continuous set of lines. To be "
"continuous, adjacent lines must share the connecting keypoint (the end "
"keypoint of one line must also be first keypoint of the next line)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:94
msgid ""
"Generates volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, lines, and areas) by "
"sweeping a given area pattern along a characteristic drag path. If the drag "
"path consists of multiple lines, the drag direction is determined by the "
"sequence in which the path lines are input ( ``NLP1``, ``NLP2``, etc.). If "
"the drag path is a single line ( ``NLP1`` ), the drag direction is from the "
"keypoint on the drag line that is closest to the first keypoint of the given"
" area pattern to the other end of the drag line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:101
msgid ""
"The magnitude of the vector between the keypoints of the given pattern and "
"the first path keypoint remains constant for all generated keypoint patterns"
" and the path keypoints. The direction of the vector relative to the path "
"slope also remains constant so that patterns may be swept around curves. "
"Lines are generated with the same shapes as the given pattern and the path "
"lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:106
msgid ""
"Keypoint, line, area, and volume numbers are automatically assigned "
"(beginning with the lowest available values ( :ref:`numstr` )). Adjacent "
"lines use a common keypoint, adjacent areas use a common line, and adjacent "
"volumes use a common area. For best results, the entities to be dragged "
"should be orthogonal to the start of the drag path. Drag operations that "
"produce an error message may create some of the desired entities prior to "
"terminating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:112
msgid ""
"If element attributes have been associated with the input area via the "
":ref:`aatt` command, the opposite area generated by the :ref:`vdrag` "
"operation will also have those attributes (that is, the element attributes "
"from the input area are copied to the opposite area). Note that only the "
"area opposite the input area will have the same attributes as the input "
"area; the areas adjacent to the input area will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:118
msgid ""
"If the input areas are meshed or belong to a meshed volume, the area(s) can "
"be extruded to a 3D mesh. Note that the ``NDIV`` argument of the "
":ref:`esize` command should be set before extruding the meshed areas. "
"Alternatively, mesh divisions can be specified directly on the drag line(s) "
"( :ref:`lesize` ). See the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vdrag:125
msgid ""
"You can use the :ref:`vdrag` command to generate 3D interface element meshes"
" for elements ``INTER194`` and ``INTER195``. When generating interface "
"element meshes using :ref:`vdrag`, you must specify the line divisions to "
"generate one interface element directly on the drag line using the "
":ref:`lesize` command. The source area to be extruded becomes the bottom "
"surface of the interface element. Interface elements must be extruded in "
"what will become the element's local x direction, that is, bottom to top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:2
msgid "Generates additional volumes by extruding areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VEXT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VEXT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:23
msgid ""
"Set of areas ( ``NA1`` to ``NA2`` in steps of ``NINC`` ) that defines the "
"pattern to be extruded. ``NA2`` defaults to ``NA1``, ``NINC`` defaults to 1."
" If ``NA1`` = ALL, ``NA2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is "
"defined by all selected areas. If ``NA1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled "
"and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A "
"component name may also be substituted for ``NA1`` ( ``NA2`` and ``NINC`` "
"are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:38
msgid ""
"Increments to be applied to the X, Y, and Z keypoint coordinates in the "
"active coordinate system ( DR, Dθ, DZ for cylindrical; DR, Dθ, DΦ for "
"spherical)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:42
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:50
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:58
msgid ""
"Scale factors to be applied to the X, Y, and Z keypoint coordinates in the "
"active coordinate system ( RR, Rθ, RZ for cylindrical; RR, Rθ, RΦ for "
"spherical). Note that the Rθ and RΦ scale factors are interpreted as angular"
" offsets. For example, if CSYS = 1, ``RX``, ``RY``, ``RZ`` input of "
"(1.5,10,3) would scale the specified keypoints 1.5 times in the radial and 3"
" times in the Z direction, while adding an offset of 10 degrees to the "
"keypoints. Zero, blank, or negative scale factor values are assumed to be "
"1.0. Zero or blank angular offsets have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:79
msgid ""
"Generates additional volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, lines, and "
"areas) by extruding and scaling a pattern of areas in the active coordinate "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:82
msgid ""
"If element attributes have been associated with the input area via the "
":ref:`aatt` command, the opposite area generated by the :ref:`vext` "
"operation will also have those attributes (that is, the element attributes "
"from the input area are copied to the opposite area). Note that only the "
"area opposite the input area will have the same attributes as the input "
"area; the areas adjacent to the input area will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:88
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:44
msgid ""
"If the areas are meshed or belong to meshed volumes, a 3D mesh can be "
"extruded with this command. Note that the ``NDIV`` argument on the "
":ref:`esize` command should be set before extruding the meshed areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:92
msgid ""
"Scaling of the input areas, if specified, is performed first, followed by "
"the extrusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:94
msgid ""
"In a non-Cartesian coordinate system, the :ref:`vext` command locates the "
"end face of the volume based on the active coordinate system. However, the "
"extrusion is made along a straight line between the end faces. Note that "
"solid modeling in a toroidal coordinate system is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vext:100
msgid ""
"Use of the :ref:`vext` command can produce unexpected results when operating"
" in a non-Cartesian coordinate system. For a detailed description of the "
"possible problems that may occur, see `Solid Modeling "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD5_10.html>`_"
" in the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:2
msgid "Generates additional volumes from a pattern of volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VGEN "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VGEN.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:28
msgid ""
"Generate volumes from pattern beginning with ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to"
" ``NV1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL, ``NV2`` "
"and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is all selected volumes ( "
":ref:`vsel` ). If ``NV1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:53
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:45
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:41
msgid ""
"``0`` - Generate nodes and elements associated with the original volumes, if"
" they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:58
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:46
msgid "Specifies whether to redefine the existing volumes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:60
msgid ""
"``0`` - Generate additional volumes as requested with the ``ITIME`` "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:62
msgid ""
"``1`` - Move original volumes to new position retaining the same keypoint "
"line, and area numbers ( ``ITIME``, ``KINC``, and ``NOELEM`` are ignored). "
"Corresponding meshed items are also moved if not needed at their original "
"position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vgen:80
msgid ""
"Generates additional volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, lines, "
"areas and mesh) from a given volume pattern. The MAT, TYPE, REAL, and ESYS "
"attributes are based upon the volumes in the pattern and not upon the "
"current settings of the pointers. End slopes of the generated lines remain "
"the same (in the active coordinate system) as those of the given pattern. "
"For example, radial slopes remain radial, etc. Generations which produce "
"volumes of a size or shape different from the pattern (that is, radial "
"generations in cylindrical systems, radial and phi generations in spherical "
"systems, and theta generations in elliptical systems) are not allowed. Note "
"that solid modeling in a toroidal coordinate system is not recommended. "
"Volume, area, and line numbers are automatically assigned (beginning with "
"the lowest available values ( :ref:`numstr` ))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist:2
msgid "Lists the defined volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VLIST "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VLIST.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist:23
msgid ""
"List volumes from ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to ``NV1`` ) in steps of "
"``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL (default), ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` "
"are ignored and all selected volumes ( :ref:`vsel` ) are listed. If ``NV1`` "
"= P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are "
"ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component name may also be substituted "
"for ``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlist:43
msgid ""
"An attribute (TYPE, MAT, REAL, or ESYS) listed as a zero is unassigned; one "
"listed as a positive value indicates that the attribute was assigned with "
"the :ref:`vatt` command (and will not be reset to zero if the mesh is "
"cleared); one listed as a negative value indicates that the attribute was "
"assigned using the attribute pointer [TYPE, MAT, REAL, or ESYS] that was "
"active during meshing (and will be reset to zero if the mesh is cleared). A "
"\"-1\" in the \"nodes\" column indicates that the volume has been meshed but"
" there are no interior nodes. The volume size is listed only if a "
":ref:`vsum` command has been performed on the volume. Volume orientation "
"attributes (KZ1 and KZ2) are listed only if a :ref:`veorient` command was "
"previously used to define an orientation for the volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:2
msgid "Generates a scaled set of volumes from a pattern of volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VLSCALE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VLSCALE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:23
msgid ""
"Set of volumes ( ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` in steps of ``NINC`` ) that defines the "
"pattern to be scaled. ``NV2`` defaults to ``NV1``, ``NINC`` defaults to 1. "
"If ``NV1`` = ALL, ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is "
"defined by all selected volumes. If ``NV1`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may also be substituted for ``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and "
"``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:38
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:46
msgid ""
"Scale factors to be applied to the X, Y, and Z keypoint coordinates in "
"active coordinate system ( RR, R θ, RZ for cylindrical; RR, R θ, R Φ for "
"spherical). Note that the R θ and R Φ scale factors are interpreted as "
"angular offsets. For example, if CSYS = 1, ``RX``, ``RY``, ``RZ`` input of "
"(1.5,10,3) would scale the specified keypoints 1.5 times in the radial and 3"
" times in the Z direction, while adding an offset of 10 degrees to the "
"keypoints. Zero, blank, or negative scale factor values are assumed to be "
"1.0. Zero or blank angular offsets have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:60
msgid ""
"``0`` - Nodes and elements associated with the original volumes will be "
"generated (scaled) if they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:66
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:50
msgid "Specifies whether volumes will be moved or newly defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:68
msgid "``0`` - Additional volumes will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:70
msgid ""
"``1`` - Original volumes will be moved to new position ( ``KINC`` and "
"``NOELEM`` are ignored). Use only if the old volumes are no longer needed at"
" their original positions. Corresponding meshed items are also moved if not "
"needed at their original position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vlscale:88
msgid ""
"Generates a scaled set of volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, lines,"
" areas, and mesh) from a pattern of volumes. The MAT, TYPE, REAL, and ESYS "
"attributes are based on the volumes in the pattern and not the current "
"settings. Scaling is done in the active coordinate system. Volumes in the "
"pattern could have been generated in any coordinate system. However, solid "
"modeling in a toroidal coordinate system is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:2
msgid "Generates a volume, offset from a given area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VOFFST "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VOFFST.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:9
msgid ""
"Area from which generated volume is to be offset. If ``NAREA`` = P, "
"graphical picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored "
"(valid only in the GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:13
msgid ""
"Distance normal to given area at which keypoints for generated volume are to"
" be located. Positive normal is determined from the right-hand rule keypoint"
" order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:17
msgid ""
"Increment to be applied to the keypoint numbers between sets. If zero, "
"keypoint numbers will be automatically assigned beginning with the lowest "
"available value ( :ref:`numstr` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:34
msgid ""
"Generates a volume (and its corresponding keypoints, lines, and areas) by "
"offsetting from an area. The direction of the offset varies with the given "
"area normal. End slopes of the generated lines remain the same as those of "
"the given pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.voffst:38
msgid ""
"If element attributes have been associated with the input area via the "
":ref:`aatt` command, the opposite area generated by the :ref:`voffst` "
"operation will also have those attributes (that is, the element attributes "
"from the input area are copied to the opposite area). Note that only the "
"area opposite the input area will have the same attributes as the input "
"area; the areas adjacent to the input area will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:2
msgid "Displays the selected volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VPLOT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VPLOT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:19
msgid ""
"Display volumes from ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to ``NV1`` ) in steps of "
"``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL (default), ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` "
"are ignored and all selected volumes ( :ref:`vsel` ) are displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:28
msgid ""
"``DEGE`` - A red star is placed on keypoints at degeneracies (see the "
"`Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_)."
" Not available if :ref:`facet`,WIRE is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vplot:49
msgid ""
"Displays selected volumes. (Only volumes having areas within the selected "
"area set ( :ref:`asel` ) will be plotted.) With PowerGraphics on ( "
":ref:`graphics`,POWER), :ref:`vplot` will display only the currently "
"selected areas. This command is also a utility command, valid anywhere. The "
"degree of tessellation used to plot the volumes is set through the "
":ref:`facet` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:2
msgid ""
"Generates cylindrical volumes by rotating an area pattern about an axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VROTAT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VROTAT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:23
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:37
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:44
msgid ""
"List of areas in the pattern to be rotated (6 maximum if using keyboard "
"entry). Areas must lie to one side of, and in the plane of, the axis of "
"rotation. If ``NA1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all remaining "
"command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). If ``NA1`` = ALL, all "
"selected areas will define the pattern to be rotated. A component name may "
"also be substituted for ``NA1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:51
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:54
msgid ""
"Keypoints defining the axis about which the area pattern is to be rotated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:61
msgid ""
"Number of volumes (8 maximum) around circumference. Defaults to minimum "
"required for 90° (maximum) arcs, that is, 4 for 360°, 3 for 270°, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:78
msgid ""
"Generates cylindrical volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, lines, and"
" areas) by rotating an area pattern (and its associated line and keypoint "
"patterns) about an axis. Keypoint patterns are generated at regular angular "
"locations (based on a maximum spacing of 90°). Line patterns are generated "
"at the keypoint patterns. Arc lines are also generated to connect the "
"keypoints circumferentially. Keypoint, line, area, and volume numbers are "
"automatically assigned (beginning with the lowest available values). "
"Adjacent lines use a common keypoint, adjacent areas use a common line, and "
"adjacent volumes use a common area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:86
msgid ""
"To generate a single volume with an arc greater than 180°, ``NSEG`` must be "
"greater than or equal to 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:89
msgid ""
"If element attributes have been associated with the input area via the "
":ref:`aatt` command, the opposite area generated by the :ref:`vrotat` "
"operation will also have those attributes (that is, the element attributes "
"from the input area are copied to the opposite area). Note that only the "
"area opposite the input area will have the same attributes as the input "
"area; the areas adjacent to the input area will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vrotat:95
msgid ""
"If the given areas are meshed or belong to meshed volumes, the 2D mesh can "
"be rotated (extruded) to a 3D mesh. See the `Modeling and Meshing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_mod/Hlp_G_MOD14.html>`_"
" for more information. Note that the ``NDIV`` argument on the :ref:`esize` "
"command should be set before extruding the meshed areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsum.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsum:2
msgid "Calculates and prints geometry statistics of the selected volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsum:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VSUM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VSUM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsum:27
msgid ""
"Calculates and prints geometry statistics (volume, centroid location, "
"moments of inertia, etc.) associated with the selected volumes. Geometry "
"items are reported in the global Cartesian coordinate system. A unit density"
" is assumed unless the volumes have a material association via the "
":ref:`vatt` command. Items calculated by :ref:`vsum` and later retrieved by "
"a :ref:`get` or :ref:`starvget` command are valid only if the model is not "
"modified after the :ref:`vsum` command is issued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsum:37
msgid ""
"For very thin volumes, such that the ratio of the minimum to the maximum "
"dimension is less than 0.01, the :ref:`vsum` command can provide erroneous "
"volume information. To ensure that such calculations are accurate, make "
"certain that you subdivide such volumes so that the ratio of the minimum to "
"the maximum is at least 0.05."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:2
msgid "Generates volumes from a volume pattern by symmetry reflection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VSYMM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VSYMM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:18
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:25
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:32
msgid ""
"Reflect volumes from pattern beginning with ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to "
"``NV1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL, ``NV2`` "
"and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is all selected volumes ( "
":ref:`vsel` ). If ``NV1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:52
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:48
msgid "``0`` - Generate additional volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:54
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:50
msgid ""
"``1`` - Move original volumes to new position retaining the same keypoint "
"numbers ( ``KINC`` and ``NOELEM`` are ignored). Corresponding meshed items "
"are also moved if not needed at their original position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vsymm:72
msgid ""
"Generates a reflected set of volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, "
"lines, areas and mesh) from a given volume pattern by a symmetry reflection "
"(see analogous node symmetry command, :ref:`nsym` ). The MAT, TYPE, REAL, "
"and ESYS attributes are based upon the volumes in the pattern and not upon "
"the current settings. Reflection is done in the active coordinate system by "
"changing a particular coordinate sign. The active coordinate system must be "
"a Cartesian system. Volumes in the pattern may have been generated in any "
"coordinate system. However, solid modeling in a toroidal coordinate system "
"is not recommended. Volumes are generated as described in the :ref:`vgen` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/prep7/volumes.rst:34:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:2
msgid "Transfers a pattern of volumes to another coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `VTRAN "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_VTRAN.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:28
msgid ""
"Transfer volumes from pattern beginning with ``NV1`` to ``NV2`` (defaults to"
" ``NV1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NV1`` = ALL, ``NV2`` "
"and ``NINC`` are ignored and the pattern is all selected volumes ( "
":ref:`vsel` ). If ``NV1`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may also be substituted for ``NV1`` ( ``NV2`` and ``NINC`` are "
"ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/prep7/volumes.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.prep7.volumes.Volumes.vtran:68
msgid ""
"Transfers a pattern of volumes (and their corresponding keypoints, lines, "
"areas and mesh) from one coordinate system to another (see analogous node "
"transfer command, :ref:`transfer` ). The MAT, TYPE, REAL, and ESYS "
"attributes are based upon the volumes in the pattern and not upon the "
"current settings. Coordinate systems may be translated and rotated relative "
"to each other. Initial pattern may be generated in any coordinate system. "
"However, solid modeling in a toroidal coordinate system is not recommended. "
"Coordinate and slope values are interpreted in the active coordinate system "
"and are transferred directly. Volumes are generated as described in the "
":ref:`vgen` command."
msgstr ""

