#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashfdele:35
msgid ""
"Deletes as soon as possible (or prevents writing) a binary file created by "
"Mechanical APDL to save space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashfdele:40
msgid ""
"Deleting files that are necessary for the next substep, load step, or "
"analysis will prevent continuation of the run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/session/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.session.files.Files.slashrename"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/session/files.rst:30:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:2
msgid "Renames a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `/RENAME "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RENAME.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:9
msgid ""
"The file to be renamed. You can also include an optional directory path as "
"part of the specified file name; if not, the default file location is the "
"working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:12
msgid "File name defaults to the current :file:`Jobname`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:18
msgid ""
"The new name for the file. You can also include an optional directory path "
"as part of the new file name; if not, the default is the working directory. "
"A maximum of 248 characters is allowed for the file name (or combined file "
"name and directory path, if both are specified)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:28
msgid ""
"Key that specifies which rename operation is performed on all processes in "
"distributed-memory parallel mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:31
msgid ""
"``0 (OFF or NO)`` - The program performs the rename operation only on the "
"master process (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:34
msgid ""
"``1 (ON or YES)`` - The program performs the rename operation locally on "
"each process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:36
msgid ""
"``2 or BOTH`` - The program performs the rename operation for ``Fname``. "
"``Ext`` on the master process and for ``FnameN``. ``Ext`` on all processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:53
msgid ""
"Renames a file. Ex: :ref:`slashrename`,A,,,B renames file A to B in the same"
" directory. :ref:`slashrename`,A,DAT,,,INP renames file A.DAT to A.INP. On "
"all systems, this command will overwrite any existing file named B. See the "
"`Operations Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ope/Hlp_G_OPE8.html>`_"
" for details. Only Mechanical APDL binary files should be renamed. Use "
":ref:`sys` and system renaming commands for other files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:60
msgid ""
"In distributed-memory parallel (DMP) mode, only the master process will "
"rename ``Fname1``. ``Ext1`` to ``Fname2``. ``Ext2`` by default. However, "
"when ``DistKey`` is set to 1 (or ON, or YES) or 2 (or BOTH), the command is "
"executed by all processes. In this case, ``Fname1`` and ``Fname2`` will "
"automatically have the process rank appended to them. This means "
"``Fname1N``. ``Ext1`` will be renamed to ``Fname2N``. ``Ext2`` by all "
"processes, where ``N`` is the DMP process rank. For more information see in "
"the `Parallel Processing Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_dan/HybParallel.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/files.pydocstring of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.slashrename:68
msgid ""
"Renaming across system partitions may be internally done by a copy and "
"delete operation on some systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/session/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.files.Files.starlist.rst:2
