"You can use the :ref:`memm` command to ensure that memory intensive "
"operations will always have the same memory available when the operations "
"occur intermittently. Normally, if a large amount of memory is allocated for"
" a specific operation, it will be returned to the system once the operation "
"is finished. This option always maintains the highest level used during the "
"analysis until the analysis is finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/session/run_controls.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.session.run_controls.RunControls.memm:39
msgid ""
"The :ref:`memm` command does not affect the value you specify with the -m "
"switch. When you allocate memory with the -m switch, that amount will always"
" be available. However, if dynamic memory allocation in excess of the -m "
"value occurs, you can use the :ref:`memm` command to ensure that amount is "
"retained until the end of your analysis."
msgstr ""

