#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.additive_manufacturing.AdditiveManufacturing.ampowder:16
msgid ""
"Knockdown factor applied to the solid material properties (to obtain the "
"powder material properties). Default = 0.01."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/additive_manufacturing.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.additive_manufacturing.AdditiveManufacturing.ampowder:33
msgid ""
"This command applies only to the powder-bed fusion ( :ref:`amtype`,PBF) "
"process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/additive_manufacturing.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.additive_manufacturing.AdditiveManufacturing.ampowder:35
msgid ""
"To estimate the convection coefficient ( ``HPOWDER`` ), divide the "
"conduction property of the powder (its KXX) by a characteristic conduction "
"length into the powder (for example, ¼ of the distance from the part "
"boundary to the build-chamber wall)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/additive_manufacturing.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.additive_manufacturing.AdditiveManufacturing.ampowder:39
msgid ""
"The program uses the knockdown factor ( ``MATFACTOR`` ) to estimate the "
"powder properties. The program applies the factor (typically 0.01) to the "
"solid material properties to estimate the properties of the material in its "
"powder state. The powder-state properties are used during the heating of the"
" new layer (before its subsequent solidification and cooldown) prior to the "
"next layer being applied."
msgstr ""

