msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:14
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.dspoption:29
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.lanboption:22
msgid "**memory_option** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:15
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.dspoption:30
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.lanboption:23
msgid "Memory allocation option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:17
msgid ""
"``DEFAULT`` - Use the default memory allocation strategy for the sparse "
"solver. The default strategy attempts to run in the INCORE memory mode. If "
"there is not enough available physical memory when the solver starts to run "
"in the INCORE memory mode, the solver will then attempt to run in the "
"OUTOFCORE memory mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:22
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.dspoption:37
msgid ""
"``INCORE`` - Use a memory allocation strategy in the sparse solver that will"
" attempt to obtain enough memory to run with the entire factorized matrix in"
" memory. This option uses the most amount of memory and should avoid doing "
"any I/O. By avoiding I/O, this option achieves optimal solver performance. "
"However, a significant amount of memory is required to run in this mode, and"
" it is only recommended on machines with a large amount of memory. If the "
"allocation for in-core memory fails, the solver will automatically revert to"
" out-of-core memory mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:29
msgid ""
"``OUTOFCORE`` - Use a memory allocation strategy in the sparse solver that "
"will attempt to allocate only enough work space to factor each individual "
"frontal matrix in memory, but will store the entire factorized matrix on "
"disk. Typically, this memory mode results in poor performance due to the "
"potential bottleneck caused by the I/O to the various files written by the "
"solver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.dspoption:49
msgid ""
"``FORCE`` - This option, when used in conjunction with the ``Memory_Size`` "
"option, allows you to force the sparse solver to run with a specific amount "
"of memory. This option is only recommended for the advanced user who "
"understands sparse solver memory requirements for the problem being solved, "
"understands the physical memory on the system, and wants to control the "
"sparse solver memory usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:39
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.dspoption:54
msgid "**memory_size** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:40
msgid ""
"Initial memory size allocation for the sparse solver in GB. This argument "
"allows you to tune the sparse solver memory and is not generally required. "
"Although there is no upper limit for ``Memory_Size``, the ``Memory_Size`` "
"setting should always be well within the physical memory available, but not "
"so small as to cause the sparse solver to run out of memory. Warnings and/or"
" errors from the sparse solver will appear if this value is set too low. If "
"the FORCE memory option is used, this value is the amount of memory "
"allocated for the entire duration of the sparse solver solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.bcsoption:48
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
