"``DELE`` - Deletes all files from the SPARSE solver run, including the "
"factorized file, :file:`.DSPsymb`, upon :ref:`finish` or ``/EXIT`` "
"(default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eqslv:163
msgid ""
"``KEEP`` - Retains all necessary files from the SPARSE solver run, including"
" the :file:`.DSPsymb` file, in the working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eqslv:180
msgid ""
"The selection of a solver can affect the speed and accuracy of a solution. "
"For a more detailed discussion of the merits of each solver, see `Solution "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS3_stopsolmatrix.html>`_"
" in the `Basic Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/afbRsqe0ldm.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eqslv:188
msgid ""
"Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction All equation solvers are "
"supported in a DMP analysis. However, the SPARSE and PCG solvers are the "
"only distributed solvers that always run a fully distributed solution. The "
"JCG solver runs in a fully distributed mode in some cases; in other cases, "
"it does not. The ICCG and QMR solvers are not distributed solvers; "
"therefore, you will not see the full performance improvements with these "
"solvers that you would with a fully distributed solution."
msgstr ""

