"For coupled pore-pressure-thermal elements ( ``CPT212``, ``CPT213``, "
"``CPT215``, ``CPT216``, ``CPT217`` ), the default behavior is to copy "
"integration-point results to the nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eresx:19
msgid "Extrapolation key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eresx:21
msgid ""
"``DEFA`` - If element is fully elastic (no active plasticity, creep, or "
"swelling nonlinearities), extrapolate the integration-point results to the "
"nodes. If any portion of the element is plastic (or other active material "
"nonlinearity), copy the integration-point results to the nodes (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eresx:25
msgid ""
"``YES`` - Extrapolate the linear portion of the integration-point results to"
" the nodes and copy the nonlinear portion (for example, plastic strains)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eresx:28
msgid "``NO`` - Copy the integration-point results to the nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eresx:44
msgid ""
"Specifies whether the solution results at the element-integration points are"
" extrapolated or copied to the nodes for element and nodal postprocessing. "
"Structural stresses, elastic and thermal strains, field gradients, and "
"fluxes are affected. Nonlinear data (such as plastic, creep, and swelling "
"strains) are always copied to the nodes, never extrapolated. For shell "
"elements, :ref:`eresx` applies only to integration-point results in the in-"
"plane directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.eresx:50
msgid ""
"Extrapolation occurs in the element-solution coordinate system. For elements"
" allowing different solution systems at integration points (such as "
"``SHELL281`` and ``SOLID186`` ), extrapolation can produce unreliable "
"results when the solution coordinate systems in each element differ "
"significantly. (Varying element-solution coordinate systems can be created "
"via the :ref:`esys` command or from large deformation.) Examine results "
"carefully in such cases, and disable extrapolation if necessary."
msgstr ""

