#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:56
msgid ""
"If you manually force :ref:`msave`,ON by including it in the input file, the"
" model can include the following additional conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:59
msgid ""
"The analysis can be a modal analysis using the PCG Lanczos method ( "
":ref:`modopt`,LANPCG)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:61
msgid ""
"Large deflection effects ( :ref:`nlgeom`,ON) can be included for "
"``SOLID186`` and/or ``SOLID187`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:64
msgid ""
"``SOLID185`` (brick shapes and KEYOPT(2) = 3 only) elements can be included "
"for small strains ( :ref:`nlgeom`,OFF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:67
msgid ""
"All other element types or other parts of the model that don't meet the "
"above criteria will be solved using global assembly ( :ref:`msave`,OFF). "
"This command can result in memory savings of up to 70 percent over the "
"global assembly approach for the part of the model that meets the criteria. "
"Depending on the hardware (for example, processor speed, memory bandwidth, "
"etc.), the solution time may increase or decrease when this feature is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:73
msgid ""
"This memory-saving feature runs in parallel when multiple processors are "
"used with the :ref:`config` command or in a distributed-memory parallel "
"(DMP) solution. The gain in performance with using multiple processors with "
"this feature turned on should be similar to the default case when this "
"feature is turned off. Performance also improves when using the uniform "
"reduced integration option for ``SOLID186`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:79
msgid ""
"This command does not support the layered option of the SOLID185 and "
"``SOLID186`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:81
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`msave`,ON with the :ref:`pcgopt` command, note the "
"following restrictions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:83
msgid ""
"For static and modal analyses, :ref:`msave`,ON is not valid when using a "
"``Lev_Diff`` value of 5 on the :ref:`pcgopt` command; ``Lev_Diff``  is "
"automatically reset to 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:86
msgid ""
"For modal analyses, :ref:`msave`,ON is not valid with the ``StrmCk`` option "
"of the :ref:`pcgopt` command; ``Strmck``  is set to OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:89
msgid ""
"For all analysis types, :ref:`msave`,ON is not valid when the Lagrange "
"multiplier option ( ``LM_Key`` ) of the :ref:`pcgopt` command is set to ON; "
"the :ref:`msave` activation key is set to OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:93
msgid ""
"For linear perturbation static and modal analyses, :ref:`msave`,ON is not "
"valid; the :ref:`msave` activation key is set to OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:96
msgid ""
"For static analyses, :ref:`msave`,ON is not valid when the ``Fallback`` "
"option of the :ref:`pcgopt` command is enabled; ``Fallback`` is "
"automatically reset to OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msave:99
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`msave`,ON for modal analyses, no :file:`.FULL` file will be"
" created. The :file:`.FULL` file may be necessary for subsequent analyses "
"(for example, harmonic, transient mode- superposition, or spectrum "
"analyses). To generate the :file:`.FULL` file, rerun the modal analysis "
"using the :ref:`wrfull` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:2
msgid "Starts multiple solutions for an acoustic analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MSOLVE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MSOLVE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:8
msgid "**numslv** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:9
msgid ""
"Number of multiple solutions (load steps). This number corresponds to the "
"number of random samplings for the diffuse sound field in a random acoustic "
"analysis, or the incident angles of the plane wave when the Floquet periodic"
" boundary condition is present. Default = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:14
msgid "The meaning of ``VAL1`` depends on the ``Lab`` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:16
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = DSF, ``VAL1`` is the norm convergence tolerance defined by "
"comparing the averaged radiated diffuse sound power of two multiple sampling"
" sets over the frequency range for the diffuse sound field (default = 0.05)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:20
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = APHI or ATHETA, ``VAL1`` is the beginning angle for the "
"incident angle sweep of the plane wave (default = 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:24
msgid "The meaning of ``VAL2`` depends on the ``Lab`` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:26
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = DSF, ``VAL2`` is the interval of the norm convergence check "
"for the diffuse sound field (default = 5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:29
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = APHI or ATHETA, ``VAL2`` is the ending angle for the incident "
"angle sweep of the plane wave (default = 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:33
msgid "Label indicating the type of acoustic analysis:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:35
msgid "``DSF`` - Diffuse sound field with multiple solutions (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:37
msgid ""
"``APHI`` - Plane wave angle sweep with fixed :math:`equation not available`"
"  angle and varied :math:`equation not available`  angle (see the  "
":ref:`aport` command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:40
msgid ""
"``ATHETA`` - Plane wave angle sweep with fixed :math:`equation not "
"available`  angle and varied :math:`equation not available`  angle (see the"
"  :ref:`aport` command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:43
msgid "**angfix** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:44
msgid ""
"The value of the fixed incident angle for the plane wave angle sweep (used "
"only when ``Lab`` = APHI or ATHETA)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:59
msgid ""
"The :ref:`msolve` command starts multiple solutions (load steps) for a "
"random acoustic analysis with multiple samplings or for the angle sweep of "
"the incident plane wave with the Floquet periodic boundary condition, as "
"described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:63
msgid "**Random Acoustic Analysis (** ``Lab`` = DSF)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:65
msgid ""
"Use ``Lab`` = DSF for a random acoustic analysis. The process is controlled "
"by the norm convergence tolerance ( ``VAL1`` ) or the number of multiple "
"solutions ( ``NUMSLV`` ) if the solution steps reach the defined number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:69
msgid ""
"The program checks the norm convergence by comparing two averaged sets of "
"radiated sound powers with the interval ``VAL2`` over the frequency range. "
"For example, if ``VAL2`` = 5, the averaged values from 5 solutions are "
"compared with the averaged values from 10 solutions, then the averaged "
"values from 10 solutions are compared with the averaged values from 15 "
"solutions, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:74
msgid ""
"The incident diffuse sound field is defined via the :ref:`dfswave` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:76
msgid ""
"The average result of multiple solutions with different samplings is "
"calculated via the :ref:`pras` or :ref:`plas` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:79
msgid "**Plane Wave Incident Angle Sweep (** ``Lab`` = APHI or ATHETA)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:81
msgid ""
"Use ``Lab`` = APHI or ATHETA to perform an angle sweep for the incident "
"plane wave defined by the :ref:`aport` command. The process is controlled by"
" the number of multiple solutions ( ``NUMSLV`` ). The plane wave port must "
"be defined with the default values of incident angles prior to the "
":ref:`msolve` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.msolve:86
msgid ""
"The sound power parameters are calculated over the sweeping angles during "
"postprocessing by the :ref:`pras` or :ref:`plas` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:2
msgid ""
"Sets decision parameter for automatically increasing the time step interval "
"in a pure thermal analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:5
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `OPNCONTROL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_OPNCONTROL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:10
msgid ""
"``TEMP`` - Degree-of-freedom label used to base a decision for increasing "
"the time step (substep) interval in a nonlinear or transient analysis. The "
"only DOF label currently supported is TEMP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:13
msgid ""
"``OPENUPFACTOR`` - Key to set a multiplier for increasing the time step "
"interval as specified in ``VALUE`` > 1.0 (up to 10.0). Valid only when "
":ref:`autots`,ON has been issued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:16
msgid ""
"The multiplier is set by issuing :ref:`opncontrol`,OPENUPFACTOR, ``VALUE`` "
"as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:18
msgid ""
"For a pure thermal analysis, if ``VALUE`` > 1.0, the OPENUPFACTOR is the "
"minimum of 10.0, ``VALUE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:21
msgid "If the user does not specify the multiplier, the default is 3.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:23
msgid ""
"Generally, ``VALUE`` > 3.0 is not recommended. Note that in some rare cases "
"this specification can be overwritten by internal heuristics in determining "
"the new time step interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:27
msgid "A context sensitive value that depends on ``Lab`` :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:29
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = TEMP, ``VALUE`` is used together with ``NUMSTEP`` in the "
"algorithm for determining if the time step interval can be increased. The "
"time step interval is increased if the maximum absolute value of the "
"incremental solution is less than ``VALUE`` for the number of contiguous "
"time steps specified by ``NUMSTEP`` (default ``VALUE`` = 0.1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:34
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = OPENUPFACTOR, ``VALUE`` is a multiplier (= 1.0 - 10.0) that can"
" be specified for a pure thermal analysis as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:37
msgid "**numstep** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:38
msgid ""
"Valid only when ``Lab`` = TEMP. A value used together with ``VALUE`` in the "
"algorithm for determining if the time step interval can be increased. The "
"time step interval is increased if the maximum absolute value of the "
"incremental solution at the specified TEMP label is less than ``VALUE`` for "
"the number of contiguous time steps specified by ``NUMSTEP`` (default "
"``NUMSTEP`` = 3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:58
msgid ""
"This command is available only for nonlinear static or full transient "
"analyses. :ref:`opncontrol` enables an increase in the current time step "
"size. It is analogous to the :ref:`cutcontrol` command, but with the "
"opposite effect. :ref:`cutcontrol` reduces the step size for analyses "
"experiencing convergence difficulties while :ref:`opncontrol` increases the "
"step size to speed up converging analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:64
msgid ""
"The increase in the current time step size via :ref:`opncontrol` occurs "
"when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:66
msgid "a trigger mechanism is encountered and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:68
msgid "a multiplier (greater than 1.0) is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:70
msgid ""
"Different internal heuristics are used to automatically trigger the increase"
" of the time step for different physics. However, for a pure thermal "
"analysis, an additional trigger to increase the step size can be implemented"
" by issuing :ref:`opncontrol`,TEMP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:74
msgid ""
"The multiplier is set by issuing :ref:`opncontrol`,OPENUPFACTOR, ``VALUE`` "
"(see details for different analysis types in the OPENUPFACTOR argument "
"description above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.opncontrol:77
msgid ""
"For linear full transient analysis, where the time step interval can be "
"predominantly determined by the estimated modal frequency (number of "
"solution points in a cycle in the dynamic system), the multiplier set via "
"the OPENUPFACTOR argument may show no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:2
msgid ""
"Outputs the superelement matrices and load vectors to formatted files for "
"aeroelastic analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `OUTAERO "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/None>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:9
msgid ""
"Name of the superelement that models the wind turbine supporting structure. "
"Defaults to the current Jobname."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:12
msgid "**timeb** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:13
msgid ""
"First time at which the load vector is formed (defaults to be read from "
":file:`SENAME.sub` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:16
msgid ""
"Time step size of the load vectors (defaults to be read from "
":file:`SENAME.sub` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:32
msgid ""
"Both TIMEB and DTIME must be blank if the time data is to be read from the "
":file:`SENAME.sub` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:34
msgid ""
"The matrix file ( :file:`SENAME.SUB` ) must be available from the "
"substructure generation run before issuing this command. This superelement "
"that models the wind turbine supporting structure must contain only one "
"master node with six freedoms per node: UX, UY, UZ, ROTX, ROTY, ROTZ. The "
"master node represents the connection point between the turbine and the "
"supporting structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.outaero:39
msgid ""
"This command will generate four files that are exported to the aeroelastic "
"code for integrated wind turbine analysis. The four files are "
":file:`Jobname.GNK` for the generalized stiffness matrix, "
":file:`Jobname.GNC` for the generalized damping matrix, :file:`Jobname.GNM` "
"for the generalized mass matrix and :file:`Jobname.GNF` for the generalized "
"load vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
