msgid ":rspan:`1` 0, 2, 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.perturb:313
msgid ""
"When ``ContKey`` is set to CURRENT, all contact related parameters (such as "
"normal stiffness and tangential stiffness) will remain unchanged throughout "
"the linear perturbation analysis. However when ``ContKey`` is set to "
"STICKING or BONDED, the program will re-evaluate the contact normal and "
"tangential stiffness in order to perform the linear perturbation analysis "
"based on the actual sticking behavior regardless of the friction coefficient"
" value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.perturb:319
msgid ""
"Note that the :ref:`cnkmod` command allows you to take points in the base "
"analysis that are near contact (within the pinball region) and modify them "
"to be treated as \"in contact\" in the linear perturbation analysis; see the"
" \"1 - near-field\" row in the above table with KEYOPT(12) values set to 4 "
"or 5. :ref:`cnkmod` also allows you to take points that are sliding in the "
"base analysis and treat them as sticking in the linear perturbation "
"analysis, irrespective of the MU value; see the \"2 - sliding\" row in the "
"above table with KEYOPT(12) values set to 1,5, or 6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.perturb:326
msgid ""
"If an open gap exists at the restart point of the base static/transient "
"solution and the contact status is adjusted as sliding or sticking due to a "
"“bonded” or “no separation” contact behavior definition, then the program "
"will treat it as near-field contact when executing the :ref:`cnkmod` command"
" in a downstream linear perturbation analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:2
msgid ""
"Controls the behavior of an analysis when a negative or zero equation solver"
" pivot value is encountered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:5
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `PIVCHECK "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PIVCHECK.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:11
msgid ""
"The program checks for negative or zero pivot values ( ``Key`` = AUTO). If "
"any are found, the analysis may stop with an error or may proceed with only "
"a warning, depending on various criteria pertaining to the type of analysis "
"being solved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:18
msgid ""
"Determines whether to stop or continue an analysis when a negative or zero "
"equation solver pivot value is encountered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:21
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Check for negative or zero pivot values for analyses performed "
"with the sparse and PCG solvers. When one is encountered, an error or "
"warning is issued, per various criteria relating to the type of analysis "
"being solved. An error causes the analysis to stop; a warning allows the "
"analysis to continue. A negative pivot value may be valid for some nonlinear"
" and multiphysics analyses (for example, electromagnetic and thermal "
"analyses); this key has no effect in these cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:27
msgid ""
"``ERROR`` - Check for negative or zero pivot values for analyses performed "
"with the sparse and PCG solvers. When one is encountered, an error is "
"issued, stopping the analysis. A negative pivot value may be valid for some "
"nonlinear and multiphysics analyses (for example, electromagnetic and "
"thermal analyses); this key has no effect in these cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:32
msgid ""
"``WARN`` - Check for negative or zero pivot values for analyses performed "
"with the sparse and PCG solvers. When one is encountered, a warning is "
"issued and the analysis continues. A negative pivot value may be valid for "
"some nonlinear and multiphysics analyses (for example, electromagnetic and "
"thermal analyses); this key has no effect in these cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:37
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - Pivot values are not checked. This key causes the analysis to "
"continue in spite of a negative or zero pivot value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:40
msgid "**prntcntrl** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:41
msgid ""
"Provides print options. Print output with these options will be sent to the "
"default output file, not to the files created by the nonlinear diagnostic "
"tools ( :ref:`nldiag` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:44
msgid ""
"``ONCE`` - Print only the maximum and minimum pivot information on the first"
" call to the sparse solver (which is the default solver). This is the "
"default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:47
msgid ""
"``EVERY`` - Print the maximum and minimum pivot information at every call to"
" the sparse solver. This option is provided for nonlinear analysis "
"diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:64
msgid ""
"This command is valid for all analyses. In a nonlinear analysis, a negative "
"pivot may be valid. In some cases, rigid body motions in a nonlinear "
"analysis will be trapped by error routines checking infinitely large "
"displacements (DOF limit exceeded) or nonconvergence status. An under-"
"constrained model may avoid the pivot check, but fail with a DOF limit "
"exceeded error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:69
msgid ""
"Machine precision may affect whether a small pivot triggers an error or "
"bypasses this checking logic. You may wish to review the ratio of the "
"maximum to absolute minimum pivot values. For ratios exceeding 12 to 14 "
"orders of magnitude, the accuracy of the computed solution may be degraded "
"by the severe ill-conditioning of the assembled matrix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pivcheck:74
msgid ""
"Note that negative pivots corresponding to Lagrange multiplier based mixed "
"u-P elements are not checked or reported by this command. Negative pivots "
"arising from the u-P element formulation and related analyses can occur and "
"lead to correct solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol:2
msgid ""
"Specifies whether to include pressure load stiffness in the element "
"stiffness formation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `PRSCONTROL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PRSCONTROL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol:9
msgid ""
"Pressure load stiffness key. In general, use the default setting. Use a non-"
"default setting only if you encounter convergence difficulties. Pressure "
"load stiffness is automatically included when using eigenvalue buckling "
"analyses ( :ref:`antype`,BUCKLE), equivalent to ``Key`` = INCP. For all "
"other types of analyses, valid arguments for ``Key`` are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol:13
msgid "``NOPL`` - Pressure load stiffness not included for any elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol:15
msgid ""
"``(blank) (default)`` - Include pressure load stiffness for elements "
"``SURF153``, ``SURF154``, ``SURF156``, ``SURF159``, ``SHELL181``, "
"``PLANE182``, ``PLANE183``, ``SOLID185``, ``SOLID186``, ``SOLID187``, "
"``SOLSH190``, ``BEAM188``, ``BEAM189``, ``FOLLW201``, ``SHELL208``, "
"``SHELL209``, ``SOLID272``, ``SOLID273``, ``SHELL281``, ``SOLID285``, "
"``PIPE288``, ``PIPE289``, and ``ELBOW290``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.prscontrol:34
msgid ""
"This command is rarely needed. The default settings are recommended for most"
" analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:2
msgid "Enables or disables shared-memory parallel operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `PSCONTROL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PSCONTROL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:6
msgid ""
"**Command default:** None. The command is ignored if issued with no "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:12
msgid ""
"Specify the operations for which you intend to enable/disable parallel "
"behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:14
msgid "``ALL`` - Enable/disable parallel for all areas (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:16
msgid ""
"``PREP`` - Enable/disable parallel during preprocessing ( :ref:`prep7` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:18
msgid ""
"``SOLU`` - Enable/disable parallel during solution ( :ref:`slashsolu` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:20
msgid "``FORM`` - Enable/disable parallel during element matrix generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:22
msgid "``SOLV`` - Enable/disable parallel during equation solver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:24
msgid "``RESU`` - Enable/disable parallel during element results calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:26
msgid ""
"``POST`` - Enable/disable parallel during postprocessing ( :ref:`post1` and "
":ref:`post26` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:28
msgid "``STAT`` - List parallel operations that are enabled/disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:31
msgid "Option control key. Used for all ``Option`` values except STAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:33
msgid "``ON`` - Enable parallel operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:35
msgid "``OFF`` - Disable parallel operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:49
msgid "Use this command in shared-memory parallel operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:51
msgid ""
"This command is useful when you encounter minor discrepancies in a nonlinear"
" solution when using different numbers of processors. A parallel operation "
"applied to the element matrix generation can produce a different nonlinear "
"solution with a different number of processors. Although the nonlinear "
"solution converges to the same nonlinear tolerance, the minor discrepancy "
"created may not be desirable for consistency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:57
msgid ""
"Enabling/disabling parallel behavior for the solution ( ``Option`` = SOLU) "
"supersedes the activation/deactivation of parallel behavior for element "
"matrix generation (FORM), equation solver (SOLV), and element results "
"calculation (RESU)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:61
msgid ""
"The SOLV option supports only the sparse direct and PCG solvers ( "
":ref:`eqslv`,SPARSE or PCG). No other solvers are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.pscontrol:64
msgid ""
"This command applies only to shared-memory architecture. It does not apply "
"to distributed-memory parallel processing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:2
msgid "Directs the program to perform a partial solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `PSOLVE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_PSOLVE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:9
msgid "Valid labels defining the solution step. All characters are required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:11
msgid ""
"``EIGDAMP`` - Calculates the eigenvalues and eigenvectors using the damped "
"eigensolver. Requires :file:`Jobname.FULL` from :ref:`modopt`,UNSYM or "
":ref:`modopt`,DAMP options. Produces :file:`JobnameMODE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:15
msgid ""
"``EIGQRDA`` - Calculates eigenvalues and eigenvectors using the QR damped "
"eigensolver. Requires :file:`Jobname.EMAT` from :ref:`modopt`,QRDAMP option."
" Produces :file:`JobnameMODE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:18
msgid ""
"``EIGEXP`` - Expands the eigenvector solution. Requires :file:`Jobname.ESAV`"
" and :file:`Jobname.MODE`. Produces :file:`JobnameRST`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:21
msgid ""
"``EIGLANB`` - Calculates the eigenvalues and eigenvectors using Block "
"Lanczos. Requires :file:`Jobname.EMAT` from :ref:`modopt`,LANB option. "
"Produces :file:`JobnameMODE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:24
msgid ""
"``EIGLANPCG`` - Calculates the eigenvalues and eigenvectors using PCG "
"Lanczos. Requires :file:`Jobname.EMAT` from :ref:`modopt`,LANPCG option. "
"Produces :file:`JobnameMODE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:27
msgid ""
"``EIGSNODE`` - Calculates the eigenvalues and eigenvectors using the "
"Supernode method. Requires :file:`Jobname.EMAT` from :ref:`modopt`,SNODE "
"option. Produces :file:`Jobname.MODE`. (See the :ref:`modopt` command for "
"more information on the SNODE modal solver.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:31
msgid ""
"``EIGUNSYM`` - Calculates the eigenvalues and eigenvectors using the "
"unsymmetric eigensolver. Requires :file:`Jobname.EMAT` from "
":ref:`modopt`,UNSYM or :ref:`modopt`,DAMP options. Produces "
":file:`JobnameMODE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:35
msgid ""
"``ELFORM`` - Creates the element matrices. Produces :file:`Jobname.EMAT` and"
" :file:`JobnameESAV`. If you want to include prestress effects ( "
":ref:`pstres`,ON) from a previous prestress analysis, the ELFORM option "
"requires the :file:`Jobname.EMAT` and :file:`Jobname.ESAV` files generated "
"by that analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:54
msgid ""
"Directs the program to perform a partial solution (that is, one step of an "
"analysis sequence). Predefined analysis types ( :ref:`antype` ) perform a "
"defined subset of these solution steps in a predefined sequence. You can use"
" the partial-solution procedure to repeat a certain step of an analysis or "
"to restart an analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:59
msgid ""
"Not all steps are valid for all analysis types. The order of the steps may "
"vary depending on the result you desire. See the `Basic Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS19.html>`_"
" for a description of how to perform partial and predefined solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:68
msgid ""
"In a cyclic symmetry analysis, :ref:`psolve`,EIGLANB or "
":ref:`psolve`,EIGLANPCG performs the modal analysis at multiple load steps, "
"one for each nodal-diameter specified via the :ref:`cycopt` command. In "
"addition, the eigenvector solution is expanded at each nodal-diameter "
"solution, eliminating the need for a separate expansion pass ( "
":ref:`psolve`,EIGEXP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:73
msgid ""
"If :file:`Jobname.EMAT` is required, run the prior analysis with "
":ref:`ematwrite`,YES to ensure that a :file:`Jobname.EMAT` is generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.psolve:76
msgid ""
"Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction Only the EIGLANB, and "
"EIGLANPCG options on this command are supported in a DMP solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rate.rst:2
msgid ""
