#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:12
msgid "Residual vector key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:14
msgid "``OFF`` - Do not calculate or include residual vectors (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:16
msgid "``ON`` - Calculate or include residual vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:18
msgid "**keyresp** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:19
msgid "Residual response key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:21
msgid "``OFF`` - Do not calculate or include residual responses (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:23
msgid "``ON`` - Calculate or include residual responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:37
msgid ""
"In a `modal analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/Hlp_G_STR_SMSUP.html>`_,"
" the :ref:`resvec` command calculates residual vectors (or responses). In a "
"`mode-superposition transient "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/Hlp_G_STR5_10.html#a4iQxq2c8mcm>`_,"
" `mode-superposition harmonic "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/Hlp_G_STR4_MODESUPER.html#aMhQxq6emcm>`_,"
" PSD or `spectrum "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/Hlp_G_STR6_2.html#>`_"
" analysis, the command includes residual vectors. The command must be issued"
" during the first modal solve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:47
msgid ""
"In the expansion pass of a mode-superposition transient or mode-"
"superposition harmonic analysis, the command includes residual responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:50
msgid ""
"In a component mode synthesis (CMS) `generation pass "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_substr/advcmssuperelem.html#usingcms_elemcalc>`_,"
" the :ref:`resvec` command calculates one residual vector which is included "
"in the normal modes basis used in the transformation matrix. It is supported"
" for the three available `CMS methods "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_anproc6.html#eq39b62ffb-3890-471d-a79e-2d6096214d0b>`_."
" :ref:`resvec`,ON can only be specified in the first load step of a "
"generation pass and is ignored if issued at another load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:58
msgid ""
"If rigid-body modes exist, pseudo-constraints are required for the "
"calculation. Issue the :ref:`d`,,,SUPPORT command to specify only the "
"minimum number of pseudo-constraints necessary to prevent rigid-body motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:62
msgid ""
"Both residual vector and residual response approaches cannot be used in the "
"same analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.resvec:64
msgid ""
"For more information about residual vector or residual response formulation,"
" see `Residual Vector Method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_tool9.html#resvec_125>`_"
" `Residual Response Method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_tool9.html#thy_antools_resresp_eqn2>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:2
msgid "Offsets node or element IDs in the FE geometry record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RSTOFF "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RSTOFF.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:10
msgid ""
"Issuing the :ref:`rstoff` command with no specified argument values applies "
"no offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:15
msgid "The offset type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:17
msgid "``NODE`` - Offset the node IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:19
msgid "``ELEM`` - Offset the element IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:22
msgid ""
"A positive integer value specifying the offset value to apply. The value "
"must be greater than the number of nodes or elements in the existing "
"superelement results file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:37
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rstoff` command offsets node or element IDs in the FE geometry "
"record saved in the :file:`.rst` results file. Use the command when "
"expanding superelements in a bottom-up substructuring analysis (where each "
"superelement is generated individually in a `generation pass "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_substr/advcmssuperelem.html#usingcms_elemcalc>`_,"
" and all superelements are assembled together in the `use pass "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_substr/an9Auq1d6ldm.html#advobsl5jla062999>`_"
" )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:45
msgid ""
"With appropriate offsets, you can write results files with unique node or "
"element IDs and thus display the entire model even if the original "
"superelements have overlapping element or node ID sets. (Such results files "
"are incompatible with the :file:`.db` database file saved at the generation "
"pass.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:50
msgid ""
"The offset that you specify is based on the original superelement node or "
"element numbering, rather than on any offset specified via a :ref:`sesymm` "
"or :ref:`setran` command. When issuing an :ref:`rstoff` command, avoid "
"specifying an offset that creates conflicting node or element numbers for a "
"superelement generated via a :ref:`sesymm` or :ref:`setran` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:55
msgid ""
"If you issue the command to set non-zero offsets for node or element IDs, "
"you must bring the geometry into the database via the :ref:`set` command so "
"that Mechanical APDL can display the results. Specify appropriate offsets to"
" avoid overlapping node or element IDs with other superelement results "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.rstoff:61
msgid ""
"The command is valid only in the first load step of a `superelement "
"expansion pass "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_substr/axcAuq367ldm.html#adv5note4jla062999>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:2
msgid "Specifies System Coupling options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SCOPT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SCOPT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:8
msgid "**tempdepkey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:9
msgid ""
"Temperature-dependent behavior key based on the convection coefficient:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:11
msgid ""
"``YES`` - A negative convection coefficient, - ``N``, is assumed to be a "
"function of temperature and is determined from the HF property table for "
"material ``N`` ( :ref:`mp` command). This is the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:15
msgid ""
"``NO`` - A negative convection coefficient, - ``N``, is used as is in the "
"convection calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:17
msgid "**mappingkey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:18
msgid ""
"Controls whether midside nodes of higher-order elements are used for mapping"
" on System Coupling interfaces:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:21
msgid "``YES`` - Both corner and midside nodes are used (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:23
msgid "``NO`` - Only corner nodes are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.scopt:39
msgid ""
"By default in the Mechanical APDL program, a negative convection coefficient"
" value triggers temperature- dependent behavior. In some one-way CFD to "
"Mechanical APDL thermal simulations, it is desirable to allow convection "
"coefficients to be used as negative values. To do so, issue the command "
":ref:`scopt`,NO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:2
msgid "Specifies options for the substructure expansion pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SEEXP "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SEEXP.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:9
msgid ""
"The name (case-sensitive) of the superelement matrix file created by the "
"substructure generation pass ( :file:`Sename.SUB` ). Defaults to the initial"
" jobname :file:`File`. If a number, it is the element number of the "
"superelement as used in the use pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:13
msgid "**usefil** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:14
msgid ""
"The name of the file containing the superelement degree-of-freedom (DOF) "
"solution created by the substructure use pass ( :file:`Usefil.DSUB` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:17
msgid "**imagky** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:18
msgid ""
"Key to specify use of the imaginary component of the DOF solution. "
"Applicable only if the use pass is a harmonic ( :ref:`antype`,HARMIC) "
"analysis:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:21
msgid "``OFF`` - Use real component of DOF solution (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:23
msgid "``ON`` - Use imaginary component of DOF solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:25
msgid ""
"If all solutions are to be expanded ( :ref:`numexp`,ALL), ``Imagky`` is "
"ignored and both the real"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:26
msgid "and imaginary solutions are expanded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:28
msgid "**expopt** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:29
msgid ""
"Key to specify whether the superelement ( :ref:`antype` ,SUBSTR) expansion "
"pass ( :ref:`expass`,ON) should transform the geometry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:31
msgid "``OFF`` - Do not transform node or element locations (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:33
msgid ""
"``ON`` - Transform node or element locations in the FE geometry record of "
"the :file:`.rst` results file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:50
msgid ""
"Specifies options for the expansion pass of the substructure analysis ( "
":ref:`antype`,SUBSTR). If used in SOLUTION, this command is valid only "
"within the first load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seexp:53
msgid ""
"If you specify geometry transformation ( ``Expopt`` = ON), you must retrieve"
" the transformation matrix (if it exists) from the specified :file:`.SUB` "
"file. The command updates the nodal X, Y, and Z coordinates to represent the"
" transformed node locations. The ``Expopt`` option is useful when you want "
"to expand superelements created from other superelements (via :ref:`setran` "
"or :ref:`sesymm` commands). For more information, see and."
msgstr ""

