#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:68
msgid "**lpnamekey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:69
msgid ""
"``ON`` - All files created during the generation pass are named using "
"``Sename``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:71
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - All files created during the generation pass are named using the "
":file:`Jobname` defined for the analysis (see :ref:`filname` command) except"
" for the :file:`.sub` file, which uses ``Sename`` if specified (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:89
msgid ""
":ref:`seopt` specifies substructure analysis options ( "
":ref:`antype`,SUBSTR). If used during solution, the command is valid only "
"within the first load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:92
msgid ""
"When ocean waves ( :ref:`octype`,,WAVE) are present, the ``SeOcLvL`` "
"argument specifies the ocean height or level to use for the added-mass "
"calculation, as the use-run analysis type is unknown during the generation "
"run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:96
msgid ""
"The expansion pass method RESOLVE is not supported with component mode "
"synthesis analysis ( :ref:`cmsopt` ). ``ExpMth`` is automatically set to "
"BACKSUB for CMS analysis. The RESOLVE method invalidates the use of the "
":ref:`numexp` command. The RESOLVE method does not allow the restarting of "
"the substructure generation pass and the computation of results based on "
"nodal velocity and nodal acceleration (damping force, inertial force, "
"kinetic energy, etc.) in the substructure expansion pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:103
msgid ""
"If ``ExpMth`` = NONE or BCLV in a substructure analysis or component mode "
"synthesis (CMS) analysis ( :ref:`cmsopt` ) using the fixed-interface ( "
":ref:`cmsopt`,FIX) or free-interface ( :ref:`cmsopt` ,FREE) methods, you "
"cannot restart the generation pass or perform the expansion pass. (In CMS "
"analyses using those methods, however, the expansion pass is possible when "
"element-results calculation is activated in the generation pass ( ``ELCALC``"
" = YES on :ref:`cmsopt` )). The ``ExpMth`` argument is not required for CMS "
"analysis using the residual-flexible free-interface method ( "
":ref:`cmsopt`,RFFB)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.seopt:111
msgid ""
"For linear perturbation substructure generation pass with multiple "
"substructures, set ``LPnameKey`` = ON to avoid copying files at the end of "
"each generation pass with the :ref:`copy` command. For an example with CMS "
"analysis using the fixed-interface method, see."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:2
msgid "Specifies Supernode (SNODE) eigensolver options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SNOPTION "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SNOPTION.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:10
msgid ""
"``RangeFact`` = 2.0. ``BlockSize`` is set to min( ``NMODE``,40), where "
"``NMODE`` is the number of modes to be computed as set on the :ref:`modopt` "
"command. ``RobustLev`` = 0. ``Compute`` = BOTH. Additional output is not "
"printed ( ``Solve_Info`` = OFF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:16
msgid "**rangefact** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:17
msgid ""
"Factor used to control the range of eigenvalues computed for each supernode."
" The value of ``RangeFact`` must be a number between 1.0 and 10.0. By "
"default the ``RangeFact`` value is set to 2.0, which means that all "
"eigenvalues between 0 and 2\\* ``FREQE`` are computed for each supernode "
"(where ``FREQE`` is the upper end of the frequency range of interest as "
"specified on the :ref:`modopt` command). As the ``RangeFact`` value "
"increases, the eigensolution for the SNODE solver becomes more accurate and "
"the computational time increases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:19
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:103
msgid "**blocksize** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:20
msgid ""
"``BlockSize`` to be used when computing the final eigenvectors. The value of"
" ``Blocksize`` must be either MAX or a number between 1 and ``NMODE``, where"
" ``NMODE`` is the number of modes to be computed as set on the :ref:`modopt`"
" command. Input a value of MAX to force the algorithm to allocate enough "
"memory to hold all of the final eigenvectors in memory and, therefore, only "
"read through the file containing the supernode eigenvectors once. Note that "
"this setting is ONLY recommended when there is sufficient physical memory on"
" the machine to safely hold all of the final eigenvectors in memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:28
msgid "**robustlev** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:29
msgid ""
"Parameter used to control the robustness of the SNODE eigensolver. The value"
" of ``RobustLev`` must be a number between 0 and 10. Lower values of "
"``RobustLev`` allow the eigensolver to run in the most efficient manner for "
"optimal performance. Higher values of ``RobustLev`` often slow down the "
"performance of the eigensolver, but can increase the robustness; this may be"
" desirable if a problem is detected with the eigensolver or its "
"eigensolution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:35
msgid "**compute** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:36
msgid ""
"Key to control which computations are performed by the Supernode "
"eigensolver:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:38
msgid "``EVALUE`` - The eigensolver computes only the eigenvalues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:40
msgid ""
"``EVECTOR`` - The eigensolver computes only the eigenvectors (must be "
"preceded by a modal analysis where the eigenvalues were computed using the "
"Supernode eigensolver)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:43
msgid ""
"``BOTH`` - The eigensolver computes both the eigenvalues and eigenvectors in"
" the same pass (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:49
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - Turns off additional output printing from the Supernode "
"eigensolver (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:51
msgid ""
"``PERFORMANCE`` - Turns on additional output printing from the Supernode "
"eigensolver, including a performance summary and a summary of file I/O for "
"the Supernode eigensolver. Information on memory usage during assembly of "
"the global matrices (that is, creation of the :file:`Jobname.FULL` file) is "
"also printed with this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:70
msgid "This command specifies options for the Supernode (SNODE) eigensolver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:72
msgid ""
"Setting ``RangeFact`` to a value between 2.0 and 10.0 will improve the "
"accuracy of the computed eigenvalues and eigenvectors, but will often "
"increase the computing time of the SNODE eigensolver. Conversely, setting "
"``RangeFact`` to a value less than 2.0 will deteriorate the accuracy of the "
"computed eigenvalues and eigenvectors, but will often speed up the computing"
" time of the SNODE eigensolver. The default value of 2.0 has been set as a "
"good blend of accuracy and performance. If the model has rigid body modes, "
"setting ``RangeFact`` higher than 2 is recommended to achieve better "
"solution accuracy for the lower flexible modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:80
msgid ""
"The SNODE eigensolver reads the eigenvectors and related information for "
"each supernode from a file and uses that information to compute the final "
"eigenvectors. For each eigenvalue/eigenvector requested by the user, the "
"program must do one pass through the entire file that contains the supernode"
" eigenvectors. By choosing a ``BlockSize`` value greater than 1, the program"
" can compute ``BlockSize`` number of final eigenvectors for each pass "
"through the file. Therefore, smaller values of ``BlockSize`` result in more "
"I/O, and larger values of ``BlockSize`` result in less I/O. Larger values of"
" ``BlockSize`` also result in significant additional memory usage, as "
"``BlockSize`` number of final eigenvectors must be stored in memory. The "
"default ``Blocksize`` of min( ``NMODE``,40) is normally a good choice to "
"balance memory and I/O usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:90
msgid ""
"The ``RobustLev`` field should only be used when a problem is detected with "
"the accuracy of the final solution or if the Supernode eigensolver fails "
"while computing the eigenvalues/eigenvectors. Setting ``RobustLev`` to a "
"value greater than 0 will cause the performance of the eigensolver to "
"deteriorate. If the performance deteriorates too much or if the eigensolver "
"continues to fail when setting the ``RobustLev`` field to higher values, "
"then switching to another eigensolver such as Block Lanczos or PCG Lanczos "
"is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:97
msgid ""
"Setting ``Compute`` = EVALUE causes the Supernode eigensolver to compute "
"only the requested eigenvalues. During this process a :file:`Jobname.SNODE` "
"file is written; however, a :file:`Jobname.MODE` file is not written. Thus, "
"errors will likely occur in any downstream computations that require the "
":file:`Jobname.MODE` file (for example, participation factor computations, "
"mode superpostion transient/harmonic analysis, PSD analysis). Setting "
"``Compute`` = EVECTOR causes the Supernode eigensolver to compute only the "
"corresponding eigenvectors. The :file:`Jobname.SNODE` file and the "
"associated :file:`Jobname.FULL` file are required when requesting these "
"eigenvectors. In other words, the eigenvalues must have already been "
"computed for this model before computing the eigenvectors. This field can be"
" useful in order to separate the two steps (computing eigenvalues and "
"computing eigenvectors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.snoption:108
msgid ""
"For more information on the eigensolver's accuracy and a discussion of its "
"known limitations, see in the `Mechanical APDL Theory Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_biblio.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.solve.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.solve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.solve:2
msgid "Starts a solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.solve:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `SOLVE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SOLVE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.solve:9
msgid ""
"Action to be performed on solve (used only for linear perturbation "
"analyses)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.solve:11
msgid ""
"``ELFORM`` - Reform all appropriate element matrices in the first phase of a"
" linear perturbation analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.solve:28
msgid ""
"Starts the solution of one load step of a solution sequence based on the "
"current analysis type and option settings. Use ``Action`` = ELFORM only in "
"the first phase of a `linear perturbation analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strlinpertother.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:2
msgid ""
"Activates stabilization for all elements that support nonlinear "
"stabilization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `STABILIZE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_STABILIZE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:9
msgid "Key for controlling nonlinear stabilization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:11
msgid "``OFF`` - Deactivate stabilization (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:13
msgid ""
"``CONSTANT`` - Activate stabilization. The energy-dissipation ratio or "
"damping factor remains constant during the load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:16
msgid ""
"``REDUCE`` - Activate stabilization. The energy-dissipation ratio or damping"
" factor is reduced linearly to zero at the end of the load step from the "
"specified or calculated value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:20
msgid "The stabilization-control method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:22
msgid ""
"``ENERGY`` - Use the energy-dissipation ratio as the control. This value is "
"the default when ``Key`` ≠ OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:25
msgid "``DAMPING`` - Use the damping factor as the control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:28
msgid ""
"The energy-dissipation ratio ( ``Method`` = ENERGY) or damping factor ( "
"``Method`` = DAMPING). This value must be greater than 0 when ``Method`` = "
"ENERGY or ``Method`` = DAMPING. When ``Method`` = ENERGY, this value is "
"usually a number between 0 and 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:32
msgid "**substpopt** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:33
msgid "Option for the first substep of the load step:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:35
msgid ""
"``NO`` - Stabilization is not activated for the first substep even when it "
"does not converge after the minimal allowed time increment is reached. This "
"value is the default when ``Key`` ≠ OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:38
msgid ""
"``MINTIME`` - Stabilization is activated for the first substep if it still "
"does not converge after the minimal allowed time increment is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:41
msgid ""
"``ANYTIME`` - Stabilization is activated for the first substep. Use this "
"option if stabilization was active for the previous load step via ``Key`` = "
"CONSTANT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:44
msgid "**forcelimit** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:45
msgid ""
"The stabilization force limit coefficient, such that 0 < ``FORCELIMIT`` < 1."
" The default value is 0.2. To omit a stabilization force check, set this "
"value to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:48
msgid "**recalcdamp** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:49
msgid "Key for controlling damping recalculation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:51
msgid "0 - No recalculation of the damping factor (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:52
msgid ""
"1 - Recalculate the damping factor for the energy-based stabilization-"
"control method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:68
msgid ""
"Once issued, a :ref:`stabilize` command remains in effect until you reissue "
"the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:70
msgid ""
"For the energy dissipation ratio, specify ``VALUE`` = 1.0e-4 if you have no "
"prior experience with the current model; if convergence problems are still "
"an issue, increase the value gradually. The damping factor is mesh-, "
"material-, and time-step-dependent; an initial reference value from the "
"previous run (such as a run with the energy-dissipation ratio as input) "
"should suggest itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:75
msgid ""
"Exercise caution when specifying ``SubStpOpt`` = MINTIME or ANYTIME for the "
"first load step; Ansys, Inc. recommends this option only for experienced "
"users. If stabilization was active for the previous load step via ``Key`` = "
"CONSTANT and convergence is an issue for the first substep, specify "
"``SubStpOpt`` = ANYTIME."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:80
msgid ""
"When the L2-norm of the stabilization force (CSRSS value) exceeds the "
"L2-norm of the internal force multiplied by the stabilization force "
"coefficient, the program issues a message displaying both the stabilization "
"force norm and the internal force norm. The ``FORCELIMIT`` argument enables "
"you to change the default stabilization force coefficient (normally 20 "
"percent)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:85
msgid ""
"When using the energy-based stabilization-control method and ``RECALCDAMP`` "
"= 1, the damping factor is recalculated in the following cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:88
msgid ""
"In an analysis `restart "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS3_12.html#bassolumodres>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:91
msgid ""
"In a nonlinear adaptivity analysis in the substep following the remeshing "
"substep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:93
msgid ""
"This command stabilizes the degrees of freedom for `current-technology "
"elements "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/EL2oldnewtable.html#EL2curtechelembenefits>`_"
" only. Other elements can be included in the FE model, but their degrees of "
"freedom are not stabilized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.stabilize:98
msgid ""
"For more information about nonlinear stabilization, see `Unstable Structures"
" "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/Hlp_G_STRUNST.html#strnonstabvsarclen>`_"
" in the `Structural Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/str_enercalc_app.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:2
msgid "Enables or disables thermal loading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `THEXPAND "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_THEXPAND.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:11
msgid "``ON`` - Thermal loading is included in the load vector (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:13
msgid "``OFF`` - Thermal loading is not included in the load vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:29
msgid ""
"Temperatures applied in the analysis are used by default to evaluate "
"material properties and contribute to the load vector if the temperature "
"does not equal the reference temperature and a coefficient of thermal "
"expansion is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:33
msgid ""
"Use :ref:`thexpand`,OFF to evaluate the material properties but not "
"contribute to the load vector. This capability is particularly useful when "
"performing a harmonic analysis where you do not want to include harmonically"
" varying thermal loads. It is also useful in a modal analysis when computing"
" a modal load vector but excluding the thermal load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thexpand:38
msgid ""
"This command is valid for all analysis types except linear perturbation "
"modal and linear perturbation harmonic analyses. For these two linear "
"perturbation analysis types, the program internally sets "
":ref:`thexpand`,OFF, and it cannot be set to ON by using this command ( "
":ref:`thexpand`,ON is ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thopt.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.analysis\\_options.AnalysisOptions.thopt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/analysis_options.rst:70:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thopt:2
msgid "Specifies nonlinear transient thermal solution options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.analysis_options.AnalysisOptions.thopt:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `THOPT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_THOPT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/analysis_options.pydocstring
