#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:26
msgid ""
"The number of modes to extract. The value can depend on the value supplied "
"for ``Method``. ``NMODE`` has no default and must be specified. If "
"``Method`` = LANB, LANPCG, or SNODE, the number of modes that can be "
"extracted can equal the DOFs in the model after the application of all "
"boundary conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:31
msgid ""
"For ``Method`` = LANB, SUBSP and UNSYM, you can specify ``NMODE`` = ALL to "
"extract all eigenvalues in a given frequency range. To use this option, you "
"must also define the frequency range (that is, a ``FREQE`` value must be "
"set)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:35
msgid "Recommendation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:37
msgid ""
"When ``Method`` = LANPCG, ``NMODE`` should be less than 100 to be "
"computationally efficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:38
msgid ""
"When ``Method`` = SNODE, ``NMODE`` should be greater than 100 for 2D plane "
"or 3D shell/beam models and greater than 250 for 3D solid elements to be "
"computationally efficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:42
msgid ""
"The beginning, or lower end, of the frequency range (or eigenvalue range if "
"``FREQMOD`` is specified) of interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:45
msgid ""
"For ``Method`` = LANB, SUBSP, UNSYM, DAMP, and QRDAMP, ``FREQB`` also "
"represents the first shift point for the eigenvalue iterations. For UNSYM "
"and DAMP, the default = -1.0 For other methods, the default is calculated "
"internally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:49
msgid ""
"Eigenvalue extraction is most accurate near the shift point. Multiple shift "
"points are used internally in the LANB, SUBSP, UNSYM, and QRDAMP methods. "
"For the LANB, LANPCG, SUBSP, UNSYM, DAMP, and QRDAMP methods with a positive"
" ``FREQB`` value, eigenvalues are output beginning at the shift point and "
"increase in magnitude. For the UNSYM and DAMP methods with a negative "
"``FREQB`` value, eigenvalues are output beginning at zero magnitude and "
"increase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:55
msgid ""
"Choosing higher ``FREQB`` values with the LANPCG and SNODE methods may lead "
"to inefficient solution times because these methods will find all "
"eigenvalues between zero and ``FREQB`` before finding the requested modes "
"between ``FREQB`` and ``FREQE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:60
msgid ""
"The ending, or upper end, of the frequency range (or eigenvalue range if "
"``FREQMOD`` is specified) of interest (in Hz). Default = 100 Hz when "
"``Method`` = SNODE. The default for all other methods is to calculate all "
"modes, regardless of their maximum frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:64
msgid ""
"To maintain solution efficiency, do not set the ``FREQE`` value too high; "
"for example, not higher than 5000 Hz for an industrial problem. The higher "
"the ``FREQE`` value used for the SNODE method, the more accurate the "
"solution and the more eigenvalues produced; however, the solution time also "
"increases. For example, if ``FREQE`` is set to 1e8, it causes the underlying"
" supernodal structures to find all possible eigenvalues of each group of "
"supernodes, requiring excessive solution time. The accuracy of the SNODE "
"solution is controlled by ``FREQE`` and by the ``RangeFact`` value on the "
":ref:`snoption` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:72
msgid "**cpxmod** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:73
msgid ""
"Complex eigenmode key. (Valid only when ``Method`` = QRDAMP or ``Method`` = "
"UNSYM)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:75
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Determine automatically if the eigensolutions are real or complex"
" and output them accordingly (default when ``Method`` = UNSYM). Not "
"supported for ``Method`` = QRDAMP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:78
msgid "``ON or CPLX`` - Calculate and output complex eigenmode shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:80
msgid ""
"``OFF or REAL`` - Do not calculate complex eigenmode shapes (default). This "
"setting is required if a mode- superposition analysis is intended after the "
"modal analysis for ``Method`` = QRDAMP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:83
msgid "**nrmkey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:84
msgid "Mode shape normalization key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:86
msgid ""
"``OFF`` - Normalize the mode shapes to the mass matrix (default). This "
"option is invalid for damped modal cyclic symmetry ( ``Method`` = DAMP or "
"QRDAMP with the :ref:`cyclic` command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:89
msgid ""
"``ON`` - Normalize the mode shapes to unity instead of to the mass matrix "
"(default for damped modal cyclic symmetry [ ``Method`` = DAMP or QRDAMP with"
" the :ref:`cyclic` command])."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:92
msgid ""
"If a subsequent spectrum or mode-superposition analysis is planned, the mode"
" shapes should be normalized to the mass matrix ( ``Nrmkey`` = OFF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:95
msgid "**modtype** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:96
msgid ""
"Type of modes calculated by the eigensolver. Only applicable to the "
"unsymmetric eigensolver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:98
msgid "```` - Right eigenmodes (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:100
msgid ""
"``BOTH`` - Right and left eigenmodes. The left eigenmodes are written to "
":file:`Jobname.LMODE`. This option must be activated if a mode-superposition"
" analysis is intended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:104
msgid ""
"The block vector size to be used with the Block Lanczos or Subspace "
"eigensolver (used only when ``Method`` = LANB or SUBSP). ``BlockSize`` must "
"be an integer value between 0 and 16. When BlockSize = zero or blank, the "
"code decides the block size internally (normally, a value of 8 is used for "
"LANB and a value of 6 is used for SUBSP). Typically, higher ``BlockSize`` "
"values are more efficient under each of the following conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:106
msgid ""
"When running in out-of-core mode and there is not enough physical memory to "
"buffer all of the files written by the Block Lanczos or Subspace eigensolver"
" (and thus, the time spent doing I/O is considerable)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:110
msgid "Many modes are requested (>100)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:112
msgid "Higher-order solid elements dominate the model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:114
msgid "The memory usage only slightly increases as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:115
msgid ""
"``BlockSize`` is increased. It is recommended that you use a value divisible"
" by 4 (4, 8, 12, or 16)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:117
msgid "**freqmod** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:118
msgid ""
"The specified frequency when the solved eigenvalues are no longer "
"frequencies (for example, the model has the Floquet periodic boundary "
"condition). In a modal analysis, the Floquet periodic boundary condition "
"(body load FPBC) is only valid for the acoustic elements ``FLUID30``, "
"``FLUID220``, and ``FLUID221``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:137
msgid "Specifies modal analysis ( :ref:`antype`,MODAL) options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:139
msgid ""
"Additional options for specific eigensolvers are controlled by these "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:141
msgid ""
":ref:`snoption` specifies options for the Supernode (SNODE) eigensolver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:143
msgid ":ref:`subopt` specifies options for the Subspace (SUBSP) eigensolver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:145
msgid ":ref:`qrdopt` specifies options for the QRDAMP eigensolver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:147
msgid ":ref:`dampopt` specifies options for the damped (DAMP) eigensolver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:149
msgid ""
":ref:`lanboption` specifies options for the Block Lanczos (LANB) "
"eigensolver. For more difficult modal problems, you can specify an "
"alternative version of the Block Lanczos eigensolver ( :ref:`lanboption`, "
"ALT1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:153
msgid ""
"If ``Method`` = LANPCG, Mechanical APDL automatically switches to the PCG "
"solver internally for this modal analysis. You can further control the "
"efficiency of the PCG solver with the :ref:`pcgopt` and :ref:`eqslv` "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/dynamic_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.dynamic_options.DynamicOptions.modopt:158
msgid ""
"For models that involve a non-symmetric element stiffness matrix, as in the "
"case of a contact element with frictional contact, the QRDAMP eigensolver ( "
":ref:`modopt`, QRDAMP) extracts modes in the modal subspace formed by the "
"eigenmodes from the symmetrized eigenproblem. The QRDAMP eigensolver "
"symmetrizes the element stiffness matrix on the first pass of the "
"eigensolution, and in the second pass, eigenmodes are extracted in the modal"
" subspace of the first eigensolution pass. For such non-symmetric "
"eigenproblems, you should verify the eigenvalue and eigenmode results using "
"the non-symmetric matrix eigensolver ( :ref:`modopt`,UNSYM)."
