#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:2
msgid "Defines an element body-force load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `BFE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_BFE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:9
msgid ""
"The element to which body load applies. If ALL, apply to all selected "
"elements ( :ref:`esel` ). A component name may also be substituted for "
"``Elem``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:13
msgid ""
"Valid body load label. Valid labels are also listed for each element type in"
" the `Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_"
" under \"Body Loads\" in the input table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:21
msgid ""
"Starting location for entering ``VAL`` data, below. For example, if "
"``STLOC`` = 1, data input in the ``VAL1`` field applies to the first element"
" body load item available for the element type, ``VAL2`` applies to the "
"second element item, etc. If ``STLOC`` = 5, data input in the ``VAL1`` field"
" applies to the fifth element item, etc. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:27
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:56
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:85
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:114
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = TEMP, FLUE, DGEN, HGEN, and CHRGD, ``VAL1`` -- ``VAL4`` "
"represent body load values at the starting location and subsequent locations"
" (usually nodes) in the element. ``VAL1`` can also represent a table name "
"for use with tabular boundary conditions. Enter only ``VAL1`` for a uniform "
"body load across the element. For nonuniform loads, the values must be input"
" in the same order as shown in the input table for the element type. Values "
"initially default to the :ref:`bfunif` value (except for CHRGD which "
"defaults to zero). For subsequent specifications, a blank leaves a "
"previously specified value unchanged; if the value was not previously "
"specified, the default value as described in the `Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_"
" is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:37
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:66
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:95
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:124
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = JS and ``STLOC`` = 1, ``VAL1``, ``VAL2`` and ``VAL3`` are the "
"X, Y, and Z components of current density (in the element coordinate "
"system), and ``VAL4`` is the phase angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:41
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:70
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:99
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:128
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = EF and ``STLOC`` = 1, ``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, and ``VAL3`` are the"
" X, Y, and Z components of electric field (in the global Cartesian "
"coordinate system)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:44
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:73
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:102
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:131
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = FVIN in a unidirectional Mechanical APDL to Ansys CFX analysis,"
" ``VAL2`` is the volume interface number (not available from within the "
"GUI), and ``VAL1``, ``VAL3``, and ``VAL4`` are not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:48
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:77
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:106
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:135
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = FORC and ``STLOC`` = 1, ``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, and ``VAL3`` are "
"the real X, Y, and Z components of force density (in the global Cartesian "
"coordinate system)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:51
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:80
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:109
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:138
msgid ""
"For analyses that allow complex input, if ``Lab`` = FORC and ``STLOC`` = 4, "
"``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, and ``VAL3`` are the imaginary X, Y, and Z components of"
" force density (in the global Cartesian coordinate system)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:156
msgid ""
"Defines an element body-force load (such as the temperature in a structural "
"analysis or the heat- generation rate in a thermal analysis). Body loads and"
" element specific defaults are described for each element type in the "
"`Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_."
" If both the :ref:`bf` and :ref:`bfe` commands are used to apply a body-"
"force load to an element, the :ref:`bfe` command takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:163
msgid ""
"Imaginary values for FORC loading via :ref:`bfe` is supported by current-"
"technology solid elements ( ``PLANE182``, ``PLANE183``, ``SOLID185``, "
"``SOLID186``, ``SOLID187``, and ``SOLID285`` ) and reinforcing elements ( "
"``REINF263``, ``REINF264``, and ``REINF265`` ). Use only for modal or "
"harmonic analyses. Large-deflection effects must be disabled ( "
":ref:`nlgeom`,OFF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:168
msgid ""
"The following topics for applying HGEN loading via the :ref:`bfe` command "
"are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:170
msgid ""
"For HGEN loading on layered thermal solid elements ``SOLID278`` / "
"``SOLID279`` (KEYOPT(3) = 1 or 2), or layered thermal shell elements "
"``SHELL131`` / ``SHELL132`` (KEYOPT(3) = 1), ``STLOC`` refers to the layer "
"number (not the node). In such cases, specify ``VAL1`` through ``VAL4`` to "
"specify the heat-generation values for the appropriate layers. Heat "
"generation is constant over the layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:175
msgid ""
"For HGEN loading on `reinforcing "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/str_compreinfdirectemb.html>`_"
" elements ``REINF263``, ``REINF264``, and ``REINF265``, ``STLOC`` refers to "
"the corner locations of the reinforcing members (individual reinforcings):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:180
msgid ""
"``REINF263`` and ``REINF264`` : Specify ``VAL1`` and ``VAL2`` for each "
"member. For tables, specify ``VAL1`` only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:183
msgid ""
"``REINF265`` : Specify ``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, ``VAL3``, and ``VAL4`` for each "
"member. For tables, specify ``VAL1`` only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:186
msgid ""
"For FORC loading on reinforcing elements, ``STLOC`` refers to real ( "
"``STLOC`` = 1) or imaginary ( ``STLOC`` = 4) components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:189
msgid ""
"When using the `standard method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
" for defining reinforcing, this is the only way to apply a body load (HGEN "
"or FORC) on the reinforcing members created after generating the REINF "
"``nnn`` reinforcing elements ( :ref:`ereinf` ). If applying FORC loading, "
"Mechanical APDL applies a uniform load to all reinforcing members if there "
"are multiple members in selected elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:197
msgid ""
"When using the `mesh-independent method "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strreinfworkflow.html#>`_"
" for defining reinforcing, you can apply a body load on the reinforcing "
"members in the same way. The preferred method, however, is to apply loads on"
" the ``MESH200`` elements (via :ref:`bfe` or :ref:`bf` for HGEN, BFE for "
"FORC) before generating the REINF ``nnn`` reinforcing elements ( "
":ref:`ereinf` ). Mechanical APDL maps the loads from the ``MESH200`` "
"elements to the newly generated REINF ``nnn`` reinforcing elements "
"automatically. If you need to apply the loads after generating the "
"reinforcing elements, apply them to ``MESH200`` elements and issue "
":ref:`bfport` to transfer the loads to the reinforcing members."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:208
msgid ""
"You can specify a table name ( ``VAL1`` ) when using temperature (TEMP), "
"diffusing substance generation rate (DGEN), heat generation rate (HGEN), and"
" current density (JS) body load labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:211
msgid ""
"For the body-force-density label (FORC), you can specify a table for any of "
"the ``VAL1`` through ``VAL3`` arguments. Both 1D and 2D tables are valid; "
"however, only 1D tables are valid in mode- superposition harmonic and mode-"
"superposition transient analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:215
msgid ""
"Enclose the table name ( ``tabname`` ) in percent signs (%), for example :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:217
msgid ":ref:`bfe`, ``Elem``, ``Lab``, ``STLOC``,``tabname``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:219
msgid ""
"Use the :ref:`dim` command to define a table. For information on primary "
"variables for each load type, see `Applying Loads Using Tabular Input "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS2_6.html#gbas5dexample>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:223
msgid ""
"For ``Lab`` = TEMP, each table defines ``NTEMP`` temperatures, as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_body_loads.FeBodyLoads.bfe:225
msgid ""
"For layered elements, ``NTEMP`` is the number of layer interface corners "
"that allow temperature input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_body_loads.pydocstring
