msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `LDREAD "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_LDREAD.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:9
msgid "Valid load label:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:11
msgid ""
"``TEMP`` - Temperatures from a thermal analysis are applied as body force "
"nodal loads ( :ref:`bf` ) in a structural analysis or other type of "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:14
msgid ""
"When used in conjunction with ``KIMG`` = 1 or ``KIMG`` = 2, temperatures can"
" be applied to a subsequent thermal analysis as nodal loads ( :ref:`d` ) or "
"initial conditions ( :ref:`ic` ), respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:18
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`LDREAD_notes` section for details on transferring temperatures"
" from layered thermal shell elements ( ``SHELL131``, ``SHELL132`` ) and "
"layered thermal solid elements ( ``SOLID278``, ``SOLID279`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:22
msgid ""
"``FORC`` - Forces from an electromagnetic analysis are applied as force "
"loads ( :ref:`f` ) in a structural analysis. :ref:`ldread`,FORC reads "
"coupling forces. See the discussion on `force computation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_lof/Hlp_G_ELE6_5.html#emagreluctfig>`_"
" in the `Low-Frequency Electromagnetic Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_lof/Hlp_G_ELE16.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:28
msgid ""
"For a full harmonic magnetic analysis, FORC represents the time-averaged "
"force (use in conjunction with ``KIMG`` = 2). Values are in the nodal "
"coordinate system for the force loads ( :ref:`f` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:31
msgid ""
"``HGEN`` - Heat generations from an electromagnetic analysis are applied as "
"body-force loads ( :ref:`bfe` ) in a thermal analysis. For a full harmonic "
"analysis, HGEN represents the time-averaged heat generation load (use in "
"conjunction with ``KIMG`` = 2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:35
msgid ""
"``JS`` - Source current density from a current-conduction analysis are "
"applied as body-force loads ( :ref:`bfe` ). Values are in the global "
"Cartesian coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:38
msgid ""
"``EF`` - Electric field element centroid values from an electrostatic "
"analysis are applied as body-force loads ( :ref:`bfe` ) in a magnetic "
"analysis. Values are in the global Cartesian coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:42
msgid ""
"``REAC`` - Reaction loads from any analysis are applied as force loads ( "
":ref:`f` ) in any analysis. Values are in the nodal coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:45
msgid ""
"``CONC`` - Concentrations from a diffusion analysis are applied to a "
"subsequent diffusion analysis as nodal loads ( :ref:`d` ) or initial "
"conditions ( :ref:`ic` ) when used in conjunction with ``KIMG`` =1 or "
"``KIMG`` =2, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:49
msgid ""
"``VMEN`` - Mean flow velocities from a static mean flow analysis are applied"
" to a subsequent harmonic or modal solution of the convective wave equation "
"as body-force loads ( :ref:`bf` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:52
msgid ""
"``VOLT`` - Voltages from an electric, electrostatic, or electromagnetic "
"analysis are applied to a subsequent electric, electrostatic, or "
"electromagnetic analysis as nodal loads ( :ref:`d` ) when ``KIMG`` = 1 or as"
" initial conditions ( :ref:`ic` ) when ``KIMG`` = 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:57
msgid ""
"Load step number of the data set to be read. Defaults to 1. If LAST, ignore "
"``SBSTEP`` and ``TIME`` and read the last data set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:61
msgid ""
"Substep number (within ``LSTEP`` ). If zero (or blank), ``LSTEP`` represents"
" the last substep of the load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:65
msgid ""
"Time-point identifying the data set to be read. Used only if both ``LSTEP`` "
"and ``SBSTEP`` are zero (or blank). If ``TIME`` is between two solution time"
" points on the results file, a linear interpolation is done between the two "
"data sets. If ``TIME`` is beyond the last time point on the file, use the "
"last time point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:71
msgid ""
"When used with results from harmonic analyses ( :ref:`antype`,HARMIC) "
"``KIMG`` establishes which set of data to read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:73
msgid ""
"``0`` - Read the real part of the solution. Valid also for ``Lab`` = EHFLU "
"to read in time-average heat flux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:76
msgid "``1`` - Read the imaginary part of the solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:78
msgid ""
"``2`` - Calculate and read the time-average part. Meaningful for ``Lab`` = "
"HGEN or FORC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:80
msgid ""
"When used with the PRES label, ``KIMG`` represents the shell element face on"
" which to apply the pressure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:82
msgid "``1`` - Apply pressure to face 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:84
msgid "``2`` - Apply pressure to face 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:86
msgid ""
"When used with the TEMP label, ``KIMG`` indicates how temperatures are to be"
" applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:88
msgid "``0`` - Apply temperatures as body loads ( :ref:`bf` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:90
msgid "``1`` - Apply temperatures as nodal loads ( :ref:`d` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:92
msgid "``2`` - Apply temperatures as initial conditions ( :ref:`ic` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:94
msgid ""
"When used with the CONC label, ``KIMG`` indicates how concentrations are to "
"be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:96
msgid "``1`` - Apply concentrations as nodal loads ( :ref:`d` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:98
msgid "``2`` - Apply concentrations as initial conditions ( :ref:`ic` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:100
msgid ""
"When used with the VOLT label, ``KIMG`` indicates how voltages are to be "
"applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:102
msgid "``1`` - Apply voltages as nodal loads ( :ref:`d` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:104
msgid "``2`` - Apply voltages as initial conditions ( :ref:`ic` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:112
msgid ""
"Filename extension (eight-character maximum). The extension defaults to RST "
"(or RMF for a static mean flow analysis) if ``Fname`` is blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:129
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ldread` command reads results data from the results file and "
"applies them as loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:131
msgid ""
"The command can also apply results from an analysis defined with one physics"
" environment as loads on a second analysis using a different physics "
"environment. Results values are applied as loads for field-coupling effects "
"(for example, output temperatures from a thermal analysis as input to a "
"structural analysis)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_constraints.FeConstraints.ldread:136
msgid ""
"The command works based on the assumption that the meshes have not changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_constraints.pydocstring
#: of
