#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:88
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:108
msgid "If ``Lab`` = CONV:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:33
msgid ""
"``VALUE`` is typically the film coefficient and ``VALUE2`` (below) is "
"typically the bulk temperature. If ``VALUE`` = - ``N``, the film coefficient"
" may be a function of temperature and is determined from the HF property "
"table for material ``N`` ( :ref:`mp` ). (See the :ref:`scopt` command for a "
"way to override this option and use - ``N`` as the film coefficient.) The "
"temperature used to evaluate the film coefficient is usually the average "
"between the bulk and wall temperatures, but may be user-defined for some "
"elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:39
msgid ""
"If :ref:`kbc`,0 has been issued for ramped loads, it affects only ``VALUE2``"
"  :ref:`the bulk temperature, and the film coefficient specification is "
"unaffected. <SF_V2CONV>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:41
msgid ""
"In a viscous-thermal acoustic analysis, if ``Lab`` = CONV, ``VALUE`` is the "
"real part of the heat flux and ``VALUE2`` is the imaginary part of the heat "
"flux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:44
msgid "If ``Lab`` = RAD, ``VALUE`` is surface emissivity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:46
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = PORT, ``VALUE`` is a port number representing a waveguide "
"exterior port. The port number must be an integer between 1 and 50. For "
"acoustic 2×2 transfer admittance matrix, the port number can be any positive"
" integer. The smaller port number corresponds to the port 1 of the 2×2 "
"transfer admittance matrix and the greater number corresponds to the port 2."
" If one port of the transfer admittance matrix is connecting to the "
"acoustic-structural interaction interface, the port number corresponds to "
"the port 2 of the transfer admittance matrix. A pair of ports of the 2×2 "
"transfer admittance matrix must be defined in the same element. In an "
"acoustic analysis, the positive port number defines a transparent port, "
"through which the reflected sound pressure wave propagates to the infinity; "
"the negative port number defines a vibro port that is the structural "
"vibration surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:57
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = SHLD, ``VALUE`` is the surface normal velocity in a harmonic "
"analysis or in a transient analysis solved with the velocity potential "
"formulation; ``VALUE`` is the surface normal acceleration in a transient "
"analysis solved with the pressure formulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:61
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = IMPD, ``VALUE`` is resistance in (N)(s)/m :sup:`3` if ``VALUE``"
" > 0 and is conductance in mho if ``VALUE`` < 0 for acoustic or harmonic "
"response analyses. In acoustic transient analyses, ``VALUE2`` is not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:65
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:65
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = RDSF, ``VALUE`` is the emissivity value; the following "
"conditions apply: If ``VALUE`` is between 0 and 1, apply a single value to "
"the surface. If ``VALUE`` = - ``N``, the emissivity may be a function of the"
" temperature, and is determined from the EMISS property table for material "
"``N`` ( :ref:`mp` ). The material ``N`` does not need to correlate with the "
"underlying solid thermal elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:71
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = FSIN in a one-way structure-to-acoustic coupling, ``VALUE`` is "
"the surface interface number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:74
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:71
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = FSIN in a unidirectional Mechanical APDL to CFX analysis, "
"``VALUE`` is not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:76
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:73
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = ATTN, ``VALUE`` is the absorption coefficient of the surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sf:78
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = VIMP, ``VALUE`` is resistance of viscous impedance in (N)(s)/m "
":sup:`3`."
msgstr ""

