#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:170
msgid ""
"To update a load property or properties, reissue :ref:`sfcontrol` with the "
"new option(s) before issuing further :ref:`sf` or :ref:`sfe` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:176
msgid "To list the current set of control data, issue :ref:`sfcontrol`,STAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:178
msgid "To reset all input values to defaults, issue :ref:`sfcontrol`,NONE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:180
msgid ""
"When ``KCSYS`` = 0, the positive normal load acts in the negative surface "
"normal (- ``z`` ) direction. The positive tangential loads act in the "
"positive coordinate direction. A user-defined coordinate system ( ``VAL1`` )"
" is ignored if the load is applied on an edge of a plane element ( "
"``PLANE182``, ``PLANE183``, ``SHELL208``, ``SHELL209``, ``PLANE222``, and "
"``PLANE223`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:185
msgid ""
"When ``KCSYS`` = 1, the loading direction follows the positive direction of "
"the local coordinate system. The ID of a local coordinate system ( ``VAL1`` "
") is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:188
msgid ""
"The following figure shows how the coordinate directions are determined on a"
" face of a solid or shell element with different ``KCSYS`` and ``VAL1`` "
"input:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:191
msgid ""
"Coordinate System for Load Application on the Faces of 3D Solid and Shell "
"Elements This command contains some tables and extra information which can "
"be inspected in the original documentation pointed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:196
msgid ""
"z, x :sub:`1`, y :sub:`1` : normal and tangential directions (default "
"surface coordinate system)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:197
msgid ""
"z, x :sub:`2`, y :sub:`2` : normal and user-defined tangential directions "
"(user-defined surface coordinate system)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:199
msgid ""
"x :sub:`3`, y :sub:`3`, z :sub:`3` : x, y, and z directions defined by the "
"local coordinate system when ``KCSYS`` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:204
msgid ""
"The parametric direction determines the default coordinate system on a face."
" By default, the first parametric direction ( :math:`equation not available`"
" ) becomes the first tangential direction (x direction). If           "
"``VAL1`` = 1, the second parametric direction ( :math:`equation not "
"available` ) is selected as the x direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:208
msgid ""
"For the projected local coordinate system ( ``VAL1`` > 10), the direction of"
" the first tangential axes (x :sub:`2` ) is determined by the projection of "
"the local coordinate system onto the face. The projected tangential axes may"
" rotate if the direction of the face normal (z) changes in the space during "
"solution. If the direction of the face normal (z) is fixed (for in-plane "
"rotation, for example), the tangential axes do not follow element "
"deformation. To enable your coordinate system to always follow the element "
"deformation, specify the follower option ( ``KFOLLOW`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:214
msgid "**Coordinate System vs. Load Direction**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:215
msgid ""
"For the loads defined in the default coordinate system ( ``KCSYS`` = 0), the"
" tangential direction of a load is restricted because it is aligned to the "
"direction of the axis ( ``LCOMP`` ). The load direction can be arbitrary by "
"adding additional rotation to the load ( ``VAL3`` ). The following figure "
"shows how the load direction is determined on the face of an element. If "
"``VAL3`` > 0, ``LCOMP`` becomes the reference axis to define the rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:221
msgid ""
"Load Direction in the Default Coordinate System This command contains some "
"tables and extra information which can be inspected in the original "
"documentation pointed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:227
msgid ""
"The positive direction of the x :sub:`3`, y :sub:`3`, and z :sub:`3` axes "
"follow the direction of the local coordinate system without adjustment. "
"Therefore, they do not follow element deformation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:232
msgid ""
"The loading direction follows the positive direction of the orientation "
"vector, defined via ``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, and ``VAL3``. The direction is "
"calculated as :math:`equation not available`, where  :math:`equation not "
"available`,  :math:`equation not available`, and  :math:`equation not "
"available`  are unit vectors in the global Cartesian coordinate system. The "
"loading direction is fixed and does not follow the deformation of a face of "
"a selected element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:237
msgid "You can adjust the load magnitude ( ``KUSE`` and ``KPROJ`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:238
msgid ""
"Use the follower option ( ``KFOLLOW`` ) to specify whether the load has a "
"fixed direction ( ``KCSYS`` = 1 or 2), or projects the local coordinate "
"system to the element face to follow element deformation ( ``KCSYS`` = 0 and"
" ``VAL1`` > 10)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:242
msgid ""
"The following figure shows the default direction of the normal (z) and "
"tangential (x) components on an edge of a 3D shell element ( ``SHELL181`` or"
" ``SHELL281`` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:245
msgid ""
"Default Coordinate System of Surface Load on the Edge of a 3D Shell Element "
"If a local coordinate system is defined and ``KCSYS`` = 0 for the edge of "
"the 3D shell element, the tangential directions are adjusted in the plane of"
" the edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:249
msgid ""
"Projected Coordinate System of Surface Load on the Edge of a 3D Shell "
"Element The following figure shows the positive direction of the loads on "
"the edge of a plane element when ``KCSYS`` = 0. The positive direction of "
"the tangential load is defined by the definition of the faces (J-I, K-J, "
"L-K, I-L)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:254
msgid ""
"Positive Tangential Load on the Edge of a Plane Element If ``KCSYS`` = 1 or "
"2, the load direction does not change and ``KUSE`` = 1 or 2 is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:257
msgid ""
"If ``KCSYS`` = 1 or 2, or ``KTAPER`` > 0, you cannot specify a gradient "
"(slope) for surface loads ( :ref:`sfgrad` ) or a varying surface load ( "
":ref:`sffun` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:260
msgid "This command is also valid in the PREP7 processor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:264
msgid ""
"If ``KTAPER`` = 1, the magnitude of the load is determined by the current "
"location of a point:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:271
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:282
msgid ""
":math:`equation not available`  : Values on  :ref:`sfe` ( ``VAL1`` ~ "
"``VAL4`` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:272
msgid ""
":math:`equation not available`  : Global Cartesian coordinates at the "
"current location of the point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:275
msgid ""
"If ``KTAPER`` = 2, the magnitude of the load is determined by the initial "
"location of a point:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:283
msgid ""
":math:`equation not available`  : Global Cartesian coordinates at the "
"initial location of the point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:286
msgid "``KTAPER`` is not valid for use with :ref:`sf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:290
msgid ""
"The follower option ( ``KFOLLOW`` ) determines whether the load maintains a "
"fixed direction (default) or follows element deformation. The option applies"
" to surface loads defined by a fixed direction ( ``KCSYS`` = 1 or 2) or by a"
" projected user-defined coordinate system ( ``KCSYS`` = 0 and ``VAL1`` > "
"10)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:295
msgid "**When** ``KCSYS`` = 0 and ``VAL1`` > 10:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:297
msgid ""
"The selected local coordinate system is projected onto the face at the "
"initial state, then the projected tangential component ( ``LCOMP`` ) is "
"attached to the orthonormal basis ( **e** :sub:`1`, **e** :sub:`2`, **e** "
":sub:`3` ) of the face. The orthonormal basis may or may not be coincident "
"to the :math:`equation not available`  coordinate system. During solution, "
"the basis is updated at the current        time step and the load direction "
"is updated with respect to the basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:303
msgid ""
"Follower Load Behavior in the Projected Coordinate System **When** ``KCSYS``"
" = 1 or 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:306
msgid ""
"The global direction vector is attached to the orthonormal basis of selected"
" face at the initial state. When ``KCSYS`` = 1, the direction of selected "
"axis is considered as the direction vector and attached to the basis. During"
" solution, the basis is updated at current time step and the load direction "
"is updated with respect to the basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:311
msgid ""
"Follower Load Behavior for a User-Defined Orientation **Follower loads on "
"the edges of 3D shell and 2D elements:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:314
msgid ""
"The load is attached to the basis defined on the edge ( **e** :sub:`t`, "
"**e** :sub:`ne`, **e** :sub:`nf` [tangential, edge-normal, and face-normal "
"vector, respectively]). For 2D solid elements, the face-normal orientation ("
" **e** :sub:`nf` ) is that of the global Z axis. For 2D shell elements, the "
"edge-normal ( **e** :sub:`ne` ) is that of the global Z axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:319
msgid ""
"Follower Load Behavior on the Edges of 3D Shell and 2D Elements If it is "
"necessary to use the follower option after the first load step or at the "
"restart analysis, define the load direction with respect to the current "
"geometry (that is, the current basis of an element face). The follower "
"option for the local coordinate system ( ``KCSYS`` = 1) is not allowed after"
" the first load step or at the restart analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:325
msgid ""
"Load-stiffness effects are included in the supported elements for the real "
"part of all loads at the current configuration. All other load properties "
"are included in the load vector of the elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfcontrol:328
msgid ""
"You can specify an unsymmetric matrix ( :ref:`nropt`,UNSYM) for the load-"
"stiffness effects if needed."
msgstr ""

