"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_SFEDELE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfedele:9
msgid ""
"Element to which surface load deletion applies. If ALL, delete load from all"
" selected elements ( :ref:`esel` ). If ``ELEM`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may be substituted for ``ELEM``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfedele:14
msgid ""
"Load key associated with surface load (defaults to 1). If ALL, delete "
"surface loads for all load keys. If :ref:`sfcontrol` is issued for selected "
"elements, this value is the face number. If ALL, deletes the surface load "
"based on ``Lcomp``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfedele:19
msgid ""
"Surface load label. If ALL, use all appropriate labels. See :ref:`sfe` for "
"valid labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfedele:22
msgid ""
"Label of surface-load components. Valid when the surface load is defined via"
" :ref:`sfcontrol`. Valid labels are NORM, TANX, TAXY when ``KCSYS`` = 0, "
"LOCX, LOCY, LOCZ when ``KCSYS`` = 1, and USER when ``KCSYS`` = 2. ( "
"``KCSYS`` is specified when issuing :ref:`sfcontrol`.) If ALL, deletes all "
"component on the face defined by ``LKEY``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/fe_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfedele:41
msgid ""
"Deletes surface loads from selected elements. See the :ref:`sfdele` command "
"for an alternate surface load deletion capability based upon selected nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.fe_surface_loads.FeSurfaceLoads.sfelist.rst:2
