#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `AIRL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_AIRL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:8
msgid "**nrb** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:9
msgid "Number of rigid body modes in the model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:11
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Activate automatic inertia relief (default). The program "
"automatically determines the number of rigid body modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:14
msgid ""
"``n`` - Activate automatic inertia relief with the assumption of ``n`` rigid"
" body modes (1≤ ``n`` ≤ 6)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:17
msgid "``0`` - Deactivate automatic inertia relief."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:19
msgid "**rigid_calc** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:20
msgid "Method for computing the rigid body modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:22
msgid "``0`` - Use an eigensolver to compute rigid body modes (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:24
msgid ""
"``1`` - Use the geometry to compute rigid body modes (valid only when "
"``NRB`` = AUTO). The geometric rigid body vectors are calculated according "
"to in `Participation Factors and Mode Coefficients "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_anproc7.html#eqe483f2f2-aaa1-4080-a835-10c0e1e18f57>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:43
msgid ""
"The :ref:`airl` command activates automatic inertia relief for models having"
" up to six rigid body modes. This method is only valid for linear static "
"analyses ( :ref:`antype`,STATIC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:46
msgid ""
"By default ( ``NRB`` = AUTO), the number of rigid body modes in the "
"structure is automatically determined. The static solution is altered so "
"that the inertial effects factor into counterbalancing the external loads. "
"This method relies on calculation of the rigid body modes using either an "
"eigensolver ( ``RIGID_CALC`` = 0, which is the default) or the model "
"geometry ( ``RIGID_CALC`` = 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:51
msgid "For the ``NRB`` = AUTO option, no supports should be defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:53
msgid ""
"For a model that is partially constrained by design, you must set ``NRB`` to"
" the number of rigid body modes present in the structure and set "
"``RIGID_CALC`` = 0. The use of geometry ( ``RIGID_CALC`` = 1) to compute the"
" rigid-body modes of a partially constrained model is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:57
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.irlf:73
msgid ""
"Loads may be input as usual. Displacements and stresses are calculated as "
"usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/inertia.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.inertia.Inertia.airl:59
msgid ""
"Use :ref:`irlist` to print inertia relief calculation results. The mass and "
"moment of inertia summary printed before the solution is accurate (because "
"of the additional pre-calculations required for inertia relief). See "
"`Inertia Relief "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_tool2.html#thy_InertiaRelAnalysisTypes>`_"
" `Including Inertia Relief Calculations "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS2_6.html#>`_"
