msgid "Automatic time stepping key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.autots:11
msgid "``OFF`` - Do not use automatic time stepping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.autots:13
msgid "``ON`` - Use automatic time stepping (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.autots:15
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - The program determines whether to use automatic time stepping "
"(used by Workbench)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.autots:31
msgid ""
"Specifies whether to use automatic time stepping (or load stepping) over "
"this load step. If ``Key`` = ON, both time step prediction and time step "
"bisection will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.autots:34
msgid ""
"Bisection does not occur with :ref:`thopt`,QUASI since it uses only one "
"equilibrium iteration per substep. To ensure bisection, use the iterative "
"QUASI method ( :ref:`thopt`,QUASI,,,,,,1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.autots:37
msgid ""
"You cannot use automatic time stepping ( :ref:`autots` ), line search ( "
":ref:`lnsrch` ), or the DOF solution predictor ( :ref:`pred` ) with the arc-"
"length method ( :ref:`arclen`, :ref:`arctrm` ). If you activate the arc-"
"length method after you set :ref:`autots`, :ref:`lnsrch`, or :ref:`pred`, a "
"warning message appears. If you choose to proceed with the arc-length "
"method, the program disables your automatic time stepping, line search, and "
"DOF predictor settings, and the time step size is controlled by the arc-"
"length method internally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.load\\_step\\_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/load_step_options.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:2
msgid ""
"Prepares the result file for a subsequent Campbell diagram of a prestressed "
"structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `CAMPBELL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_CAMPBELL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:9
msgid "Campbell action:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:11
msgid ""
"``NONE`` - Do not prepare the result file. This option is the default "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:13
msgid ""
"``RSTP`` - Prepare the result file ( :file:`Jobname.RSTP` ) for a subsequent"
" `Campbell diagram "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_rot/Hlp_G_ROTCAMPDIAGS.html#rotgencamp2a>`_"
" of a prestressed structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:29
msgid ""
"For an analysis involving a prestressed structure, the :ref:`campbell` "
"command specifies whether or not to prepare the result file to support a "
"`Campbell diagram "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_rot/Hlp_G_ROTCAMPDIAGS.html#rotgencamp2a>`_"
" analysis ( :ref:`prcamp` or :ref:`plcamp` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:34
msgid ""
"To prestress a structure, the program performs a static solution before the "
"`linear perturbation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strlinpertother.html>`_"
" modal solution. For specific information about rotating structures, see "
"`Considerations for Rotating Structures "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strllinpertrotmach.html#str_rot_rotating>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:40
msgid ""
"The :ref:`campbell` command requires that modal and static analyses be "
"performed alternately. It works only when the number of static analyses is "
"the same as the number of modal analyses. Any number of analyses can be "
"performed, but the same number of each (static and modal) is expected. The "
"modal solutions are appended in the results file ( :file:`Jobname.RSTP` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.campbell:45
msgid ""
"For an example of :ref:`campbell` command usage, see in the `Rotordynamic "
"Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_rot/rotdynappenda.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.cecmod.rst:2
