msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.deltim:51
msgid ""
"Use consistent values for ``DTIME`` and ``TIME`` ( :ref:`time` ). For "
"example, using 0.9 for ``DTIME`` and 1.0 for ``TIME`` results in one time "
"step because 1.0 ( ``TIME`` ) is divisible by.9 ( ``DTIME`` ) at most once. "
"If you intend to load in 10 increments over a time span of 1.0, use 0.1 for "
"``DTIME`` and 1.0 for ``TIME``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.deltim:56
msgid ""
"The program calculates the initial incremental time so that ( ``EndingTime``"
" - ``StartingTime`` )/ ``DTIME`` is an integer, which may affect the initial"
" incremental time that you specify. For example, if the starting time is 0, "
"the ending time is 1, and the initial incremental time is 0.4, the program "
"rounds to the nearest integer and adjusts the time to 0.33333."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.deltim:61
msgid ""
"For solution efficiency, specify values for all fields of this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.deltim:63
msgid ""
"Changing the time step size upon restarting an analysis during a load step "
"is not recommended. You should only change the time step size between load "
"steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol.rst:2
