msgid ""
"Specifies the solution to be expanded for mode-superposition analyses or "
"substructure analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `EXPSOL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_EXPSOL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:12
msgid ""
"Expand the solution identified as load step ``LSTEP`` and substep "
"``SBSTEP``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:15
msgid ""
"As an alternative to ``LSTEP`` and ``SBSTEP``, expand the solution at, or "
"nearest to, the time value TIMFRQ (for :ref:`antype`,TRANS or "
":ref:`antype`,SUBSTR) or frequency value ``TIMFRQ`` (for "
":ref:`antype`,HARMIC). ``LSTEP`` and ``SBSTEP`` should be blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:22
msgid "``YES`` - Calculate element results, nodal loads, and reaction loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:24
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.numexp:30
msgid "``NO`` - Do not calculate these items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:40
msgid ""
"Specifies the solution to be expanded from analyses that use the mode-"
"superposition method ( :ref:`antype`,HARMIC or TRANS) or substructuring ( "
":ref:`antype`,SUBSTR). Use the :ref:`numexp` command to expand a group of "
"solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.expsol:44
msgid ""
"The resulting results file will maintain the same load step, substep, and "
"time (or frequency) values as the requested solution to be expanded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.load\\_step\\_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/load_step_options.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:2
msgid "Specifies ramped or stepped loading within a load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `KBC "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_KBC.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:9
msgid "Ramping key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:11
msgid ""
"``0`` - Loads are linearly interpolated (ramped) for each substep from the "
"values of the previous load step to the values of this load step. This is "
"the default value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:14
msgid ""
"``1`` - Loads are step changed (stepped) at the first substep of this load "
"step to the values of this load step (that is, the same values are used for "
"all substeps). Useful for rate-dependent behavior (for example, creep, "
"viscoplasticity, etc.) or transient load steps only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:18
msgid "**omgsqrdkey** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:19
msgid ""
"Key for the interpolation of the rotational velocity loading (only supported"
" when ``KEY`` = 0):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:21
msgid ""
"``0`` - Rotational velocities are linearly interpolated. This is the "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:23
msgid ""
"``1`` - A quadratic interpolation is used for the rotational velocities ( "
":ref:`omega`, :ref:`cmomega`, and :ref:`cmrotate` ). All other loads are "
"interpolated linearly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:40
msgid ""
"Specifies whether loads applied to intermediate substeps within the load "
"step are to be stepped or ramped. Used only if ``DTIME`` on the "
":ref:`deltim` command is less than the time span or, conversely, if "
"``NSBSTP`` on the :ref:`nsubst` command is greater than one. Flags (FSI, "
"MXWF, MVDI, etc.) are always stepped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:45
msgid ""
"Changing the ramping ``KEY`` (that is, switching between ramped and stepped "
"boundary conditions) between load steps is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:48
msgid ""
"For ramped loading ( :ref:`kbc`,0), when a load is applied for the first "
"time, it is interpolated from zero to the value of the current load step, "
"and not from the initial condition or value of the degree of freedom from "
"the previous load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:52
msgid ""
"Spatially varying tabular loads or boundary conditions do not support direct"
" ramping or stepping options and, instead, apply their full values according"
" to the supplied tabular functions regardless of the :ref:`kbc` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:56
msgid ""
"Regardless of the :ref:`kbc` setting, any tabular load is applied as step "
"change. This is the case, for example, for a static or harmonic cyclic "
"symmetry analysis with a load that varies by sector ( :ref:`cycopt`, "
"LDSECT). Note that when tabular and non-tabular loads are present in the "
"same analysis, the non-tabular loads are ramped or stepped according to the "
":ref:`kbc` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:61
msgid ""
"Irrespective of the :ref:`kbc` setting, loads are usually step-removed. See "
"`Stepping or Ramping Loads "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS2_7.html#bas.ch.2.tab.11.ft.5>`_"
" in the `Basic Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS19.html>`_"
" for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kbc:68
msgid ""
"It is sometimes difficult to obtain successful convergence with stepped "
"loading in a nonlinear transient problem. If divergence is encountered, "
"determine if stepped loading was used by default, then determine if it is "
"appropriate for the analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.load\\_step\\_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/load_step_options.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:2
msgid "Specifies whether or not to reuse factorized matrices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `KUSE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_KUSE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:9
msgid "Reuse key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:11
msgid ""
"``0`` - Program decides whether or not to reuse the previous factorized "
"matrices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:13
msgid ""
"``1`` - Force the previous factorized matrices to be reused. Used mainly in "
"a restart. Forcing reuse of the matrices is a nonstandard use of the program"
" and should be done with caution. For instance, using this option and "
"changing the number of elements, or the number or type of degrees of "
"freedom, may cause an abort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:18
msgid ""
"``-1`` - All element matrices are reformed and are used to reform new "
"factorized matrices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.kuse:34
msgid ""
"Overrides the program logic to determine whether or not to reuse the "
"previous factorized matrices for each substep of this load step. Applies "
"only to static or full transient analyses. For more details see."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.load\\_step\\_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/load_step_options.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:2
msgid "Specifies options for a 3D magnetostatic field analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MAGOPT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MAGOPT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:11
msgid ""
"``0`` - Calculate a complete H field solution in the entire domain using a "
"single (reduced) potential."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:15
msgid ""
"When used in problems with both current sources and iron regions, errors may"
" result due to numerical cancellation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:18
msgid ""
"``1`` - Calculate and store a preliminary H field in \"iron\" regions "
"(μ:sub:`r` ≠ 1). Requires flux-parallel boundary conditions to be specified "
"on exterior iron boundaries. Used in conjunction with subsequent solutions "
"with ``VALUE`` = 2 followed by ``VALUE`` = 3. Applicable to multiply- "
"connected iron domain problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:23
msgid ""
"``2`` - Calculate and store a preliminary H field in \"air\" regions "
"(μ:sub:`r` = 1). The air-iron interface is appropriately treated internally "
"by the program. Used in conjunction with a subsequent solution with "
"``VALUE`` = 3. Applicable to singly-connected iron domain problems (with "
"subsequent solution with ``VALUE`` = 3) or to multiply-connected iron domain"
" problems (when preceded by a solution with ``VALUE`` = 1 and followed by a "
"solution with ``VALUE`` = 3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:29
msgid ""
"``3`` - Use the previously stored H field solution(s) and calculate the "
"complete H field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:45
msgid ""
"Specifies the solution sequence options for a 3D magnetostatic field "
"analysis using a scalar potential (MAG). The solution sequence is determined"
" by the nature of the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:48
msgid "You cannot use constraint equations with ``Value`` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magopt:52
msgid ""
"Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction :ref:`magopt`,3 is not "
"supported in a DMP solution when the following contact elements are present "
"in the model: ``CONTA174``, ``CONTA175``, or ``CONTA177``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.load\\_step\\_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/load_step_options.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:2
msgid "Specifies magnetic solution options and initiates the solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `MAGSOLV "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_MAGSOLV.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:9
msgid "Static magnetic solution option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:11
msgid "``0`` - Vector potential (MVP) or edge formulation (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:13
msgid ""
"``1`` - Combined vector potential and reduced scalar potential (MVP-RSP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:15
msgid "``2`` - Reduced scalar potential (RSP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:17
msgid "``3`` - Difference scalar potential (DSP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:19
msgid "``4`` - General scalar potential (GSP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:21
msgid "**nramp** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:22
msgid ""
"Number of ramped substeps for the first load step of a nonlinear MVP or MVP-"
"RSP solution. Defaults to 3. If ``NRAMP`` = -1, ignore the ramped load step "
"entirely. ``NRAMP`` is ignored for linear magnetostatics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:26
msgid "**cnvcsg** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:27
msgid ""
"Tolerance value on the program-calculated reference value for the magnetic "
"current-segment convergence. Used for the MVP, the MVP-RSP, and the edge "
"formulation solution options ( ``OPT`` = 0 and 1). Defaults to 0.001."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:31
msgid "**cnvflux** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:32
msgid ""
"Tolerance value on the program-calculated reference value for the magnetic "
"flux convergence. Used for all scalar potential solution options ( ``OPT`` ="
" 2, 3, 4). Defaults to 0.001."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:35
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:8
msgid "**neqit** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:36
msgid ""
"Maximum number of equilibrium iterations per load step. Defaults to 25."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:38
msgid "**biot** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:39
msgid ""
"Option to force execution of a Biot-Savart integral solution ( "
":ref:`biot`,NEW) for the scalar potential options. Required if multiple load"
" steps are being performed with different current source primitives ( "
"``SOURC36`` elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:41
msgid ""
"``0`` - Do not force execution of Biot-Savart calculation (default); Biot-"
"Savart is automatically calculated only for the first solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:44
msgid "``1`` - Force execution of Biot-Savart calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:46
msgid "**cnvtol** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:47
msgid "Sets the convergence tolerance for AMPS reaction. Defaults to 1e-3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:63
msgid ""
":ref:`magsolv` invokes a Mechanical APDL macro which specifies magnetic "
"solution options and initiates the solution. The macro is applicable to any "
"Mechanical APDL magnetostatic analysis using the magnetic vector potential "
"(MVP), reduced scalar potential (RSP), difference scalar potential (DSP), "
"general scalar potential (GSP), or combined MVP-RSP formulation options. "
"Results are only stored for the final converged solution. (In POST1, issue "
":ref:`starset`,LIST to identify the load step of solution results.) The "
"macro internally determines if a nonlinear analysis is required based on "
"magnetic material properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:73
msgid ""
"If you use the ``BIOT`` option and issue :ref:`save` after solution or "
"postprocessing, the Biot- Savart calculations are saved to the database, but"
" will be overwritten upon normal exit from the program. To save this data "
"after issuing :ref:`save`, use the ``/EXIT``,NOSAVE command. You can also "
"issue the ``/EXIT``,SOLU command to exit Mechanical APDL and save all "
"solution data, including the Biot-Savart calculations, in the database. "
"Otherwise, when you issue :ref:`resume`, the Biot-Savart calculation will be"
" lost (resulting in a zero solution)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:81
msgid ""
"The MVP, MVP-RSP, and edge formulation options perform a two-load-step "
"solution sequence. The first load step ramps the applied loads over a "
"prescribed number of substeps ( ``NRAMP`` ), and the second load step "
"calculates the converged solution. For linear problems, only a single load "
"step solution is performed. The ramped load step can be bypassed by setting "
"``NRAMP`` to -1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:86
msgid ""
"The RSP option solves in a single load step using the adaptive descent "
"procedure. The DSP option uses two load steps, and the GSP solution uses "
"three load steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:89
msgid ""
"The following analysis options and nonlinear options are controlled by this "
"macro: :ref:`kbc`, :ref:`neqit`, :ref:`nsubst`, :ref:`cnvtol`, :ref:`nropt`,"
" :ref:`magopt`, and :ref:`outres`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:92
msgid "You cannot use constraint equations with ``OPT`` = 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.magsolv:94
msgid ""
"When the ``BIOT`` option is on ( ``BIOT`` = 1), Distributed-Memory Parallel "
"(DMP) restrictions may apply. For more information, see the :ref:`biot` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.mode.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.load\\_step\\_options.LoadStepOptions.mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/load_step_options.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
