#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.wrfull:11
msgid "``OFF or 0`` - Turn off feature (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.wrfull:13
msgid ""
"``N`` - Turn on feature and set it to stop after assembling the global "
"matrices and writing the :file:`.FULL` file for load step N."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.wrfull:30
msgid ""
"This command is used in conjunction with the :ref:`solve` command to "
"generate the assembled matrix file ( :file:`.FULL` file) only. The element "
"matrices are assembled into the relevant global matrices for the particular "
"analysis being performed and the :file:`.FULL` file is written. Equation "
"solution and the output of data to the results file are skipped. To dump the"
" matrices written on the :file:`.FULL` file into Harwell-Boeing format, use "
"the :ref:`hbmat` command in /AUX2. To copy the matrices to a postscript "
"format that can be viewed graphically, use the :ref:`psmat` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.wrfull:37
msgid ""
"To use the :ref:`lssolve` macro with this command, you may need to modify "
"the :ref:`lssolve` macro to properly stop at the load step of interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.wrfull:40
msgid ""
"This command only valid for linear static, full harmonic, and full transient"
" analyses when the sparse direct solver is selected. This command is also "
"valid for buckling or modal analyses with any mode extraction method. This "
"command is not valid for nonlinear analyses. It is not supported in a linear"
" perturbation analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/load_step_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.load_step_options.LoadStepOptions.wrfull:45
msgid ""
"In general, the assembled matrix file :file:`.FULL` contains stiffness, "
"mass, and damping matrices. However, the availability of the matrices "
"depends on the analysis type chosen when the file is written. Some analyses "
"do not write the matrices individually but instead write combined matrices. "
"For example, a full transient writes a combined stiffness/mass/damping "
"matrix to the full file."
msgstr ""

