"The ``SURF154`` surface element must be defined on the surface of the "
"structural solid element for the excitation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.dfswave:69
msgid ""
"The acoustic elements and the absorbing boundary condition must be defined "
"in the open acoustic domain. Do not define the acoustic domain on the "
"excitation side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.dfswave:72
msgid ""
"The :ref:`pras` and :ref:`plas` commands calculate the average transmission "
"loss for multiple sampling phases at each frequency over the frequency "
"range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.dfswave:75
msgid ""
"The symmetry of a panel structure cannot be used to reduce the simulation "
"size, as the incident plane waves have varying random phase angles. The z "
"axis of the Cartesian coordinate system ( ``KCN`` ) must be consistent with "
"the panel``s outward normal unit vector at the center of the panel``s "
"sending side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.fluread"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:2
msgid ""
"Reads one-way Fluent-to-Mechanical APDL coupling data via a :file:`.cgns` "
"file with one-side fast Fourier transformation complex pressure peak value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:5
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `FLUREAD "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_FLUREAD.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:10
msgid ""
"File name and directory path of a one-way Fluent-to-Mechanical APDL coupling"
" data file (248 characters maximum, including the characters needed for the "
"directory path). An unspecified directory path defaults to the working "
"directory; in this case, you can use all 248 characters for the file name. "
"Defaults to :file:`jobname`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:16
msgid ""
"File name extension of the one-way Fluent-to-Mechanical APDL coupling data "
"file. Defaults to :file:`.cgns` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:20
msgid ""
"Interpolation data for mapping. A value of 0 (default) or 2 applies 2D "
"interpolation (where interpolation occurs on a surface)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:24
msgid "Outside region results for mapping:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:26
msgid ""
"``0`` - Use the value(s) of the nearest region point for points outside of "
"the region. This behavior is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:29
msgid "``1`` - Set results extrapolated outside of the region to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:32
msgid ""
"Number of nearby nodes considered for mapping interpolation. Minimum = 5. "
"Default = 20."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:34
msgid ""
"Lower values reduce processing time; however, some distorted or irregular "
"meshes require a higher value in cases where three nodes are encountered for"
" triangulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:37
msgid "**listopt** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:40
msgid "``(blank)`` - No listing (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:42
msgid ""
"``SOURCE`` - List the node coordinates and complex pressure values on the "
"Fluent source side during the solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:45
msgid ""
"``TARGET`` - List the node coordinates and complex pressure values on the "
"mapped Mechanical APDL target side during the solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:48
msgid ""
"``BOTH`` - List the node coordinates and complex pressure values on both the"
" Fluent source side and the mapped Mechanical APDL target side during the "
"solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:65
msgid ""
"The :ref:`fluread` command reads one-way Fluent-to-Mechanical APDL coupling "
"data from a :file:`.cgns` file. The Fluent one-side fast Fourier "
"transformation (FFT) peak complex pressure values are mapped to the "
"Mechanical APDL structure model during the acoustic-structural solution at "
"each FFT frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:71
msgid "The command can be used only for the model with the acoustic elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:73
msgid ""
"To apply complex pressure to the structure model, define the ``SURF154`` "
"surface element, then define the one-way coupling interface ( "
":ref:`sf`,,FSIN) on the element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:76
msgid ""
"You can define the solving frequency range via the ``HARFRQ`` command. The "
"solver selects the FFT frequencies between the beginning and ending "
"frequencies. The number of substeps is determined by the number of FFT "
"frequencies over the frequency range. The number of substeps defined via the"
" :ref:`nsubst` command is overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:81
msgid "For better mapping performance, consider the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:86
msgid ""
"For each point in the structural destination mesh, the command searches all "
"possible triangles in the Fluent source mesh to find the best triangle "
"containing each point, then performs a linear interpolation inside this "
"triangle. For faster and more accurate results, consider your interpolation "
"method and search criteria carefully. (See ``LIMIT``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.fluread:91
msgid ""
"It is possible to apply one-way coupling excitation to multiple frequencies."
" The one-side FFT peak complex pressure values are necessary to do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.ic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:2
msgid "Specifies initial conditions at nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `IC "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_IC.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:9
msgid ""
"Node at which initial condition is to be specified. If ALL, apply to all "
"selected nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ). If ``NODE`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may be substituted for ``NODE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:14
msgid ""
"Degree-of-freedom label for which the initial condition is to be specified. "
"If ALL, use all appropriate labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:17
msgid ""
"**Structural labels** : UX, UY, or UZ (displacements); ROTX, ROTY, or ROTZ "
"(rotations); HDSP (hydrostatic pressure); PRES (pore pressure)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:19
msgid ""
"For structural static and transient analyses, specify translational and "
"rotational velocities as initial conditions using these labels: VELX, VELY, "
"VELZ (translational velocities); OMGX, OMGY, OMGZ (rotational velocities)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:22
msgid ""
"For structural transient analysis, specify translational and rotational "
"accelerations as initial conditions using these labels: ACCX, ACCY, ACCZ "
"(translational accelerations); DMGX, DMGY, DMGZ (rotational accelerations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:25
msgid ""
"The velocity and acceleration initial conditions are not included with "
"``Lab`` = ALL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:26
msgid "**Thermal labels** : TEMP, TBOT, TE2, TE3,..., TTOP (temperature)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:27
msgid ""
"**Magnetic labels** : MAG (scalar magnetic potential); AZ (vector magnetic "
"potential)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:28
msgid "**Diffusion label** : CONC (concentration)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:29
msgid "**Acoustic label** : ENKE (acoustic energy density)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:32
msgid ""
"Initial value of the degree of freedom. Defaults to the program default for "
"that degree of freedom (0.0 for structural analysis, :ref:`tunif` for "
"thermal analysis, etc.). Values are in the nodal coordinate system and in "
"radians for rotational degrees of freedom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:37
msgid ""
"Second-order degree of freedom value, mainly used for non-structural DOF "
"where VELX can't be used. Defaults to the program default for that degree of"
" freedom (0.0 for structural analysis). Values are in the nodal coordinate "
"system and in radians/time for rotational degrees of freedom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:42
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:46
msgid ""
"Specifies the same initial condition values at the range of nodes from "
"``NODE`` to ``NEND`` (defaults to ``NODE`` ), in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults"
" to 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:63
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ic` command specifies initial conditions, which are the initial "
"values of the specified degrees of freedom. It is valid only for a static "
"analysis and full method transient analysis ( :ref:`timint`,ON and "
":ref:`trnopt`,FULL). For the transient, the initial value is specified at "
"the beginning of the first load step, that is, at time = 0.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:68
msgid ""
"If constraints ( :ref:`d`, :ref:`dsym`, etc.) and initial conditions are "
"applied at the same node, the constraint specification overrides. Exercise "
"caution when specifying constraints. The degree-of- freedom values start "
"from zero, or the first value given in the table when table name is "
"specified. To match the nonzero initial condition value with the initial "
"value for degree-of-freedom constraint, use a table for the degree-of-"
"freedom constraint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:74
msgid ""
"For thermal analyses, any :ref:`tunif` specification should be applied "
"before the :ref:`ic` command; otherwise, the :ref:`tunif` specification is "
"ignored. If the :ref:`ic` command is input before any :ref:`tunif` "
"specification, use the :ref:`icdele` command and then reissue any "
":ref:`tunif` specification and then follow with the :ref:`ic` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:79
msgid ""
"When issuing the :ref:`ic` command for elements ``SOLID278``  `Layered "
"Thermal Solid "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_SOLID278.html#SOLID278L.fig.1>`_"
" and ``SOLID279``  `Layered Thermal Solid "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_SOLID279.html#SOLID279L.fig.1>`_"
" with through-the-thickness degrees of freedom (KEYOPT(3) = 2), layers are "
"always interpolated linearly based on the location of the degrees of "
"freedom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:86
msgid ""
"Define consistent initial conditions. For example, if you define an initial "
"velocity at a single degree of freedom, the initial velocity at every other "
"degree of freedom will be 0.0, potentially leading to conflicting initial "
"conditions. In most cases, you should define initial conditions at every "
"unconstrained degree of freedom in your model. If you define an initial "
"condition for any degree of freedom at the pilot node of a rigid body (see "
"`Modeling Rigid Bodies "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/ctecrigidbodies.html#strmodrigidbod>`_"
" in the `Contact Technology Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_ctec/ctec_flpressexamp.html>`_"
" for the definition of rigid body), then the same initial condition must "
"also be defined for the same degree of freedom on all other nodes of the "
"rigid body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:97
msgid ""
"After a solution has been performed, the specified initial conditions are "
"overwritten by the actual solution and are no longer available. You must "
"respecify them if you want to perform a subsequent analysis. You may want to"
" keep a database file saved prior to the first solution for subsequent "
"reuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.ic:102
msgid ""
"If you use the :ref:`cdwrite` command to archive your model, initial "
"displacements, temperatures, etc. specified via the :ref:`ic` command are "
"not written to the archive file; initial velocities and accelerations are "
"written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icdele.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.icdele"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icdele:2
msgid "Deletes initial conditions at nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icdele:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ICDELE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ICDELE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icdele:21
msgid ""
"Deletes all initial conditions previously specified with the :ref:`ic` or "
":ref:`icrotate` command at all nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.iclist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:2
msgid "Lists the initial conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ICLIST "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ICLIST.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:9
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:16
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:23
msgid ""
"List initial conditions for nodes ``NODE1`` to ``NODE2`` (defaults to "
"``NODE1`` ) in steps of ``NINC`` (defaults to 1). If ``NODE1`` = ALL "
"(default), ``NODE2`` and ``NINC`` are ignored and initial conditions for all"
" selected nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ) are listed. If ``NODE1`` = P, graphical "
"picking is enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only "
"in the GUI). A component name may be substituted for ``NODE1`` ( ``NODE2`` "
"and ``NINC`` are ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:30
msgid "Label identifying the initial condition to list out:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:32
msgid "``DISP`` - Displacements, temperature, etc. (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:34
msgid "``VELO`` - Velocities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:36
msgid "``ACC`` - Accelerations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.iclist:52
msgid ""
"Lists the initial conditions specified by the :ref:`ic`  or :ref:`icrotate`"
"  command. Listing applies to all the selected nodes ( :ref:`nsel` ) and DOF"
" labels. :ref:`iclist` is not the same as the :ref:`dlist` command. All the "
"initial conditions including the default conditions are listed for the "
"selected nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icrotate.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.icrotate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icrotate:2
msgid ""
"Specifies initial velocity at nodes as a sum of rotation about an axis and "
"translation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.icrotate:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `ICROTATE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_ICROTATE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

