msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:178
msgid ""
"In addition to :ref:`outres`, these commands also control solution output: "
":ref:`outpr`, :ref:`outgeom`, and :ref:`osresult`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:181
msgid ""
"You can issue up to 50 output-control commands for :ref:`outres`, "
":ref:`outpr`, :ref:`outgeom` in an analysis. There is no limit on the number"
" of :ref:`osresult` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:184
msgid ""
":ref:`outres`,ERASE erases the existing output specifications and resets the"
" counted number of :ref:`outres` commands to zero. The ERASE argument works "
"in a similar manner for :ref:`outpr`, :ref:`outgeom`, and :ref:`osresult`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:188
msgid ""
"A given :ref:`outres` command generally has no effect on solution items not "
"specified. For example, an :ref:`outres`,ESOL,LAST command does not affect "
"NSOL data; that is, it neither activates nor suppresses NSOL data storage in"
" any substep. An exception to this behavior involves the EANGL solution "
"item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:193
msgid ""
":ref:`outres` controls element Euler angle (EANGL) data output as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:195
msgid ""
"When ``Freq`` = NONE, no element Euler angles are output at any substeps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:197
msgid ""
"Without Euler angles, element results postprocessing can occur in the "
"element solution coordinate system only (that is, :ref:`rsys` has no effect "
"on element results); therefore, nodal averaging of element solution items "
"may not be applicable when element solution coordinate systems are not "
"uniform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:202
msgid ""
"When ``Freq`` = any other value (including the command default), element "
"Euler angles are output at substeps specified by ``Freq``, and at any "
"substeps where one or more tensorial element solution items (STRS, EPEL, "
"EPTH, EPPL, EPCR, EPDI, FGRAD, FFLUX, and AESO) are output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:206
msgid ""
"Additional results in the :file:`Jobname.DSUB` file (DSUBres = ALL) can only"
" be requested in the first load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:209
msgid ""
"In the results-item hierarchy, certain items are subsets of other items. For"
" example, element solution (ESOL) data is a subset of all (ALL) solution "
"data. An :ref:`outres`,ALL command can therefore affect ESOL data. Likewise,"
" an :ref:`outres` command that controls ESOL data can affect a portion of "
"all data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:214
msgid ""
"The :ref:`example <OUTRES_example>` :ref:`outres` commands illustrate the "
"interrelationships between"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:215
msgid ""
"solution items and the necessity of issuing :ref:`outres` thoughtfully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:217
msgid ""
"To suppress all data at every substep, issue the :ref:`outres`,ALL,NONE "
"command. ( :ref:`outres`,ERASE does not suppress all data at every substep.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:220
msgid ""
"The NSOL, RSOL, V, and A solution items are associated with nodes. The CINT "
"solution item is associated with fracture. All remaining solution items are "
"associated with elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:223
msgid ""
"Enabling nodal-averaged results ( ``Item`` = NAR or any of the associated "
"labels) generally reduces the results file size, provided the equivalent "
"element-based results are concurrently disabled. When nodal-averaged results"
" are enabled, element values for stress and strain are averaged and stored "
"as nodal values. Some limitations apply when using nodal averaged results. "
"For more information and an example, see `Nodal-Averaged Results "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_CH2_2.html#nodeavepost>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:230
msgid ""
"The boundary conditions (constraints and force loads) are written to the "
"results file only if either nodal or reaction loads (NLOAD or RSOL items) "
"are also written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:233
msgid "When specifying a ``Freq`` value, observe the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:235
msgid "For a modal analysis, only NONE or ALL are valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:237
msgid ""
"If you issue multiple :ref:`outres` commands during an analysis, you cannot "
"specify a :ref:`key time array parameter (% <freqkap>` ``array``) in a given"
" :ref:`outres` command and then specify a different ``Freq`` option in a "
"subsequent :ref:`outres` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:241
msgid ""
"For additive manufacturing analyses during the build step ( "
":ref:`amstep`,BUILD), ``Freq`` refers to the layer number (for example, "
"output ALL layers, LAST layer, or every ``N``  :sup:`th` layer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:244
msgid ""
"To specify selected results to output to the database, see :ref:`osresult`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:246
msgid ":ref:`outres` is also valid in PREP7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:248
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:252
msgid ""
"When issuing an :ref:`outres` command, think of a matrix in which you set "
"switches on and off. When a switch is on, a solution item is stored for the "
"specified substep. When a switch is off, a solution item is suppressed for a"
" specified substep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:256
msgid ""
"Assuming a static ( :ref:`antype`,STATIC) analysis, this example shows how "
"the matrix looks after issuing each :ref:`outres` command in this six-"
"substep solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:268
msgid ""
"To simplify the example, only a subset of the available solution items "
"appears in the matrix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:270
msgid ""
":ref:`outres`,ERASE -- After issuing this command, the default output "
"specifications are in effect, as shown:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:276
msgid ""
":ref:`outres`,NSOL,2 -- This command modifies the initial specifications so "
"that NSOL is enabled for substeps 2, 4 and 6, and disabled for substeps 1, 3"
" and 5, as shown:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:282
msgid ""
":ref:`outres`,ALL,3 -- This command further modifies the specifications so "
"that ALL is enabled for substeps 3 and 6, and disabled for substeps 1, 2, 4 "
"and 5, as shown:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:288
msgid ""
":ref:`outres`,ESOL,4 -- This command once again modifies the specifications "
"so that ESOL is enabled for the fourth and last substeps, and disabled for "
"substeps 1, 2, 3 and 5, as shown:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:294
msgid ":ref:`solve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.outres:296
msgid "When obtaining the solution, results data are stored as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:2
msgid "Controls file writing for multiframe restarts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RESCONTROL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RESCONTROL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:9
msgid "Command action:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:11
msgid ""
"``DEFINE`` - Specifies how often :file:`.xnnn` restart files (default) or "
":file:`.rdnn` remeshing database files (for `nonlinear mesh adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
" analysis) are written for a load step. The file type controlled by this "
"command is determined by ``Filetype``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:16
msgid ""
"``FILE_SUMMARY`` - Prints the substep and load-step information for all "
":file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` files for the current jobname in the current "
"directory. If specified, all other arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:20
msgid ""
"``STATUS`` - Issuing the command lists the current status in the tables of "
"restart controls specified previously by :ref:`rescontrol`. If this option "
"is specified, all other arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:24
msgid ""
"``NORESTART`` - Cleans up some of the restart files after a distributed-"
"memory parallel (DMP) solution. (Not valid for `nonlinear mesh adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:28
msgid ""
"The master process will not have the following files in the working "
"directory at the end of the run: :file:`.esav`, :file:`.osav`, "
":file:`.xnnn`, :file:`.rdb`, :file:`.ldhi`. The worker processes will not "
"have the following files in the working directory at the end of the run: "
":file:`.esav`, :file:`.osav`, :file:`.xnnn`, :file:`.rst` (or :file:`.rth`, "
"etc.). Some restart files are never written, some are removed upon exiting "
"the solution processor (for example, upon :ref:`finish` ), and some are "
"removed upon exiting the program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:35
msgid ""
"This option is useful for cleaning up files written by all distributed "
"processes, especially when you know that these restart files will not be "
"needed later. If this option is specified, all other arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:39
msgid ""
"If this option is used in a shared-memory parallel (SMP) environment, most "
"restart files in the working directory are removed. It has the same effect "
"as issuing :ref:`rescontrol`,,NONE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:42
msgid ""
"``LINEAR`` - Same as ``Action`` = DEFINE, but for linear static applications"
" only. For a linear static analysis, the restart capability is normally not "
"needed; however, it is typically needed when a subsequent linear "
"perturbation analysis is desired. By default, none of the restart files are "
"written for a linear static analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:47
msgid ""
"``DELETE`` - Delete the restart control specification corresponding to the "
"``Ldstep`` label on a previous :ref:`rescontrol`,DEFINE command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:51
msgid ""
"Specifies how the :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` files are written for the "
"specified load steps. This option also affects how often the load history "
"information is written to the :file:`.ldhi` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:53
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - Write the :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` files at the same substep"
" ``Frequency`` for all load steps; write the load history information to the"
" :file:`.ldhi` file for all load steps. For :file:`.rdnn` files, this option"
" is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:57
msgid ""
"``LAST`` - Write the :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` files for the last load "
"step only; write load- history information to the :file:`.ldhi` file for the"
" last load step only. This option is the default for nonlinear static and "
"full transient analyses for :file:`.xnnn` files. If specified, all remaining"
" arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:62
msgid ""
"``N`` - Number that indicates how often the :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` "
"files are written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:64
msgid ""
"Input a positive number to write the :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` files at"
" the substep ``Frequency`` indicated only for load step ``N``. Other load "
"steps will be written at the default substep frequency or at a frequency "
"defined by a previous :ref:`rescontrol` specification. Load- history "
"information is written to the :file:`.ldhi` file only for load steps ``N``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:69
msgid ""
"Specifying a negative number (- ``N`` ) is valid for controlling "
":file:`.xnnn` files only. The files are written for every ``N`` th load step"
" at the specified substep ``Frequency``. The load history information is "
"written to the :file:`.ldhi` file every ``N`` th load step. This option is "
"suitable for restart applications in which more than a few hundred load "
"steps are required. Compared to the ALL and positive ``N`` options, it can "
"save disk space, as the :file:`.ldhi` file is smaller and fewer "
":file:`.xnnn` files are written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:76
msgid ""
"If ``Ldstep`` = - ``N``, all other ``Ldstep`` options specified by "
":ref:`rescontrol` are ignored and the program follows the - ``N`` option "
"(write load history information every ``N`` th load step). If you want to "
"change this pattern, issue :ref:`rescontrol`,DELETE, - ``N``, then issue "
"another :ref:`rescontrol` command with the desired ``Ldstep`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:81
msgid ""
"``NONE`` - No multiframe restart files ( :file:`.rdb`, :file:`.ldhi`, "
":file:`.xnnn` ) are created. (Not valid for `nonlinear mesh adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
" analysis.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:85
msgid ""
"This option is the default for mode-superposition analyses. The remaining "
"arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:87
msgid ""
"For nonlinear static, linear static, and full transient analyses, this "
"option enables a restart to occur at the last or abort point (using the "
":file:`.emat`, :file:`.esav` or :file:`.osav`, and :file:`.db` files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:91
msgid ""
"For mode-superposition transient analyses, this option allows a restart from"
" the last point using the :file:`.rdsp` and :file:`.db` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:94
msgid "**frequency** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:95
msgid ""
"Frequency at which the :file:`.xnnn` files are written at the substep level,"
" or at which the :file:`.rdnn` files are written at the remeshing level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:97
msgid ""
"``NONE`` - Do not write :file:`.xnnn` files for this load step (not "
"available for :file:`.rdnn` files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:100
msgid ""
"``LAST`` - Write the :file:`.xnnn` files for the last substep of the load "
"step only (default for nonlinear static and full transient analyses), or "
"write the :file:`.rdnn` files for the last remesh of the load step only "
"(default for `nonlinear mesh adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
" analysis)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:105
msgid ""
"``N`` - If ``N`` is positive, write the :file:`.xnnn` files at every ``N`` "
"th substep of a load step, or write the :file:`.rdnn` files at every ``N`` "
"th remesh of a load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:108
msgid ""
"If ``N`` is negative (not valid for :file:`.rdnn` files), write ``N`` "
"equally spaced :file:`.xnnn` files within a load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:111
msgid ""
"In nonlinear static and full transient analyses, ``-N`` is valid only when "
"automatic time stepping is enabled ( :ref:`autots`,ON)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:114
msgid "In mode-superposition analyses, negative ``N`` is always valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:116
msgid "**maxfiles** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:117
msgid ""
"Maximum number of :file:`.xnnn` files to save within a load step ( not "
"available for :file:`.rdnn` files):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:119
msgid ""
"``-1`` - Overwrite existing :file:`.xnnn` files (default). The total maximum"
" number of :file:`.xnnn` files for one run is 999. If this number is reached"
" before the analysis is complete, the program will reset the :file:`.xnnn` "
"file numbering back to 1 and continue to write :file:`.xnnn` files; the "
"program keeps the newest 999 restart files and overwrites the oldest restart"
" files. For this option, the maximum number of files can be changed to a "
"number less than 999 by setting the MAXTotalFiles argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:126
msgid ""
"``0`` - Do not overwrite any existing :file:`.xnnn` files. The total maximum"
" number of :file:`.xnnn` files for one run is 999. If this number is reached"
" before the analysis is complete, the analysis continues but no longer "
"writes any :file:`.xnnn` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:130
msgid ""
"``N`` - Maximum number of :file:`.xnnn` files to keep for each load step. "
"When ``N`` :file:`.xnnn` files have been written for a load step, the "
"program overwrites the first :file:`.xnnn` file of that load step for "
"subsequent substeps. ``N`` must be <= 999. If a total of 999 restart files "
"is reached before the analysis is complete, the analysis continues but "
"writes no additional :file:`.xnnn` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:136
msgid "**maxtotalfiles** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:137
msgid ""
"Total number of restart files to keep. Default = 999 for :file:`.xnnn` files"
" and 99 for :file:`.rdnn` files. This option is valid only when ``MAXFILES``"
" = -1 (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:140
msgid ""
"Valid ``MAXTotalFiles`` values are 1 through 999 for :file:`.xnnn` files, "
"and 1 through 99 for :file:`.rdnn` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:143
msgid ""
"When the total number of restart files written exceeds ``MAXTotalFiles``, "
"the program resets the :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` file numbering back to"
" 1 and continues to write :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` files. The newest "
"files are retained and the oldest files are overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:147
msgid ""
"The ``MAXtotalFiles`` value specified applies to all subsequent load steps. "
"To reset it to the default, reissue the command with ``MAXTotalFiles`` = 0 "
"or some negative value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:150
msgid ""
"If ``MAXTotalFiles`` is set to different values at different load steps, and"
" if the value of ``MAXTotalFiles`` specified in the prior load step is "
"larger than that of the current load step, the program can only overwrite "
"the current number of maximum restart files up to the number "
"``MAXTotalFiles`` currently specified (which is smaller than the previous "
"number)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:155
msgid ""
"The recommended way to control the maximum number of restart files is to "
"specify ``MAXTotalFiles`` at the first load step and not vary it in "
"subsequent load steps. Also, ``MAXTotalFiles`` is best used when ``Ldstep`` "
"= - ``N`` or ALL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:160
msgid ""
"The type of restart file to be controlled by this command. Valid only when "
"``Action`` = DEFINE:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:162
msgid "``XNNN`` - Control :file:`.xnnn` files (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:164
msgid ""
"``RDNN`` - Control :file:`.rdnn` remeshing database files. Needed only for a"
" `nonlinear mesh adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
" analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:182
msgid ""
":ref:`rescontrol` sets up the restart parameters for a multiframe restart, "
"enabling you to restart an analysis from any load step and substep for which"
" there is an :file:`.xnnn` file. You can perform a multiframe restart for "
"static and transient (full or mode-superposition method) analyses only. For "
"more information about multiframe restarts and descriptions of the contents "
"of the files used, see `Restarting an Analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS3_12.html#bassolumodres>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:189
msgid "**Syntax**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:191
msgid ""
"Multiframe restart files are generically indicated here as :file:`.xnnn` "
"files. They correspond to :file:`.rnnn` files for nonlinear static and full "
"transient analyses, and :file:`.mnnn` files for mode-superposition analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:194
msgid ""
"Remeshing database files are indicated as :file:`.rdnn` files. This type of "
"restart file is needed only after remeshing during a `nonlinear mesh "
"adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
" analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:197
msgid ""
"When ``Action`` = DEFINE, the specified ``Filetype`` determines the type of "
"file ( :file:`.xnnn` or :file:`.rdnn` ) controlled by this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:200
msgid "**Number of Restart Files Allowed**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:202
msgid ""
"The total number of restart files for any analysis cannot exceed 999 (for "
"example, :file:`jobname.r001` to :file:`jobname.r999` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:204
msgid ""
"The total number of remeshing database files cannot exceed 99 (for example, "
":file:`jobname.rd01` to :file:`jobname.rd99` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:207
msgid ""
"**Considerations for** `Nonlinear Mesh Adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
" Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:210
msgid ""
"To control both  :file:`.xnnn` and :file:`.rdnn` file writing ( ``Filetype``"
" = XNNN and ``Filetype`` = RDNN, respectively), separate :ref:`rescontrol` "
"commands are necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:212
msgid ""
"``Action`` = NORESTART and ``Ldstep`` = NONE are not valid and will cause "
"the analysis to fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:213
msgid "``Ldstep`` = ``-N`` is not valid for controlling :file:`.xnnn` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:215
msgid "**Limiting the Number of Files Saved**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:217
msgid ""
"If you have many substeps for each load step and are writing :file:`.xnnn` "
"files frequently, you may want to set ``MAXFILES`` to limit the number of "
":file:`.xnnn` files saved, as they can fill your disk quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:220
msgid ""
"You can specify ``MAXFILES`` and ``Frequency`` for individual load steps. "
"These arguments take on the default value or the value defined by "
":ref:`rescontrol`,,ALL, ``Frequency``, ``MAXFILES`` if they are not "
"explicitly defined for a specific load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:223
msgid ""
"When :file:`.xnnn` files are written over many load steps, you may want to "
"further limit the number of :file:`.xnnn` files by setting "
"``MAXTotalFiles``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:226
msgid "**Maximum Number of Load Steps**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:228
msgid ""
"You can specify a maximum of ten load steps; that is, you can issue the "
":ref:`rescontrol`,,N command a maximum of ten times. Specified load steps "
"cannot be changed in a restart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:231
msgid "**Specifying** ``Ldstep`` = LAST or ``-N``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:233
msgid ""
"The program accepts only one occurrence of :ref:`rescontrol` with ``Ldstep``"
" = LAST. If you issue :ref:`rescontrol`,,LAST, ``Frequency``, ``MAXFILES`` "
"multiple times, the last specification overwrites the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:236
msgid ""
"The program accepts only one occurrence of :ref:`rescontrol` with a negative"
" ``Ldstep`` value ( :ref:`rescontrol`, ``N`` where ``N`` is a negative "
"number). If you issue :ref:`rescontrol` multiple times with a negative "
"``Ldstep`` value, the last specification overwrites the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:241
msgid "**Using** :ref:`rescontrol` in a Restarted Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:243
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rescontrol` command is not valid in the restarted load step of a "
"restart analysis. It is only valid in subsequent load steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:248
msgid ""
"`Multiframe Restart "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS3_12.html#bassolumodres>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rescontrol:250
msgid ""
"`Linear Perturbation Analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_str/strlinpertinputs.html#linpert2genpass>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.misc\\_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/misc_loads.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:2
msgid ""
"Controls whether element single value results are written to the results "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RSTCONTROL "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RSTCONTROL.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:9
msgid "Solution format for database and file-write control:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:11
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - Write element output quantities (STRS, EPEL, EPPL, EPCR, EPTH) in"
" single value form for those element types that support it, and in element "
"nodal form for all other element types (default). See `Element Single Value "
"Results "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_CH2_2.html#>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:16
msgid ""
"``ELSV`` - Write element output quantities only in single value form. If the"
" single value form is not supported by the element types in the model, none "
"of the applicable results (STRS, EPEL, EPPL, EPCR, EPTH) will be available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:20
msgid ""
"``ELND`` - Write all element output quantities only in element nodal form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:22
msgid ""
"``ERASE`` - Reset :ref:`rstcontrol` specifications to their default values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:24
msgid "``STAT`` - List the current :ref:`rstcontrol` specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:27
msgid ""
"Name of the component (created via :ref:`cm` ) defining the selected set of "
"elements for which this specification is active. If no name is entered, the "
"specification applies to all elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:31
msgid ""
"For single value results, ``Method`` controls how the integration point "
"values of each element are reduced to one value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:33
msgid ""
"``AVG`` - Use a simple average of values from all integration points "
"(default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:35
msgid ""
"``MAXE`` - Use only the integration point corresponding to the maximum "
"equivalent (EQV) stress or strain quantity specified by ``MethodItem``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:38
msgid ""
"``MAXP`` - Use only the integration point corresponding to the maximum 1st "
"principal stress or strain quantity specified by ``MethodItem``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:41
msgid ""
"``MAXS`` - Use only the integration point corresponding to the maximum shear"
" stress or strain quantity specified by ``MethodItem``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:44
msgid "**methoditem** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:45
msgid ""
"The quantity used to determine the integration point where single value "
"results are reported. Only valid when ``Method`` = MAXE, MAXP, or MAXS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:48
msgid "``STRS`` - Choose the integration point based on stress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:50
msgid "``EPEL`` - Choose the integration point based on elastic strain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:52
msgid "``EPPL`` - Choose the integration point based on plastic strain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:54
msgid "``EPCR`` - Choose the integration point based on creep strain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:56
msgid "``EPTH`` - Choose the integration point based on thermal strain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:70
msgid ""
":ref:`rstcontrol` is an optional output control command that specifies "
"whether element nodal results or element single value results are written to"
" the results file. This command works in conjunction with the :ref:`outres` "
"command. :ref:`outres` specifies when each element quantity will be output, "
"while :ref:`rstcontrol` specifies the type of result (element nodal versus "
"single value). Not all elements support single value results. For more "
"information, see `Element Single Value Results "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_CH2_2.html#>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:77
msgid "The element output quantities affected by this command are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:79
msgid "stress (STRS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:80
msgid "elastic strain (EPEL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:81
msgid "plastic strain (EPPL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:82
msgid "creep strain (EPCR)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:83
msgid "thermal/swelling strains (EPTH)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.misc_loads.MiscLoads.rstcontrol:85
msgid ""
"You can issue up to 50 :ref:`rstcontrol` commands in an analysis. "
":ref:`rstcontrol`,ERASE erases the existing output specifications and resets"
" the counted number of :ref:`rstcontrol` commands to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/misc_loads.pydocstring
