msgid ""
"``ON`` - Use a line search. Note, adaptive descent is suppressed when "
":ref:`lnsrch` is on unless explicitly requested on the :ref:`nropt` command."
" Having line search on and adaptive descent on at the same time is not "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:17
msgid ""
"``AUTO`` - The program automatically switches line searching ON and OFF "
"between substeps of a load step as needed. This option is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:20
msgid "**lstol** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:21
msgid "Line search convergence tolerance (default = 0.5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:23
msgid "**lstrun** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:24
msgid ""
"Truncation key for the line search parameter. Default = OFF, meaning no "
"truncation. To activation truncation, input the number of digits to use "
"after the decimal point for the line search parameter. (See `Line Search "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_tool10.html#eq7ef4bddb-f782-469d-ad98-a2e8f4a9309c>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:43
msgid ""
"Activates a line search to be used with the Newton-Raphson method ( "
":ref:`nropt` ). Line search is an alternative to adaptive descent (see `Line"
" Search "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_tool10.html#eq7ef4bddb-f782-469d-ad98-a2e8f4a9309c>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:47
msgid ""
":ref:`lnsrch`,AUTO can be very efficient for problems in which :ref:`lnsrch`"
" is needed at only certain substeps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.lnsrch:50
msgid ""
"You cannot use line search ( :ref:`lnsrch` ), automatic time stepping ( "
":ref:`autots` ), or the DOF solution predictor ( :ref:`pred` ) with the arc-"
"length method ( :ref:`arclen`, :ref:`arctrm` ). If you activate the arc-"
"length method after you set :ref:`lnsrch`, :ref:`autots`, or :ref:`pred`, a "
"warning message appears. If you choose to proceed with the arc-length "
"method, the program disables your line search, automatic time stepping, and "
"DOF predictor settings, and the time step size is controlled by the arc-"
"length method internally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.nonlinear\\_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.rst:38:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:2
msgid "Sets the key to terminate an analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NCNV "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NCNV.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:8
msgid "**kstop** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:9
msgid "Program behavior upon nonconvergence:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:11
msgid ""
"``0`` - Do not terminate the analysis if the solution fails to converge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:13
msgid ""
"``1`` - Terminate the analysis and the program execution if the solution "
"fails to converge (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:16
msgid ""
"``2`` - Terminate the analysis, but not the program execution, if the "
"solution fails to converge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:18
msgid "**dlim** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:19
msgid ""
"Terminates program execution if the largest nodal DOF solution value "
"(displacement, temperature, etc.) exceeds this limit. Defaults to 1.0E6 for "
"all DOF except MAG and A. Defaults to 1.0E10 for MAG and A."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:23
msgid "**itlim** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:24
msgid ""
"Terminates program execution if the cumulative iteration number exceeds this"
" limit (defaults to infinity)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:27
msgid "**etlim** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:28
msgid ""
"Terminates program execution if the elapsed time (seconds) exceeds this "
"limit (defaults to infinity)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:31
msgid "**cplim** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:32
msgid ""
"Terminates program execution if the CPU time (seconds) exceeds this limit "
"(defaults to infinity)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.ncnv:49
msgid ""
"Sets the key to terminate an analysis if not converged, or if any of the "
"following limits are exceeded for nonlinear and full transient analyses: DOF"
" (displacement), cumulative iteration, elapsed time, or CPU time limit. "
"Applies only to static and transient analyses ( :ref:`antype` ,STATIC and "
":ref:`antype`,TRANS). Time limit checks are made at the end of each "
"equilibrium iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.nonlinear\\_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.rst:38:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:2
msgid ""
"Specifies the maximum number of equilibrium iterations for nonlinear "
"analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NEQIT "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NEQIT.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:9
msgid "Maximum number of equilibrium iterations allowed each substep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:11
msgid "**forcekey** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:12
msgid "One iteration forcing key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:14
msgid ""
"``FORCE`` - Forces one iteration per substep. Leave this field blank "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.neqit:16
msgid ""
"Using one iteration per substep may result in unconverged solutions for "
"nonlinear analysis, and the program may not indicate divergence in this "
"case. This option is intended primarily for use by the Ansys Workbench "
"interface. Keep in mind that forcing one iteration per substep is only "
"recommended under very specific conditions; for example, nonlinearity in "
"bonded penalty type contact. Under these conditions the solution typically "
"converges in one iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.nonlinear\\_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.rst:38:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:2
msgid ""
"Defines the criteria under which the mesh is refined or modified during a "
"nonlinear solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NLADAPTIVE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NLADAPTIVE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:8
msgid "**component** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:9
msgid "Specifies the element component upon which this command should act:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:11
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - All selected components, or all selected elements if no component "
"is selected (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:13
msgid "``Name`` - Component name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:16
msgid "Action to perform on the selected component(s):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:18
msgid "``ADD`` - Add a criterion to the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:20
msgid "``LIST`` - List the criteria defined for the specified component(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:22
msgid ""
"``OCTREE`` - Enable adaptive mesh coarsening for additive manufacturing "
"process simulation using the AM octree method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:25
msgid ""
"``DELETE`` - Delete the criteria defined for the specified component(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:27
msgid ""
"``ON`` - Enable the defined criteria for the specified component(s) and "
"specify how frequently and when to check them (via ON, ``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, "
"``VAL3`` ):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:30
msgid ""
"``VAL1`` -- Checking frequency. If > 0, check criteria at every ``VAL1`` "
"substeps. If < 0, check criteria at each of the ``VAL1`` points "
"(approximately equally spaced) between ``VAL2`` and ``VAL3``. (Default = "
"-1.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:34
msgid ""
"``VAL2`` -- Checking start time, where ``VAL2`` < ``VAL3``. (Default = Start"
" time of load step.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:36
msgid ""
"``VAL3`` -- Checking end time, where ``VAL3`` > ``VAL2``. (Default = End "
"time of load step.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:38
msgid ""
"``VAL4`` -- ``SOLID187`` element type ID (defined prior to issuing this "
"command). Valid only for ``SOLID185`` or ``SOLID186`` components in a `NLAD-"
"ETCHG analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/nladetchgexample.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:42
msgid "``OFF`` - Disable the defined criteria for the specified component(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:44
msgid "**criterion** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:45
msgid "Type of criterion to apply to the selected component(s):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:47
msgid ""
"``CONTACT`` - Contact-based. Valid only for ``Action`` = ADD, ``Action`` = "
"LIST, or ``Action`` = DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:50
msgid ""
"``ENERGY`` - Energy-based. Valid only for ``Action`` = ADD, ``Action`` = "
"LIST, or ``Action`` = DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:53
msgid ""
"``BOX`` - A position-based criterion, defined by a box. Valid only for "
"``Action`` = ADD, ``Action`` = LIST, or ``Action`` = DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:56
msgid ""
"``MESH`` - A mesh-quality-based criterion. Valid only for ``Action`` = ADD, "
"``Action`` = LIST, or ``Action`` = DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:59
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - All criteria and options. Valid only for ``Action`` = LIST or "
"``Action`` = DELETE. ``Option`` and all subsequent arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:63
msgid "Criterion option to apply to the selected component(s):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:65
msgid ""
"``NUMELEM`` - For target elements only, defines the minimum number of "
"contact elements to contact with each target element. If this criterion is "
"not satisfied, the program refines the contact elements and the associated "
"solid elements. For this option, ``VAL1`` must be a positive integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:69
msgid ""
"Valid only for ``Criterion`` = CONTACT and ``Action`` = ADD, LIST, or "
"DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:71
msgid ""
"``MEAN`` - Checks the strain energy of any element that is part of the "
"defined component for the condition E:sub:`e` ≥ c:sub:`1` * E:sub:`total` / "
"``NUME`` (where c:sub:`1` = ``VAL1``, E:sub:`total` is the total strain "
"energy of the component, and ``NUME`` is the number of elements of the "
"component). If this criterion is satisfied at an element, the program "
"refines the element. ``VAL1`` must be non-negative. Default = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:73
msgid ""
"Valid only for ``Criterion`` = ENERGY and ``Action`` = ADD, LIST, or DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:75
msgid ""
"``XYZRANGE`` - Defines the location box in which all elements within are to "
"be split or refined. Up to six values following the ``Option`` argument "
"(representing the x1, x2, y1, y2, z1, and z2 coordinates) are allowed. An "
"unspecified coordinate is not checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:79
msgid ""
"Valid only for ``Criterion`` = BOX and ``Action`` = ADD, LIST, or DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:81
msgid ""
"``LAYER`` - Sets layer options for AM octree adaptive meshing for additive "
"simulations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:83
msgid ""
"``VAL1`` - Number of layers to keep at fine mesh resolution between the "
"current, top layer and the layers to be remeshed. Default = 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:85
msgid ""
"``VAL2`` - Number of buffer elements to keep at fine mesh resolution between"
" the part edges and the remeshed elements. Default = 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:88
msgid "Valid only for ``Action`` = OCTREE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:90
msgid ""
"``SKEWNESS`` - Mesh-quality-control threshold for elements ``SOLID187``, "
"``SOLID285``, and ``SOLID227`` :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:92
msgid ""
"``VAL1`` - Defines skewness. Valid values: 0.0 through 1.0. Default = 0.9."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:93
msgid ""
"``VAL2`` - Maximum Jacobian ratio at element integration points ( "
"``SOLID187`` and ``SOLID227`` only). Valid values: 0.0 to 1.0. Default = "
"0.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:96
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:106
msgid ""
"Valid only for ``Criterion`` = MESH and ``Action`` = ADD, LIST, or DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:98
msgid ""
"``SHAPE`` - Mesh-quality control threshold for elements ``PLANE182`` and "
"``PLANE222``. Also applies to ``SOLID185`` and ``SOLID186`` in a `NLAD-ETCHG"
" analysis "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/nladetchgexample.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:102
msgid ""
"``VAL1`` -- Maximum corner angle of an element in degrees. Valid values are "
"0 through 180. Default = 160 (2D analysis) or 155 (3D analysis). An element "
"is remeshed when any of its corner angles reach the specified value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:108
msgid ""
"``WEAR`` - For contact elements having surface wear specified ( "
":ref:`tb`,WEAR) only, defines ``VAL1`` as a critical ratio of magnitude of "
"wear to the average depth of the solid element underlying the contact "
"element. Once this critical ratio is reached for any element, the program "
"morphs the mesh to improve the quality of the elements. ``VAL1`` must be a "
"positive integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:113
msgid ""
"Valid only for ``Criterion`` = CONTACT and ``Action`` = ADD, ``Action`` = "
"LIST, or ``Action`` = DELETE. Cannot be combined with any other option "
"during solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:116
msgid ""
"``CZM`` - For contact elements with `cohesive zone material "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnacriteria.html#nladrefsubstep>`_"
" ( :ref:`tb`,CZM) only, defines ``VAL1`` as a critical value of change in "
"released energy due to debonding between reference and current substep, and "
"``VAL2`` as the critical value for the change in the damage parameter "
"between neighboring elements. Both values can be applied separately or "
"together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:123
msgid ""
"When the critical value is reached (for either of the defined options) for "
"one contact element, the solid elements underlying that contact element and "
"the corresponding deformable target element are selected as candidates for "
"remeshing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:127
msgid "``VAL1`` must be > 0. ``VAL2`` must be > 0 and < 1. No default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:129
msgid ""
"Valid only for ``Criterion`` = CONTACT and ``Action`` = ADD, LIST, or "
"DELETE. Combing the CZM criterion with `mesh-quality-based "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnacriteria.html#advmnlaskewnessopt>`_"
" criteria may be necessary to improve distorted elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:134
msgid ""
"``ALL`` - All options. Valid only for ``Action`` = LIST or ``Action`` = "
"DELETE. All subsequent arguments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:138
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:144
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:150
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:156
msgid ""
"The description of the argument is missing in the Python function. Please, "
"refer to the `command documentation "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NLADAPTIVE.html>`_"
" for further information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:175
msgid ""
"If a specified component ( ``Component`` ) is an assembly, the defined "
"criterion applies to all element components included in the assembly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:178
msgid ""
"All components must be defined and selected before the first solve ( "
":ref:`solve` ), although their nonlinear adaptivity criteria can be modified"
" from load step to load step, and upon restart. For nonlinear adaptivity to "
"work properly, ensure that all components are selected before each solve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:182
msgid ""
"After issuing this command to define a new criterion, the new criterion "
"becomes active. The program checks the new criterion once per load step, "
"roughly in mid-loading (unless this behavior is changed via ``Action`` = "
"ON)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:186
msgid ""
"When a criterion is defined, it overwrites a previously defined criterion "
"(if one exists) through the same component, or through the component "
"assembly that includes the specified component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:189
msgid ""
"During solution, the same criteria defined for an element through different "
"components are combined, and the tightest criteria and action control ( "
"``Action``,ON, ``VAL1`` ) are used. If an ON action is defined by a positive"
" ``VAL1`` value through one component and a negative ``VAL1`` value through "
"another, the program uses the positive value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:194
msgid ""
"When the AM octree option is specified ( ``Action`` = OCTREE), the checking "
"frequency ( Action,ON,, VAL1 ), checking start time ( Action,ON, VAL2 ), and"
" checking end time ( Action,ON, VAL3 ) control the checking layer frequency,"
" start layer, and end layer respectively. If start and end layers are not "
"specified, the start layer will default to the checking frequency, and the "
"end layer will default to the final layer of the AM simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:200
msgid ""
"If ``VAL1`` < 0, the program checks ``VAL1`` points between ``VAL2`` and "
"``VAL3``. The time interval between each check points is determined by ( "
"``VAL3`` - ``VAL2`` ) / ( ``VAL1`` + 1), with the first check point as close"
" to ``VAL2`` + ( ``VAL3`` - ``VAL2`` ) / ( ``VAL1`` + 1) as possible. Fewer "
"check points can be used if the number of substeps during solution is "
"insufficient (as the program can only check at the end of a substep)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:206
msgid ""
"If ``VAL2`` (start time) and/or ``VAL3`` (end time) are unspecified or "
"invalid, the program uses the start and/or end time (respectively) of the "
"load step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:209
msgid ""
"``VAL1`` applies to tetrahedral elements ``SOLID187``, ``SOLID227``, and "
"``SOLID285``. When the skewness of an element is >= ``VAL1``, the element is"
" used as the core (seed) element of the remeshed region(s). The most "
"desirable skewness value is 0, applicable when the element is a standard "
"tetrahedral element; the highest value is 1, applicable when the element "
"becomes flat with zero volume. To bypass skewness checking (not "
"recommended), set ``VAL1`` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:215
msgid ""
"``VAL2`` represents the Jacobian ratio and is required for tetrahedral "
"elements ``SOLID187`` and ``SOLID227``. When the maximum Jacobian ratio of "
"an element is <= ``VAL2``, the element is used as the core (seed) element of"
" the remeshed region(s). The most desirable maximum Jacobian ratio is 1, "
"when the element is a standard tetrahedral element; the lowest reported "
"value is -1, when the element is turned inside out. To bypass maximum "
"Jacobian ratio checking (not recommended), set ``VAL2`` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:222
msgid ""
"If this criterion is used with any other criteria defined for the same "
"component, and a mesh change is requested at the same substep, all criteria "
"defined are considered together. For more information about this special "
"case, see `Simultaneous Quality- and Refinement-Based Remeshing "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnanewmesh.html#>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:227
msgid ""
"For more information about skewness, maximum Jacobian ratio, and remeshing, "
"see `Nonlinear Mesh Adaptivity "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/advmnaexample.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nladaptive:230
msgid ""
"For more granular control of the source mesh geometry, see :ref:`nlmesh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.nonlinear\\_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.rst:38:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:2
msgid "Sets nonlinear diagnostics functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `NLDIAG "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_NLDIAG.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:9
msgid "Diagnostic function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:11
msgid "``NRRE`` - Store the Newton-Raphson residuals information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:13
msgid ""
"``EFLG`` - Identify or display elements or nodes that violate the criteria."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:15
msgid ""
"``CONT`` - Write contact information to a single :file:`Jobname.cnd` "
"diagnostic text file during solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:19
msgid "Diagnostic function characteristics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:21
msgid "``OFF or 0`` - Suppresses writing of diagnostic information (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:23
msgid ""
"``ON or 1`` - Writes diagnostic information to the :file:`Jobname.ndxxx`, "
":file:`Jobname.nrxxx`, or :file:`Jobname.cnd` file. (If ``Label`` = CONT, "
"this option is the same as the SUBS option described below.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:27
msgid ""
"``ITER`` - Writes contact diagnostic information at each iteration. Valid "
"only when ``Label`` = CONT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:30
msgid ""
"``SUBS`` - Writes contact diagnostic information at each substep. Valid only"
" when ``Label`` = CONT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:33
msgid ""
"``LSTP`` - Writes contact diagnostic information at each load step. Valid "
"only when ``Label`` = CONT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:36
msgid ""
"``STAT`` - Lists information about the diagnostic files in the current "
"working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:38
msgid ""
"``DEL`` - Deletes all diagnostic files in the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:40
msgid "**maxfile** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:41
msgid ""
"Maximum number of diagnostic files to create. Valid values are 1 through "
"999. Default = 4. Valid only when ``Label`` = NRRE or EFLG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:44
msgid ""
"Information is written to :file:`Jobname.ndxxx` or :file:`Jobname.nrxxx`, "
"where ``xxx`` iterates from 001 through ``MAXFILE``. When the specified "
"maximum number of diagnostic files is reached, the counter resets to 001 and"
" earlier files are overwritten. The ``MAXFILE`` value specified for this "
"``Label`` function applies until a new value is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:63
msgid ""
"The :ref:`nldiag` command is a nonlinear diagnostics tool valid for "
"nonlinear analyses that include structural degrees of freedom. It is a "
"debugging tool for use when you must restart after an unconverged solution. "
"The command creates :file:`Jobname.ndxxx`, :file:`Jobname.nrxxx`, or "
":file:`Jobname.cnd` files in the working directory to store the information "
"you specify."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:68
msgid "For more information, see."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:70
msgid ""
"Issue the :ref:`nldiag`,NRRE,ON command to create :file:`Jobname.nrxxx` "
"diagnostic files (for each equilibrium iteration after the first) in which "
"to store the relevant Newton-Raphson residual information of FX, FY, FZ "
"(forces), MX, MY, MZ (moments), HEAT (heat flow), AMPS (current flow), CHRG "
"(electric charge), or RATE (diffusion flow rate) for the last ``MAXFILE`` "
"equilibrium iterations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:76
msgid ""
"Issue a :ref:`nldpost`,NRRE,STAT command to list the load step, substep, "
"time, and equilibrium iteration corresponding to each of the "
":file:`Jobname.nrxxx` diagnostic files in the working directory, then issue "
"a :ref:`plnsol`,NRRES,, ``FileID`` command to point to the file from which "
"you want to create a contour plot of your Newton-Raphson residuals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:81
msgid ""
"If you restart or issue a new :ref:`solve` command, any "
":file:`Jobname.nrxxx` diagnostic files in the current (working) directory "
"are overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:84
msgid ""
"Issue a :ref:`nldiag`,EFLG,ON command to create :file:`Jobname.ndxxx` "
"diagnostic files which store IDs for elements violating the following "
"criteria:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:87
msgid "Too large a distortion (HDST)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:89
msgid ""
"Elements contain nodes that have near zero pivots (PIVT) for nonlinear "
"analyses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:91
msgid ""
"Too large a plastic/creep (EPPL/EPCR) strain increment ( :ref:`cutcontrol` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:93
msgid ""
"Elements for which mixed u-P constraints are not satisfied (mixed U-P option"
" of 18 ``x`` solid elements only) (MXUP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:96
msgid ""
"Hyperelastic element (EPHY), cohesive zone material (EPCZ), or damage strain"
" (EPDM) not converged"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:98
msgid "Radial displacement (RDSP) not converged"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:100
msgid ""
"``MPC184`` multipoint constraint elements using KEYOPT(1) = 6 through 16 "
"with the Lagrange multiplier option fail to satisfy constraint conditions "
"(184J)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:103
msgid ""
"For :ref:`nldiag`,EFLG,ON, all :file:`Jobname.ndxxx` diagnostic files (for "
"each equilibrium iteration after the first) in the current (working) "
"directory are deleted when you issue a new :ref:`solve` command (or "
"restart)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:107
msgid ""
"In the solution processor ( :ref:`slashsolu` ), use the STAT option to list "
"the active status of this command. In the postprocessor ( :ref:`post1` ), "
"issue a :ref:`nldpost`,EFLG,STAT command to list the load step, substep, "
"time, and equilibrium iteration corresponding to each of the "
":file:`Jobname.ndxxx` diagnostic files in the working directory, then issue "
"a :ref:`nldpost`,EFLG,CM, ``FileID`` command to create element components "
"that violate the criteria."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:113
msgid ""
"Issue the :ref:`nldiag`,CONT,ON command to create a :file:`Jobname.cnd` "
"diagnostic file which stores contact information for all defined contact "
"pairs at all substeps. Alternatively, you may issue one of the following "
"commands to store contact information at a specific frequency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:117
msgid ":ref:`nldiag`,CONT,ITER to write at each iteration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:119
msgid ":ref:`nldiag`,CONT,SUBS to write at each substep (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/nonlinear_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.nonlinear_options.NonlinearOptions.nldiag:121
