#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:33
msgid "**maxfluxiter** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:34
msgid ""
"Maximum number of flux iterations to be performed according to the specified"
" solver type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:36
msgid ""
"``0`` - If the FULL solver is specified ( :ref:`thopt`,FULL), convergence "
"criteria are monitored and iterations are performed until convergence "
"occurs. If the QUASI solver is specified ( :ref:`thopt`,QUASI), convergence "
"criteria are ignored and one iteration is performed. This value is the "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:41
msgid ""
"``1, 2, 3,...N`` - If the FULL solver is specified ( :ref:`thopt`,FULL), "
"convergence criteria are monitored and iterations are performed until "
"convergence occurs, or until the specified number of iterations has been "
"completed, whichever comes first. If the QUASI solver is specified ( "
":ref:`thopt`,QUASI), convergence criteria are ignored and the specified "
"number of iterations are completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:47
msgid "To view ``MAXFLUXITER`` usage illustrations, see and."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:49
msgid "**conservation** : :class:`python:int` or :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:50
msgid ""
"Key to account for the midside node temperature of underlying solid elements"
" for radiosity calculations. Under normal circumstations using lower order "
"elements, this option does not need to be activated. However, when using "
"higher elements, you can improve energy conservation by setting "
"``CONSERVATION`` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:54
msgid ""
"``0`` - Not active (default). The midside node temperatures are not "
"accounted for in the radiosity calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.radopt:57
msgid ""
"``1`` - Active. The midside node temperatures are accounted for in the "
"radiosity calculations. To work effectively, ``CONSERVATION`` requires a "
"one-to-one correspondance between the surface elements and their underlying "
"solid elements. Therefore, it cannot be activated if the :ref:`rdec` command"
" was issued when generating ``SURF251`` or ``SURF252`` elements."
msgstr ""

