"Element type number. Leave blank to indicate the next available number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:40
msgid ""
"This command generates the radiosity surface elements ( ``SURF251``, "
"``SURF252`` ) based on the :ref:`rsymm` and :ref:`rdec` parameters and "
"stores them in the database. It works only on the faces of selected "
"underlying elements that have RDSF flags on them and all corner nodes "
"selected. You can issue multiple :ref:`rsurf` commands to build the "
"radiosity model. However, all :ref:`rsurf` commands must be issued after "
"issuing the :ref:`rsymm` command, and after the model is complete (that is, "
"after all meshing operations are complete)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:47
msgid ""
"If you do issue multiple :ref:`rsurf` commands for different regions, you "
"must first mesh the different regions, and then generate the radiosity "
"surface elements on each meshed region individually. Use "
":ref:`rsurf`,,,ETNUM to assign a separate element type number to each "
"region. This procedure allow you to identify the individual regions later in"
" the multi-field analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:52
msgid ""
"If the underlying solid elements are higher order, the radiosity surface "
"elements are always lower order (4- or 3-node in 3D or 2-node in 2D). "
"Decimation will always occur before any symmetry operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:56
msgid ""
"For 2D axisymmetric YR models, the newly-generated nodes can have only "
"positive Y coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:58
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rsurf` command assigns real constant set number 1 to all "
"``SURF251`` and ``SURF252`` elements generated, irrespective of the current "
"real constant set attribute pointer ( :ref:`real` command). If the generated"
" elements require a real constant set other than number 1, you must manually"
" change the set number for those elements by using the :ref:`emodif`,,REAL "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:63
msgid ""
"If you have already issued :ref:`rsurf` for a surface and you issue "
":ref:`rsurf` again, the program creates a new set of radiosity surface "
"elements and nodes over the existing set, resulting in an erroneous "
"solution. Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction This command is not "
"supported in a DMP solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsurf:68
msgid ""
"This is an action command (that creates or deletes surface meshes) and is "
"serial in nature. Even if a DMP solution is running, the :ref:`rsurf` "
"command runs serially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/radiosity.rst:29:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:2
msgid ""
"Defines symmetry, rotation, or extrusion parameters for the radiosity "
"method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `RSYMM "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RSYMM.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:11
msgid ""
"``CLEAR`` - Deletes all symmetry/extrusion definitions. Other command "
"options are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:13
msgid "``DEFINE`` - Defines the symmetry/extrusion definition (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:17
msgid ""
"``COND`` - Activates or deactivates condensation for all defined radiation "
"symmetries/extrusions, which reduces the size of the radiosity equation "
"system (see :ref:`cmd_rsymm_fig1` ). Default is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:21
msgid ""
"Condensation via :ref:`rsymm`,COND is not recommended as the most efficient "
"solution for symmetric models. To best leverage model symmetry to improve "
"efficiency, use view factor condensation via the :ref:`vfco` command, which "
"condenses the view factor matrix in addition to simplifying the radiosity "
"equations (see :ref:`RSYMM_VFCO_notes` for details)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:27
msgid ""
"Local coordinate system ( :math:`equation not available` 11) as defined "
"using the  :ref:`local` or :ref:`cs` commands or the global coordinate "
"system (0). For planar reflection, the coordinate system origin must be on "
"the plane of symmetry (POS) and one of its axes must be normal to the POS. "
"For cyclic reflection, the coordinate system origin must be coincident with "
"the center of rotation (COR). Only Cartesian systems are valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:34
msgid ""
"Axis label of the coordinate system ( ``CS`` ) that is normal to the POS for"
" planar reflection, or label to indicate the type of extrusion. For cyclic "
"reflection, this field must be blank, and it is assumed that the Z axis is "
"aligned with the axis of rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:38
msgid ""
"``X, Y, or Z`` - Planar reflection. For 2D model planar reflections, valid "
"labels are X or Y. For 3D model planar reflections, valid labels are X, Y, "
"or Z."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:41
msgid ""
"``ZEXT`` - Linear extrusion of a line element in the X-Y plane, in the Z "
"direction, to create 4-noded ``SURF252`` elements. ``NSECT`` indicates how "
"many elements will be created. ``SVAL`` is the starting Z value, and "
"``EVAL`` is the ending Z value. ``CS`` must be 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:45
msgid ""
"``CEXT`` - Circumferential extrusion (theta direction) around the global "
"Y-axis. A 2-noded line element in the X-Y plane is extruded to create "
"4-noded ``SURF252`` elements. ``NSECT`` indicates how many elements will be "
"created. ``SVAL`` is the starting angle, and EVAL is the ending angle (in "
"degrees). The angles are with respect to the global X-axis. ``CS`` must be "
"0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:50
msgid "``(blank)`` - Cyclic reflection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:53
msgid ""
"Number of cyclic reflections to be done, or number of elements in the "
"extrusion direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:55
msgid "For planar reflection, this field must be 0 or blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:57
msgid ""
"For cyclic reflection, this field must be ≥ 1 or ≤ -1. Use a positive value "
"if you want the sector angle to be computed automatically. Use a negative "
"value if you want the sector angle to be computed manually. See `Notes "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_cmd/Hlp_C_RSYMM.html#cmd_rsymm_fig1>`_"
" Notes for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:63
msgid "**condvalue** : :class:`python:str`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.radiosity.Radiosity.rsymm:64
msgid "Condensation key. Valid only when ``Option`` = COND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/radiosity.pydocstring
