"variables are the tensor component. For strain-like tensors, the shear "
"components saved as state variables are twice the tensor components. "
"Therefore, issue the :ref:`mapvar` command to define the stress-like and "
"strain-like tensors individually. The command ensures that user-defined "
"state variables are mapped correctly during `rezoning "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/Hlp_G_ADVRZSMP.html>`_"
" and in `2D to 3D analyses "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_adv/Hlp_G_ADV2DTO3DREST.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.mapvar:74
msgid ""
"In a rezoning operation, :ref:`mapvar` must be issued after remeshing ( "
":ref:`remesh`,FINISH) but before mapping ( :ref:`mapsolve` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/rezoning.rst:23:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:2
msgid ""
"Specifies the starting and ending remeshing points, and other options, for "
"rezoning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `REMESH "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_REMESH.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:9
msgid "``START`` - Starts the remeshing operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:11
msgid "``FINISH`` - Ends the remeshing operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:13
msgid ""
"``READ`` - Reads in a generic ( :file:`.cdb` format) new mesh file generated"
" by a third-party application. This remeshing option applies to both 2D and "
"3D rezoning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:16
msgid ""
"``SPLIT`` - Splits selected elements of an existing 2D or 3D mesh such that "
"a quadrilateral element is split into four quadrilaterals, a degenerate "
"quadrilateral is split into three quadrilaterals, and a quadratic triangular"
" element is split into four quadratic triangles. A tetrahedral element is "
"split into eight tetrahedra."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:22
msgid ""
"Name of a :file:`.cdb` generic mesh file. The default value is "
":file:`jobname`. Valid only when ``Action`` = READ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:26
msgid ""
"File name extension. The only valid (and the default) extension is CDB. "
"Valid only when ``Action`` = READ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:30
msgid ""
"Specifies options for the new mesh when using a generic imported mesh file "
"or the mesh-splitting remeshing method. Valid only when ``Action`` = READ or"
" ``Action`` = SPLIT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:33
msgid ""
"``REGE`` - Regenerates all node and element numbers on the new mesh using an"
" offset of the highest existing node and element numbers. This is the "
"default behavior when ``Action`` = READ; otherwise, this value is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:37
msgid ""
"``KEEP`` - Keeps the similarly numbered nodes and elements in the new and "
"the old meshes unchanged. Valid only when ``Action`` = READ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:40
msgid ""
"``TRAN`` - Generates transition elements to ensure nodal compatibility "
"between split and unsplit parts of the mesh. Valid only when ``Action`` = "
"SPLIT for 2D analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:44
msgid ""
"Specifies transition options for the mesh when elements are split. These "
"options are valid only when ``Action`` = SPLIT for 2D analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:47
msgid ""
"``QUAD`` - Minimizes the number of degenerate elements in the transition "
"mesh and tries to maximize the number of quadrilateral transition elements "
"across several layers of elements from the split regions. This is the "
"default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:51
msgid ""
"``DEGE`` - Creates transition zones between the split and unsplit parts of "
"the mesh using mostly degenerate elements with a single element layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:66
msgid ""
"This command is valid only during the rezoning ( :ref:`rezone` ) process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:68
msgid ""
"In rezoning, :ref:`remesh`,START exits the solution processor temporarily "
"and enters a special mode of the PREP7 preprocessor, after which a limited "
"number of preprocessing commands are available for `mesh control "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/Hlp_G_ADVRZREM.html#advrezcmdtbl>`_,"
" but no solution commands are valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:74
msgid ""
":ref:`remesh`,FINISH exits the remeshing process and reenters the solution "
"processor, at which point no preprocessing commands are available. If the "
"new mesh exists, the command creates contact elements if needed, and "
"transfers all boundary conditions (BCs) and loads from the original mesh to "
"the new mesh. You can issue any list or plot command to verify the created "
"contact elements, transferred BCs, and loads. :ref:`remesh`,FINISH is valid "
"only after a previously issued :ref:`remesh`,START, and is the only way to "
"safely end the remeshing operation (and exit the special mode of PREP7)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:82
msgid ""
":ref:`remesh`,READ is valid only when you want to perform a rezoning "
"operation using a generic new mesh generated by a third-party application "
"(rather than a new mesh generated internally by Mechanical APDL). The "
"command is valid between :ref:`remesh`,START and :ref:`remesh`,FINISH. In "
"this case, the only valid file extension is :file:`.cdb` ( ``Ext`` = CDB). "
"When ``Option`` = KEEP, Mechanical APDL assumes that the common node and "
"element numbers between the old and the new mesh are topologically similar "
"(that is, these commonly numbered areas have the same element connectivity "
"and nodal coordinates)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:92
msgid ""
":ref:`remesh`,SPLIT is valid only when performing a rezoning operation via "
"splitting the existing mesh. The command is valid between "
":ref:`remesh`,START and :ref:`remesh`,FINISH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:95
msgid ""
"You can use :ref:`remesh`,READ and :ref:`remesh`,SPLIT for horizontal "
"multiple rezoning provided that the meshes used in :ref:`remesh`,READ do not"
" intersect. (Avoid issuing :ref:`aremesh` after issuing either of these "
"commands.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.remesh:99
msgid ""
"For more information about the remeshing options available during rezoning, "
"see `Rezoning "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/Hlp_G_ADVRZSMP.html>`_"
" Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction This command is not supported"
" in a DMP solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone.rst:2
msgid "ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/rezoning.rst:23:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:2
msgid ""
"Initiates the rezoning process, sets rezoning options, and rebuilds the "
"database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `REZONE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_REZONE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:9
msgid ""
"The `rezoning "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/Hlp_G_ADVRZSMP.html>`_"
" method to employ:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:13
msgid ""
"``MANUAL`` - Manual rezoning. You decide when to use rezoning, what "
"region(s) to rezone, and what remeshing method to use on the selected "
"region(s). This method is currently the default and only option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:18
msgid ""
"The load step number at which rezoning should occur. The default value is "
"the highest load step number found in the :file:`Jobname.Rnnn` files (for "
"the current jobname and in the current directory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:23
msgid ""
"The substep number of the specified load step ( ``LDSTEP`` ) at which "
"rezoning should occur. The default value is the highest substep number found"
" in the specified load step in the :file:`Jobname.Rnnn` files (for the "
"current jobname and in the current directory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:41
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rezone` command rebuilds the database ( :file:`.db` file) based on"
" the specified load step and substep information, and updates nodes to their"
" deformed position for remeshing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:44
msgid ""
"Before issuing this command, clear the database via the :ref:`clear` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/rezoning.pydocstring
#: of ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.rezoning.Rezoning.rezone:46
msgid ""
"For more information, see `Rezoning "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_nlad/Hlp_G_ADVRZSMP.html>`_"
" Distributed-Memory Parallel (DMP) Restriction This command is not supported"
" in a DMP solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.solid\\_body\\_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.rst:31:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:2
msgid "Defines a body-force load on an area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `BFA "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_BFA.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:9
msgid ""
"Area to which body load applies. If ALL, apply to all selected areas ( "
":ref:`asel` ). A component name may also be substituted for ``Area``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfk:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfv:13
msgid ""
"Valid body load label. Load labels are listed under \"Body Loads\" in the "
"input table for each element type in the `Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:21
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:29
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:37
msgid ""
"Value associated with the ``Lab`` item or a table name for specifying "
"tabular boundary conditions. Use only ``VAL1`` for TEMP, FLUE, HGEN, CHRGD. "
"For ``Lab`` = JS in magnetics, use ``VAL1``, ``VAL2``, and ``VAL3`` for the "
"X, Y, and Z components. For ``Lab`` = IMPD in acoustics, ``VAL1`` is the "
"resistance and ``VAL2`` is the reactance in ohms/square. When specifying a "
"table name, you must enclose the table name in percent signs (%), e.g., "
":ref:`bfa`, ``Area``, ``Lab``,``tabname``. Use the :ref:`dim` command to "
"define a table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:45
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfl:45
msgid "If ``Lab`` = JS, ``VAL4`` is the phase angle in degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:61
msgid ""
"Defines a body-force load (such as temperature in a structural analysis, "
"heat generation rate in a thermal analysis, etc.) on an area. Body loads may"
" be transferred from areas to area elements (or to nodes if area elements do"
" not exist) with the :ref:`bftran` or :ref:`sbctran` commands. Body loads "
"default to the value specified on the :ref:`bfunif` command, if it was "
"previously specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:66
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfk:75
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfl:65
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfv:73
msgid ""
"You can specify a table name only when using temperature (TEMP) and heat "
"generation rate (HGEN) body load labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfa:69
msgid ""
"Body loads specified by the :ref:`bfa` command can conflict with other "
"specified body loads. See Resolution of Conflicting Body Load Specifications"
" in the `Basic Analysis Guide "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_bas/Hlp_G_BAS19.html>`_"
" for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.solid\\_body\\_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.rst:31:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele:2
msgid "Deletes body-force loads on an area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `BFADELE "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_BFADELE.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele:9
msgid ""
"Area at which body load is to be deleted. If ALL, delete for all selected "
"areas ( :ref:`asel` ). A component name may also be substituted for "
"``AREA``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele:13
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist:14
msgid ""
"Valid body load label. If ALL, use all appropriate labels. Load labels are "
"listed under \"Body Loads\" in the input table for each element type in the "
"`Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_."
" See the :ref:`bfa` command for labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfadele:32
msgid ""
"Deletes body-force loads (and all corresponding finite element loads) for a "
"specified area and label. Body loads may be defined on an area with the "
":ref:`bfa` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.solid\\_body\\_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.rst:31:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist:2
msgid "Lists the body-force loads on an area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist:4
msgid ""
"Mechanical APDL Command: `BFALIST "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en//ans_cmd/Hlp_C_BFALIST.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist:9
msgid ""
"Area at which body load is to be listed. If ALL (or blank), list for all "
"selected areas ( :ref:`asel` ). If ``AREA`` = P, graphical picking is "
"enabled and all remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the "
"GUI). A component name may also be substituted for ``AREA``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfalist:33
msgid ""
"Lists the body-force loads for the specified area and label. Body loads may "
"be defined on an area with the :ref:`bfa` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/_autosummary/ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_body_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfk.rst:2
msgid ""
"ansys.mapdl.core.\\_commands.solution.solid\\_body\\_loads.SolidBodyLoads.bfk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/doc/source/mapdl_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.rst:31:<autosummary>:1
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_body_loads.pydocstring
