msgid "documentation pointed above... _sfa1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:31
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:24
msgid ""
"For an acoustic analysis, apply the fluid-structure interaction flag (Label "
"= FSI) to only the ``FLUID129`` or ``FLUID130`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:39
msgid ""
"``VALUE`` is typically the film coefficient and ``VALUE2`` (below) is "
"typically the bulk temperature. If ``Lab`` = CONV and ``VALUE`` = - ``N``, "
"the film coefficient may be a function of temperature and is determined from"
" the HF property table for material ``N`` ( :ref:`mp` ). (See the "
":ref:`scopt` command for a way to override this option and use - ``N`` as "
"the film coefficient.) The temperature used to evaluate the film coefficient"
" is usually the average between the bulk and wall temperatures, but may be "
"user-defined for some elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:45
msgid ""
"If :ref:`kbc`,0 has been issued for ramped loads, it affects only "
"``VALUE2``, :ref:`the bulk temperature, and the film coefficient "
"specification is unaffected. <SFA_V2CONV>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:49
msgid "If ``Lab`` = RAD, ``VALUE`` is the surface emissivity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:51
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = PORT, ``VALUE`` is a port number representing a waveguide "
"exterior port. The port number must be an integer between 1 and 50. For "
"acoustic 2×2 transfer admittance matrix, the port number can be any positive"
" integer. The smaller port number corresponds to the port 1 of the 2×2 "
"transfer admittance matrix and the greater port number corresponds to the "
"port 2. If one port of the transfer admittance matrix is connecting to the "
"acoustic-structural interaction interface, the port number corresponds to "
"the port 2 of the transfer admittance matrix. A pair of ports of the 2×2 "
"transfer admittance matrix must be defined in the same element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:59
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = SHLD, ``VALUE`` is the surface normal velocity in harmonic "
"analysis and the surface normal acceleration in transient analysis for "
"acoustics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:62
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = IMPD, ``VALUE`` is resistance in (N)(s)/m :sup:`3` if ``VALUE``"
" > 0 and is conductance in mho if ``VALUE`` < 0 for acoustics. In acoustic "
"transient analyses, ``VALUE2`` is not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:80
msgid "``VALUE2`` is typically the bulk temperature for thermal analyses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:81
msgid ""
"If :ref:`kbc`,0 has been issued for ramped loads, the bulk temperature is "
"ramped from the value defined by :ref:`tunif` to the value specified by "
"``VALUE2`` for the first loadstep. If :ref:`tabular boundary conditions are "
"defined, the <SFA_tabBC>` :ref:`kbc` command is ignored and tabular values "
"are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:85
msgid "For acoustic analyses, VALUE2 is not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:87
msgid "If ``Lab`` = RAD ``VALUE2`` is ambient temperature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:95
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = RDSF, ``VALUE2`` is the enclosure number. Radiation will occur "
"between surfaces flagged with the same enclosure numbers. If the enclosure "
"is open, radiation will also occur to ambient. If ``VALUE2`` is negative, "
"radiation direction is reversed and will occur inside the element for the "
"flagged radiation surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:117
msgid ""
"Surface loads may be transferred from areas to elements with the "
":ref:`sftran` or :ref:`sbctran` commands. See the :ref:`sfgrad` command for "
"an alternate tapered load capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfa:120
msgid ""
"Tabular boundary conditions Tabular boundary conditions ( ``VALUE`` = "
"``tabname`` and/or ``VALUE2`` = ``tabname``) are available for the following"
" surface load labels ( ``Lab`` ) only: PRES (real and/or imaginary "
"components), CONV (film coefficient and/or bulk temperature) or HFLUX, and "
"RAD (surface emissivity and ambient temperature). Use the :ref:`dim` command"
" to define a table."
msgstr ""

