msgid ""
"Line to which surface load applies. If ALL, apply load to all selected lines"
" ( :ref:`lsel` ). If ``Line`` = P, graphical picking is enabled and all "
"remaining command fields are ignored (valid only in the GUI). A component "
"name may be substituted for ``Line``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:14
msgid ""
"Valid surface load label. Load labels are listed under \"Surface Loads\" in "
"the input table for each element type in the `Element Reference "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_BIBLIO.html>`_."
"  This command contains some tables and extra information which can be "
"inspected in the original documentation pointed above... _sfl1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:28
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:56
msgid ""
"Surface load values at the first keypoint ( ``VALI`` ) and at the second "
"keypoint ( ``VALJ`` ) of the line, or table name for specifying tabular "
"boundary conditions. If ``VALJ`` is blank, it defaults to ``VALI``. If "
"``VALJ`` is zero, a zero is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:34
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:62
msgid ""
"``VALI`` and ``VALJ`` are the film coefficients and ``VAL2I`` and ``VAL2J`` "
"are the bulk temperatures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:36
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:64
msgid ""
"To specify a table, enclose the table name in percent signs (%), e.g., "
"``tabname``. (Issue :ref:`dim` to define a table.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:38
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:66
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = CONV and ``VALI`` = - ``N``, the film coefficient may be a "
"function of temperature and is determined from the HF property table for "
"material ``N`` ( :ref:`mp` ). (See :ref:`scopt` for a way to override this "
"option and use - ``N`` as the film coefficient.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:41
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:69
msgid ""
"If :ref:`kbc`,0 has been issued for ramped loads, it affects only the bulk "
"temperatures, ``VAL2I`` and ``VAL2J``, and the film coefficient "
"specification, ``VALI`` and ``VALJ``, are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:44
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:72
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = RAD, ``VALI`` and ``VALJ`` values are surface emissivities and "
"``VAL2I`` and ``VAL2J`` are ambient temperatures. The temperature used to "
"evaluate the film coefficient is usually the average between the bulk and "
"wall temperatures, but may be user-defined for some elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:48
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:76
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = RDSF, ``VALI`` is the emissivity value. If ``VALI`` = ``-N``, "
"the emissivity may be a function of the temperature and is determined from "
"the EMISS property table for material ``N`` ( :ref:`mp` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:52
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:80
msgid ""
"If ``Lab`` = FSIN in a unidirectional Mechanical APDL-to-CFX analysis, "
"``VALJ`` is the surface interface number (not available from within the GUI)"
" and ``VALI`` is not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:84
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:104
msgid ""
"Second surface load values (if any). If ``VAL2J`` is blank, it defaults to "
"``VAL2I``. If ``VAL2J`` is zero, a zero is used. To specify a table ( "
"``Lab`` = CONV), enclose the table name in percent signs (%), for example, "
"``tabname``. Use the :ref:`dim` command to define a table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:90
#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:110
msgid "``VAL2I`` and ``VAL2J`` are the bulk temperatures."
msgstr ""

