#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:121
msgid "``VAL2I`` and ``VAL2J`` are not used for other surface load labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:137
msgid ""
"Specifies surface loads on the selected lines of area regions. The lines "
"represent either the edges of area elements or axisymmetric shell elements "
"themselves. Surface loads may be transferred from lines to elements via "
":ref:`sftran` or :ref:`sbctran`. See :ref:`sfe` for a description of surface"
" loads. Loads input on this command may be tapered. See :ref:`sfgrad` for an"
" alternate tapered load capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:143
msgid ""
"You can specify a table name only when using structural (PRES) and thermal "
"(CONV [film coefficient and/or bulk temperature], HFLUX), and surface "
"emissivity and ambient temperature (RAD) surface load labels. ``VALJ`` and "
"``VAL2J`` are ignored for tabular boundary conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/solid_surface_loads.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.solid_surface_loads.SolidSurfaceLoads.sfl:147
msgid ""
"In a mode-superposition harmonic or transient analysis, you must apply the "
"load in the modal portion of the analysis. Mechanical APDL calculates a load"
" vector and writes it to the :file:`MODE` file, which you can apply via "
":ref:`lvscale`."
msgstr ""

