" to base excitation multi-point response spectrum analysis ( :ref:`spopt`, "
"MPRS) and power spectral density analysis ( :ref:`spopt`, PSD). Defaults to "
"no component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../pymapdl/src/ansys/mapdl/core/_commands/solution/spectrum_options.pydocstring
#: of
#: ansys.mapdl.core._commands.solution.spectrum_options.SpectrumOptions.sed:42
msgid ""
"In single-point response spectrum analysis ( :ref:`spopt`,SPRS), the "
"excitation direction without rocking ( :ref:`rock` ) is normalized to one so"
" that the ``SEDX``, ``SEDY``, and ``SEDZ`` values do not scale the spectrum."
" The excitation direction with rocking is not normalized. The ``SEDX``, "
"``SEDY``, and ``SEDZ`` values must be consistent with the linear components "
"of ``OMX``, ``OMY``, and ``OMZ`` values on the :ref:`rock` command. The "
"calculated direction then scales the spectrum. For more information, see "
"`Participation Factors and Mode Coefficients "
"<https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/Views/Secured/corp/v232/en/ans_thry/thy_anproc7.html#eqe483f2f2-aaa1-4080-a835-10c0e1e18f57>`_."
msgstr ""

